er":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T06:33:23-08:00","id":1353539,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, Goths make perfect sense for Lunars, Lunars love invading corrupt empires, sacking their cities, freeing slaves, and causing carnage.<br /> Maybe not so much the having high-ranking positions within the Empire and converting to a version of that Empire's religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-08-2019, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T07:46:48-08:00","id":1353542,"title":"","content":"Given that my group just decided to place Exalted 3rd on the &quot;Beloved but Unplayable&quot; shelf after realizing that we spent more time fretting over rules than actually playing, even after a few years of trying to wrap our heads around the systems, this is hopeful news for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T12:50:46-08:00","id":1353608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353527#post1353527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's things I could pick at here but you've already made up your mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realise tone over text is incredibly hard to convey. That doubles when said text is placed in the context of being on an Internet forum. So I have to request that you believe me when I say I ask this question in good faith and out of genuine confusion: <br /> <br /> What was the point of that comment? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353527#post1353527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you were doing that for any game I'd advise against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","user":"Jang","date":". 12-08-2019, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:52:40-08:00","id":1353629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353308#post1353308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does sound a bit better, as long as people can't b*llshit easy ones. We've often said how it's a pity that the Exalted system doesn't really go into the quests for the exotic materials, which ought to be the most interesting part of forging magical weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most interesting part should be the one that has the least to do with the actual crafters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T14:16:14-08:00","id":1353633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353629#post1353629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The most interesting part should be the one that has the least to do with the actual crafters?</div> </div> </div> </div>The bit that actually involves the rest of the party and engaging with the game world?<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> The bit where the crafter begs for downtime to spend twenty minutes rolling by themselves as they consult five pages of Craft Charms (FRONT AND BACK) is the least interesting part. And the contrivance to try to shoehorn in some basic objectives is the second least interesting part.<br /> <br /> (That said, I'd quite like people to BS the easy objectives so we can get on with the game.)<br /> <br /> I mean, if you're an Athletics Supernal who needs to leap a ten-foot gap over a bottomless chasm lest you fall to certain doom... then the forboding journey to that chasm and the reward that awaits on the other side are probably both more interesting than saying &quot;I activate Monkey Leap Technique&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-08-2019, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T14:30:53-08:00","id":1353636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353608#post1353608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realise tone over text is incredibly hard to convey. That doubles when said text is placed in the context of being on an Internet forum. So I have to request that you believe me when I say I ask this question in good faith and out of genuine confusion:<br /> <br /> What was the point of that comment?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Doing what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scratch building NPCs and discarding them because they've been used. That's behaviour I associate with myself when my OCD is being challenging. I'm not saying you have a mental illness just that you appear to be approaching this game (and possibly others) in a way which practically guarantees diminished returns and is inviting some serious burnout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T15:51:29-08:00","id":1353643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353636#post1353636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scratch building NPCs and discarding them because they've been used. That's behaviour I associate with myself when my OCD is being challenging. I'm not saying you have a mental illness just that you appear to be approaching this game (and possibly others) in a way which practically guarantees diminished returns and is inviting some serious burnout.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That comes across way more harsh (and kinda passive-aggressive) than I think it's meant to? I get the feeling that you're trying to say &quot;Hey, that is something that, when I do it, doesn't work for me (and is usually unhelpful for my OCD) why don't you try this way instead?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Everyone approaches RPG's differently. Some people don't like just reusing stat blocks of NPC's for encounters, or find it hard to just migrate one thing to another. If they want it be a &quot;soldier&quot; unit rather than &quot;ghost&quot; unit, it may take more work for them. Finding 3e hard to get into because of this is....completely understandable! I really hope that Exalted: Essence is the right fit then!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T16:03:02-08:00","id":1353647,"title":"","content":"I don't care for 3E at all. None of my group Exalted players (who have all played since 1E) have played the game in years or bought any of the products because of it. This is a welcome thing to me and I look forward to buying and trying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Map of Third Edition Creation in a First Edition Style<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2F18ttip13xdsc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D35f3d332551385032587cde8b093e4923ed687ee\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b</a>, (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fpjil7fcr0esc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3Dcfdff833d8e8afe3e86ca27c06569cad0bb44be9\" target=\"_blank\">3E Locations Only</a>) (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fik6dit8lrlrc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D0e0c488dea6e066af00d52c6d5994592bb4d8359\" target=\"_blank\">1E, 2E, 3E Amalgam</a>)\u200b<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/kashi85\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt, where I post some Exalted stuffs.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/853-kashi","name":"Kashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar853_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T16:15:12-08:00","id":1353649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353629#post1353629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The most interesting part should be the one that has the least to do with the actual crafters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well generally the crafter is going to get it, but I guess not always. The thing is, as John says, getting the magical materials can be fun plot (like when my PCs got the soul of Chejop Kejak to make into a staff, or when I beat up the champion of the Thunderbirds and took his blue jade batons which I then reforged into a prosthetic hand as mine got chopped off), sitting in your forge rolling lots of dice isn't. At least, that is my experience with Crafting (something I've tried with multiple characters and so far been quite disappointed with. I ought to give up and stop trying I guess, but yet I keep trying).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T16:51:27-08:00","id":1353657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353636#post1353636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scratch building NPCs and discarding them because they've been used. That's behaviour I associate with myself when my OCD is being challenging. I'm not saying you have a mental illness just that you appear to be approaching this game (and possibly others) in a way which practically guarantees diminished returns and is inviting some serious burnout.</div> </div> </div> </div>The amount of prep I referred to was in understanding every attacker\u2019s charms - my use of the word \u201cstated\u201d is probably what threw you off and that was sloppy wording on my part. Understanding and picking the charms took time and effort, to a degree where it felt like work. And, like I amended in the very comment you quoted, I did try and re-use them, but it felt oddly same-y and boring for me to run. If you have a fix for running what I think is a dodgy combat system, in a game I am praising every other aspect of, I\u2019d happily hear it.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also why I was a little taken aback by your, \u201cyou've already made up your mind\u201d comment. In an exchange of opinions, I really can\u2019t see the point of that, other than to mark me as needlessly pigheaded. You making links between this one example and OCD also seems a little harsh and quick on the trigger. I normally wouldn\u2019t address this, but I am getting some vibes of frustration from you, a moderator. Maybe I am misreading things, maybe it is something else. Or maybe I am coming across in a way that warrants frustration. And if that is how I come across to a moderator, it sounds like I need to fix how I come across in writing. Hence why I am raising the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","user":"Jang","date":".  Clarification 12-08-2019, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T18:07:01-08:00","id":1353667,"title":"","content":"You don't like Ex3's combat system and I do respect that. The part of this conversation that's frustrated me is that there's an underlying assertion that I'm trying to keep you playing 3rd edition when I just commented on an aspect of your encounter planning that would still be a negative if you liked the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-08-2019, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T18:36:45-08:00","id":1353669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353667#post1353667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't like Ex3's combat system and I do respect that. The part of this conversation that's frustrated me is that there's an underlying assertion that I'm trying to keep you playing 3rd edition when I just commented on an aspect of your encounter planning that would still be a negative if you liked the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lioness, <i>nobody said that.</i> Nobody even <i>implied that.</i> I don't know where this is coming from! I'm actually kinda annoyed by this!<br /> <br /> As far as I can read, all that has gone on is that Jang said: &quot;this is why I don't like 3e, why I don't play it, and why I'm exited by Exalted: Essence&quot; and then got a bit miffed that you dismissed his concerns and conflated his style of making NPC's with a mental disorder, even though the connection was unintentional. That's <i>all that is going on.</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T22:42:09-08:00","id":1353708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353667#post1353667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part of this conversation that's frustrated me is that there's an underlying assertion that I'm trying to keep you playing 3rd edition [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>It is kind of reassuring to see that the vibes I was getting weren\u2019t just my imagination, but... I never thought you were doing that, I wasn\u2019t trying to convey that you were, and, looking back over our exchange with that in mind, I still have no earthly idea how you got that impression?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T01:49:17-08:00","id":1353734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353649#post1353649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well generally the crafter is going to get it, but I guess not always. The thing is, as John says, getting the magical materials can be fun plot (like when my PCs got the soul of Chejop Kejak to make into a staff, or when I beat up the champion of the Thunderbirds and took his blue jade batons which I then reforged into a prosthetic hand as mine got chopped off)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all still part of it. &quot;all artifacts require high-quality tools and significant amounts of the magical materials; most also demand various exotic or mystical reagents such as frozen flame, behemoth bones, the captured love of a raksha noble, or other such wonders.&quot; It's not a heavily systemic thing sure (and never was before), but it's the parameters for the set of conditions that the Storyteller designates before a superior crafting project can even begin. No Artifact can be made from a box of scraps.<br /> <br /> It's still a part of the process that involves no actual crafting, although a Storyteller might elect to designate that the prospective crafter needs to personally assess any such materials in order to be sure of what they can be used towards. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">sitting in your forge rolling lots of dice isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will admit that while I like the crafting system as the basis for stringing together a series of scenarios as part of composing the overall narrative of a crafter's life and how it prioritises the context of the results, the basic system is still limited in its capacity to represent the process of crafting itself. One listens to accounts that real life crafters give or watches competitive reality shows such as British Bake-Off or Forged in Fire (or maybe even has personal experience of doing that stuff) and gets the point that these things start off with a creative vision and then becomes a series of decision making and problem solving to actually bring it to life. In that context, I should think that the process necessary to convert a soul into a staff should be the most engaging thing about being a crafter, and apart from the incentive to creatively stunt every single roll made on it to maximize all of those very necessary dice the system remains somewhat limited in how to do it.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure how effectively Storyteller is suited to representing that side of the process. While I have basically no familiarity with any other game system, I'm also not sure of how any might be capable of doing so, and if the result might not end up being excessively convoluted. At times like this, I think back to the time somebody talked about the idea of trying to use the Storytelling System to represent playing baseball in the New World of Darkness, and how ultimately no process based in a dice rolling engine was going to look or feel very much like playing baseball (although that person used the point to interrogate why exactly somebody would want to represent that in the system in the first place, an easier dismissal than something as prominent in this game as crafting is supposed to be).<br /> <br /> But that's moving far off topic. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T02:11:11-08:00","id":1353740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353633#post1353633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit that actually involves the rest of the party and engaging with the game world?<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> The bit where the crafter begs for downtime to spend twenty minutes rolling by themselves as they consult five pages of Craft Charms (FRONT AND BACK) is the least interesting part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should the person who made Craft their Supernal Ability not get the most interesting part of making things?<br /> <br /> Is this an objection also to Sorcery? Or combat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the contrivance to try to shoehorn in some basic objectives is the second least interesting part. </div> </div> </div>Shoehorning in basic objectives?<br /> <br /> Basic objectives are making other characters feel more strongly about you, benefitting one of your own Intimacies or accomplishing some goal in the game.<br /> <br /> If a craft project is doing none of those things then what is it even there for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you're an Athletics Supernal who needs to leap a ten-foot gap over a bottomless chasm lest you fall to certain doom... then the forboding journey to that chasm and the reward that awaits on the other side are probably both more interesting than saying &amp;quot;I activate Monkey Leap Technique&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, presumably the foreboding journey also consists of a series of Athletics actions, possibly with some variety, such that the entire thing together is akin to the making of an intricately designed sword.<br /> <br /> Still, this might just be an essential frustration with dice-based roleplaying systems; that they're better at approaching various activities as a means to an end and simplifying the process in a manner that overlooks the intricacies that make it thrilling to truly do those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T03:39:37-08:00","id":1353751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353740#post1353740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should the person who made Craft their Supernal Ability not get the most interesting part of making things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Twenty minutes of trying to work out how your craft charms work isn't fun or interesting. My old Twilight player found it quite annoying, he just wanted to make cool stuff, and I had to tell him that first he needed to gather the craft xp, then use all these charms. I ended up writing out the final combination of craft charms for him:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Flawless Handiwork Method (re-roll 10s)<br /> <br /> Bright-Forging Prana (1/story):<br /> <br /> [Supreme Masterwork Focus x3 (double 7s)<br /> <br /> Experiential Conjuring of the Void (1 success and 10 extra dice, all non-charm)<br /> <br /> Unbroken Image Focus (5 extra successes plus 1 per success rolled before double 9s, all non-charm)]<br /> <br /> So, in conclusion:<br /> Roll 20 dice with re-roll 10s<br /> <br /> 7s, 8s and 9s are each worth 3 successes, 10s are worth 4<br /> <br /> Then roll another 10 dice with re-roll 10s and double 7s<br /> (so they're just worth 2 each this time)<br /> <br /> Now add 6 successes<br /> <br /> Now take away 4 (because the roll is difficulty 5)<br /> <br /> You need 100 total, and can't roll more than 6 times.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is this an objection also to Sorcery? Or combat? </div> </div> </div>No, because combat tends to involve everyone, and sorcery is much simpler than Craft (or combat, obviously).<br /> Some people do complain combat is too complex of course.<br /> <br /> (Oh, though actually I do see people complain that sorcerous workings often seem to just be squatting in downtime rolling dice and then something amazing happens. I'm okay with that, see below.*)<br /> <br /> This is why I'm looking forward to Exalted: Essence, as I think my players would appreciate a simpler system (well, they're mixed obviously).<br /> <br /> Now, when it comes to Craft there are different ways to do it. You could just do the 2nd ed system: you need a lot of downtime, make a roll. There were a few objections (A: If you have say a year of downtime, you could churn out artefacts in a dull way, and B: if you're on adventures to save the world, you never have time to make artefacts. Admittedly I found that even with ex3's much shorter downtimes for Craft).<br /> <br /> So that's one way Exalted: Essence could go with Craft. Just nice and simple.*<br /> <br /> *And so yes, you are right:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, this might just be an essential frustration with dice-based roleplaying systems; that they're better at approaching various activities as a means to an end and simplifying the process in a manner that overlooks the intricacies that make it thrilling to truly do those things. </div> </div> </div>Here, the goal of the crafting system is simply for the end-goal; ie, crafting isn't the interesting bit, it's what you craft. The magic sword, the giant defensive fortress, etc. That's mostly the way Sorcerous Workings work. It's what the guy who played a Twilight in my game wanted. It's the way DnD tends to do it, although DnD's not very good at it as it doesn't bother with anything that's not a magic item.<br /> <br /> Anyway, a while ago I had a conversation with some of my players about how, if you're going to have an intricate Craft system with different steps, could you make it interesting? And we thought maybe more could be done about the ingredients. In some computer games I find the Crafting system dull, but in others I like it, and this is generally stuff like how after you kill a boss it drops some special ingredient (dragon scales, say) that can make amazing armour.<br /> <br /> So I was interested to hear this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Crafting system in Scion is pretty excellent. It's like the opposite of the Ex3 Craft System. To build something, you need to accomplish a number of Milestones, and have a Path that justify it. No building of smaller things to get to bigger things. No points to keep track of. Hell, if you spend time obtaining a logical material, that can count towards the project without even rolling.<ul><li>Hypothetical Path of Exalts parallel: Amilar Harken, who has the Path of &quot;Twilight Exalt&quot;, wants to build a sword. This is an entirely mortal weapon, so would probably only require three or so Milestones. Drafting plans with a Close Combat + Intellect roll would be one Milestone, the Night Caste using their contacts to get some quality iron (Or Chiaroscuro Glass, if you're feeling exotic) would be another Milestone, and a scene of working in his forge would count as another Milestone. Bing bang boom, he made a sword. For something like a Daiklave, he'd need more Milestones, and would need to work harder to get more exotic ingredients.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div> But this is just someone's description of a Crafting system, I'd need to see the detail for how it worked.<br /> <br /> Certainly, if the point of Exalted: Essence is to be simpler, then any system beyond &quot;time+materials+roll&quot; might be too complex, and maybe better suited for the rumoured (or confirmed? I think confirmed) alternate Crafting system in the Storyteller's Companion. The above sounds simple, but I'm not sure if Kyman is simplifying it to explain it.<br /> <br /> Still, it doesn't sound like Exalted: Essence is boiled all the way down to the way some modern rules-lite systems are, it still has Attribute+Ability combos for example. Which is good, as I don't like systems with no complexity at all (at least for things like combat or social influence) as I find them dull. I just find Exalted about 20% too complex. (Obviously if I thought it was way, way too complex I wouldn't be running it.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shoehorning in basic objectives?<br /> <br /> Basic objectives are making other characters feel more strongly about you, benefitting one of your own Intimacies or accomplishing some goal in the game.<br /> <br /> If a craft project is doing none of those things then what is it even there for? </div> </div> </div>Generating points to make artefacts.<br /> <br /> I can see that the design goal with the objectives was to make sure people <i>didn't</i> just churn out basic objectives for the points, but crafted in a way that matters. But in my experience, sometimes people do it the way the Devs intended, sometimes people find ways to churn them out for Craft xp and it feels artificial.<br /> And of course, sometimes (especially in high-level games) there are simply no basic projects that really need doing, so it's purely a case of &quot;Hmmm, I need a way to generate craft points, what basic projects can I shoehorn in?&quot; and not &quot;What cool ways can I use my basic crafts?&quot;<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I don't do this, because my Zenith generates 2 gold and 12 silver a day from charms, and my Full Moon has 1679 silver points and 108 gold points on her sheet currently. Their issue is more lacking the time to sit down and make artefacts (which would have been worse in 2nd ed, though at least there wasn't many charms so I wouldn't feel like I'd wasted all this XP on craft).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, Exalted: Essence will definitely need a simpler way to handle it, even if it keeps the idea of needing to have scenes of crafting besides just the final scene of &quot;roll your dice, make your daiklaive&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sigh... the Craft system suckers me in, every time I go &quot;hmmm, maybe I could play a Crafter, surely I could do fun things with this system.&quot; I know some players do (not mine, but Alucard for example said he really enjoyed the system). And then I'm frustrated with it. I don't know if that's the nature of the games, or that I play characters with Craft as a secondary thing and it only really works well as a primary thing. Or maybe it's because I have, with Solars, gone down the Craft-xp-generating tree, which some forumites say is a trap.<br /> Still, that's not really important when talking about a hypothetical different, simpler, Crafting system, other to maybe inform some things about what not to do. But I'm not entirely sure <i>why</i> I always find I regret making a Crafter, what exactly is wrong with it, so I'm not sure how to inform it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-09-2019, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T05:42:24-08:00","id":1353771,"title":"","content":"What I think of it ? I reacted with shock and horror to the news. It think this is the worst possible news, (I really cannot think of anything that could be worse except bankruptcy for the developers ) and this might be the death to the line. I am also outraged that this has at all been an idea among the developers when it is so strikingly obvious that what we need, more than anything, is the creation and production of more main splats (we are lacking Abyssals and Sidereals !!!!). I cannot fathom how anyone thinks it is a good idea to waste resources on this pet project before Sidereals and Abyssals ! I simply cannot fathom the thinking behind this outrageous idea and I am incredibly disappointed. This basically means that we cannot expect Abyssals and Sidereals for 3-4 years. Again, what the hell are they thinking? This is so catastrophic ! This is NOT needed ! Alternative rules before we even have rules for important main splats, I don't even understand the logic ! Disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24253,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","user":"Magnus K","date":". 12-09-2019, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T05:53:10-08:00","id":1353773,"title":"","content":"Exalted Essence has its own development team. It's not drawing resources away from Ex3 anymore than Scion or Trinity are by having Exalted writers and developers working on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T05:58:22-08:00","id":1353775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353771#post1353771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I think of it ? I reacted with shock and horror to the news. It think this is the worst possible news, (I really cannot think of anything that could be worse except bankruptcy for the developers ) and this might be the death to the line. I am also outraged that this is has at all been an idea among the developers when it is so strikingly obvious that what we need, more than anything, is the creation and production of more main splats (we are lacking Abyssals and Sidereals !!!!). I cannot fathom how anyone thinks it is a good idea to waste resources on this pet project before Sidereals and Abyssals ! I simply cannot fathom the thinking behind this outrageous idea and I am incredibly disappointing. This basically means that we cannot expect Abyssals and Sidereals for 3-4 years. Again, what the hell are they thinking? This is so catastrophic ! This is NOT needed ! Alternative rules before we even have rules for important main splats, I don't even understand the logic ! Disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been said upthread, but there's a different development team working on this, so it won't affect the main line. There will be no delays of existing projects due to this one.<br /> <br /> Also, ExEss will include rules for Abyssals, Infernals, etc. So you'll actually get a rules-light(er) version of the splats you want to play even sooner because of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:11:33-08:00","id":1353781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353773#post1353773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted Essence has its own development team. It's not drawing resources away from Ex3 anymore than Scion or Trinity are by having Exalted writers and developers working on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't share Magnus's view point (I could not be more stoked by this -- I can't wait!)... but does that really hold?<br /> <br /> We've got a bunch of writers who know Exalted well enough to write an entire system book for Exalted.<br /> We've got money to pay these writers.<br /> These writers have time to write.<br /> <br /> Surely they could be given work writing books for E3, getting content out quicker?<br /> <br /> And the same for Scion or Trinity -- time spent working on those books is time not spent working on Exalted.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path chooses what work to commission from its freelancers, and the freelancers fit those commissions around their other life commitments: there isn't some infinite pool of labor, these books do draw writers away from the Exalted main-line. If you're writing something else instead of Exalted... you're not writing Exalted.<br /> <br /> Now an argument can be made that the devs want to maintain creative control: they don't want a dozen different freelancers writing half-a-dozen different books, they want manageable projects which they can check balance on, and putting all these writers on too many books too fast is bad for game quality. That's an absolutely valid argument. EE having its own team though... why couldn't they work on the Exalted mainline?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:12:48-08:00","id":1353785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353771#post1353771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I think of it ? I reacted with shock and horror to the news. It think this is the worst possible news, (I really cannot think of anything that could be worse except bankruptcy for the developers ) and this might be the death to the line. I am also outraged that this has at all been an idea among the developers when it is so strikingly obvious that what we need, more than anything, is the creation and production of more main splats (we are lacking Abyssals and Sidereals !!!!). I cannot fathom how anyone thinks it is a good idea to waste resources on this pet project before Sidereals and Abyssals ! I simply cannot fathom the thinking behind this outrageous idea and I am incredibly disappointed. This basically means that we cannot expect Abyssals and Sidereals for 3-4 years. Again, what the hell are they thinking? This is so catastrophic ! This is NOT needed ! Alternative rules before we even have rules for important main splats, I don't even understand the logic ! Disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should read the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:13:09-08:00","id":1353786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353775#post1353775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been said upthread, but there's a different development team working on this, so it won't affect the main line. There will be no delays of existing projects due to this one.<br /> <br /> Also, ExEss will include rules for Abyssals, Infernals, etc. So you'll actually get a rules-light(er) version of the splats you want to play even sooner because of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, that is mitigating news to be fair. But as one who has hoped that more resources would be put into the creation of Exalted products, I cannot see how this helps us. Because I read this as it would have been possible to start work on Abyssals or Sidereals but they opted for alternative rules instead. I don't understand it. It is much too soon for alternative rules when the game is so lacking in its main departments. But maybe my reaction is not warranted, but at this point in time, this is certainly how I feel about it. Very disappointed and I got to admit that as an exalted Story Teller waiting patiently for main splats, this just made me incredibly sad.<br /> <br /> Edit: After having scrolled through the thread, I read nothing there that can assure me that this will not impact the creation and production of main splats after Exigents. If so, and if this alternative rules thing takes precedent over main splats, it would be a tragedy for Exalted in my opinion. A real tragedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24253,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","user":"Magnus K","date":". 12-09-2019, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:16:17-08:00","id":1353788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353785#post1353785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should read the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe so and I am doing that now (don't see any particular good news so far), but you have to realise that the thread starter asked a question. I just answered, without reading the thread, true, but a question is a question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:23:22-08:00","id":1353791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353781#post1353781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now an argument can be made that the devs want to maintain creative control: they don't want a dozen different freelancers writing half-a-dozen different books, they want manageable projects which they can check balance on, and putting all these writers on too many books too fast is bad for game quality. That's an absolutely valid argument. EE having its own team though... why couldn't they work on the Exalted mainline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creative control is probably exactly the reason. Working on a rules lite version of the game with all splats that will not actually affect any future books or anything down the line is pretty isolated. If they make some major mistake or produce something kind of dissonant with the main game line the effect is isolated. Maybe on other projects, but that kind of thing should be taken really carefully before producing a splatbook.<br /> <br /> It also might ultimately be better. Generating interest in Exalted, which leads to more revenue and more ability to justify money spent on the line, and also giving a stepping stone for new players. Exalted in general is kind of a brick wall of rules that\u2019s really hard to penetrate at first, being able to learn the basic rules in a simplified way and still have fun makes the transition easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:23:38-08:00","id":1353792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353773#post1353773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted Essence has its own development team. It's not drawing resources away from Ex3 anymore than Scion or Trinity are by having Exalted writers and developers working on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it not drawing resources away from the development of Exalted main splats after Exigents ? How so ? This team could surely have worked on an actual third edition splat ? I don't understand. I mean, exalted third edition products already comes out incredibly slowly, and as buyers of this product we are already a patient lot who wait year in and year out for releases, and this could have meant that another book we actually need could have been created in tandem with what Vance and Minton are doing, or that's how I understand it at least. I really don't get this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24253,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","user":"Magnus K","date":". 12-09-2019, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:26:24-08:00","id":1353795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353786#post1353786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: After having scrolled through the thread, I read nothing there that can assure me that this will not impact the creation and production of main splats after Exigents. If so, and if this alternative rules thing takes precedent over main splats, it would be a tragedy for Exalted in my opinion. A real tragedy.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the developers this is a one off book. It\u2019ll stand alone as a simple, less comprehensive product. Adding supplements to that would basically just be telling people to buy the ex3 core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:31:24-08:00","id":1353797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353795#post1353795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the developers this is a one off book. It\u2019ll stand alone as a simple, less comprehensive product. Adding supplements to that would basically just be telling people to buy the ex3 core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I am too negative, but it is depressing to wait so many years for Exalted releases so this kind of ticked me off a bit. I just viewed this as a great chance to have another Exalted product released, and of all possible things we need, they chose what we don't need and it is confusing as hell to me. Sorry if I come across as whining. I am just perplexed and disappointed as to how they have now been revealed to prioritize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:32:18-08:00","id":1353798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353792#post1353792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it not drawing resources away from the development of Exalted main splats after Exigents ? How so ? This team could surely have worked on an actual third edition splat ? I don't understand. I mean, exalted third edition products already comes out very slowly, this could have meant that another book we actually need could have been created in tandem with what Vance and Minton are doing. I really don't get this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't too many cooks spoil the broth? I have a pretty tiny kitchen at my current apartment; having even two people in there doing something simultaneously is not really viable, let alone helpful for cooking something faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-09-2019, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:33:24-08:00","id":1353799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353792#post1353792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it not drawing resources away from the development of Exalted main splats after Exigents ? How so ? This team could surely have worked on an actual third edition splat ? I don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>They got people who were not attached to other projects to work on this. That means that, by definition, it is not drawing resources away, as the same amount of resources are on the other projects before and after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:34:37-08:00","id":1353801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353798#post1353798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a pretty tiny kitchen.<br /> <br /> If I cook my dinner at my house, my dinner gets cooked.<br /> <br /> If I have you cook your dinner at your house, your dinner gets cooked.<br /> <br /> If I have you and I cook both our dinners at my house together, it's going to be a crowded mess, and your efforts won't especially make our dinners get cooked much faster.<br /> <br /> If I cook my dinner at my house, and have you cook your dinner at your house, both our dinners get cooked.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are critical of my opinion, then be frank, don't bullshit me with this please, it is impolite. You make no sense with your analogy and you do not adress any of my concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:35:28-08:00","id":1353802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353797#post1353797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I am too negative, but it is depressing to wait so many years for Exalted releases so this kind of ticked me off a bit. I just viewed this as a great chance to have another Exalted product released, and of all possible things we need, they chose what we don't need and it is confusing as hell to me. Sorry if I come across as whining. I am just perplexed and disappointed as to how they have now been revealed to prioritize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the length of time the Core book required, the pace has actually been pretty good for the various splats.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:36:42-08:00","id":1353803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353781#post1353781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely they could be given work writing books for E3, getting content out quicker?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes adding more people to a project will not help it get out faster.<br /> <br /> Sure, we could hire a thousand people and get them all to write a single paragraph for a book, but the amount of organization they'd need in order to make a <i>good</i> book would delay the production process far more than the standard method.<br /> <br /> Sometimes making a baby takes nine months, and it's going to take nine months no matter how many additional people are involved.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:39:30-08:00","id":1353805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353799#post1353799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They got people who were not attached to other projects to work on this. That means that, by definition, it is not drawing resources away, as the same amount of resources are on the other projects before and after.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, and it would be nice if that succeeded of course. But I am skeptical when you claim that it has no impact. It seems to me that this could have mean a development of one of the books we actually need and it exasperates me that priority is given to this project which not at all seems critical for any campaign anywhere.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:41:47-08:00","id":1353806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353805#post1353805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, and it would be nice if that succeeded of course. But I am skeptical when you claim that it has no impact. It seems to me that this could have mean a development of one of the books we actually need and it exasperates me that priority is given to this project which not at all seems critical for any campaign anywhere.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is gonna include splats and material for a whole slew of other exalts, which will be transferable to E3 proper. In my book, that is material that can help any campaign anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:42:30-08:00","id":1353807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353805#post1353805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, and it would be nice if that succeeded of course. But I am skeptical when you claim that it has no impact. It seems to me that this could have mean a development of one of the books we actually need and it exasperates me that priority is given to this project which not at all seems critical for any campaign anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>My younger sister has a disability that limits her ability to do things. She's barely got enough in her to take care of herself in a given day.<br /> <br /> \u200bHaving an easier to master system would help my sister to play the game. If I want her to play in an Exalted campaign, this project is entirely critical for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:47:41-08:00","id":1353809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353803#post1353803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes adding more people to a project will not help it get out faster.<br /> <br /> Sure, we could hire a thousand people and get them all to write a single paragraph for a book, but the amount of organization they'd need in order to make a <i>good</i> book would delay the production process far more than the standard method.<br /> <br /> Sometimes making a baby takes nine months, and it's going to take nine months no matter how many additional people are involved.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really understand how you answered his very good question. Your answer strikes me as a non-answer and more as a marketing explanation as you don't really explain anything with your words. More specifically then: Why is it that these people could not have worked on an exalted product ? Are they unable to create such a product and only able to re-write the rules (which seems like a big project, which again makes me wonder, like John Dee, why they are not working on something we actually need aka missing main splats or source books)<br /> Is this question really such a bad question ? For me, it is the obvious one to ask and one I think you guys should honestly answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:52:31-08:00","id":1353811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353807#post1353807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My younger sister has a disability that limits her ability to do things. She's barely got enough in her to take care of herself in a given day.<br /> <br /> \u200bHaving an easier to master system would help my sister to play the game. If I want her to play in an Exalted campaign, this project is entirely critical for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gave you a like there, for that was a fair answer. My response to that is however that your sister is probably not the target for advanced RPGs. Look, I understand what you mean, and I sympathise with those who are frightened by the rules. But I really, really do think, and I think that is fair, that it is the Exalted target group, us who are Story tellers and buy all the products, that should be peddled to first and foremost and not people with learning difficulties or disabilities. There are other easier games with a less complex settings and rules. And source material is being released very rarely, so I do not understand how they prioritize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:53:35-08:00","id":1353812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353809#post1353809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand how you answered his very good question. Your answer strikes me as a non-answer and more as a marketing explanation as you don't really explain anything with your words. More specifically then: Why is it that these people could not have worked on an exalted product ? Are they unable to create such a product and only able to re-write the rules (which seems like a big project, which again makes me wonder, like John Dee, why they are not working on something we actually need aka missing main splats or source books)<br /> Is this question really such a bad question ? For me, it is the obvious one to ask and one I think you guys should honestly answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you worked on a creative project before? Because you hit diminishing returns by adding people after a while. It is also why they don\u2019t hire 20 people to write a script to make that process faster; it probably wouldn\u2019t help. <br /> <br /> And, again, you get some material for each splat in this book. So it will be material to use until the other splats are released in full.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:58:39-08:00","id":1353816,"title":"","content":"Also keep in mind that having a whole stable of writers throwing what they think is cool into their books without giving the developers time to give it more than a cursory glance before it hits the publishers, was what got us the worst aspects of 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T06:58:54-08:00","id":1353817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353812#post1353812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you worked on a creative project before? Because you hit diminishing returns by adding people after a while. It is also why they don\u2019t hire 20 people to write a script to make that process faster; it probably wouldn\u2019t help.<br /> <br /> And, again, you get some material for each splat in this book. So it will be material to use until the other splats are released in full.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand how you seem to be entirely convinced that having a group work on this project means that they could not have worked on another project. You don't know this. It is speculative. It could be true but it absolutely could be untrue. Perhaps you are right, but perhaps I am right. You don't know and I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T07:02:04-08:00","id":1353819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353816#post1353816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also keep in mind that having a whole stable of writers throwing what they think is cool into their books without giving the developers time to give it more than a cursory glance before it hits the publishers, was what got us the worst aspects of 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. But it still comes across as using precious, precious, rare, Exalted development resources for a parallel project that is unecessary. When the project comes out, I may love it, I hope so, but I would have appreciated a main splat more. Anyway, I am done complaining. I can't change their minds, so all i can do is to wish them the best of luck. I hope they give us a project which we can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T07:05:14-08:00","id":1353822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353817#post1353817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand how you seem to be entirely convinced that having a group work on this project means that they could not have worked on another project. You don't know this. It is speculative. It could be true but it absolutely could be untrue. Perhaps you are right, but perhaps I am right. You don't know and I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The writers themselves are saying this in the discord. E.g. this book is being developed in the &quot;off-cycle&quot; phase. Fatsplat books are not being affected. At most, you could make an argument that a supplement book (like Arms) is being &quot;sacrificed&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, the main line is unaffected, or barely affected at all, and it gives what some of us (like me and all my friends) have been asking for ever since 3e came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T07:14:50-08:00","id":1353827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353819#post1353819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand how you seem to be entirely convinced that having a group work on this project means that they could not have worked on another project. You don't know this. It is speculative. It could be true but it absolutely could be untrue. Perhaps you are right, but perhaps I am right. You don't know and I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353819#post1353819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I am done complaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you didn't know either, why were you complaining? After all, it is speculative. For me, I am hopeful because I just don't mind giving OnyxPath the benefit of the doubt that this is a good move. I guess you just aren't willing to give them that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T07:19:49-08:00","id":1353831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353781#post1353781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't share Magnus's view point (I could not be more stoked by this -- I can't wait!)... but does that really hold?<br /> <br /> We've got a bunch of writers who know Exalted well enough to write an entire system book for Exalted.<br /> We've got money to pay these writers.<br /> These writers have time to write.<br /> <br /> Surely they could be given work writing books for E3, getting content out quicker?<br /> <br /> And the same for Scion or Trinity -- time spent working on those books is time not spent working on Exalted.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path chooses what work to commission from its freelancers, and the freelancers fit those commissions around their other life commitments: there isn't some infinite pool of labor, these books do draw writers away from the Exalted main-line. If you're writing something else instead of Exalted... you're not writing Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual bottleneck in production isn't writing, although that's a long process in and of itself. Development takes time and resources and a coherent vision. That's hard enough with one person; even for Minton and Vance, or for Monica and myself, all of whom have known each other and been colleagues for more than a decade, you get tone and vision disagreements that take time to resolve lest they find themselves in the final product. I've made no secret that I think every Abyssal <i>absolutely needs </i>the definitive article in front of their name in light of Creation's naming conventions and the fact that what they're called is a title, not a name - and yet, people have incredibly strong opinions about what to call Abyssals and what a proper naming schema for them is. Reading and revising all of these things to take interlocking elements into account <i>takes time</i>. Ensuring cohesion for the line <i>takes time</i>. No, the actual bottleneck in production lies with the developers.<br /> <br /> Books are developed on a certain timeframe, at which time it's only possible to produce a certain amount of work, and this work isn't a question of how many people are willing to write. It involves those bottlenecks of development time, art direction, proofing, printing, and they are unavoidable.<br /> <br /> Now, what <i>have </i>we developed? All of the high-level pieces for each Exalt splat have been designed internally, but that bottleneck still exists. One of the selling points of <i>Essence </i>is the ability to play with these new Exalt types a while before it's feasible to fully flesh them out, and for you to enjoy their aesthetics, themes, and unique playstyles at your table without a lot of cognitive load.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now an argument can be made that the devs want to maintain creative control: they don't want a dozen different freelancers writing half-a-dozen different books, they want manageable projects which they can check balance on, and putting all these writers on too many books too fast is bad for game quality. That's an absolutely valid argument. EE having its own team though... why couldn't they work on the Exalted mainline? </div> </div> </div>Many of them do. As I said before, <i>they </i>have more time than we have developers on Exalted, and if you don't want an atonal mess of a line that contradicts itself every new splat you've got to have a line developer. It takes time and extra effort when you bring on a new dev, because you have to ensure they'll work with the singular vision of the line. Ian works closely with every <b>Trinity</b> developer regardless of line, and I do the same on <b>Scion</b> in addition to developing my own books. Monica had her <i>bona fides </i>established a long time ago in <b>Exalted</b> land, I'd hope that I've earned some too, and Dixie already has a slew of credits to her name on the line and incredible project management skills for many other lines handled by Onyx Path. I remember when the <b>Exalted</b> board was black and orange with white text, for crying out loud. We know the line.<br /> <br /> <b><u>tl;dr:</u></b><br /> <br /> 1) It's still going to take a lot of time to produce all of those books. A thousand monkeys on a thousand typewriters isn't going to write the novel faster.<br /> 2) All of the high-level aesthetics and thematics for the Exalt types have been largely designed already, but can't be put into full splatbook form yet without the above process.<br /> 3) This <i>is </i>writing <b>Exalted</b>, so those writers &quot;not writing <b>Exalted</b>&quot; are still writing <b>Exalted</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T07:35:49-08:00","id":1353833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353798#post1353798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't too many cooks spoil the broth? I have a pretty tiny kitchen at my current apartment; having even two people in there doing something simultaneously is not really viable, let alone helpful for cooking something faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've already seen this analogy play out with 2e where books frequently had their own internal development process giving rise to serious inconsistencies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T07:36:16-08:00","id":1353834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353831#post1353831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The actual bottleneck in production isn't writing, although that's a long process in and of itself. Development takes time and resources and a coherent vision. That's hard enough with one person; even for Minton and Vance, or for Monica and myself, all of whom have known each other and been colleagues for more than a decade, you get tone and vision disagreements that take time to resolve lest they find themselves in the final product. I've made no secret that I think every Abyssal <i>absolutely needs </i>the definitive article in front of their name in light of Creation's naming conventions and the fact that what they're called is a title, not a name - and yet, people have incredibly strong opinions about what to call Abyssals and what a proper naming schema for them is. Reading and revising all of these things to take interlocking elements into account <i>takes time</i>. Ensuring cohesion for the line <i>takes time</i>. No, the actual bottleneck in production lies with the developers.<br /> <br /> Books are developed on a certain timeframe, at which time it's only possible to produce a certain amount of work, and this work isn't a question of how many people are willing to write. It involves those bottlenecks of development time, art direction, proofing, printing, and they are unavoidable.<br /> <br /> Now, what <i>have </i>we developed? All of the high-level pieces for each Exalt splat have been designed internally, but that bottleneck still exists. One of the selling points of <i>Essence </i>is the ability to play with these new Exalt types a while before it's feasible to fully flesh them out, and for you to enjoy their aesthetics, themes, and unique playstyles at your table without a lot of cognitive load.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Many of them do. As I said before, <i>they </i>have more time than we have developers on Exalted, and if you don't want an atonal mess of a line that contradicts itself every new splat you've got to have a line developer. It takes time and extra effort when you bring on a new dev, because you have to ensure they'll work with the singular vision of the line. Ian works closely with every <b>Trinity</b> developer regardless of line, and I do the same on <b>Scion</b> in addition to developing my own books. Monica had her <i>bona fides </i>established a long time ago in <b>Exalted</b> land, I'd hope that I've earned some too, and Dixie already has a slew of credits to her name on the line and incredible project management skills for many other lines handled by Onyx Path. I remember when the <b>Exalted</b> board was black and orange with white text, for crying out loud. We know the line.<br /> <br /> <b><u>tl;dr:</u></b><br /> <br /> 1) It's still going to take a lot of time to produce all of those books. A thousand monkeys on a thousand typewriters isn't going to write the novel faster.<br /> 2) All of the high-level aesthetics and thematics for the Exalt types have been largely designed already, but can't be put into full splatbook form yet without the above process.<br /> 3) This <i>is </i>writing <b>Exalted</b>, so those writers &quot;not writing <b>Exalted</b>&quot; are still writing <b>Exalted</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this explanation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353827#post1353827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you didn't know either, why were you complaining? After all, it is speculative. For me, I am hopeful because I just don't mind giving OnyxPath the benefit of the doubt that this is a good move. I guess you just aren't willing to give them that?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Because I had read about some coming Exalted news, then i read it is another alternative version of the Core, which annoys me as stated previously since I as stated previously assumed that these people could have worked on an actual exalted product we need. I complained because I view myself as quite patient, but the slow release of Exalted source books are grinding on my patience, then you can probably imagine that the news that a new developer team is in fact re-working the rules instead of working on one of the books we really need, well, yes, that I found that more than a bit irritating and confusing. Then I read the opening sentence of this thread which starts by asking everyone what their opinions are, and I gave mine. That is at least my explanation to my complaint. As for giving a commercial company the benefit of the doubt before you apply some cynicism and question their motives, well I don't know how wise that is in general.<br /> <br /> I hope this explanation is good enough, as I am , as stated quite finished complaining. I am not a particularly difficult man, just a Story teller anxious and maybe a bit impatient, for source books.<br /> I can only hope the developers are right. That this will not impact other Exalted releases. And finally, wish them all the best of luck with this new project, even though I at current think it is a giant waste of resources. It might end up being smashingly fine book and that is what i hope it will be !</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T08:07:29-08:00","id":1353844,"title":"","content":"One of Storyteller-Exalted's problems is needing exactly five Abilities for each of five Ability-based Castes to Favor, and exactly three Attributes for each of at least three Attribute-based Castes to Favor.<br /> <br /> This leads to:<ul><li>Martial Arts being an entirely separate thing from all other combat Abilities in a MARTIAL ARTS GAME which should be one of the best places to acknowledge that the phrase &quot;martial arts&quot; is literally synonymous with &quot;combat skill&quot;, and if you really want to distinguish non-philosophical warriors who focus entirely on physical, external hard force from &quot;martial artists&quot; then the Attribute / Ability divide was a perfectly acceptable path. Just give them more dots in Strength and Dexterity than in Abilities.</li> <li>Charisma and Manipulation being largely the SAME Attribute but with exactly one unique application apiece (Charisma can be used to command troops, and Manipulation determines Guile). Imagine if we had two versions of Dexterity, but only one of them allowed you to keep your balance and only the other would allow you to climb things, but both of them could be used to roll for every kind of attack and defense.</li> <li>Appearance being an Attribute when NWOD rightly treats it as a Merit.</li> </ul><br /> YET, I love Third Edition's social influence system. I feel it could be more clear about the timing of Read Intentions actions, and that successfully determining that someone is lying to you should be a viable alternative to defeating their influence, but I like what it does with Intimacies and the various social influence actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only reason I gravitated to something as hideously complex as Exalted when something simpler like Big Eyes, Small Mouth existed was because Exalted's mechanics DID represent the physics engine of its world. BESM would have &quot;Charms&quot; like &quot;Massive Attack&quot;, but shirked any responsibility for explaining why some people would have that Charm and others wouldn't.<br /> <br /> First Edition Exalted would explain that &quot;Massive Attack&quot; worked because the Exalt had figured out Hungry Tiger Technique, the skill by which they made their sword EXPLODE with Solar Essence after they had successfully hit someone, so the more successfully they hit someone (ie: the more vulnerable a place they hit) the more damage the explosion would do. The Alchemical Exalted version of Hungry Tiger Technique was Piston-Driven Megaton Hammer, which was also &quot;after successfully hitting someone, make your fist explode forward to capitalize on it&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you're going to have Minutia Mechanics, then each cog in the machine needs to represent something in reality, and each different kind of exception to the rules needs to represent something.<br /> <br /> Sidereal Exalted did this with their &quot;reject reality and substitute your own by rerolling a bad roll&quot; and &quot;nudge the very laws of probability in your favor by lowering Target Numbers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted Charms largely do this simply by being Attribute-based, representing shocking raw power independent of any learned skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T08:11:33-08:00","id":1353847,"title":"","content":"Sadly, evidence suggests that some people can be persuaded to do something atrocious even when they know the argument in favor of it is based on a lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-09-2019, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T09:10:27-08:00","id":1353860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of Storyteller-Exalted's problems is needing exactly five Abilities for each of five Ability-based Castes to Favor, and exactly three Attributes for each of at least three Attribute-based Castes to Favor.<br /> <br /> This leads to...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, yet I feel while it can sometimes be awkward when the ST has to decide which Ability or Attribute people should be rolling, and I've no big problem with them reducing the number of abilities and attributes (which Vance strongly hinted they will), it's not really why the system is complex.<br /> (Essentially, I agree it is one of Storyteller's problems, but I think it's a small problem.)<br /> <br /> For example, when my group do social influence scenes and get stuck and have to check things and argue over rules interpretations, we're never leafing through the books looking for the exact difference between Charisma and Manipulation, it's for which reduction/increase of intimacies can be blocked with WP, or stuff about Decision Points, or 80% of the time the exact wording of charms (especially ones that make your targets &quot;count as&quot; having intimacies), or for some small differences in how different social influence types (Instill, Threaten, Bribe, Persuade) work in terms of when you can try them, etc.<br /> <br /> So while I don't mind if they reduce the number of Abilities and Attributes, and would likely be pleased if they did (I certainly agree with you about Martial Arts), it's not really the main thing they need to simplify for Exalted: Essence, I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-09-2019, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T09:35:56-08:00","id":1353870,"title":"","content":"All my attempts at running Exalted ultimately fall apart due to mechanics. Even with 3e, which at least is able to provide interesting results, the complexity is too much of a hurdle for most of the people I play with. I'm really looking forward to Essence - in theory, it's exactly what my players and I need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T09:46:22-08:00","id":1353874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353847#post1353847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, evidence suggests that some people can be persuaded to do something atrocious even when they know the argument in favor of it is based on a lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they wanted to believe or do it that much already, then you wasted the group's time by rolling for it instead of simply roleplaying it.<br /> <br /> You only need to roll for something when the subject does NOT want to accept the influence, ESPECIALLY if it's based on a lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T09:52:44-08:00","id":1353876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353802#post1353802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the length of time the Core book required, the pace has actually been pretty good for the various splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I largely understand the reasoning behind Exalted: Essence, but this line is absolutely too much.<br /> <br /> We have <b>one </b>&quot;splat&quot; released at this time after the core. Sure there's another that's pretty much done and they're working on a third, but... I remember long ago when the developers (the previous ones, I admit) said that we'd be getting two &quot;splats&quot; a year. And I remember <b>that </b>seeming slow to me. So saying that the pace has been good is just... not true.<br /> <br /> The pace has been... maybe <i>better </i>would be a preferable way to say it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T09:55:32-08:00","id":1353877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353860#post1353860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we're ...leafing through the books looking for ...which reduction/increase of intimacies can be blocked with WP, or stuff about Decision Points... or for some small differences in how different social influence types (Instill, Threaten, Bribe, Persuade) work in terms of when you can try them, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the system I was defending as worthwhile, though I'm willing to consider a simplified system.<br /> <br /> Including a simplified Charm system.<br /> <br /> Though honestly, I'm falling out of love with Exalts and Charms. I'm grower fonder of people who are exceptional because they are exceptionally skilled rather than because they were chosen by one of several gods who enable them to be exceptional in one of several different, mutually exclusive ways that no one else in the world can be.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts and Sorcery are the only universal abilities, and only one of those is actually available to mortals, and the other suffers from being distinct from all of the unique and exclusive &quot;martial arts / combat skills&quot; practiced by each kind of Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T10:15:22-08:00","id":1353887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353860#post1353860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true, yet I feel while it can sometimes be awkward when the ST has to decide which Ability or Attribute people should be rolling, and I've no big problem with them reducing the number of abilities and attributes (which Vance strongly hinted they will), it's not really why the system is complex.<br /> (Essentially, I agree it is one of Storyteller's problems, but I think it's a small problem.)<br /> <br /> For example, when my group do social influence scenes and get stuck and have to check things and argue over rules interpretations, we're never leafing through the books looking for the exact difference between Charisma and Manipulation, it's for which reduction/increase of intimacies can be blocked with WP, or stuff about Decision Points, or 80% of the time the exact wording of charms (especially ones that make your targets &amp;quot;count as&amp;quot; having intimacies), or for some small differences in how different social influence types (Instill, Threaten, Bribe, Persuade) work in terms of when you can try them, etc.<br /> <br /> So while I don't mind if they reduce the number of Abilities and Attributes, and would likely be pleased if they did (I certainly agree with you about Martial Arts), it's not really the main thing they need to simplify for Exalted: Essence, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between Attributes or Abilities has never really been a problem for us. Sure, some Attributes are more useful than others, but it's not the biggest barrier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T10:38:06-08:00","id":1353896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353633#post1353633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit that actually involves the rest of the party and engaging with the game world?<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> The bit where the crafter begs for downtime to spend twenty minutes rolling by themselves as they consult five pages of Craft Charms (FRONT AND BACK) is the least interesting part. And the contrivance to try to shoehorn in some basic objectives is the second least interesting part.<br /> <br /> (That said, I'd quite like people to BS the easy objectives so we can get on with the game.)<br /> <br /> I mean, if you're an Athletics Supernal who needs to leap a ten-foot gap over a bottomless chasm lest you fall to certain doom... then the forboding journey to that chasm and the reward that awaits on the other side are probably both more interesting than saying &quot;I activate Monkey Leap Technique&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T10:44:28-08:00","id":1353898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353877#post1353877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though honestly, I'm falling out of love with Exalts and Charms. I'm grower fonder of people who are exceptional because they are exceptionally skilled rather than because they were chosen by one of several gods who enable them to be exceptional in one of several different, mutually exclusive ways that no one else in the world can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good news! The <b>Trinity Continuum </b>core rulebook is <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/onyx-path-publishing-announces-trinity-continuum-core-and-trinity-continuum-aeon-now-available-in-stores-and-online/\" target=\"_blank\">now available for purchase</a>!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T11:19:35-08:00","id":1353905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353876#post1353876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I largely understand the reasoning behind Exalted: Essence, but this line is absolutely too much.<br /> <br /> We have <b>one </b>&quot;splat&quot; released at this time after the core. Sure there's another that's pretty much done and they're working on a third, but... I remember long ago when the developers (the previous ones, I admit) said that we'd be getting two &quot;splats&quot; a year. And I remember <b>that </b>seeming slow to me. So saying that the pace has been good is just... not true.<br /> <br /> The pace has been... maybe <i>better </i>would be a preferable way to say it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Exigents is slated to early next year. The pace of &quot;one hardcover a year&quot; Is actually to my udnerstanding one of the more productive of the various OPP lines right now to be hoenst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T11:53:06-08:00","id":1353915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353876#post1353876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I largely understand the reasoning behind Exalted: Essence, but this line is absolutely too much.<br /> <br /> We have <b>one </b>&quot;splat&quot; released at this time after the core. Sure there's another that's pretty much done and they're working on a third, but... I remember long ago when the developers (the previous ones, I admit) said that we'd be getting two &quot;splats&quot; a year. And I remember <b>that </b>seeming slow to me. So saying that the pace has been good is just... not true.<br /> <br /> The pace has been... maybe <i>better </i>would be a preferable way to say it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original statement, long ago, was one big splat and one skinny splat a year.<br /> <br /> The &quot;per year&quot; part isn't there at the moment, but we've got four books so far. Core, Arms, Dragon-Blood, Realm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T11:59:12-08:00","id":1353917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353915#post1353915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original statement, long ago, was one big splat and one skinny splat a year.<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;per year&amp;quot; part isn't there at the moment, but we've got four books so far. Core, Arms, Dragon-Blood, Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Five, we also got miracles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T12:49:20-08:00","id":1353929,"title":"","content":"Not to mention all the little Hundred Devils and Adversaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T13:10:03-08:00","id":1353935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353877#post1353877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the system I was defending as worthwhile, though I'm willing to consider a simplified system.<br /> <br /> Including a simplified Charm system.<br /> <br /> Though honestly, I'm falling out of love with Exalts and Charms. I'm grower fonder of people who are exceptional because they are exceptionally skilled rather than because they were chosen by one of several gods who enable them to be exceptional in one of several different, mutually exclusive ways that no one else in the world can be.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts and Sorcery are the only universal abilities, and only one of those is actually available to mortals, and the other suffers from being distinct from all of the unique and exclusive &amp;quot;martial arts / combat skills&amp;quot; practiced by each kind of Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on why the exalt was selected doesn\u2019t it? And can be a chicken and egg thing where the god or other being in question chooses the person as exemplifying traits or abilities that represent something exceptional to that being, making more of what they are already rather making them something wholly new.<br /> <br /> And this only applies to Celestial exalts anyways, as Dragonblooded are chosen by no being, but, just like a persons abilities, are intrinsic to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unless you ascribe the the philosophy of course that a person\u2019s abilities are primarily determined by their will and drive to enhance them and are not an innate part of who they are of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T13:22:53-08:00","id":1353940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353929#post1353929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention all the little Hundred Devils and Adversaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, that\u2019s kind of two halves of another book there. Or something like that, I\u2019m not sure how big the final ones will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T15:06:14-08:00","id":1353972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353905#post1353905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, Exigents is slated to early next year. The pace of &quot;one hardcover a year&quot; Is actually to my udnerstanding one of the more productive of the various OPP lines right now to be hoenst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think the Exigents kickstarter with raw text to backers is slated for early next year (and I don't think it'll be as early in the year as Dragonblood or Lunars were, ie March, because I'm sure we'd had previews by the previous Christmas, and this year there's nothing).<br /> The splat that'll be released in 2020 is Lunars. In fact, if you look at the brochure that my friend's link on the first page leads to, it says for 2020 they're aiming to release Lunars, Across the Eight Directions, and Exalted: Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T15:08:09-08:00","id":1353974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353940#post1353940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, that\u2019s kind of two halves of another book there. Or something like that, I\u2019m not sure how big the final ones will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I asked and they said there's still quite a lot to go.<br /> <br /> It may be worth nothing that there are way, way more entries released for Hundred Devils than for Adversaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T15:22:16-08:00","id":1353976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353974#post1353974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I asked and they said there's still quite a lot to go.<br /> <br /> It may be worth nothing that there are way, way more entries released for Hundred Devils than for Adversaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sort of wondering how far they're going with it. Like, they can't be shooting for a Monster Manual size literal hundreds of creatures, it's too big and it'd take too long, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T15:53:52-08:00","id":1353983,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a>, that sounds a bit like being burned out on Exalted; sounds like it's worth embracing the flavour that you're into right now, but I bet at some point you'll turn around and be like &quot;<i>Man, all these hyper-driven, naturally skilled, dynamic heroes are getting a bit samey... what about a story where it's just, like, a fairly ordinary guy/girl who suddenly has mystic powers thrust upon them in a sudden bolt of enlightenment? Like Aang or Neo</i>.&quot;. And the fire and magic of Exalts will be back for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T16:06:10-08:00","id":1353987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353976#post1353976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sort of wondering how far they're going with it. Like, they can't be shooting for a Monster Manual size literal hundreds of creatures, it's too big and it'd take too long, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so far there's 50-ish creatures, they're each about 2 pages, so that's 100 pages. The original MM was 160 pages, the current one I don't know but apparently it has 150 monsters (I'm sure some are variants of others and on the same page though).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I suspect it depends on how much money they're making from it, and whether they intend to do a seperate spirits book or not. It seems to be a format that's working for them, so maybe they'll just keep doing it until they run out of ideas.<br /> <br /> Antagonists on the other hand only has like... 25 entries maybe? And Crucible of Legends is apparently going to have<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I did my first good fight using Hundred Devils yesterday. Previously I've found it a bit awkward because the creatures in there are so weak compared to high level Solars, but in yesterday's session the Full Moon summoned the biggest storm serpent he could to fight via a dance and drumming taught to him by the No Moon, and then leaped off the party's airship to fight him while hanging from a long rope. Serpent and Tiger-Bull battled in the sky, and the serpent was smashed into a mountaintop. The serpent returned, but the Tiger-Bull ripped out its eye and sent it weeping away. Since then, they've been able to fly through the storms on the way to the Elemental Pole of Air without the other Storm Serpents having the guts to take them on.<br /> <br /> I found the entry a little repetitive after the first couple of rounds (as he just kept spamming his defensive charm and his counterattack, having such an enormous mote pool, as Elementals do), but it was decent, the power level was about right for a dealable challenge for a Full Moon.<br /> More Elementals and Demons plz!<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder what Exalted: Essence will do in terms of antagonists. Maybe there'll be simple stats. I asked them about animals on the Discord, as I've found Lunars who turn into a lot of different animals gets complex, and they said they'd thought about it, but can't describe what they're doing with it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T17:14:12-08:00","id":1354007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353987#post1353987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found the entry a little repetitive after the first couple of rounds (as he just kept spamming his defensive charm and his counterattack, having such an enormous mote pool, as Elementals do), but it was decent, the power level was about right for a dealable challenge for a Full Moon.<br /> More Elementals and Demons plz!</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you think it might fare against young dragonblooded? Next year I'll be running some and really hope to make more use out of the antagonists than I have with my Solar campaigns so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T19:49:13-08:00","id":1354043,"title":"","content":"Heh. I wouldn't want to turn the whole thread into a litigation on problem craft systems, but I do want to note that Ford v Ferrari is a recent example of the kind of narrative about making things that I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> And when I thought more about it I remembered how, hey, driver Ken Miles needs to regularly get into the thing and test it out (at considerable risk to his life) not only to put their experiments into practice but to provide expert feedback on how things are working out and identifying further problems.<br /> <br /> So if crafting things was more iterative and you had incentives to put them in the hands of people skilled in their use at each stage of development, there's making sure the rest of the circle is involved while centering the process of development right there.<br /> <br /> Even has a social and bureaucratic side in the form of needing to report back to corporate on their progress, justifying their decisions and navigating executive intrigue, which one could find as inspiration for things such as complications arising from funding the project or having the use of the work space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T01:02:23-08:00","id":1354085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354007#post1354007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you think it might fare against young dragonblooded? Next year I'll be running some and really hope to make more use out of the antagonists than I have with my Solar campaigns so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should be fine I think. It's very tough against Withering, but not decisive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T13:38:23-08:00","id":1354242,"title":"","content":"I, for one, am very excited about this announcement. <br /> <br /> I am in the same camp as many that I have played Exalted since 1e was released. My first game was actually with Geoff Grabowski at Gen Con. I was hooked. I didn't play a lot during 1e, but when 2e came along my local group went a bit mad and had a weekly game for several years. We played well together and didn't even have many problems with the broken aspects of some of the more problematic charms that people reference so often when they talk about 2e.<br /> <br /> Then 3e came out and the Kickstarter suffered so many delays. We still stayed hyped, but when we received the final product we all examined it and collectively cringed. We tried to muddle through it, but after a couple of combats that lasted for more than 1 session, we decided that it wasn't for us. I thought maybe it was just our group. I have now played a few times with others though (online and with OP at cons) and I know it wasn't. The truth is that 3e is not a playable system for me and any of the groups I have been around. I have gone through some of the stages of grief over this game that I have loved so much.<br /> <br /> I am literally jumping up and down excited over this announcement though. I have sky-high hopes and seeing Dixie Cochran on the Dev Team has me even more excited for the project. I honestly thought that it would take another edition after all of the 3e splats were released before I would be able to play again sometime in 2028, but now that all may change. <br /> <br /> I will say again, I am SUPER excited for this edition!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5172-navar","name":"Navar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T03:52:14-08:00","id":1354332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Navar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354242#post1354242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then 3e came out and the Kickstarter suffered so many delays. We still stayed hyped, but when we received the final product we all examined it and collectively cringed. We tried to muddle through it, but after a couple of combats that lasted for more than 1 session, we decided that it wasn't for us. I thought maybe it was just our group. I have now played a few times with others though (online and with OP at cons) and I know it wasn't. The truth is that 3e is not a playable system for me and any of the groups I have been around. I have gone through some of the stages of grief over this game that I have loved so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about 3e is, it actually does what it does quite well, but what it does is definitely not for everybody, or even for most people.<br /> <br /> Dunno if you're familiar with the complexity vs depth dilemma in game design. Simply put, complexity is how many things the player has to keep in mind when making their decisions, and depth is how many meaningful choices and strategies the game offers. Ideally, you want maximum depth with minimum complexity, but some degree of complexity is unavoidable, especially if you really want a lot of depth. Finding the right balance between the two is an art.<br /> <br /> In that context, 2e had very high complexity, but very little depth, in that the optimal way to play was to put up the so-called 2/7 filter Combo in every round and maintain a constant offense without mote expenditure, and if two characters with that build clashed, the fight was determined by a combination of who has the bigger mote pool and who can stunt better. 3e has significantly upped the depth, but it's done nothing to reduce the complexity - in fact, it has increased it!<br /> <br /> If I had 3e ten years ago, when I was younger, had more time and more readily available players, I'd have loved that stuff. But now that I'm having trouble gathering my team every two months and rarely can count on more than a couple hours of prep time, it just doesn't work. Last time I tried running a campaign, I managed to keep players invested and the dice rolling for two sessions, then ran one more well received session that was nevertheless almost dice-free, then on my fourth session I tried running a combat and it was an utter disaster because no player could remember half the combat Charms they had, and they still curbstomped the opponent because I forgot to give him a couple bread and butter survivability Charms and messed up the timing on what was supposed to be his big &quot;gotcha&quot; trick, allowing players to counter it easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T07:16:07-08:00","id":1354349,"title":"","content":"I think you are likely correct, in general, about 2e. The question I have always had though is what percentage of tables play optimally? In all of Role Playing the objective is to tell a story collectively, and our groups have never focused on &quot;optimal&quot; anything. I believe that I have been fortunate to have not been a part of groups that have done this. Even now my routine playgroup involves a math professor at an NCAA Division 1 university and we have a lot of probability and optimization conversations, but (to invoke a D&amp;D reference because we cannot play 3e) we will still cast vicious mockery and build characters with that cantrip despite it being suboptimal if it is better for the story/our enjoyment at the table. <br /> <br /> When you frame the system as complexity vs. depth than I totally see what you mean though. It really does feel like you have found the exact problem, and I totally understand how you could have combat fall apart because of a small error on the terms of the ST because the system is so complex. When I played at Gen Con this summer the ST was a ROCK STAR. He actually simplified the system just a bit. He had printed out laminated cards for every player with our combat tricks and dice pools on them. And STILL, the 4-hour session was 1 hour of role play and 3 hours of combat. It wasn't unusual for a player to flip through their cards for 10 minutes trying to decide if it was time to make a decisive attack or not. And all but 1 player at the table had at least played 3e before (but not necessarily Dragon Bloods.) While playing my heart just keep sinking because that morning I had played in a very fun Pathfinder 2e game, and, given the choice between the systems there isn't one. At 40, with adult players, I cannot play Exalted 3e nor do I have the time to do all of the work to make it playable for the other adults I game with. (For the record we don't play Pathfinder either.)<br /> <br /> But Exalted Essense has me VERY hyped. I am really excited and cannot wait for the news to start trickling in. I am one of those who still buys all of the Kickstarters (I have a bit of fatigue when it comes to the MOTW Drivethrurpg products), but it will be nice to buy an exalted product that I will actually be able to play <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I know I said it before, but I have so much faith in the Fabolous Dixie Cochran that I am sure this product will be suppurative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5172-navar","name":"Navar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T08:14:07-08:00","id":1354360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353898#post1353898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good news! The <b>Trinity Continuum </b>core rulebook is <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/onyx-path-publishing-announces-trinity-continuum-core-and-trinity-continuum-aeon-now-available-in-stores-and-online/\" target=\"_blank\">now available for purchase</a>!</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it differentiate any form of fighting from martial arts? Or is a karateka separated from a street brawling punk by being formally trained to punch, kick, and throw <i>effectively</i>, but might still lose because the street punk pulls some sort of underhanded, tournament-illegal trick that the karateka could organically learn to do himself without having to learn a completely redundant Brawl Ability before finally learning &quot;Brawl Charms&quot;?<br /> <br /> Would there be just as much support for fighting with a battle-ax as with a slashing sword, let alone a bloody <i>hook sword?</i><br /> <br /> This is why I looked fondly back at Burn Legend. Where a karateka doesn't have to learn Karate as an Ability gated off by a Merit, he can just start purchasing Karate Techniques, and if he discovers that doesn't offer him a necessary counter-technique to someone who is kicking his ass, he can study Wrestling and begin practicing the specific Wrestling Technique he needs without needing to buy up dots in a Wrestling Ability which is virtually identical to the Karate Ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Storyteller system was designed to <i>abstract </i>all forms of punching, kicking, and grappling to just any roll of 1-to-10 dice, because the Storyteller system wasn't specialized for combat. It was for playing vampires who spent more time scheming and talking than fighting, and when they fought it was generally dirty, vicious street brawls between untrained fighters.<br /> <br /> Then <i>Exalted</i> tried to layer Charms over that system, with Charms effectively taking the place of tactical choices like Fierce Punch, High Kick, Block, etc. So a system that wasn't meant for nuanced combat was tasked with running a MARTIAL ARTS GENRE GAME.<br /> <br /> And this was further complicated by needing exactly 9 Attributes and 25 Abilities for dividing evenly among Castes and Aspects, and then basing all magic on those Traits. And realizing too late how this effectively gave Solars four different Martial Arts Styles that no one else could learn, and which would operate oddly if combined with any universally available Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm hopeful that &quot;Path of Exalts&quot; system can find a nice middle ground between Exalted 3rd Edition and Burn Legend.<br /> <br /> A system where the sub-systems (combat, social influence, crafting, introducing facts) are made the first design priority, with the Traits necessary for them tailor-made for the sub-systems rather than the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-11-2019, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T08:21:46-08:00","id":1354363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Navar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354349#post1354349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are likely correct, in general, about 2e. The question I have always had though is what percentage of tables play optimally? In all of Role Playing the objective is to tell a story collectively, and our groups have never focused on &quot;optimal&quot; anything. I believe that I have been fortunate to have not been a part of groups that have done this. Even now my routine playgroup involves a math professor at an NCAA Division 1 university and we have a lot of probability and optimization conversations, but (to invoke a D&amp;D reference because we cannot play 3e) we will still cast vicious mockery and build characters with that cantrip despite it being suboptimal if it is better for the story/our enjoyment at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I ever wanted out of Exalted was a good shonen-level fight. Not necessarily Dragon Ball level, but at least Bleach. So yeah, I totally expected everyone at the table to play optimally. I myself was sifting through books, thinking up one broken combo after another, with the explicit understanding that the players will do the same and bring their own bullshit powers to bear against those of my NPCs.<br /> <br /> The problem with 2e is, you can't have that regardless if you play optimally or not. If you play optimally, everyone turtles behind a perfect without any offensive Charm use and the fight becomes a boring slog. If you ban perfects, the game becomes rocket tag, as non-perfect defences can't stand up to Essence-powered offense, and almost every Essence-powered attack becomes lethal. Damned if you do, damned if you don't. And neither option carries any significant tactical depth with it, which is what you'd expect from a system that has you choose from dozens discrete magical powers for every action you take.<br /> <br /> In general, a well written system shouldn't have you choose between playing optimally and telling a good story. If optimal choices lead to bullshit story, the system itself is bullshit.<br /> <br /> 3e solves most of my problems with Exalted, just not in a way I can comfortably play. Again, if I had it at that time when I was itching to start my first 2e game, perhaps things would have been different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T08:57:48-08:00","id":1354377,"title":"","content":"Who has used the Introduce Facts mechanic extensively, and would you want to see it used in &quot;Path of Exalts&quot;?<br /> <br /> Would you want to see the injury/ailment and medical treatment systems simplified, or ported over as-is?<br /> <br /> I like the sound of the milestone system for crafting and sorcerous works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T09:07:45-08:00","id":1354380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354377#post1354377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who has used the Introduce Facts mechanic extensively, and would you want to see it used in &quot;Path of Exalts&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely one of my fav things about 3e, saw constant use in every session I ran. Makes knowledge checks in pretty much every other system clumsy and uninteresting in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T09:26:58-08:00","id":1354383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354380#post1354380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely one of my fav things about 3e, saw constant use in every session I ran. Makes knowledge checks in pretty much every other system clumsy and uninteresting in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often did it interact with your group's attempts at social influence?<br /> <br /> How often did someone try to persuade your characters based on information that someone attempted to retroactively make a lie (or delusion) based on an introduced fact?<br /> <br /> How often did you introduce a fact before trying to convince a character to do something based on that knowledge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T09:33:21-08:00","id":1354385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354383#post1354383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often did it interact with your group's attempts at social influence?<br /> <br /> How often did someone try to persuade your characters based on information that someone attempted to retroactively make a lie (or delusion) based on an introduced fact?<br /> <br /> How often did you introduce a fact before trying to convince a character to do something based on that knowledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to all those is &quot;rarely&quot;, but that's also how often social influence sees use at my table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T09:36:37-08:00","id":1354386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354377#post1354377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who has used the Introduce Facts mechanic extensively, and would you want to see it used in &quot;Path of Exalts&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't use it much until recently. Or rather, as the ST I didn't see PCs use it much. I've been trying to encourage the No Moon's player to use it, as he said he doesn't like it... but now he's started using it it's pretty good. I think it's essentially a good system if the players use it the way it's supposed to be used, and accept that the ST might edit it.<br /> <br /> I used it once to establish that there was an evil, decadent sorcerer who lived nearby when we were stranded on the Plateau of Leng, so we could go and try to trick him into using his powers to take us where we wanted (as our airship had been eaten by giant worms). If I'd tried to use it to say there was a super-friendly sorcerer who loved helping random Exalts, well that'd be cheating my lack of Ally.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the No Moon used an Establish Fact to declare that he knew who the mysterious villains from another player's backstory were. He declared they were mercenaries called the World Eaters (ie Khorne Berzerkers from 40k). Which could have been really awkward, but I kind of built it in by basically having the villains using the name as a cover to hide their true identities.<br /> <br /> Then, last session as the PCs were travelling through a massive thunderstorm on their way to the Elemental Pole of Air, he used it to declare that if the Full Moon did a special dance and drumming, it would summon the local top Storm Serpent and if he defeated it no other Storm Serpents would bother them. Now, that seems really powerful for what is essentially a roll supported by no charms. But the thing is, frankly, I would much rather have the Full Moon fight one elemental and the No Moon look like he's really good at his job of knowing about spirits, than actually have to run multiple fights against Storm Serpents which would be dull or feel too easy if I handwaved it.<br /> <br /> I have sometimes felt the charm where he makes an Introduce Fact to declare that some spirit actually really loves this herb he has in his pocket is a bit... I don't know, anticlimatic? But again, I don't care that much if the shaman finds it easy to convince spirits of stuff, that's what he's supposed to do. And the charm is harder to use if you don't have to go on a quest to find a rare thing.<br /> <br /> So, overall, I could see how some players might be awkward with it, but I've found it fine. It's also not very complicated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you want to see the injury/ailment and medical treatment systems simplified, or ported over as-is? </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... what precisely are you referring to?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T09:42:56-08:00","id":1354387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354383#post1354383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often did someone try to persuade your characters based on information that someone attempted to retroactively make a lie (or delusion) based on an introduced fact?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't exactly understand what you mean, could you give an example?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How often did you introduce a fact before trying to convince a character to do something based on that knowledge? </div> </div> </div>I've seen this quite a lot because there's a Lunar charm that works this way, but it's very specific. Specifically, the shaman announces that he knows a spirit the PCs want to talk to actually really loves some rare herb that he happens to have in his pocket, and the charm then makes him able to make a Bargain action with the spirit as if the spirit has a Major Intimacy to it.<br /> <br /> I think it's pretty dull, and he could do it in a more interesting way, but... eh. A shaman's good at convincing spirits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T09:45:05-08:00","id":1354388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354363#post1354363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I ever wanted out of Exalted was a good shonen-level fight. Not necessarily Dragon Ball level, but at least Bleach.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great way to look at it. A fun note of exalted history is that it was originally sold (at least partially) as kind of &quot;ninja scroll the RPG.&quot; if you are familiar with the old movie. <br /> <br /> And if you are not familiar with the old movie then you should fix that, post-haste. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5172-navar","name":"Navar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:04:58-08:00","id":1354394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354387#post1354387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't exactly understand what you mean, could you give an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to buy a horse and cart from a farmer you encounter on the road. The storyteller says the farmer doesn't want to part with either because he needs them for the harvest season.<br /> <br /> You introduce a fact that this harvest season is going to be a massive failure for some reason that even the farmer wouldn't know. Suddenly the farmer sees a less more value in keeping his horse and cart than in gaining cold, hard coin that he can use to buy long-lasting food to survive the next season.<br /> <br /> <br /> You disguise yourself as a citizen of Foreign Country A to infiltrate Foreign Culture B. A guard stops you because Foreign Culture B doesn't trust people from Foreign Culture A.<br /> <br /> You introduce a fact that your particular disguise distinguishes you as a real subculture of Foreign Culture A that the guard knows about but didn't recognize you as, and this subculture is one that his culture actually approves of. He is now more inclined to let you through unmolested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:07:59-08:00","id":1354396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354360#post1354360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it differentiate any form of fighting from martial arts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Training in advanced combat techniques is done via purchasing Edges (basically Merits). These might be stand-alone boosts (One Against An Ocean gives you a bonus on your next attack whenever you take an opponent down), or Style Edges which are a string of moves you learn in sequence. Style Edges that are broadly applicable need to be bought per weapon (including unarmed), while Style Edges that focus on a specific thing (ex: Sniper) apply with any appropriate weapon. Though at the moment there are only three Style Edges that would be classify as martial arts (the others might be useful in a fight, but aren't about fighting specifically).<br /> <br /> Edges can be gated by ratings in Attributes and/or Skills, and sometimes a Path (ex: a character with no Paths that provide a reason to be trained in combat might not be able to get some combat Edges).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or is a karateka separated from a street brawling punk by being formally trained to punch, kick, and throw <i>effectively</i>, but might still lose because the street punk pulls some sort of underhanded, tournament-illegal trick that the karateka could organically learn to do himself without having to learn a completely redundant Brawl Ability before finally learning &quot;Brawl Charms&quot;? </div> </div> </div>The Trinity Storypath rules only use Aim (ranged) and Close Combat for fighting. The difference between a karateka and a street brawling punk are going to be Close Combat rating, Specialties (full characters get one at 3 dots), Skill Tricks (also achieved by fulled stated characters with high ratings in Close Combat), and Edges. Antagonists stated up as basic antagonists don't have Specialties or Skill Tricks.<br /> <br /> So the street brawling punk wouldn't be able to do anything the karateka couldn't do, but might be better at it despite having lower Close Combat, and the karateka wouldn't have to buy something different from besides choosing to learn some dirty tricks via Edges or a Skill Trick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would there be just as much support for fighting with a battle-ax as with a slashing sword, let alone a bloody <i>hook sword?</i> </div> </div> </div>Weapons in Storypath are just based on Tags. As noted, if you bought up Precise Martial Arts Style Edge for hook swords, you couldn't apply the bonuses to a battle-ax, but you could relearn it with a battle-ax. But you'd still have all your basic Close Combat stuff to use with the battle-ax.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So a system that wasn't meant for nuanced combat was tasked with running a MARTIAL ARTS GENRE GAME. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure this is entirely fair since Exalted isn't just a martial arts genre game.<br /> <br /> The current versions of Storypath aren't specifically oriented towards a specific martial arts genre, so you're not going to find the depth of techniques as something like Burn Legend. But the engine could be tuned towards that if desired.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:22:43-08:00","id":1354405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Navar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354388#post1354388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a great way to look at it. A fun note of exalted history is that it was originally sold (at least partially) as kind of &quot;ninja scroll the RPG.&quot; if you are familiar with the old movie.<br /> <br /> And if you are not familiar with the old movie then you should fix that, post-haste.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is yeah, an important bit. Exalted origianlly was written with a pretty specific set of anime in mind. It's just that it hit the zeitgeist when it did pretty solidly, but in the process became more &quot;broadly anime&quot;. And in some groups,t hat meant more DBZ and TTGL than it did Ninja Scroll or Escaflowne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:22:56-08:00","id":1354406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Navar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354388#post1354388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a great way to look at it. A fun note of exalted history is that it was originally sold (at least partially) as kind of &quot;ninja scroll the RPG.&quot; if you are familiar with the old movie.<br /> <br /> And if you are not familiar with the old movie then you should fix that, post-haste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely one of my favorite anime of all times. And I know it was also a major inspiration for the original 3e developers. Holden specifically mentioned it as the kind of story he thought 2e emulated really badly when discussing his design priorities for 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:49:14-08:00","id":1354413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354396#post1354396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure this is entirely fair since Exalted isn't just a martial arts genre game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is when the game shifts to combat resolution rules.<br /> <br /> Even sooner than that; when you're designing a character who has trained in how to fight, and where the fighting abilities that truly matter act like distinct techniques (Charms).<br /> <br /> In <i>Berserk</i>, is Guts not essentially a martial artist with his enormous sword? I read the fight where he was challenged by a smaller, nimble fencer who trapped Guts in a room filled with tightly-placed stone columns to prevent Guts from using his Heavy Swordsman Style's Wide Swing Technique. And where Guts was confronted on a narrow ledge with his sword arm up against the cliff, once again effectively sealing his most dangerous Techniques.<br /> <br /> Guts was prodigiously strong for a human, but he didn't just rely on his Strength Attribute. His combat skills are martial arts. The two phrases are completely synonymous.<br /> <br /> SUPERNATURAL martial arts is a different story. That's when someone uses magic to transcend mortal martial skill to use an enormous sword to do the kind of crazy shit that Cloud Strife achieved through Limit Breaks, like Whirlwind, Meteor Rain, and Omnislash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-11-2019, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T11:51:28-08:00","id":1354422,"title":"","content":"To approach this from another direction.<br /> <br /> Burn Legend can model a &quot;martial artist&quot;, because that's precisely what it is geared to do.<br /> <br /> But such a system is also easily capable of modeling a tiger or bear. Even if you don't give the beast any Okami/Lunar Techniques, you can give them whichever Basic Techniques you want, at any level of expertise you want, and then scale their Attribute dots as high as you want. Plenty of bestial brute strength to make the animal into a combat threat without any Advanced Techniques.<br /> <br /> The system can also model untrained thugs. It works exactly like modeling a bear, but far more modest Attributes, and maybe one Advanced Technique if they have any informal training at all, or maybe they fight as a hobby when they're not working as someone's dumb muscle.<br /> <br /> And of course, anyone who invested almost entirely in non-combat skills is easily modeled, with their low Attributes and only the single &quot;Basic Strike&quot; Basic Technique at the lowest possible level of investment. They won't perform very well, but they CAN perform. The system is built to recognize and resolve even their level of contribution.<br /> <br /> The system scales all the way up (Bruce Lee, with fireballs), it scales all the way down (pencil-pusher), and it scales completely sideways (fucking bear).<br /> <br /> <br /> Compare this to the base Storyteller system made for <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i>, which was meant to model untrained thugs and not to scale so finely upwards into master martial artists. The Gangrel had a trick in one of their Disciplines for turning their hands into claws, and all Vampires could be super-strong or super-fast, but few to none of their powers took the form of a specific kind of punch, kick, or block. Any attack with fist, foot, sword, or bar stool was entirely abstracted with a dice roll, with greater skill being represented solely with more dots resulting in more dice and maybe more successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Exalted </i>cannot sell itself on allowing you to play <i>Ninja Scroll</i> if the system cannot properly model a master martial artist as well as those with no strength or skill, or those with no skill who rely on brute strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-11-2019, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T12:14:08-08:00","id":1354424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354422#post1354422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To approach this from another direction.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <i>Exalted </i>cannot sell itself on allowing you to play <i>Ninja Scroll</i> if the system cannot properly model a master martial artist as well as those with no strength or skill, or those with no skill who rely on brute strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet the Exalted System seems, in my experience, to model everything you just described... In fact, I played pretty much each of those martial descriptions in Storyteller System (from Vampire to Werewolf to Changeling to Mortals). I will admit that maybe my standards differ from yours, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T12:30:50-08:00","id":1354426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354422#post1354422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Exalted </i>cannot sell itself on allowing you to play <i>Ninja Scroll</i> if the system cannot properly model a master martial artist as well as those with no strength or skill, or those with no skill who rely on brute strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might be overthinking this a bit, Sunder. Exalted doesn\u2019t have particular moves or merits representing MA techniques because at the mortal level those are abstracted down to just gambits, trips, holds, unarmed disarming techniques. The granularity is in charms because that\u2019s where most of the game takes place, where the entry level is Bruce Lee with fireballs, and it scales all the way up to becoming a Dragon Deer Carp...thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T12:40:37-08:00","id":1354429,"title":"","content":"A Dragon Deer Carp... Thing? I really wanna see that one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T12:53:32-08:00","id":1354430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354394#post1354394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to buy a horse and cart from a farmer you encounter on the road. The storyteller says the farmer doesn't want to part with either because he needs them for the harvest season.<br /> <br /> You introduce a fact that this harvest season is going to be a massive failure for some reason that even the farmer wouldn't know. Suddenly the farmer sees a less more value in keeping his horse and cart than in gaining cold, hard coin that he can use to buy long-lasting food to survive the next season.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he doesn't know, how can you use it to convince him?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You disguise yourself as a citizen of Foreign Country A to infiltrate Foreign Culture B. A guard stops you because Foreign Culture B doesn't trust people from Foreign Culture A.<br /> <br /> You introduce a fact that your particular disguise distinguishes you as a real subculture of Foreign Culture A that the guard knows about but didn't recognize you as, and this subculture is one that his culture actually approves of. He is now more inclined to let you through unmolested. </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean that he now recognises you as, but I see your point. I guess these are possible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T12:59:28-08:00","id":1354434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354429#post1354429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dragon Deer Carp... Thing? I really wanna see that one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's the capstone to Dreaming Pearl Courtesan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:00:35-08:00","id":1354435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354429#post1354429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dragon Deer Carp... Thing? I really wanna see that one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well the description is...<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201c Her neck lengthens up towards the heavens <br /> as she grows up to five times her normal height, while her <br /> head becomes that of a delicate, gold-beaked foal. Four sets <br /> of spiraling gazelle\u2019s horns adorn her brow, and her arms <br /> and legs vanish while opalescent fins like those of a carp <br /> hold her new form aloft in the air. Countless eyes run down <br /> either side of her narrow snout and continue down her <br /> back, ranging from the size of small pearls to that of goose <br /> eggs, blazing like sapphires in the noonday sun\u201d<br /> <br /> And the picture is...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/0ea30c78-dd1f-434e-93b0-b6c5474eb735/dpn9ka-642475b9-a8e2-4e42-8a50-6b274cc48da3.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..xg2L7lZTePUcPd_-HQC0_G7c0mmhZsoWIc2t5D76958\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/0ea30c78-dd1f-434e-93b0-b6c5474eb735/dpn9ka-642475b9-a8e2-4e42-8a50-6b274cc48da3.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..xg2L7lZTePUcPd_-HQC0_G7c0mmhZsoWIc2t5D76958\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/0ea30c78-dd1f-434e-93b0-b6c5474eb735/dpn9ka-642475b9-a8e2-4e42-8a50-6b274cc48da3.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..xg2L7lZTePUcPd_-HQC0_G7c0mmhZsoWIc2t5D76958\" target=\"_blank\"> https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/0ea30c78-dd1f-434e-93b0-b6c5474eb735/dpn9ka-642475b9-a8e2-4e42-8a50-6b274cc48da3.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..xg2L7lZTePUcPd_-HQC0_G7c0mmhZsoWIc2t5D76958 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:17:26-08:00","id":1354439,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Stroyteller did have punches do less damage with more accuracy and kicks the inverse. It also had body slams, grapples, sweeps, tackles and throws. Werewolf added bite attacks (to the claw Gangrel already had). 1E Exalted had Brawl and Martial Arts Charms. nWoD introduced fighting styles like Boxing as merits. Storyteller has knock backs, knock downs, multiple attacks as a flurry of blows.<br /> <br /> It doesn't model combat as well as, say, Burn Legend, sure.<br /> <br /> But it's a LOT more complex than E3 having &quot;unarmed attack&quot; at a fixed TN of 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:36:30-08:00","id":1354446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354435#post1354435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the description is...<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201c Her neck lengthens up towards the heavens<br /> as she grows up to five times her normal height, while her<br /> head becomes that of a delicate, gold-beaked foal. Four sets<br /> of spiraling gazelle\u2019s horns adorn her brow, and her arms<br /> and legs vanish while opalescent fins like those of a carp<br /> hold her new form aloft in the air. Countless eyes run down<br /> either side of her narrow snout and continue down her<br /> back, ranging from the size of small pearls to that of goose<br /> eggs, blazing like sapphires in the noonday sun\u201d<br /> <br /> And the picture is...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/0ea30c78-dd1f-434e-93b0-b6c5474eb735/dpn9ka-642475b9-a8e2-4e42-8a50-6b274cc48da3.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..xg2L7lZTePUcPd_-HQC0_G7c0mmhZsoWIc2t5D76958\" target=\"_blank\">https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca88...soWIc2t5D76958</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahhh Yes... Thank You - I forgot about Dreaming Pearl Courtesan...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:05:07-08:00","id":1354453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354413#post1354413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is when the game shifts to combat resolution rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not inherently.<br /> <br /> The problem here is that pesky word &quot;genre.&quot; Genre is the sort of context that can take phrases that have base definitions that mean the same thing, and then have them mean completely different things.<br /> <br /> Just having a combat system doesn't mean your game's genre has turned into martial arts.<br /> <br /> Or to put it a different way: Is Saving Private Ryan a martial arts genre film? If you think it isn't, then you get the distinction that having people demonstrate martial capabilities isn't the same thing the set of tropes/norms/etc. that define a genre. If you think it is a martial arts genre film... I think we're not going to get anywhere because you're rejecting the common use meaning of words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In <i>Berserk</i>, is Guts not essentially a martial artist with his enormous sword? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure this is the best example consider that Guts isn't actually that skilled at fighting techniques and all that. His strength (keeping in mind he one-hands a sword most people couldn't use with two hands, and cleanly cuts things in half with it despite it effectively being too dull to properly call a blade), his tenacity, and most importantly his tactical skills are what carries him most of the time. His fights are rarely refined techniques vs. different refined techniques. They're mostly about whether or not Gutz can get himself in a position to use a powerful but basic attack on his enemy. He's really good at getting into a spot where he can smash you with that sword, but all he's really doing is swinging a giant sword around because very few things can take a hit from it and survive. He doesn't have a deep bench of advanced techniques, which is why he struggles against smarter opponents that manage to out maneuver him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354422#post1354422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare this to the base Storyteller system made for <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i>, which was meant to model untrained thugs and not to scale so finely upwards into master martial artists.</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't really demonstrated this. As noted the Storyteller system for VtM had a number of combat techniques. While you didn't learn them individually, many were too difficulty for low ranked characters to pull off successfully. What can't you do in the Storyteller system with the techniques in the book?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Gangrel had a trick in one of their Disciplines for turning their hands into claws, and all Vampires could be super-strong or super-fast, but few to none of their powers took the form of a specific kind of punch, kick, or block. </div> </div> </div>Because vampires in VtM don't have &quot;superpowered fighting techniques,&quot; as part of their powers. That doesn't meant the system can't handle this. Many WtA Gifts do take the form of specific attacks (though a lot are claw and bite based because they're werewolves). In Mage, depending on edition a bit, Do grants access to specific attacks as well; and a rote might incorporate specific attacks. So just saying that vampires didn't get these sorts of powers doesn't mean the system can't do them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any attack with fist, foot, sword, or bar stool was entirely abstracted with a dice roll, with greater skill being represented solely with more dots resulting in more dice and maybe more successes. </div> </div> </div>Isn't this just describing the process of how games need to abstract things to make them functional in play? There are games that go into more or less detail, but they all end up simplifying it to some level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Exalted </i>cannot sell itself on allowing you to play <i>Ninja Scroll</i> if the system cannot properly model a master martial artist as well as those with no strength or skill, or those with no skill who rely on brute strength. </div> </div> </div>The only thing I see lacking here is the brute strength based fighter who's actually a threat to a well trained fighter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:06:29-08:00","id":1354454,"title":"","content":"I also advocate certain MAs giving weapon tags to the unarmed attack of the user for more variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:51:17-08:00","id":1354468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354453#post1354453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure this is the best example consider that Guts isn't actually that skilled at fighting techniques and all that. His strength (keeping in mind he one-hands a sword most people couldn't use with two hands, and cleanly cuts things in half with it despite it effectively being too dull to properly call a blade), his tenacity, and most importantly his tactical skills are what carries him most of the time. His fights are rarely refined techniques vs. different refined techniques. They're mostly about whether or not Gutz can get himself in a position to use a powerful but basic attack on his enemy. He's really good at getting into a spot where he can smash you with that sword, but all he's really doing is swinging a giant sword around because very few things can take a hit from it and survive. He doesn't have a deep bench of advanced techniques, which is why he struggles against smarter opponents that manage to out maneuver him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this different from how an Earth Dragon Stylist fights? Tanking blows with tenacity and sometimes heavy armor, while trying to use withering attacks with a heavy weapon to maneuver the opponent into a vulnerable position for one decisive attack?<br /> <br /> How are his skills not &quot;refined&quot; compared to those of his &quot;refined&quot; opponents? Are thpse opponents using Martial Arts instead of Melee? Then Guts could never &quot;refine&quot; his techniques, because they would stem from a fundamentally different and incompatible source.<br /> <br /> His technique can only be unrefined if he and his opponents are operating on the same basic principles, and Guts simply has fewer dots in the shared Ability, or fewer Techniques.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As noted the Storyteller system for VtM had a number of combat techniques. </div> </div> </div>Conceded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:56:57-08:00","id":1354471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354454#post1354454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also advocate certain MAs giving weapon tags to the unarmed attack of the user for more variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T17:14:14-08:00","id":1354494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354426#post1354426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might be overthinking this a bit...</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that not what forums are for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T17:33:34-08:00","id":1354499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354454#post1354454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also advocate certain MAs giving weapon tags to the unarmed attack of the user for more variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Though we'd need a revision of equipment and tags for it to work well. I've tried it. It works, but the 3e design structure leaves it OK, but still not worth the cost for non-Charm users as long as it has to be balanced for the Charm users.<br /> <br /> Trinity 2e uses tags for this purpose (though not exclusively), and it works great. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354468#post1354468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this different from how an Earth Dragon Stylist fights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... rather significantly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tanking blows with tenacity and sometimes heavy armor, while trying to use withering attacks with a heavy weapon to maneuver the opponent into a vulnerable position for one decisive attack? </div> </div> </div>First, Guts doesn't tank much when he's fighting his main opponents. He's extremely tough for a human, but he's still human, and can die extremely easily if he gets hit. Tanking and enduring is his backup option.<br /> <br /> Second, he focuses on first hit kills, not withering a lot. Again, his primary foes are insanely deadly, and he knows his best tactics are to kill them ASAP; esp. if he can surprise them (something he's pretty damn good at despite the sword), or trap them with explosives/his hidden cannon/hidden crossbow.<br /> <br /> Third, he's propped up significantly by equipment rather than techniques. He's skilled, but he never demonstrates greater skill than his opponents or techniques beyond the basics of swordsmanship. He's got a sword that's supernaturally good against demons, armor that boosts his physical ability and heals some damage while risking is life in the process, and weapons hidden in his prosthetic arm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are thpse opponents using Martial Arts instead of Melee? </div> </div> </div>Who knows? Exalted's mechanics aren't the basis for Berserk's physics. Probably a mix given the variety of things he's fought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His technique can only be unrefined if he and his opponents are operating on the same basic principles, and Guts simply has fewer dots in the shared Ability, or fewer Techniques. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The Exalted separation of Brawl/Melee and Martial Arts is completely artificial. The whole point of it is to emulate the <u>genre</u> elements that make the martial arts genre inspirations for the game present. In Berserk this separate is irrelevant and thus never addressed, and thus he's operating on the same basic principles and has fewer techniques than many of his foes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T18:35:54-08:00","id":1354505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354468#post1354468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His technique can only be unrefined if he and his opponents are operating on the same basic principles, and Guts simply has fewer dots in the shared Ability, or fewer Techniques.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call melee so much unrefined as...uncodified maybe? Somebody who has melee 5 and a specialty has certainly refined their ability to use a sword, but it's different from Single Point or Steel Devil. The guy who's gotten melee 5 has got there through intuition and experience, and training in it teaches more principles than specific techniques. Like you might learn about lines of attack or something.<br /> <br /> It differs from Martial Arts in that MA is almost always about unarmed combat as well as weapons, with currently 23 publishes martial arts and 3 don't use unarmed attacks. It also differs because MA tend to have somewhat discreet techniques and accompanying philosophy. A brawler wouldn't lean forward and kick over their own back while saying &quot;Quickly Strikes the Scorpion!&quot; or roll their body with a blow in a really specific way, taught as Ocean Rolls with Tide technique.<br /> <br /> In the real world that kind of thinking probably only really helps in training your body to move a certain way, and the philosophy behind emulating the ocean, or a tiger, or whatever is ultimately not going to be as good at fighting as somebody who's just made a martial art for pure combat. In Exalted this is not the case. In Exalted you really do gain power from emulating an eagle. Mechanically this doesn't do much though, except let you block lethal without a stunt, which in universe is actually pretty badass, being able to block a sword blade or spray of needles with your bare hand.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, this isn't how the real world works, but it's how Exalted works. European knife fighting could be refined and defined in the real world as a martial art, but in Exalted it would just be melee, because it doesn't act like a fantastical mystical martial art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 12-11-2019, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T05:17:57-08:00","id":1354554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354505#post1354505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call melee so much unrefined as...uncodified maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Laughs in Agrippa*<br /> <br /> EDIT: I know you specifically acknowledge this isn't how it works IRL, but just couldn't resist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T05:35:04-08:00","id":1354556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354554#post1354554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Laughs in Agrippa*<br /> <br /> EDIT: I know you specifically acknowledge this isn't how it works IRL, but just couldn't resist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naturally, and you\u2019ll want to study your Agrippa in case you\u2019re facing a master who studied Thibault and are fighting in rocky terrain!<br /> <br /> In Exalted you actually could have something like that with melee but it\u2019s probably going to look like something straightforward and practical, where martial arts are flashy and showy. It\u2019s the fantasy world of Exalted though that lets somebody use a flashy barehanded animal style kung-fu and perfectly match somebody with a sword using expert sword techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T09:13:28-08:00","id":1354586,"title":"","content":"I'm not even sure what I'm arguing anymore, or why, and I feel like it is detracting from the subject of the thread, so I'll just concede the argument.<br /> <br /> But if a simplified Exalted would result in fewer distinct Traits and make it easier to grow from &quot;I'm a master of the firewand&quot; into &quot;I'm a master of Righteous Devil Style&quot;, I think that would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-12-2019, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T09:16:35-08:00","id":1354588,"title":"","content":"I agree. Whether that is due to a philosophical change in terms of how MA vs Melee vs Brawl is depicted or not, the point of Essence is to be simpler, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T10:59:20-08:00","id":1354617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354468#post1354468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conceded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...<br /> <br /> It's been a long time since I played Storyteller. But IIRC...<br /> <br /> You always wanted to Kick. Never Punch. Whether you were throwing 3 dice or 10, Kick was mathmatically superior at every level in terms of DPR (unless your opponent had, like 1 health level remaining).<br /> <br /> Likewise you always wanted to Bite. Bite was far and away better than any other combat option. Period. And if you were in the dire wolf form you got an extra die on bite attacks.<br /> <br /> It was nothing like a good combat system. Alternity (Fallout 1) had distinct punches and kicks, and unlocked more powerful moves as you got stronger (like haymaker and roundhouse) and more accurate techniques (like jab) as your unarmed skill increased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T11:24:58-08:00","id":1354624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354617#post1354617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...<br /> <br /> It's been a long time since I played Storyteller. But IIRC...<br /> <br /> You always wanted to Kick. Never Punch. Whether you were throwing 3 dice or 10, Kick was mathmatically superior at every level in terms of DPR (unless your opponent had, like 1 health level remaining).<br /> <br /> Likewise you always wanted to Bite. Bite was far and away better than any other combat option. Period. And if you were in the dire wolf form you got an extra die on bite attacks.<br /> <br /> It was nothing like a good combat system. Alternity (Fallout 1) had distinct punches and kicks, and unlocked more powerful moves as you got stronger (like haymaker and roundhouse) and more accurate techniques (like jab) as your unarmed skill increased.</div> </div> </div> </div>And bite is usually aggravated if you're a werewolf or vampire. We once had a crutch-wielding Nosferatu leap onto the back of a vozhd and do enough bite damage that her more combat-capable friends could leap onto it and help finish it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T14:19:59-08:00","id":1354669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1354617#post1354617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You always wanted to Kick. Never Punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, it's the other way around. Lower difficulty to attack &gt; more damage. You hit more often, with more successes, so your average damage is better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise you always wanted to Bite. Bite was far and away better than any other combat option. Period. And if you were in the dire wolf form you got an extra die on bite attacks. </div> </div> </div>This is a bit mixed outside of WtA. Most characters need to grapple, and then bite as part of a grapple, which is pretty weak without decent biting teeth. VtM makes this tactic useful since their bites are agg instead of lethal, and Potence makes grappling ridiculously powerful. Werewolves can bite without a grapple in Crinos/Hispo/Lupus and get a very good bite attack move (that's not in the other games even with something like a Gangrel using Protean to become a wolf and then biting you).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was nothing like a good combat system. </div> </div> </div>Good is a bit more subjective than this.<br /> <br /> However it's not a fun combat system for action oriented games with interesting combat options and tactics that avoid making one way of fighting the best.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T17:10:26-08:00","id":1354699,"title":"","content":"Were there any published spells that Mages had that made bite attacks the optimal combat path? In my brief experience with an oWoD game, the Mage who hung around with my vampire from time to time used Correspondence and Forces to open an itty-bitty portal on his hand to the other side of the planet to let sunlight through,* but I never saw him bite anybody.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> _______________________________________<br /> \u200b*<i>Yes</i>, he called it the &quot;Sundouken.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T19:06:55-08:00","id":1354708,"title":"","content":"None that would classify as optimal, because anything you could to boost bites you could do to boost any unarmed attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T10:18:11-08:00","id":1355654,"title":"","content":"About &quot;General Exalted Charms&quot;.<br /> <br /> What would you say are general capabilities of all exalts? I would say excellencies,but! each exalt had differences in them. Maybe things like Graceful Crane Stance, and of course, Ox-Body Tech. I wonder how EE will handle this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T10:59:41-08:00","id":1355659,"title":"","content":"If the point is to make a much simpler system, you can honestly cover all the workhorse stuff with universal charms; jump further, lift more, punch harder, parry better, run faster, talk more convincingly, take more damage. Then just give Solars upgrades to those, more dots, more essence, and other splats different stuff. Yes, dice-adders are less interesting if they're all the same, but are they that interesting anyway?<br /> (And I hope there'll be less dice-adding from charms anyway, because rolling 20-odd dice slows things down.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:29:09-08:00","id":1355664,"title":"","content":"Really 90% of what Exalted do is the same, they just do it in different ways, and I imagine a lot of that could be simplified. We don\u2019t know how many unique charms every splat is getting but you could probably get by with 20 or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T18:14:13-08:00","id":1355736,"title":"","content":"If there are less abilities, maybe, yeah. I think that might be a little low for a lot of them though. It's probably fine for Solars, but not for Sidereals or Dragonblood. They still need to play differently. Probably you want each Ability to have 2-3 iconic things.<br /> <br /> Couple of other things: <br /> A Universal Charm could have different flavour for different splats but work the same way. A DB adds damage on a stab with fire, while a Lunar does it with strength, but they both have +3 damage.<br /> <br /> A simpler system might have simpler charms, which might take up less space both on the page and cognitively. Exalts may also have less (DBs start with 20. 20! That isn't simple), if the game is rebalanced so they need less, meaning less charms need to be written generally.<br /> Anyway, this may mitigate against needing to use Universal Charms to reduce word count to fit in all the Exalt types.<br /> <br /> <br /> On an unrelated matter, consider: if you want to reduce the number of dice Exalts are rolling, but still have them at the same power level, how do you do it? I'm wondering if you do it by changing mortals. Some of the mortals in the Core have 7-9 dice on some things. Perhaps you change it so mortal spods have 1 dice, professionals or dangerous beasts have 3, demons have 5. Then if a Solar has 8 dice, that's truly impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-19-2019, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T04:25:08-08:00","id":1355811,"title":"","content":"From a variance of results perspective vs simplicity, always seems better for mortals to have something like 4 dice and then Exalted mostly to have success adders and not dice adders. Otherwise you get high and very binary variance of results at the very low bound (1 dice). At least the way Storyteller does things.<br /> <br /> Presuming you're mostly throwing Sux=1 things at mortals, you want them to succeed on the whole, and the gains of exceeding threshold successes are not very large, and then for things that are hard for mortals then you've got Sux=2 (hard but still over 50% of the time?) and Sux=3 (about 20% of the time?). Then you can give trained professionals / etc. at +1 sux, &quot;heroes&quot; at +2 sux.<br /> <br /> Ideally more dice=&gt;smoother function of successes of course. I get that this may not be as fun from a &quot;Big pools o' dice&quot; perspective for players, and means more rolling for STs than 1 die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T06:05:03-08:00","id":1355820,"title":"","content":"Simplifying is great. My players like it.<br /> <br /> It used the &quot;obscurity system&quot; for simple testing (not extended and not resisted). If difficulty = ability - 2 then success is automatic. BoS5, pg 25-26.<br /> <br /> I created a turn system for 2ed. Turn = 6 tick (speed of a simple charm), same actions act on the same tick (best initiative first), penalty ends on the remaining ticks of turn (punch without penalty on tick 6 and 2nd circle magic without penalty on ticks 5-6 of second turn).<br /> <br /> I adapted the techniques of Burn Legend. You bought each type of martial art to use martial art techniques and increased your levels. Attacking with a technique outside of your Martial Art counted only as a Stunt in one of 5 basic techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T09:39:36-08:00","id":1355874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1355664#post1355664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really 90% of what Exalted do is the same, they just do it in different ways, and I imagine a lot of that could be simplified. We don\u2019t know how many unique charms every splat is getting but you could probably get by with 20 or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>With enough work, any Exalt could have the Lunar trick of &quot;I've actually been here the whole time in disguise&quot;. It's just that Lunars have it easiest, since they can be anyone or any creature, whereas Solars are limited to people, and Terrestrials find the trick hardest of all to pull off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T00:29:53-08:00","id":1356013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1355736#post1355736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there are less abilities, maybe, yeah. I think that might be a little low for a lot of them though. It's probably fine for Solars, but not for Sidereals or Dragonblood. They still need to play differently. Probably you want each Ability to have 2-3 iconic things.<br /> <br /> Couple of other things: <br /> A Universal Charm could have different flavour for different splats but work the same way. A DB adds damage on a stab with fire, while a Lunar does it with strength, but they both have +3 damage.<br /> <br /> A simpler system might have simpler charms, which might take up less space both on the page and cognitively. Exalts may also have less (DBs start with 20. 20! That isn't simple), if the game is rebalanced so they need less, meaning less charms need to be written generally.<br /> Anyway, this may mitigate against needing to use Universal Charms to reduce word count to fit in all the Exalt types.<br /> <br /> <br /> On an unrelated matter, consider: if you want to reduce the number of dice Exalts are rolling, but still have them at the same power level, how do you do it? I'm wondering if you do it by changing mortals. Some of the mortals in the Core have 7-9 dice on some things. Perhaps you change it so mortal spods have 1 dice, professionals or dangerous beasts have 3, demons have 5. Then if a Solar has 8 dice, that's truly impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the idea upthread of just adding successes instead. In Vampire, an 'average' mortal only has 4 dice. If your vamp has 6-10, that's pretty impressive in most cases. If Exalts have a limit of 10 dice with success adding Charms, you have a very simple system. <br /> <br /> Similarly, Exalted v WoD had a rule that Exalts never increase the difficulty for doing complicated things. That could work too. Or you could have target number 6 for Exalts and 7 for everyone else. Little things like that will help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T06:07:09-08:00","id":1356282,"title":"","content":"Who wants <i>Essence</i> to use the Withering/Decisive attack schema, and who doesn't, and why?<br /> <br /> Who wants <i>Essence</i> to introduce different terms for some or all of the terms currently called &quot;Essence&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T06:52:06-08:00","id":1356289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356282#post1356282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who wants <i>Essence</i> to use the Withering/Decisive attack schema, and who doesn't, and why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have yet to play Exalted in any way, but I believe the Withering/Decisive combat scheme is much more elegant than &quot;just give 'em more Hit Points&quot; or &quot;make 'em harder to hurt through difficulty to hit or actually do real damage&quot; from... other systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356282#post1356282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who wants <i>Essence</i> to introduce different terms for some or all of the terms currently called &quot;Essence&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some more specificity might be good, especially as it pertains to the Essence manipulation of sorcerous workings vs. the Essence that Exalts have by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T06:57:15-08:00","id":1356290,"title":"","content":"I've mentioned this before elsewhere, but one of the people I recently introduced to Exalted singled out motes as the most complicated part of the system.<br /> <br /> She's got a good handle on initative and craft xp but forgets about mote recovery because it's fixed at an automatic 5m/round that she doesn't interact with and that across the board mote costs/pools are grossly inflated and that you could divide all the numbers involved and lose very little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T07:57:37-08:00","id":1356297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356282#post1356282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who wants <i>Essence</i> to use the Withering/Decisive attack schema, and who doesn't, and why?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Withering/Decisive attack schema is important to the cinematic style of 3e combat so I'd be sad if it went away completely. That said it can certainly be simplified. An example of a much simpler model for that is Anima Prime, where there is no Soak/Hardness and Withering attacks are just one roll which ignores enemy Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T08:46:50-08:00","id":1356303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356289#post1356289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have yet to play Exalted in any way, but I believe the Withering/Decisive combat scheme is much more elegant than [...] make 'em harder to hurt through difficulty to hit </div> </div> </div> </div>Yyyeahhh but Exalted has both of those.<br /> <br /> And I'll be honest, I kind of hoped at one point that the former would preclude the latter a bit. Yet I still hear too many accounts of how easy it is to make a Defence that means the majority of opponents have no hope of ever actually hitting you, which to my mind sounds like it takes away from the lot of the potential of the combat system to shine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T09:24:11-08:00","id":1356308,"title":"","content":"Like others, I'm happy with the basic concept of Withering/Decisives, but it could be made simpler; and it doesn't have to even be similar in terms of how it works to the main game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T09:29:03-08:00","id":1356309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356290#post1356290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've mentioned this before elsewhere, but one of the people I recently introduced to Exalted singled out motes as the most complicated part of the system.<br /> <br /> She's got a good handle on initative and craft xp but forgets about mote recovery because it's fixed at an automatic 5m/round that she doesn't interact with and that across the board mote costs/pools are grossly inflated and that you could divide all the numbers involved and lose very little.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also keeping track of your anima.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think in a simpler system you could have less motes, less cost for charms, more permanent charms, scratch willpower and scratch in-combat mote regeneration. Make animas really simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T10:03:11-08:00","id":1356316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356290#post1356290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've mentioned this before elsewhere, but one of the people I recently introduced to Exalted singled out motes as the most complicated part of the system.<br /> <br /> She's got a good handle on initative and craft xp but forgets about mote recovery because it's fixed at an automatic 5m/round that she doesn't interact with and that across the board mote costs/pools are grossly inflated and that you could divide all the numbers involved and lose very little.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've felt the same way for years.<br /> <br /> Motes are well-named, because they're so damn SMALL. One mote is so insignificant. But there are SO MANY of the little, insignificant things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T10:52:56-08:00","id":1356329,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of motes in 1e as a mechanic to emulate JRPGs and to emulate martial arts manga and movies where characters have a fixed reserve of &quot;chi&quot; which they must marshall against their foes (and their foes want to deplete it). <br /> <br /> (Maybe the editions kind of lost some awareness of this, in the sense that they didn't align the incentives very well to encourage players to spend motes on offense, in order to force your opponent to spend more of theirs, and motes were generally best preserved by engaging defense Charms and hacking away with a huge damage weapon. But it seems fine in principal?)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you are doing like 3e and doing away with this for a lot of mote regen, and a more fighting-game kind of style where characters aren't really very limited by a fixed resource and are constrained from pulling off super moves by risk vs reward / rock-paper-scissors, and introduces a new active-fluctuating resource to manage, then it seems like you could do away with it entirely. Or make it something which where motes are relatively infrequently replenished and big and easy to track with tokens? Maybe?<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Q: What about the divide between Personal and Peripheral mote pools that cause anima-flare differently? Complexity that's not worth the trade off, or present an interesting choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T11:00:42-08:00","id":1356331,"title":"","content":"Fairly tangential thought sparked by adam's comment on previous page, comparing Exalt dice pools to oWoD dice pools and ExVWoD, that kind of makes me wonder how much Exalted dicepools are actually optimized to a certain size in order to tackle the sort of threats from Creation that they are fighting, vs how much they are optimized to be bigger than WoD's big dogs, in order to make a statement to WoD fans picking up Ex1e...? (Which works well in ExVWoD where the idea of the game as HS designed it is Exalts mashing WoD monsters, but doesn't serve much purpose otherwise). Maybe another point to consider?<br /> <br /> (I kind of feel like that would have dropped away after a couple of editions if that were the case that Exalt dicepools were generally overkill for the sort of characters implied by the setting, hence this may be totally idiotic but seemed interesting enough to put out there.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T11:18:40-08:00","id":1356334,"title":"","content":"Several points; I don't feel motes are complicated per-se, it's just that it's yet another thing to keep track of. If you weren't keeping track of initiative/overwhelming/willpower/anima/wounds at the same time, it'd be fine.<br /> <br /> Anima banner though is overly-complex, and could definitely be simplified.<br /> In terms of the choice, I feel that it is important for the game that there is a reason not to throw your full power at everything, and that when you do unleash your full power you get the anime glow.<br /> But does there need to be two different ways to make this happen at the same time? Ie personal/peripheral and spending 5+ motes at a time? Why not just have one pool and spending X motes at a time takes you up a level? Or you can spend personal motes fine and peripheral makes you glow? (But that shouldn't be separated from regen. Though it'd be much easier to have no regen at all in combat. Just stick with sleep or meditation.)<br /> <br /> If charms represent your skill, do basic workhorse ideas need to cost motes? <br /> For example, I occasionally run Star Wars: Edge of the Empire. As well their Attributes+Abilities, characters buy Talents for some XP, which might need to spend a resource to use, but a lot are &quot;+1 health level&quot; or stuff like &quot;ignore 1 point of penalty when flying a spaceship&quot;. If, say, your sailor has a charm to reduce penalties from sailing against the wind, does that really need to cost a resource? (Especially one you'll get back easily, 5 an hour or 5/round in combat)<br /> <br /> You've also got charms that work 1/scene or 1/day. Again, do they need to also cost a resource? (Especially if they lose reset conditions due to simplification)<br /> Most of all, do they need to cost 2 different resources, one of which is recovered 1/day (ie Willpower).<br /> <br /> I don't want to say that resource-management is a terrible idea, it's not, it's more that Exalted tends to have a whole bunch of different resources going on at the same time, which I feel is very unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T11:29:56-08:00","id":1356336,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it a bit more, if they kept the Withering-changes-your-initiative (which I think is quite elegant, though there are some bits that could be simplified), then there could just be two resources: Initiative and Willpower. Charms could have small permanent effects or special moves that cost willpower or initiative, spending a willpower on a charm makes you flare, the social system still uses willpower, etc.<br /> <br /> Though charms giving you a 1/scene special move/big bonus would work fine too. It worked well for 4th ed DnD, and the lack of combining the charms keeps the game simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T11:57:51-08:00","id":1356339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356329#post1356329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: What about the divide between Personal and Peripheral mote pools that cause anima-flare differently? Complexity that's not worth the trade off, or present an interesting choice?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can spend 4ph in an Instant without flaring. It's pretty trivial to pay 4ph+Xpp to prevent flare. I've not had any trouble doing so for high end Solar combat theory-crafts nor in my Deeb game.<br /> <br /> I like the Mote Reactor Hack homebrew for fixing this, which changes anima from your aura which flares if you're incautious when drawing spiritual energy from the world to a spiritual powerhouse that you ramp up to gain more power.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> For combat, I like getting rid of weapon statlines completely.<br /> <br /> Attribute+Ability is your Withering attack, no Defense, successes steal Initative on a 1-for-1 basis.<br /> <br /> Decisives are vs Defense, Attribute+Ability to hit and Initative-Hardness dice in damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-21-2019, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T12:21:47-08:00","id":1356343,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I am not keen on weapons being entirely irrelevant, but they could just work on tags. And certainly there's no need to be adding and subtracting such large amounts, when a giant tetsubo could just be &quot;+1 damage if you have Strength 3+&quot; or something. (Having much lower damage from weapons would make Strength better)<br /> And if armour is just reducing decisive damage, it also can just be, say, -3 or something.<br /> <br /> I'm also not keen on the defender's stats having no effect whatsoever on Withering, though I do get that the idea is you attack back. The decisive looks fine. I also note there's no Stamina included, but maybe we can just... not have Stamina. You've still got Resistance against poison, fatigue, etc.<br /> <br /> I actually found that, after my initial surprise, the fact that armour is vs Withering and not Decisive actually makes sense (knock a knight around until you can get your dagger in his eye, bruise a man-at-arms by bashing his chainmail with your sword to tire him so you can stab him in the face). I don't think I would want armour to reduce damage from being stabbed in the face; the difference it's made there is the fact that it's much harder to stab someone in the face than the belly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T12:23:21-08:00","id":1356344,"title":"","content":"I would definitely like Withering attacks to be one roll though.<br /> <br /> Though not as much as I would like grapple to be one roll!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T12:24:21-08:00","id":1356345,"title":"","content":"Anyway, while I don't agree exactly with your suggestion, that kind of simpler set of rolls works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T13:36:25-08:00","id":1356363,"title":"","content":"Well, on the Discord they said there's still motes. But hopefully they can make the stuff you do with them simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T14:09:24-08:00","id":1356370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356343#post1356343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... I am not keen on weapons being entirely irrelevant</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> From a game balance point of view, I get that light, quick weapons should be more accurate and slow, heavy weapons should do more damage. I totally get the premise. But should a dagger be strictly, mechanically, BETTER than a tetsubo? I say &quot;no&quot;: the weapons should be balanced. So you can find a theorical tipping point where X Accuracy = Y Damage (which no Stoyteller game has ever managed), or you just accept that some weapons are better... or you make all weapons identical. And if they're identical... why add extra math?<br /> <br /> I'm not a massive fan of Tags. Why can't I Disarm someone with a sword? Or pin them to a wall? Why shouldn't a shield block a meteor hammer? Why can't I sweep someone's legs with my staff? <br /> <br /> If Essence is going to be a simpler game, make it simpler.<br /> <br /> The idea for no Defense on Withering is indeed that you just attack back. No Onslaught. No matter how skilled you are at combat, being attacked swings the combat against you. If you devote time and energy to parry or dodge out of the way, then you're losing Initative. A skilled opponent is going to turn that tide pretty quickly... once they fight back. But if they just continue to give ground, sooner or later that attacker is going to get their lucky hit in -- they're not going to knock the other guy out from dodging.<br /> <br /> As for armor, it is just as easy to feint, or get a near miss against a fully armored knight. It's just as easy to strike at their limbs or set them off balance. It is harder to get a death blow.<br /> <br /> 3E simulates this by making it harder to wrong-foot the knight, encouraging you to cut down the unarmored squire, making armored characters weaker the more allies they have. That's completely backwards. Knocking the knight around shouldn't take a penalty -- the face-stabbing, which is harder than belly-stabbing, is what should take the penalty. The dynamic ebb and flow of combat shouldn't slow to a crawl from armor... but armor should help stop you dying.<br /> <br /> You are still using Withering attacks to gain the advantage you need to land a killing blow. Armor still makes it harder for you, meaning you have to work to gain more advantage.<br /> <br /> I like mortal armor having a Hardness equal to its Mobility Penalty, and upping the penalty by 1: 1 for light, 2 for medium, 3 for heavy. I like Hardness 3/6/9 for artifact armor.<br /> <br /> Stamina as an Attribute can just go, maybe roll it into Strength and call it Constituion. I think Social could just be one Attribute. Maybe combine Perception and Wits (call it Wits, maybe Wisdom). I wouldn't be against folding the Attributes down to just three: Physical/Body, Social/Charisma, and Mental/Brain (have Solaroids/Deebs with 4/3/2 arrays, Lunars/Alchemicals with 5/3/3, Mortals on 3/2/1).<br /> <br /> If you wanted to keep the 9 Attributes, then have Decisive damage = (Initative+Strength)-(Hardness+Stamina), but make Withering attacks and Defense run off Dexterity+Ability. (Again, being stronger doesn't help you feint, and being tougher doesn't stop you getting wrong-footed: if these factors should be considered it's on Decisives, not Withering. A weaker character needs to build up more Initative to land a death blow.)<br /> <br /> That's just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-21-2019, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T14:20:45-08:00","id":1356373,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I don't think light, accurate weapons do need to be more accurate. They have the extremely strong advantage of being convenient to carry and use (especially your fists). I think it's fine for a dagger to have no stat modifications, a sword to have +1 damage, and a tetsubo to have +2 damage but it's two-handed and needs Strength 3*. I wouldn't give any weapons accuracy bonuses (or penalties) at all, just Dex+Melee is fine.<br /> <br /> *Or Brawn, or Constitution, or whatever. I can definitely see merging some attributes, and Vance implied there would be less stats. Stamina isn't really needed, as everything it represents can be done with other things; health levels, mote pools, Resistance.<br /> <br /> With tags I was thinking more that some weapons are better at, say, Disarming, or whatever, rather than you can't do it at all... Which is basically how 3rd ed works for the most part. I do see your point about simplification, but honestly, the weapon system (and armour) of 3rd ed is simplified, there's loads of stuff that needs to be simplified in Exalted but light/medium/heavy isn't a key area of complexity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-21-2019, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T17:50:54-08:00","id":1356405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356339#post1356339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can spend 4ph in an Instant without flaring. It's pretty trivial to pay 4ph+Xpp to prevent flare. I've not had any trouble doing so for high end Solar combat theory-crafts nor in my Deeb game..</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you could only draw from two different pools if you were emptying one of them, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T18:01:36-08:00","id":1356407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356405#post1356405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought you could only draw from two different pools if you were emptying one of them, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can draw from a different pool <i>per cost paid</i>. If activating a charm would require more motes than one pool has, you can empty that pool and take the rest from the other pool. <br /> So if I'm defending with +2 Parry from my Excellency and some other stuff, I can pay the Excellency from peripheral and the rest from personal and not flare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T19:04:10-08:00","id":1356412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356363#post1356363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, on the Discord they said there's still motes. But hopefully they can make the stuff you do with them simpler.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean to get rid of motes. But having fewer motes, and needing to spend fewer motes, sounds like a great idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356370#post1356370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a massive fan of Tags. Why can't I Disarm someone with a sword? Or pin them to a wall? Why shouldn't a shield block a meteor hammer? Why can't I sweep someone's legs with my staff?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Disarming tag just makes it easier to disarm. No tag models pinning something to a wall or sweeping legs. A shield can block a meteor hammer because you can still use one to apply your Parry against one, even if you can't turtle up behind the shield as easily because a flexible weapon can strike around corners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T19:11:32-08:00","id":1356413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356407#post1356407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can draw from a different pool <i>per cost paid</i>. If activating a charm would require more motes than one pool has, you can empty that pool and take the rest from the other pool. <br /> So if I'm defending with +2 Parry from my Excellency and some other stuff, I can pay the Excellency from peripheral and the rest from personal and not flare.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s weird that it\u2019s divorced from the grouping on anima raising. Or is it? Can you pay for a bunch of 4m charms with periph?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T01:20:23-08:00","id":1356453,"title":"","content":"If you simultaneously use two 4m charms both from peripheral, that'd be 8 peripheral so you'd flare anyway.<br /> <br /> This is something I am sure can be simplified massively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T02:53:02-08:00","id":1356458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356405#post1356405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought you could only draw from two different pools if you were emptying one of them, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. vwllss trnt prncss made the point nicely that it's per cost in that instant. You're not always going to have a nice 4m even spend.<br /> <br /> 2. I have SUPER been playing this wrong. I totally missed that rule. And the rule that mote regen always refills peripheral before personsal. My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T03:25:58-08:00","id":1356460,"title":"","content":"I do think that the two mote pools are a bit of an artefact from First Edition wearing its World of Darkness lineage a bit more on its sleeve. That core book reads to me as placing a good deal more emphasis on a tone of the returning Solar Exalted needing to keep a bit of a low profile, and that is the context in which I read the idea of choosing between a smaller more pool and one in which you risk giving yourself away with a Super Saiyan aura. Others (mostly Dragon Blooded) build on that foundation with novel takes on the dichotomy, but I think that was the fire concept.<br /> <br /> I like it as a bit of a legacy thing, and discretion undermined by anima banner is not without significance in the setting, but its definitely something I could see being trimmed in the interest of simplicity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T08:29:02-08:00","id":1356480,"title":"","content":"Basically agree with that, and to quote the relevant section<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Yet, they are hunted creatures. Regarded as akin to demon princes in many regions, the re-born Solars must live like shadows. Cosmic beings, they must work their plans among men subtly and walk unseen if they are able ... Thus goes the existence of the Solar Exalted - to wield the power of the Sun, but to do so with the greatest economy possible, showing their true might only when the need is great. Travelling the roads as mendicants, pilgrims and fugitives, they tread lightly and fight when they have no choice, or when their conscience compels them to ... Those Solars who wish to survive the maturity of their power must play a game of high and low - living as vagabonds, bandits and troubadours while they master their great power and learn the secrets of their Exalted state&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Of course, as resident one-note-all-1e-setting-upselling-all-the-time person I think that style of playing the &quot;Return of the Solars&quot; sounds pretty great - it's Tsubaki Sanjuro, it's Vash the Stampede, it's Ogami Itto, it's every mysterious drifter, marginal vagabond and ronin outsider with a past who rolls into town to get underestimated and to eventually show their real power and skill and every chosen one who has to hide their true power.<br /> <br /> But if that's not actually how the game is played these days, and actually games don't spend that much time in that and it's not what Exalted fans are really seeking from Exalted, in favour of a more &quot;I am the Bull Of The North! See me declare my rule!&quot; vibe and experience (or a bunch of other scenarios that inherently more open and challenging and immediately upsetting to the status quo), maybe that's something that can be simplified to reflect less focus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T09:50:45-08:00","id":1356491,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I think you can keep that idea (which I personally are quite happy with) while still having a simpler system than now.<br /> <br /> For example, if there's no mote regen outside of sleep/meditation, you can just have:<br /> A personal pool<br /> A peripheral pool<br /> As soon as you spend 1+ dots of peripheral essence in a scene your caste mark appears for a scene.<br /> Once you have spent 10 peripheral essence in a scene, you're surrounded by a huge bonfire of essence with an iconic image until the end of the scene, then it fades to a caste mark for 20 minutes.<br /> <br /> That doesn't seem very complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T10:39:20-08:00","id":1356498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356480#post1356480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if that's not actually how the game is played these days, and actually games don't spend that much time in that and it's not what Exalted fans are really seeking from Exalted, in favour of a more &quot;I am the Bull Of The North! See me declare my rule!&quot; vibe and experience (or a bunch of other scenarios that inherently more open and challenging and immediately upsetting to the status quo), maybe that's something that can be simplified to reflect less focus?</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that unfortunate for a lot of reasons, that and how many people just handwave or ignore limit break. Solars are the greatest and mightiest of the Exalted, with no real exception in any area. On the other hand they're also among the most hunted along with Lunars, and have the least support and are the least able to hide and flee intrinsically compared to any of the other celestial exalted.<br /> <br /> They also live in the shadow of a curse that twists their hearts. There may be a time when your general is sitting there weeping for his lost honor while his soldiers are being slain by the enemy, unable to bring himself to stand and defend them.<br /> <br /> They're both big things that you have to work with, and it frames the setting less as &quot;You've got all this power, who could stand against you?&quot; and more as &quot;Thank the Sun you have this power, without it you wouldn't stand a chance. Just make sure your passions don't turn you against yourself.&quot; Which is good, it makes the Solar games just more epic, with greater challenges and greater risks, without making it just like every other splat except easymode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T10:44:01-08:00","id":1356499,"title":"","content":"You could also cut down (keeping the personal/peripheral split or not) by having more of the bread-and-butter (esp. non-combat) Charms be indefinite with motes committed to them.<br /> <br /> That would let you have a bunch of Charms you keep running most of the time, and are more than enough boost to handle most situations, and then you bust out the bigger Charms and anima with them.<br /> <br /> So if there was a universal Excellency that you committed 4m (in the current math, less if motes are made more valuable in Essence), and you get +2 successes, and each splat gains a unique bonus, you're running around with 2-4 of these on, anima not an issue unless you activate them that scene, and you can generally get past at least mortal opponents by just being better than them. A fight breaks out and there's some combat in there, you basically have mote regen covered, and you can focus on spending stuff on your more potent Charms that will risk anima.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T13:12:35-08:00","id":1356521,"title":"","content":"Honestly, rather than having indefinite commitments, why not have loads of permanent low-power bread and butter effects? That'd be simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T13:28:56-08:00","id":1356524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356521#post1356521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, rather than having indefinite commitments, why not have loads of permanent low-power bread and butter effects? That'd be simpler.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of that concept, just because it generates a floor for Exalted that can make certain interactions difficult. It's like Infinite Ability Mastery all over again except it's not even scenelong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T13:31:34-08:00","id":1356525,"title":"","content":"It works for other games. And you pay 8xp for a Melee 4 warrior to get a permanent +1 on all Melee rolls.<br /> <br /> The thing about Infinite Ability Mastery is it gave you 8-10 extra dice. I'm talking about reducing a penalty by 1 or 2 dice, something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-22-2019, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T13:31:40-08:00","id":1356526,"title":"","content":"Something vaguely in the shape of Weapons of the Gods kung fu styles, but with Strength of Chi determined by Exalt type?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T13:32:45-08:00","id":1356528,"title":"","content":"It's ages since I read Weapons of the Gods, so I don't remember how that worked?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T14:56:48-08:00","id":1356536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356528#post1356528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's ages since I read Weapons of the Gods, so I don't remember how that worked?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strength of Chi was a bonus added to rolls based on Attributes, where 1-3 gave a +5 roll bonus, 4-6 gave a +10, etc. Not every technique used SoC, but it was quite common to see as a buff, and I could see Exalted making it more about the type of being since it's less about individual cultivation than what order of power you are a lot of the time. Some other universal mechanics could be tiered that way as well, or else made uniform, like supernatural balancing acts, acrobatics, or weightlessness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T19:04:39-08:00","id":1356568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356521#post1356521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, rather than having indefinite commitments, why not have loads of permanent low-power bread and butter effects? That'd be simpler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> One advantage to the committed approach is that you only have to remember a few Charms most of the time (even if you can swap load outs in down time easily).<br /> <br /> If they're all perm. Charms instead, they're all on all the time, and you have to remember all of them that might be relevant to any given situation.<br /> <br /> So committed has less simple in bookkeeping, but also more simple on cognitive load as more come up at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T22:05:56-08:00","id":1356591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356316#post1356316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've felt the same way for years.<br /> <br /> Motes are well-named, because they're so damn SMALL. One mote is so insignificant. But there are SO MANY of the little, insignificant things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, unfortunately Ex3 was trying to cover all the bases and appeal to 2e players who don't want their characters to be nerfed. So most mote pools are on a par with maximum willpower and virtues but I don't think anyone ever looked at those numbers and said &quot;is this necessary?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T02:05:50-08:00","id":1356608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356568#post1356568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> One advantage to the committed approach is that you only have to remember a few Charms most of the time (even if you can swap load outs in down time easily).<br /> <br /> If they're all perm. Charms instead, they're all on all the time, and you have to remember all of them that might be relevant to any given situation.<br /> <br /> So committed has less simple in bookkeeping, but also more simple on cognitive load as more come up at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point, but in my experience people want to commit every charm relevant to the situation if possible, so I don't think it makes a difference. If people think they're going into a combat situation, they'll commit all their combat charms, etc.<br /> <br /> And then sometimes they won't have them on, and will have to recalculate their pools or whatever without those charms.<br /> <br /> Also, the load-out system doesn't fit the genre of most Exalt types.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd be quite happy if there's no commitment at all, it'd make it simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-23-2019, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T02:20:49-08:00","id":1356610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356591#post1356591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, unfortunately Ex3 was trying to cover all the bases and appeal to 2e players who don't want their characters to be nerfed. So most mote pools are on a par with maximum willpower and virtues but I don't think anyone ever looked at those numbers and said &quot;is this necessary?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have no particular problem with, say, a mote pool of 10 and most charms costing 1, or something, but I don't really mind the current amount of motes. 34-7 or 42-6 or whatever isn't a difficult sum. It's the amount of different resources and penalties to keep track of, and the number of different sums you have to do during an attack, that causes mistakes. Each particular sum is individually very easy.<br /> <br /> I do very much approve of dropping assumptions though, and not feeling beholden to previous rulesets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-23-2019, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T03:05:49-08:00","id":1356611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356608#post1356608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point, but in my experience people want to commit every charm relevant to the situation if possible, so I don't think it makes a difference. If people think they're going into a combat situation, they'll commit all their combat charms, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if you're assuming too much of a lack of change from other parts of the current systems, or not actually understanding what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> If you're committing half your motes, and there's no more combat mote regen, you might have a lot of +X to your rolls, you've significantly limited your pool to toss around better Charms that do more impactful effects. As well, the idea is to cut down on options so there's not so much energy and time spent on weighing them. No more, &quot;I regen 5m, so I going to spend 1 on this Charm, 2 on this Charm, and 2 on my Excellency,&quot; because that's at lot harder for more people to juggle than, &quot;+X to the following Skill rolls.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the load-out system doesn't fit the genre of most Exalt types. </div> </div> </div>It's not a literal load out like Alchemicals. It's what all Exalts already do with committed motes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I'd be quite happy if there's no commitment at all, it'd make it simpler. </div> </div> </div>Again though, there's different forms of simplicity. Making every Charm permanent would remove the entire need for motes and make it simpler to not have to track them. But now anima is going to be harder to work into the game, and Charms themselves didn't actually get mechanically simpler to use in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T04:09:28-08:00","id":1356614,"title":"","content":"I don't think every charm should be permanent, just the bread-and-butter ideas. Reducing surprise penalties, not perfect dodges. Increasing punch damage a bit, not doing your signature comet throw.<br /> <br /> For example, a Dodge tree might look like this:<br /> <br /> Spend motes, get + 2 Evasion.<br /> When enemies miss you, they lose 1 initiative.<br /> When enemies miss you, you gain 1 initiative.<br /> Reduce penalties by 1.<br /> Spend motes, perfect dodge. 1/scene. Solars and Abyssals only.<br /> +1 Evasion. Solars and Abyssals only.<br /> If enemies miss, spend motes, enemy takes fire damage. Dragonblood only.<br /> Spend motes, make a roll. If you succeed, you were never there. Sidereals only.<br /> <br /> That's just a quick example, but I hope it explains it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T06:36:18-08:00","id":1356635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356536#post1356536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength of Chi was a bonus added to rolls based on Attributes, where 1-3 gave a +5 roll bonus, 4-6 gave a +10, etc. Not every technique used SoC, but it was quite common to see as a buff, and I could see Exalted making it more about the type of being since it's less about individual cultivation than what order of power you are a lot of the time. Some other universal mechanics could be tiered that way as well, or else made uniform, like supernatural balancing acts, acrobatics, or weightlessness.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of little ways you can establish power tiers, even in a system where all things are equal. I think the Mastery/Terrestrial or Resonant/Dissonant keywords in Ex3's Martial Arts are a good start, since they give you three levels of power stratification in one Charm. That said, I think one of the nice things about Ex3 is that Dragon-Blooded need to be taken seriously on an individual level - I've seen lucky and well-built DBs who go for the kill beat unfocused, unlucky, and un-serious Solars with some regularity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T07:34:05-08:00","id":1356642,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Terrestrial/Mastery could easily be spread out to a more varied set of Universal charms, though if the goal is making the game simpler, I'd prefer if generally power tiers are split by unique charms and differences in pools and ratings. It's kind of a hassle when a lot of your charms have a paragraph atthe end that edits what it says above, rather than just a nice straightforward explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T09:22:36-08:00","id":1356656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356610#post1356610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have no particular problem with, say, a mote pool of 10 and most charms costing 1, or something, but I don't really mind the current amount of motes. 34-7 or 42-6 or whatever isn't a difficult sum. It's the amount of different resources and penalties to keep track of, and the number of different sums you have to do during an attack, that causes mistakes. Each particular sum is individually very easy.<br /> <br /> I do very much approve of dropping assumptions though, and not feeling beholden to previous rulesets.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main area I've seen people struggle with their mote pools is when extra action charms come into play and are used in conjunction with other charms. If you're not using a spreadsheet it's not impossible to miss data and be way off on your mote expenditure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T13:50:47-08:00","id":1356685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356656#post1356656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main area I've seen people struggle with their mote pools is when extra action charms come into play and are used in conjunction with other charms. If you're not using a spreadsheet it's not impossible to miss data and be way off on your mote expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I ran again, I'd get two colors of plastic beads and force people to print charm cards.<br /> When you spend Essence, you do so by putting the beads on the cards. When a Charm ends, you put the beads in the &quot;discard&quot; bowl. At the end of your turn, you take five beads from the &quot;discard&quot; bowl.<br /> Physical manipulation works wonders for memory, though it comes at a cost to execution speed.<br /> <br /> The other thing I've considered is color-coded dice to help with pools and caps. Have a color for Ability dice, a similar color for Specialty dice, a color for Attribute dice, Equipment dice, Stunt dice. Have two more colors for Charm dice, similar to but distinct from Ability and Attribute dice.<br /> So when Sam Solar wants to know what his die cap is, I can point to the number of Ability and Attribute dice he has and his bowl of Charm dice and tell him to match colors. This would also let me use the Stunt dice as a physical reminder of &quot;Hey you! Stunt that roll!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T13:58:00-08:00","id":1356687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356642#post1356642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Terrestrial/Mastery could easily be spread out to a more varied set of Universal charms, though if the goal is making the game simpler, I'd prefer if generally power tiers are split by unique charms and differences in pools and ratings. It's kind of a hassle when a lot of your charms have a paragraph atthe end that edits what it says above, rather than just a nice straightforward explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could also be a matter of affixing a special effect by Exalt instead of a straight-up bonus (though Solars have typically been presented as having a bonus as their special effect). In any case, I would be expecting a body of mostly fixed-cost effects in a chain that notes a required Ability or Attribute (or whatever base stats there are), as basing powers on Attributes and Abilities is kind of Exalted's thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T14:19:42-08:00","id":1356693,"title":"","content":"Is there anything wrong with using BESM's &quot;Tri-Stat&quot; system? Body, Mind, Spirit, with Spirit being your raw social charisma, and any granularity or specificity being determined by your Abilities/Skills/Merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T15:51:21-08:00","id":1356709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356693#post1356693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything wrong with using BESM's &quot;Tri-Stat&quot; system? Body, Mind, Spirit, with Spirit being your raw social charisma, and any granularity or specificity being determined by your Abilities/Skills/Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with BESM, but I could see a compression of Attributes working.<br /> Heck, I could see a total switch over to Attributes of Physical, Social, Mental and Abilities of Dawn, Night, Zenith, Twilight, Midnight. Then move Specialties up to the old granularity level and you'd have a pretty decent framework for a simplified Attribute+Ability system.<br /> You'd be mostly abandoning character granularity at the mortal level, but you could shift character distinction over to Charms and probably get away fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","user":"vwllss trnt prncss","date":". 12-23-2019, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T16:36:54-08:00","id":1356720,"title":"","content":"As I've said before, I don't think it's a problem to reduce the number of Attributes and Abilities, but I also don't think it's necessary (with the exception of Craft abilities and maybe Martial Arts). Essentially, I just don't think that the Attributes+Abilities are the complicated part of the system, except in a few cases where they're not well-defined. I'm willing to lose granularity for simplicity, but I think this is one that's not greatly necessary. A bit of a reduction is fine, but not too much.<br /> I'd probably have 5-7 Attributes and 10-20 Abilities. 3 Attributes I think would not be enough, as you couldn't have a big strong dude or small quick one. <br /> <br /> Whereas I'm quite happy to see the number of charms reduced massively: my characters have an average of about 40 charms, and I'd be quite happy with 10-15 if they were balanced accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T00:18:03-08:00","id":1356765,"title":"","content":"Reducing Attributes makes the idea of Attribute based Exalted pretty much impossible to execute. We could debate the value of Attribute based Exalts, but in terms of keeping things distinct, it makes it easier if we're going to have ten types of Exalted (albeit 3/10 are Solar based).<br /> <br /> Reducing Abilities is a bit easier. As 3e Solars show, the 5 by 5 paradigm really isn't necessary. If you cut the Abilities to 20, and each Caste/Aspect of Ability based Exalt pick 4 Caste Abilities from 6 of them, I don't think it would be a significant issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T00:49:57-08:00","id":1356768,"title":"","content":"It's easy enough to compress combat Abilities. Melee really means any chaotic fight; it's similar in meaning to 'fray', 'skirmish' or 'scrimmage'. (Heck, Thesaurus.com even suggests 'brawl'.) Splitting it into armed and unarmed isn't really necessary.<br /> <br /> You could, therefore, easily have one close combat skill (Melee) and one ranged combat skill (Ballistics). Athletics could cover Thrown and general evasion, while Melee could cover parry and block actions. That means you've got a fairly narrow set of skills for use in combat.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts styles are like Charms anyway, so you could just use Melee + a Martial Arts Specialty to act as gatekeepers to the Martial Arts styles. Likewise, you might put more fancy weapons behind a Martial/Exotic Weapons Speciality or similar, so that everyone can use knives but experts get to use the special stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T00:56:40-08:00","id":1356769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356765#post1356765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reducing Attributes makes the idea of Attribute based Exalted pretty much impossible to execute.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could do it just fine. Full Moon gets Physical as Caste Attribute, Changing Moon gets Social, New Moon gets Mental. Then lay out sensible Charm trees so you don't get people picking up an E4 &quot;Intelligence&quot; charm without any other &quot;Intelligence&quot; charms and you'll have shifted distinction over to Charm choice instead of dot distribution. <br /> <br /> And heck, you could bring back some of the dot-level customization by allowing Attribute Specialties. They'd have to be a bit more expensive if you wanted old-Attributes to be valid Specialties, but it should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T01:19:11-08:00","id":1356771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356685#post1356685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I ran again, I'd get two colors of plastic beads and force people to print charm cards.<br /> When you spend Essence, you do so by putting the beads on the cards. When a Charm ends, you put the beads in the &quot;discard&quot; bowl. At the end of your turn, you take five beads from the &quot;discard&quot; bowl.<br /> Physical manipulation works wonders for memory, though it comes at a cost to execution speed.<br /> <br /> The other thing I've considered is color-coded dice to help with pools and caps. Have a color for Ability dice, a similar color for Specialty dice, a color for Attribute dice, Equipment dice, Stunt dice. Have two more colors for Charm dice, similar to but distinct from Ability and Attribute dice.<br /> So when Sam Solar wants to know what his die cap is, I can point to the number of Ability and Attribute dice he has and his bowl of Charm dice and tell him to match colors. This would also let me use the Stunt dice as a physical reminder of &quot;Hey you! Stunt that roll!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's when I run online that this troubles me the most.<br /> Since for my own sanity I trust people to manage their own character sheet resources (essence, willpower, health levels) until they do something that makes me stop, do the mental arithmetic based on the last couple of rounds and go &quot;wait, what the fuck?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T01:57:41-08:00","id":1356776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356769#post1356769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you could do it just fine. Full Moon gets Physical as Caste Attribute, Changing Moon gets Social, New Moon gets Mental. Then lay out sensible Charm trees so you don't get people picking up an E4 &quot;Intelligence&quot; charm without any other &quot;Intelligence&quot; charms and you'll have shifted distinction over to Charm choice instead of dot distribution.<br /> <br /> And heck, you could bring back some of the dot-level customization by allowing Attribute Specialties. They'd have to be a bit more expensive if you wanted old-Attributes to be valid Specialties, but it should work.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, that only works if everyone's a Lunar/Lunar knock off. What about an Exigent that favors Strength/Charisma/Intelligence as the chosen of a god of direct personal power?<br /> <br /> If each of the original nine Attributes becomes a specialty, and one you could take multiple times... than what's even the point?<br /> <br /> This is also skipping how hard it is to make &quot;sensible&quot; Charms with just three traits to base them on.<br /> <br /> If the end result is basically no different than having the nine original Attributes, but they're all set at the same level within the same category, the loss of customization is much greater than the gain in simplicity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T02:22:32-08:00","id":1356781,"title":"","content":"Also, even for Lunars, every single Full Moon has Body 5, every Changing Moon has Social 5, every No Moon has Mind 5. Duuuul.<br /> Whereas in my current game both Full Moons have Strength 5 and Dex 2, the other combat character had 4 in all physical attributes, one Changing Moon had Appearance 5 while the other had... 1 I think?<br /> <br /> If the Attributes were really complex and confusing, sure, but they're one of the easier parts for most players.<br /> The fact that, say, the Full Moon has a different Strength and Dex is fine. What's confusing is the rules for turning into an Aurochs, the way some charms change effect when he does, and most of all his grapple charms (though more because of the base grapple rules than the charms).<br /> <br /> Anyway. I think you can go with, say, Brawn/Dexterity/Charisma/Manipulation/Intelligence/Wits, or whatever, but I wouldn't want to go down to 3.<br /> <br /> Just like I wouldn't want to go down to 5 abilities. That'd be, what, Combat/Social/Knowledge/Athletics/Craft? Eh, it doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... <br /> Close Combat<br /> Ranged Combat<br /> War<br /> Athletics<br /> Integrity<br /> Presence<br /> Resistance<br /> Survival<br /> Craft<br /> Investigation<br /> Knowledge<br /> Dodge<br /> Larceny<br /> Stealth<br /> Travel<br /> Socialise<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Yeah, besides combat and a few others, that's still quite tricky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T02:25:24-08:00","id":1356782,"title":"","content":"No, what needs simplifying is the rulesets (Combat, Social, Craft, definitely movement) and the charms: simpler, less of them, less combinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T02:42:32-08:00","id":1356785,"title":"","content":"I don't know about 3/5 for Att and Abl but I've seen a few conversions that go 6/15 or 6/10 and seem to have enough space to express things. It depends a bit on whether E:E is leaning as heavily on these to express characters anyway I guess. I'm not sure that the stats need huge simplification though, unless it removes confusion about what to apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T02:42:45-08:00","id":1356786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356771#post1356771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's when I run online that this troubles me the most.<br /> Since for my own sanity I trust people to manage their own character sheet resources (essence, willpower, health levels) until they do something that makes me stop, do the mental arithmetic based on the last couple of rounds and go &quot;wait, what the fuck?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find this with those, but I often find it with dice pools, especially when the players are shapeshifted.<br /> Personally, I tend to make mistakes with forgetting the NPC's wound penalties and Overwhelming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-24-2019, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T02:54:01-08:00","id":1356787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356771#post1356771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's when I run online that this troubles me the most.<br /> Since for my own sanity I trust people to manage their own character sheet resources (essence, willpower, health levels) until they do something that makes me stop, do the mental arithmetic based on the last couple of rounds and go &quot;wait, what the fuck?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are web applications for it (Game-Playing Arete or something?) but fundamentally no trick is going to fix the person who isn't doing their work. I really empathize with your situation, my current Champions group has a player who has been flaking on getting his character sheet to the GM for months now. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356776#post1356776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First off, that only works if everyone's a Lunar/Lunar knock off. What about an Exigent that favors Strength/Charisma/Intelligence as the chosen of a god of direct personal power?<br /> <br /> If each of the original nine Attributes becomes a specialty, and one you could take multiple times... than what's even the point?<br /> <br /> This is also skipping how hard it is to make &quot;sensible&quot; Charms with just three traits to base them on.<br /> <br /> If the end result is basically no different than having the nine original Attributes, but they're all set at the same level within the same category, the loss of customization is much greater than the gain in simplicity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homebrew will require homebrew. Sarcastic tautologies aside, I'd express that favoring by providing a (second) Excellency that only applied to appropriate tasks. Then I'd follow that up with tightly focused charms. And as an Exigent, they'd only have favored charms so there'd be no need to worry about XP cost differences. End result would be immediate mechanical benefits for playing to theme and benefits similar to old-Attribute specialization. <br /> <br /> What would the point of any reduction in quantity of anything be? <br /> <br /> I don't see why charm design would have to change for anything but combat Abilities. The current Abilities/Attributes could easily exist as thematically distinct sets of trees. <br /> <br /> I think I need to clarify that I'm arguing this <i>can</i> be done and still work, not that it <i>should</i> be done. As The Wizard of Oz mentions, the 9+25 spread is not a big driver of complexity and the only issues it causes are the Dawn Problem and when the lines aren't clearly drawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T04:06:52-08:00","id":1356790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356781#post1356781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, even for Lunars, every single Full Moon has Body 5, every Changing Moon has Social 5, every No Moon has Mind 5. Duuuul.<br /> Whereas in my current game both Full Moons have Strength 5 and Dex 2, the other combat character had 4 in all physical attributes, one Changing Moon had Appearance 5 while the other had... 1 I think?<br /> <br /> If the Attributes were really complex and confusing, sure, but they're one of the easier parts for most players.<br /> The fact that, say, the Full Moon has a different Strength and Dex is fine. What's confusing is the rules for turning into an Aurochs, the way some charms change effect when he does, and most of all his grapple charms (though more because of the base grapple rules than the charms).<br /> <br /> Anyway. I think you can go with, say, Brawn/Dexterity/Charisma/Manipulation/Intelligence/Wits, or whatever, but I wouldn't want to go down to 3.<br /> <br /> Just like I wouldn't want to go down to 5 abilities. That'd be, what, Combat/Social/Knowledge/Athletics/Craft? Eh, it doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... <br /> Close Combat<br /> Ranged Combat<br /> War<br /> Athletics<br /> Integrity<br /> Presence<br /> Resistance<br /> Survival<br /> Craft<br /> Investigation<br /> Knowledge<br /> Dodge<br /> Larceny<br /> Stealth<br /> Travel<br /> Socialise<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Yeah, besides combat and a few others, that's still quite tricky.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably go with:<br /> <br /> Melee<br /> Ballistics<br /> Athletics (incorporating most of Dodge and all of Thrown)<br /> Integrity<br /> Command (incorporating Presence and intimidation)<br /> Socialise<br /> Resistance<br /> Survival<br /> Awareness (incorporating Alertness)<br /> Talent (artistic, pick one type)<br /> Skill (such as manual skills, pick one type)<br /> Medicine (includes making of)<br /> Investigation<br /> Larceny<br /> Stealth<br /> Empathy<br /> Linguistics (each extra language is a specialty; this is general fluency, discursive skills, etc)<br /> Knowledge (pick one, e.g., Realm Culture, Bureaucracy, Occult, etc)<br /> <br /> They split roughly into six groups of three, so you could have each Caste get three plus a choice of two others (e.g., the three combat skills plus two others).<br /> <br /> You could probably drop Linguistics (nest it under Knowledge), Empathy (fold into Socialise) and Integrity (fold into Command, since it's harder to control domineering personalities). Then you'd neatly have five groups of three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T06:12:41-08:00","id":1356797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356787#post1356787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there are web applications for it (Game-Playing Arete or something?) but fundamentally no trick is going to fix the person who isn't doing their work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less that they're avoiding doing what they're supposed to, more making mistakes because there's a lot going on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> What would the point of any reduction in quantity of anything be?<br /> I think I need to clarify that I'm arguing this <i>can</i> be done and still work, not that it <i>should</i> be done. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, same here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T06:16:13-08:00","id":1356798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356720#post1356720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 Attributes I think would not be enough, as you couldn't have a big strong dude or small quick one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whilst most of what I wanted to say has been said by others, I just wanted to address this real quick.<br /> <br /> This is a lot like saying you can't have a character with red hair, or a D-cup, or a scar on your chest.<br /> <br /> I don't think that if two characters are equally invested in combat that the small, quick chatacter should have an advantage compared to the big, strong dude. I think they should be equally effective for equal investment. So why not represent it in a way which is mechanically identical but narrated differently?<br /> <br /> This is a matter of narration, flavor, fluff.<br /> <br /> Attributes and Abilities are the foundation of the complexity. The reason dice caps in animal forms is so difficult is because you're matching up all your Attribute/Ability combos with all the animal form's QC pools. By reducing the possible combinations, you reduce the number of things to keep track of.<br /> <br /> I'd fully back:<br /> <br /> Body/Charisma/Mind<br /> <br /> Combat (all five combat abilities and War)<br /> Athletics (including Resistance and Dodge)<br /> Presence (including Performance and Integrity)<br /> Larceny (including Investigation, Socailize, Stealth)<br /> Lore (including Craft, Medicine, Occult and Linguistics)<br /> <br /> Specialities are still capped at 1 extra die, but become as broad as the old Abilities (so you could take a Combat specialty in &quot;Archery&quot; for example). Lunars can buy specialties in the old Attributes.<br /> <br /> Simplified Charms and mote pools.<br /> <br /> Divide all mote pools/costs by 5 and have different effects based on whether you use Personal or Peripheral Essence.<br /> <br /> For example, all Exalted get a generic 2nd Excellency style power they can use on any roll. Spend 1m to get bonus successes on a roll. If you spend Personal motes you gain (Ability) extra successes for Solars and Deebs, or (Attribute) extra successes for Lunars. Spend 1m Peripheral and your Anima goes up one level and you gain (Attribute+Ability) extra successes for Solars and Lunars or (Attribute+1) extra successes for Deebs. This would be the only dice adder Charm in the game. All other Charms would do something -- like let you Craft without tools or banish a weapon Elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-24-2019, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T06:20:59-08:00","id":1356799,"title":"","content":"So, one thing about Abilities, is that some Abilities are generally more useful than others. Melee vs Sail, for example. Or Presence vs Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, some of the easiest ones to merge are the more useful ones (Melee/Brawl, Presence/Performance). Which could mean merging them together ends up with everyone putting max points into, say, Melee and Social, and Survival and Sail or whatever get left behind.<br /> <br /> Ideally, it's things like Linguistics, Bureaucracy, Sail, Ride, Survival, Larceny, etc, that you want incorporated into wider abilities while you can actually leave Brawl and Melee seperate. Not that you have to, but balance wise that'd be better than combining Melee/Brawl and Presence/Performance.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T06:36:22-08:00","id":1356800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356798#post1356798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think that if two characters are equally invested in combat that the small, quick chatacter should have an advantage compared to the big, strong dude. I think they should be equally effective for equal investment. So why not represent it in a way which is mechanically identical but narrated differently?</div> </div> </div> </div>Combat is fine, but at that point why even have an Attribute+Ability? Why not just have a combat stat?<br /> The point is that the strong tough dude is great at Athletics rolls to lift heavy objects, or drink tons of booze, but he's rubbish at dancing or needlework or dodging a falling boulder.<br /> <br /> Again, as I said, I don't think it's impossible to reduce the attributes/abilities, I wouldn't mind reducing them a bit (especially Craft!) but I don't really see any benefit to reducing them massively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attributes and Abilities are the foundation of the complexity. The reason dice caps in animal forms is so difficult is because you're matching up all your Attribute/Ability combos with all the animal form's QC pools. </div> </div> </div>Not really, as most of the time it's literally using their Dexterity+Brawl that confuses my players. It's their accuracy that applies or doesn't apply, successes from merits, stunts adding more to the cap, etc. In your example (I'm fine with the categories you've given, incidentally, I just don't see a great need for it) you'd still have those issues (unless you removed them of course, but that's a seperate thing). Body+Combat instead of Dex+Brawl to attack, Body+Athletics for resisting poison, Mind+something for awareness, Body+Larceny for stealth.<br /> <br /> 2nd ed animal rules never confused my players. Werewolf shapeshifting was never a problem. And they had just as many Ability+Attributes.<br /> <br /> No, it'd be fine if it was &quot;In Bear form, get +1 Strength and Stamina and on smelling rolls. In snake form, get +1 on stealth rolls and a poison bite.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've recently started running Vampire and Mage for my DnD group, who've never played a White Wolf game before. They've grasped the Attribute+Ability system easily, with its combinations, no problems beyond a few poorly-defined Abilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simplified Charms </div> </div> </div>Now this is the key thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and mote pools. </div> </div> </div>This too, but it's not the mote pools themselves that get awkward, it's mote pools+regen+anima+initiative+wound penalties+overwhelming+willpower+etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This would be the only dice adder Charm in the game. All other Charms would do something -- like let you Craft without tools or banish a weapon Elsewhere. </div> </div> </div>Oh please yes, I'm fed up of a million dice adders. Stick to one.<br /> (Although your example is way too powerful in terms of number of successes on a roll. I'm happy with the idea that it does more if you flare your anima, although at that point why bother having Personal and Peripheral? Just the &quot;flare one level, get more dice/successes&quot; is fine.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-24-2019, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T07:09:22-08:00","id":1356803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356800#post1356800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh please yes, I'm fed up of a million dice adders. Stick to one.<br /> (Although your example is way too powerful in terms of number of successes on a roll. I'm happy with the idea that it does more if you flare your anima, although at that point why bother having Personal and Peripheral? Just the &quot;flare one level, get more dice/successes&quot; is fine.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My feeling is that whilst this dice adder is waaay more powerful than the current baseline, once you take out the granularity of being able to spend the exact number of motes you need from a larger pool, AND the power of combos (double 7s, reroll 1s and 6s, 10s explode, each 7/8/9 run adds a success, +1 non-Charm die)... it probably balances if it's the only dice adder.<br /> <br /> Definitely love your idea of a single mote pool though.<br /> <br /> I definitely want it adding successes. Rolling buckets of 20-40 dice loses its appeal real fast. You could always just make it, say, 1 success for 1m or (Ability) successes for 1m 1a ((Attribute) successes for Lunars).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-24-2019, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T07:55:37-08:00","id":1356805,"title":"","content":"If it's like, add 2 dice, it's fine, if it's add 10 then yeah.<br /> It works for Warhammer, but not for an rpg.<br /> <br /> In terms of adding a whole bunch of successes... Hmm...<br /> <br /> So the issue with all the re-rolls, doubles, etc, is they're multiple charms, not one. I think it would be dull if every Solar can add multiple successes to every roll at character gen. Maybe it works if many other things change.<br /> Or do what many other systems do; it adds one success, you can upgrade it multiple times for more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T08:42:22-08:00","id":1356806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356786#post1356786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't find this with those, but I often find it with dice pools, especially when the players are shapeshifted.</div> </div> </div> </div> Would you actually know if one of your players was spending the wrong number of motes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356787#post1356787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there are web applications for it (Game-Playing Arete or something?) but fundamentally no trick is going to fix the person who isn't doing their work. I really empathize with your situation, my current Champions group has a player who has been flaking on getting his character sheet to the GM for months now.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks. It doesn't seem to be a problem with anyone in the current group, but good to know tools and resources are out there. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T10:25:18-08:00","id":1356817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356806#post1356806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would you actually know if one of your players was spending the wrong number of motes?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T11:42:51-08:00","id":1356830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356787#post1356787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I need to clarify that I'm arguing this <i>can</i> be done and still work, not that it <i>should</i> be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can homebrew Exalted into the most mechanically simple thing possible: freefrom acting.<br /> <br /> There's a point where, &quot;I'm just saying what 'can' be done,&quot; isn't fruitful for an actual discussion. We can do anything with the game we're willing to put the time and energy into. What should be done matters to having an actual talk about these things. Otherwise it's just throwing ideas at a dart board and not even caring what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T12:10:55-08:00","id":1356836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356830#post1356830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can homebrew Exalted into the most mechanically simple thing possible: freefrom acting.<br /> <br /> There's a point where, &amp;quot;I'm just saying what 'can' be done,&amp;quot; isn't fruitful for an actual discussion. We can do anything with the game we're willing to put the time and energy into. What should be done matters to having an actual talk about these things. Otherwise it's just throwing ideas at a dart board and not even caring what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are any of us writers, playtesters, devs... or... anyone with any influence over the gameline? Like... at all?<br /> <br /> We're just fans spitballing what a simplified Exalted could look like given the limited information those in the know have provided. We know freeform acting doesn't fit with what the devs have leaked/teased. So...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T12:41:41-08:00","id":1356842,"title":"","content":"We know that reducing it to three Attributes and five Abilities doesn't fit with what the devs have leaked/teased either.<br /> <br /> So... now what?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T13:15:27-08:00","id":1356847,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... Do we? Vance hinted they'll reduce it, but not by how much. Maybe it's by a little, maybe a lot.<br /> <br /> Saying this, I think we've probably said all there is to say about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-24-2019, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T23:59:13-08:00","id":1356992,"title":"","content":"So, are there any parts of the ruleset that you think should be kept (even if changed a bit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T06:00:33-08:00","id":1357034,"title":"","content":"The idea of debilitaring attacks (which I hope are just called attacks) and finishing strikes is worth keeping IMO. <br /> <br /> BTW, does anyone remember the First Edition's quickstart? Ir had the simplest Exalted system ever. It was a bit &quot;too simple&quot; but I tried it once and fights were kinda fin actually (although, we had to do a fast and easy homebrew).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T07:52:40-08:00","id":1357049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356992#post1356992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are there any parts of the ruleset that you think should be kept (even if changed a bit).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Castes/Aspects as is. Not too complex but pretty diverse.<br /> I like the Merit system as is. I don't think that needs too much tidying up.<br /> I like the Sail rules (I'm not convinced that Sail needs to be its own Ability, but I like the look of the subsystem).<br /> I think the Social rules are pretty much perfect. (Maybe needs a rule about how quickly you can strengthen an Intimacy.)<br /> Definitely want the &quot;Skip It&quot; combat sidebar.<br /> Golden/Oracalcum rule (could be one rule but whatever).<br /> I think the Red Rule needs serious revision. It should stay, absolutely, but needs to be rephrased into a rule about not making the other players uncomfortable rather than a sex thing (and if it stays a sex thing it should be the Blue Rule). A player who was physically abused by their parents is way more entitled to an opt-out than a power-gamer who just doesn't want their character influenced: the Red Rule as written serves the latter not the former. It doesn't really need to be more specific than &quot;Don't be an ass. Respect other people's boundaries.&quot; Traditionally this has been in the Storytelling Chapter.<br /> <br /> I like the sex charms. I've said repeatedly that I don't think they're appropriate for the Corebook and should have been in a seperate AO supplement... but I don't think EE is going to get very many supplements. If there was any will from OP to make an AO supplement for Exalted, I'd say nuke the sex charms from orbit for EE (making it more accessible) but include EE rules in the 3E AO supplement... But I don't think we're ever going to see an AO Exalted supplement, and it would be a shame if EE didn't support mature themes and adult plotlines. I'm on the fence on this, I guess.<br /> <br /> I like Evocations. I'd like to see them dramatically simplified for EE, but they've become an important part of the game.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Withering/Decisive attacks and Initative/Momentum. I don't like 3E's execution but I hope it stays in EE in a simplified form.<br /> <br /> I think that covers my thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-26-2019, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T10:33:47-08:00","id":1357215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1356806#post1356806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. It doesn't seem to be a problem with anyone in the current group, but good to know tools and resources are out there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they are referring to <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T11:03:08-08:00","id":1357220,"title":"","content":"I'm familiar with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T04:00:55-08:00","id":1357338,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that the Red Rule isn't an X card so much as an attempt to keep sex and seduction a part of the game without the worst kind of powergamers ruining it. It's less there to be invoked and more there to deter the kind of person who sees this kind of veto as totally arbitrary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T04:41:52-08:00","id":1357343,"title":"","content":"Social rules I think could do with simplification, as people often forget the values of intimacies for/against, when you can't spend willpower, little details like that. But the basic ideas I think are pretty good. It can sometimes feel like it's just &quot;roll dice, strip willpower&quot; but I think there's not a great deal around that.<br /> Though if Willpower is gone (because in combat it is yet more book-keeping) I don't know what they would do.<br /> <br /> Evocations are a good concept for the game, but might be tricky to simplify, or rather, it might be tricky to write multiple charmsets for all those artefacts and fit them in to a book with 10 exalt types, sorcery, martial arts, etc. But that depends on how complex charms are anyway. <br /> <br /> I thought the sailing system looked kind of interesting (haven't used it), but DrLoveMonkey said in practice he didn't find it to be, it was just roll-off, roll-off, Solar wins. That might be a Solar charms things though, rather than a sail thing.<br /> <br /> I don't like Castes (I like Aspects, though there's never been a simple way to do inter-element stuff with DBs: presumably that's an obvious aim for the writers of Essence though) but I know I am in the minority. Simpler ways of doing them might reduce my objections to them anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T13:38:10-08:00","id":1357399,"title":"","content":"I think it could be possible to do Castes/Aspects without favoring Traits and therefore needing easily-divisible numbers of traits. Or at least so many of them.<br /> <br /> If crafting swords is simplified into an Intelligence + Melee roll, then gating certain crafting projects (especially Artifacts) off could be done with Merits.<br /> <br /> If Sailing rolls don\u2019t come up often enough, Sailing might also require a Merit that is numerically rated and rolled like an Ability, while being far cheaper than an Ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T15:29:35-08:00","id":1357419,"title":"","content":"From the Discord;<br /> <br /> Since you want to know about Charms:<br /> As the podcast explained, Universal Charms reduce overlap. Evocations and Martial Arts are types of Universal Charms.<br /> Universal Charms have Modes.<br /> Each Exalt Type will also have unique Charms. No one type has more words assigned than another - no matter what we joke about. <br /> Charms will have a new format that saves word count.<br /> Charms that are &quot;the Charm before it but better&quot; or &quot;the Charm before it but higher Essence&quot; will be condensed into one Charm that can be repurchased or self-upgrades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T16:47:23-08:00","id":1357426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357399#post1357399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it could be possible to do Castes/Aspects without favoring Traits and therefore needing easily-divisible numbers of traits. Or at least so many of them.<br /> <br /> If crafting swords is simplified into an Intelligence + Melee roll, then gating certain crafting projects (especially Artifacts) off could be done with Merits.<br /> <br /> If Sailing rolls don\u2019t come up often enough, Sailing might also require a Merit that is numerically rated and rolled like an Ability, while being far cheaper than an Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm quite happy for there to be no favoured traits; if all charms/traits cost the same, the only difference is characters will develop in interesting ways later in the game rather than be stuck on decisions the player made 20 sessions before.<br /> There's plenty of other ways to do Castes.<br /> Again though, this isn't something so complex it needs drastically to be simplified. I mean, I would, but it's not terribly necessary.<br /> <br /> If you're gating artefact-crafting, the most obvious thing to me would be to gate them with charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T06:46:27-08:00","id":1357528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357426#post1357426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're gating artefact-crafting, the most obvious thing to me would be to gate them with charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from that, if you wanted to section off fields of crafting in a system with no Craft Ability, you could treat the differences between Woodworking, Swordsmithing, and Masonry the way 3rd Edition currently treats the difference between languages. Each one is a single variation of the same Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T06:56:40-08:00","id":1357531,"title":"","content":"You could, yeah.<br /> Though honestly, for a simplified system, it seems much easier to me to have a single Craft ability with specialties.<br /> <br /> Or make Craft a specialty for other abilities and roll those, ie a blacksmith rolls Strength+Melee(+1 specialty in Crafting), a boat-builder rolls Int+Sail(+1 specialty in Crafting), etc.<br /> <br /> Not perfect solutions, but they're simple. I prefer the first to the second for Exalted though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-29-2019, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T14:21:10-08:00","id":1357602,"title":"","content":"Single biggest source of complexity in the game for me is the fact that charm cascades tend to have an unspoken design thesis that often necessitates a more experienced member of the community to help a new player navigate the gap between their character concept and whats in the book.<br /> <br /> Its gotten worse in Ex3 because of the enduring ill-will towards the former developers, so inquiring about design intent can be like stepping on a landmine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T15:23:24-08:00","id":1357615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357602#post1357602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its gotten worse in Ex3 because of the enduring ill-will towards the former developers, so inquiring about design intent can be like stepping on a landmine.</div> </div> </div> </div>My perception is that Vance harbours no I'll intent towards the old devs, merely that he's working from the same text as the rest of us. So if intent isn't clear to you, he has no additional insight making it clear to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T16:58:30-08:00","id":1357638,"title":"","content":"This has nothing to do with how Vance or Minton engage with people, the fact they try to engage with the core book beyond the parts they personally wrote is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 12-29-2019, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T17:05:50-08:00","id":1357641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1353037#post1353037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Around the release of the Third Edition corebook I jumped out Exalted's window in a rain of glass shards and ran away into the night with no intent to return. So big, so bulky, such a lack of addressing my personal problems with the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>What were your personal problems with the system?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T01:02:15-08:00","id":1357716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357602#post1357602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its gotten worse in Ex3 because of the enduring ill-will towards the former developers, so inquiring about design intent can be like stepping on a landmine.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair we used to have the reverse problem. When I first joined the community Dr Moran seemed to have a vocal fanbase that marched to war against all percieved detractors. Being called dumb for not understanding aspects of Exalted: the Fair Folk on my first read was an experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T01:30:34-08:00","id":1357724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357602#post1357602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Single biggest source of complexity in the game for me is the fact that charm cascades tend to have an unspoken design thesis that often necessitates a more experienced member of the community to help a new player navigate the gap between their character concept and whats in the book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give an example?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, anyone want to speculate on what Modes are? I wonder if it's like Terrestrial/standard/Mastery, and it changes how the charm works for different splats.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though it doesn't have to be that standardised; perhaps Ox-Body gives 2 health levels to DBs and Sidereals, 3 to Solaroids and Stamina 5 DBs, 4 to Lunars and Sta5 Solars, and 5 to Sta5 Lunars. Or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T01:32:15-08:00","id":1357725,"title":"","content":"Again from the Discord; the social rules are not changing much, just getting a bit simpler.<br /> <br /> Which sounds like what most of us want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-30-2019, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T07:05:12-08:00","id":1357764,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m assuming someone in charge strongly believes sales could be better for Exalted 3rd Edition, or I doubt this would ever be happening.<br /> <br /> This sounds like a very wise move on Onyx Path's part.<br /> <br /> When it says &quot;appeal to long term fans alike,&quot; do any of you believe part of the purpose of this product is to try to draw back buyers who have become disenfranchised &amp; left 3rd Edition? Bring in new fans &amp; bring back the old?<br /> <br /> It's ambitious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T07:31:08-08:00","id":1357770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357716#post1357716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair we used to have the reverse problem. When I first joined the community Dr Moran seemed to have a vocal fanbase that marched to war against all percieved detractors. Being called dumb for not understanding aspects of Exalted: the Fair Folk on my first read was an experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jenna has a ride or die fandom. Worth five regular Exalted fans in a fight, easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T07:58:59-08:00","id":1357774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357764#post1357764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m assuming someone in charge strongly believes sales could be better for Exalted 3rd Edition, or I doubt this would ever be happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that they feel there are accessibility issues regardless, and think they could get yet more people in with something less complex. (Based on its Kickstarters and sales rankings, from an outside perspective 3e looks to be doing very healthily.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T08:26:29-08:00","id":1357783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357724#post1357724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you give an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>How the bard archetype is split between Solar Performance and Silver-Voiced Nightingale.<br /> It is not intuative from the corebook alone why this seperation exists and why Solars seem to require a martial art or evocations to kill with music.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T08:31:49-08:00","id":1357784,"title":"","content":"I don't know how intrinsic &quot;kill with music&quot; is to &quot;the bard archetype,&quot; as I've played bards before, and <i>never </i>once killed someone directly with my music.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T10:04:31-08:00","id":1357813,"title":"","content":"Nightingale was a Backer-selected MA, and killing with music as ntoed was never really a Solar thing in 1e or 2e save Demon-Wracking Shout or talking about yelling so hard things explode. Which you get a bit of in Presence with the anti-CoD auras. There may have been more support for it, but I think it was generally a matter that no one thought that that was an especially Solar theme to do or worry about. It's kind of clear from the Charms that Morke was thinking about like...Performance itself more than going too oddball there.<br /> <br /> The one that I think was more an issue was that there's not as much flame weapon support in Archery as could be due to Righteous Devil, which I would say is a more justifiable issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T10:08:31-08:00","id":1357816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357783#post1357783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the bard archetype is split between Solar Performance and Silver-Voiced Nightingale.<br /> It is not intuative from the corebook alone why this seperation exists and why Solars seem to require a martial art or evocations to kill with music.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this have to do with \u201cunspoken design theses\u201d? <br /> <br /> It\u2019s supposed to be weird for any Performance Charms to allow for lethal attacks, not weird that Solars are the only ones who have none.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T10:10:57-08:00","id":1357817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357813#post1357813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The one that I think was more an issue was that there's not as much flame weapon support in Archery as could be due to Righteous Devil, which I would say is a more justifiable issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is really just one example of the greater problem with the division between Martial Arts and everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T10:20:53-08:00","id":1357822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357817#post1357817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is really just one example of the greater problem with the division between Martial Arts and everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs have talked about how they did try to tie MAs with the four other Abilities, but it led to weirdness in implementation, though. I actually am not against hte current setup. MAs lets you dip into an exotic fighting style that your native Charmset might not do due to their tendnacy to be more straight-forward, or they give optiosn with wepaons you normally wouldn't. And due to hteir shared nature, you can do things out of your Exalt type entirelyr eally.<br /> <br /> It's only really a problem with Solar Charms and at times just a weird thing where we have a lot of them (which I like) but often too many on some things (we don't need that many Charms buffing boat speed or breaking the Sail system more-er) and missing stuff on others (Occult for stuff besides spirits, some meta-sorcery stuff, or in this case, yell-so-hard-eardrums-explode Charms)<br /> <br /> These ultimately boil down to I think at times focused-but-on-the-wrong-things Charm design in the Solar Charmset, rather than anything to do with MAs. Hell, most hte MAs weren't written by John Morke anyhow, but were written by Robert Vance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:06:02-08:00","id":1357850,"title":"","content":"This was an actual question that someone I know asked their group.<br /> <br /> A player who backed the Kickstater could have explained that Nightingale was a legacy MA that people voted to come back by popular demand.<br /> A player with experience of previous editions could have explained that using your music to kill and maim people is more appropriate to Abyssals.<br /> Even the potentially prickly explaination that Exalted is not a dungeon crawler and that &quot;how do I kill things with this skill!&quot; is a narrow way of looking at things.<br /> <br /> Instead they got a rant about Holden not listening to people and more questions than answers. Obviously these people were dealing with their own issues and should not have been trying to initiate a new player, but the thought process made me realise how much this new edition of Exalted expects veterans of previous editions to nod sagely and go &quot;ah it is the wisdom of the developers&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 12-30-2019, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T13:30:26-08:00","id":1357876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357817#post1357817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is really just one example of the greater problem with the division between Martial Arts and everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, or that a lot of flame weapons should be in Brawl or Melee instead of Archery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T14:04:01-08:00","id":1357882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357876#post1357876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That, or that a lot of flame weapons should be in Brawl or Melee instead of Archery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t understand your logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T16:06:06-08:00","id":1357894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357882#post1357882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t understand your logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flame weapons tended to have such short ranges that you effectively were in close combat when you got to use them, and the Storyteller system has a history of utilizing Brawl to shoot guns in a fistfight (also to exhale fire). Blazing Solar Bolt and other ranged Melee attack Charms also shared the flame weapon characteristic of &quot;this range is an absolute maximum and not an increment&quot;. It also allows crossbows to slide into the place of the range weapon to use if you didn't pick up high Strength, while the flame weapons get to be an alternate for low-Strength characters in Melee, which could provide a bit of thematic breathing room, even given the limited quantity of shots for flame weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T23:24:23-08:00","id":1357964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1357770#post1357770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jenna has a ride or die fandom. Worth five regular Exalted fans in a fight, easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's unique in that unlike every other instance of lynchmob fans I've encountered before, or since Jenna never seems to have used her influence irresponsibly to have caused this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T09:03:46-08:00","id":1358019,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I think a lot of Jenna's genius probably was over venerated in hindsight (in the sense that despite successes, there are more unforeseen consequences, and too much veneration and hero worship means you don't fix those quickly enough), but I far prefer her fanboys to... a certain set of her extreme fandom detractors, who often seem to be on the verge of calling 'pretentious' anything slightly challenging, creative or unconventional (even her writing style!), and out to build themselves up by &quot;felling the giant&quot; or &quot;announcing the Emperor is naked&quot; and so forth.<br /> <br /> (On a tangent, actually makes think the only Ex fan I ever recall claiming Ex:The Fair Folk was *simple* was Shreyas Sampat (fourwillowsweeping) and that Jenna's writing there was both straightforward and yet punishing (as was completely proper) to readers who did not read both literally and in order, and who assumed redundancy in text, and that this was a wonderful quality in writing. Which was an unusual stance. Guy isn't active in the fandom any more, so I assume this isn't pushing into a PA.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T09:25:53-08:00","id":1358023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358019#post1358019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(On a tangent, actually makes think the only Ex fan I ever recall claiming Ex:The Fair Folk was *simple* was Shreyas Sampat (fourwillowsweeping) and that Jenna's writing there was both straightforward and yet punishing (as was completely proper) to readers who did not read both literally and in order, and who assumed redundancy in text, and that this was a wonderful quality in writing. Which was an unusual stance. Guy isn't active in the fandom any more, so I assume this isn't pushing into a PA.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we've... unfortunately crossed paths.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T09:56:50-08:00","id":1358027,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve found Moran\u2019s stuff really intriguing and almost impossible to actually implement in a game.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like if there was an RPG where the players each play as a memory, a person\u2019s first kiss, the time they had the chicken pox, their graduation ceremony, ect. It\u2019d be interesting, if I could ever actually figure out how to make it work. Unfortunately sitting behind the DM screen changes a lot about what you need for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T10:24:12-08:00","id":1358029,"title":"","content":"Wasn\u2019t part of the problem with Second Edition Raksha that Moran was part of the second wave team on the project after the first team failed to deliver the desired product, or am I thinking of First Edition?<br /> <br /> The instructions were to avoid \u201cEuro Fae\u201d but the writers delivered \u201cEuro Fae\u201d, so the second wave replaced all European terms with Arabic and Indian terms to give it an Eastern/Middle-Eastern aesthetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T10:25:55-08:00","id":1358030,"title":"","content":"That was First Edition. The problem with Second Edition is that they largely rehashed First Edition without knowing the context for why it was the way it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T10:34:52-08:00","id":1358033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358029#post1358029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn\u2019t part of the problem with Second Edition Raksha that Moran was part of the second wave team on the project after the first team failed to deliver the desired product, or am I thinking of First Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition. She didn't write anything from the 2e book. This is actually a bit of the issues too since hwile Shaping Combat is interesting, I think it mainly didn't completley implode in taht she's a skilled writer who at least coud make it read well. 2e went with more or less assuming the 2e version, including flaws fo the 1e one where writers went rogue and GCG and Jenna were patching things, was as-intended. Plus often reading some fo the subtler bits of her stuff and taking htem to weird conclusions. (Nirguna doesn't exist, so her aspect Advaita Iraivan doesn'te exist...except then it became crucial to the foundaitno of the universe for-real-actually in 2e.)<br /> <br /> 2e went in assuming the issues with 1e was they weren't clear enough, not that really in the end, Shaping to some extent was just not a good base system to use. Plus over-emphasis on the shinma compared to the 1e take, which were not clear to like...be real. And Jenna had just better purple prose, which made teh shinma interesting. Just read the 1e and 2e Dharma descriptions osmetime to show that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Graceful Wicked Masques[/quote</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The shinma Dharma perhaps epitomizes why the nature of the Fair Folk is so impenetrable to the people of Creation. Dharma simultaneously represents desire and apathy, resilience and decay, ignorance and omniscience. To the raksha, concepts such as desire and apathy are not merely descriptions of specific motives for action\u2014they are pinpoints on a multi-dimensional graph that encompasses the entire spectrum of all possible imperatives for action. As Thief of Words so wisely said: \u201cAs the progenitor of corruption, Dharma is, himself, pure; as the definition of ignorance, he is, himself all-knowing; as the forerunner of every desire, he is, himself, free of hunger.\u201d ...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Exalted: the Fair Folk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The shinma Dharma defines corrosion, ignorance and desire. Dharma is the mad addictions and cravings that subvert the nature of the raksha. As the progenitor of corruption, Dharma is, himself, pure; as the definition of ignorance, he is, himself, all-knowing; as the forerunner of every desire, he is, himself, free of hunger. Thus, Dharma is, in all ways, righteous, self-sacrificing and wise. He is the pillar of perfect devotion that upholds a cosmos tainted by his own existence. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Both say a bit more on raksha and Dharma, but I do think that, one has a lot more like, <i>impact</i> that does a bit to make it more paletteable, even if I think ultiamtely Shaping as a whole had problmes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358029#post1358029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The instructions were to avoid \u201cEuro Fae\u201d but the writers delivered \u201cEuro Fae\u201d, so the second wave replaced all European terms with Arabic and Indian terms to give it an Eastern/Middle-Eastern aesthetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moslty Hindu and some Persian actually. And yeah, that was the 1e book. Including &quot;Thief of Words wasn't in the original outline&quot; I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T13:34:01-08:00","id":1358064,"title":"","content":"Do we want to keep battle groups, and do we want battle groups to be more challenging in a simplified combat system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T13:38:00-08:00","id":1358067,"title":"","content":"I think the power of battle groups is fine.<br /> They're also fairly simple. I often use them instead of another NPC to reduce complexity.<br /> There's probably a few ways to reduce their complexity though, especially in terms of making them and their stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T13:44:57-08:00","id":1358070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358067#post1358067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the power of battle groups is fine.<br /> They're also fairly simple. I often use them instead of another NPC to reduce complexity.<br /> There's probably a few ways to reduce their complexity though, especially in terms of making them and their stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like battle groups who focus on a single target should penalize that target\u2019s Defense with a preemptive onslaught penalty. Solar Charms can still negate it, and particularly White Reaper Style\u2019s Revolving Crescent Defense.<br /> <br /> if their numbers give them the power to attack multiple targets with the same attack, why shouldn\u2019t those numbers help them overwhelm a single target with a focused attack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T14:50:51-08:00","id":1358087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358070#post1358070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like battle groups who focus on a single target should penalize that target\u2019s Defense with a preemptive onslaught penalty. Solar Charms can still negate it, and particularly White Reaper Style\u2019s Revolving Crescent Defense.<br /> <br /> if their numbers give them the power to attack multiple targets with the same attack, why shouldn\u2019t those numbers help them overwhelm a single target with a focused attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that's what the Engage action is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T17:34:50-08:00","id":1358110,"title":"","content":"And engage with a command action is absolutely brutal.<br /> <br /> Regardless, if Essence is aiming to be simpler, then at no point should extra rules that make things more complex be added.<br /> <br /> I actually hope Overwhelming penalties won't be in Essence. Not that I have anything against them per-se, but it seems that Essence will have motes and mote regen in-combat from stunts, and so it's important to take out other things to keep track of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T18:29:36-08:00","id":1358117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358087#post1358087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe that's what the Engage action is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hadn\u2019t considered that. I saw it as dogpiling someone, but that would involve knocking the target prone as well as engaging them. Simply engaging a target would work like focusing down a single target, and Revolving Crescent Defense still logically helps against such a tactic.<br /> <br /> But there\u2019s no RAW limitation to how many characters a battle group can engage. I suppose that\u2019s better to leave to ST discretion, based on the size, composition, and circumstances of the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T00:31:58-08:00","id":1358151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358110#post1358110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually hope Overwhelming penalties won't be in Essence. Not that I have anything against them per-se, but it seems that Essence will have motes and mote regen in-combat from stunts, and so it's important to take out other things to keep track of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Removing onslaught is tricky with static defence values, it's the kind of thing that could fuck newbies for not optimising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T00:39:07-08:00","id":1358152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358151#post1358151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Removing onslaught is tricky with static defence values, it's the kind of thing that could fuck newbies for not optimising.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also one of the things keeping Wasted Turn Syndrome at bay. It's not great at it, but it helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T00:42:52-08:00","id":1358154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358151#post1358151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Removing onslaught is tricky with static defence values, it's the kind of thing that could fuck newbies for not optimising.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope character creation is less of a newbie trap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T03:19:52-08:00","id":1358167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358154#post1358154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope character creation is less of a newbie trap.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify I don't mean in the typical bp/xp way and more that players used to classes and trait ratings being a pretty big part of the character they're playing might make a group where the difference between the Twilight's combat ability vs. the Dawn's prevents them from meaningfully participating in the same combat. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T07:02:36-08:00","id":1358183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358064#post1358064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we want to keep battle groups, and do we want battle groups to be more challenging in a simplified combat system?</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally I wouldn't mind something closer to <b>Scion</b>'s Followers, where they're heavily abstracted into something more like a character trait for the PC.<br /> <br /> Antagonistic katamaris can suffice with a trait comparable to Legendary Size in how it distinguishes them from singular actors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T20:10:37-08:00","id":1358526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358183#post1358183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally I wouldn't mind something closer to <b>Scion</b>'s Followers, where they're heavily abstracted into something more like a character trait for the PC.<br /> <br /> Antagonistic katamaris can suffice with a trait comparable to Legendary Size in how it distinguishes them from singular actors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am intrigued.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T21:22:37-08:00","id":1358542,"title":"","content":"Scion's Followers, in summary:<ul><li>They're a Birthright (similar to a Merit) rated from 1-5.</li> <li>They have a single area they function in (Mental/Physical/Social).</li> <li>They can take two Injury Conditions (i.e. they have two health levels) and have Defense equal to half their rating. The player decides if the Follower or the PC takes damage from any attack; a defeated Follower comes back into play after a session.</li> <li>They get a <i>tag</i> per dot, which cover things like being able to flurry (due to being a group rather than an individual), a secondary area of focus (your warboys are also fuckboys), being unruly (higher difficulty to command them, but you get a game resource when you fail), or having a minor supernatural ability.</li> </ul><br /> When commanding them, you roll (Attribute + [Followers rating or Leadership skill]) using your action. They can't act independently unless you're incapacitated, which denies them your Leadership, but that only matters if it's higher than your dots in the Birthright.<br /> <br /> Antagonists can have a Swarm trait, which is simpler and only makes non-AoE attacks less effective. Unlike Followers, I'd like something more complex for EE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T22:05:35-08:00","id":1358549,"title":"","content":"As an important note on how tough Followers are, in Scion (and Storypath in general) normal attacks can only do 1-2 damage per hit. So trying to take out Followers isn't hard, but it at least eats up time in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T02:09:56-08:00","id":1358573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358183#post1358183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally I wouldn't mind something closer to <b>Scion</b>'s Followers, where they're heavily abstracted into something more like a character trait for the PC.<br /> <br /> Antagonistic katamaris can suffice with a trait comparable to Legendary Size in how it distinguishes them from singular actors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main purpose of battle groups should not be as war-trousers for a PC like 2nd ed, it should be so you can run a fight quickly between a PC and 20 bandits. The BG rules do that pretty fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T10:03:06-08:00","id":1358638,"title":"","content":"They do it <i>fine</i>, yes, but there's still room for streamlining. For one, I fully expect EE to have significantly simplified antagonists, even compared to quick characters in EX3, because that's a recurring property of lightweight systems (though not the <i>lightest</i> ones). Just look at, again, Scion, or the &quot;quick Horrors&quot; of the nWoD, or the diceless threats in Powered by the Apocalypse. Simplifying battlegroups down further to a single paragraph of special properties is a natural step following that.<br /> <br /> Now, simplified antagonists and simplified battlegroup properties are, strictly speaking, <i>enough</i>. The system could just allow PCs to have a pet entity, but this means more actors in combat and rules to fulfill the fantasy of being a commander, both which will take extra time.<br /> For a specific example, I have a Night Caste with a War investment. Whenever I roll her hundred-something Kenyan yakuza into battle, it means I'll be spending most of my turns making rolls so that they can make separate, bigger rolls. It's not unsatisfying, but it could stand to be sped up for a simpler system.<br /> <br /> Scion does it by treating your murderous katamari as an extension of the character \u2013 living equipment, more complex than the equivalent antagonist option but aimed at being as quick to use and resolve as any other roll. Broken Worlds (built off PbtA, above) is even simpler, applying the same <i>group</i> tag to the PC-with-mooks as to enemy armies. Recent DnD releases see PC pet options use the same rules as all other system entities, but with their range of actions limited by opportunity costs for the player \u2013 for example, your pet can only make an attack if you spend an action to command it, but this requires no roll on the player's part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 01-03-2020, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T11:05:56-08:00","id":1358655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1358638#post1358638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do it <i>fine</i>, yes, but there's still room for streamlining. For one, I fully expect EE to have significantly simplified antagonists, even compared to quick characters in EX3, because that's a recurring property of lightweight systems (thoughnot the <i>lightest</i> ones). Just look at, again,Scion, or the &quot;quick Horrors&quot; of the nWoD, or the diceless threats in Powered by the Apocalypse. Simplifying battlegroups down further to a single paragraph of special properties is a natural step following that.<br /> <br /> Now, simplified antagonists and simplified battlegroup properties are, strictly speaking, <i>enough</i>. The system could just allow PCs to have a pet entity, but this means more actors in combat and rules to fulfill the fantasy of being a commander, both which will take extra time.<br /> For a specific example, I have a Night Caste with a War investment. Whenever I roll her hundred-something Kenyan yakuza into battle, it means I'll be spending most of my turns making rolls so that they can make separate, bigger rolls. It's not unsatisfying, but it could stand to be sped up for a simpler system.<br /> <br /> Scion does it by treating your murderous katamari as an extension of the character \u2013 living equipment, more complex than the equivalent antagonist option but aimed at being as quick to use and resolve as any other roll. Broken Worlds (built off PbtA, above) is even simpler, applying the same <i>group</i> tag to the PC-with-mooks as to enemy armies. Recent DnD releases see PC pet options use the same rules as all other system entities, but with their range of actions limited by opportunity costs for the player \u2013 for example, your pet can only make an attack if you spend an action to command it, but this requires no roll on the player's part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you ! I'd even appreciate if these rules were somewhat compatible with the existing Ex3 core !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T13:34:36-08:00","id":1359563,"title":"","content":"Returning to the question of how necessary motes are, consider the Blood Ape.<br /> <br /> It has 45 motes left over if it materializes right before a fight.<br /> <br /> Combat generally lasts no more than five rounds at most, and a blood ape should get combat respiration, so if it lasts that long it can get about 25 motes back in total. Roughly 60 motes.<br /> <br /> But its most useful and powerful Charms either cost Willpower or can only be used once per fight without fulfilling a reset condition. And none of them can be used together in the same turn, so timing becomes a valuable resource as well.<br /> <br /> So what is the point of its motes?<br /> <br /> If it avoids spending Willpower, it\u2019s effectively never going to run out of motes. When was the last time you ran into a blood ape (or anything) when it was tapped out on motes?<br /> <br /> What if it only had as many motes as Willpower points, and spent those few motes in the place of Willpower points for its stronger Charms? Leaving its Willpower alone for resisting social influence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T14:49:01-08:00","id":1359581,"title":"","content":"I ran the Storm Serpent from Hundred Devils against one of my PCs last session; it was spending like 15 motes a round, basically using all its combat charms, and by the time it fled, badly injured... it still had like 60 motes left.<br /> Does seem pretty pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T15:42:05-08:00","id":1359590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1359563#post1359563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what is the point of its motes?<br /> <br /> If it avoids spending Willpower, it\u2019s effectively never going to run out of motes. When was the last time you ran into a blood ape (or anything) when it was tapped out on motes?<br /> <br /> What if it only had as many motes as Willpower points, and spent those few motes in the place of Willpower points for its stronger Charms? Leaving its Willpower alone for resisting social influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even crazier idea: <i>Why should spirits even have mote pools?</i> Gate their bigger abilities behind WP costs or resets and they instantly become <i>different</i> instead of just Exalts with unique charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T19:19:47-08:00","id":1359627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1359590#post1359590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even crazier idea: <i>Why should spirits even have mote pools?</i> Gate their bigger abilities behind WP costs or resets and they instantly become <i>different</i> instead of just Exalts with unique charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely one way to simplify NPCs, and I would approve.<br /> <br /> It would also be interesting if it prevented spirits from using artifacts. When was the last time we saw a spirit with an artifact that wasn't actually part of the god somehow?<br /> <br /> <br /> But aside from limiting players from walking around draped in every artifact they've ever looted from a corpse, why do Exalted need motes either?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T21:48:49-08:00","id":1359645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1359627#post1359627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When was the last time we saw a spirit with an artifact that wasn't actually part of the god somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only really two exceptions that come to mind and they've got good reasons.<br /> Sunipa- she's the war goddess of the east she's a far better reflection of warfare in the Scavenger Lands so she's got a few bits of magitech rather than a divine panopoly that's a reflection of who she is. Her predecessor Darunla the wolf goddess, was I assume geared more towards warfare among forests.<br /> Ninegala- a forge goddess whose ability to wield weapons is determined by the amount of work she put into making it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T22:08:38-08:00","id":1359651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1359627#post1359627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definitely one way to simplify NPCs, and I would approve.<br /> <br /> It would also be interesting if it prevented spirits from using artifacts. When was the last time we saw a spirit with an artifact that wasn't actually part of the god somehow?<br /> <br /> <br /> But aside from limiting players from walking around draped in every artifact they've ever looted from a corpse, why do Exalted need motes either?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it\u2019s not just artifacts, you want to limit players from being able to activate every charm they have all day every day. <br /> <br /> You could swap charms over to having willpower costs but you\u2019d lose a bit of the fine control that you have now. Like Peony Blossom isn\u2019t worth one of your 10 charm activations that day. You could scrap the idea of small charms and just have each charm be super powerful, which might work since in my experience most players tend to play Exalted like they\u2019re trying to spend their whole pool in as few actions as possible, as long as they\u2019re somewhere safe to show anima. You\u2019d miss out on the ability to turn up he heat only a touch though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T22:32:32-08:00","id":1359652,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure motes not running out before an opponent loses is as conclusive of evidence as it sounds.<br /> <br /> After all, a complaint about 2e was &quot;motes as hit-points,&quot; where beating opponents generally didn't happen until they ran out of motes to spent. This was seen as, in general, a bad thing that just dragged combat out with bother lack of progress outside of mote efficiency.<br /> <br /> So the idea that a spirit might run away while it still has plenty of motes seems like a good thing to me. It means Ex3 combat isn't overly focused on mote attrition.<br /> <br /> I'm not convinced that &quot;the fight shouldn't be over until the losing side is close to zero motes,&quot; is a good design ideal to focus on.<br /> <br /> Now, I still agree that motes are something to look at reducing in terms of numbers and complexity, but I would focus on making things easier for play rather than more abstract considerations like that.<br /> <br /> If motes were dropped completely... it seems like there's still a lot you would have to do (or also cut?). How do you know when anima increases? How do you make sure Charm activation costs match their effects without some more granularity than dumping motes completely would entail?<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure there's a good way to cut without making other things more complex in return, where simplifying but keeping motes (and reducing the numbers) seems more effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T23:17:49-08:00","id":1359658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1359652#post1359652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If motes were dropped completely... it seems like there's still a lot you would have to do (or also cut?). How do you know when anima increases? How do you make sure Charm activation costs match their effects without some more granularity than dumping motes completely would entail?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just spitballing here, but...<br /> Every round, everyone gets one &quot;flare&quot;. That is, at any point they do a thing (attack, parry, persuade, etc) they can raise their Anima a level. Then give every charm an Anima prereq. Or make effects scale based on Anima, or something to make the fight start at low intensity and ramp up as people go blonde. <br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, bring back Charm Activations. You get Anima+1 per instant. Want more? You're flaring! <br /> Not as elegant and harder to balance, but does prevent &quot;OK, let me look up these seven charms I'm applying here&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T02:53:08-08:00","id":1359673,"title":"","content":"The point I was making Heavy Arms is that for many spirits motes are mostly irrelevant extra book-keeping, because if they use every charm they can they're still going to win or lose a fight to Exalts way quicker than they run out of motes.<br /> <br /> It's not really the same for Exalts.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this is an area where things used 99% as NPCs (spirits, Raksha, etc) don't have to work the same as things often used as PCs (Exalts).<br /> <br /> I'll also say it's relevant that &quot;motes&quot; are staying for Essence... Though of course they may be quite different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T08:04:14-08:00","id":1359729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1359652#post1359652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you know when anima increases?</div> </div> </div> </div>Make increasing (but not decreasing) anima flare entirely voluntary to the player/character, and have your most powerful Charms require a minimum level of flare.<br /> <br /> Most Stealth and Disguise Charms only work at Dim anima level, some Celestial Exalted combat Charms require you to at least have your Caste Mark shining, and your mightiest Charms demand that you be at bonfire.<br /> <br /> That would definitely make playing Dragon-Blooded less annoying. If bonfire is entirely voluntary, you can never accidentally lock yourself out of out-of-Aspect Auras. Certain Charms can be gated behind anima levels as well as specific Auras, which still rewards a Dragon-Blood for going full bonfire and locking themselves into Charms of their Aspect's element.<br /> <br /> <br /> Spending anima can still remain in this framework, if you can only voluntarily raise your anima one level each round, because lowering your Anima to pay for one Charm could lock you out of other Charms that demanded that much anima flare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T10:28:31-08:00","id":1359742,"title":"","content":"I certainly think Quck Characters could've been done 'better' in the alternative universe where the Ex3 corebook had support for all exalt types. The ones we've got have an air of compromise around them which makes them more useful for homebrewers but nowhere near as steamlined as they could be.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T11:16:26-08:00","id":1359748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1359742#post1359742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly think Quck Characters could've been done 'better' in the alternative universe where the Ex3 corebook had support for all exalt types. The ones we've got have an air of compromise around them which makes them more useful for homebrewers but nowhere near as steamlined as they could be.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T11:59:40-08:00","id":1359760,"title":"","content":"I think mote pools/charms could've been expressed in a way that'd be easier for a Storyteller to field (for example) a group of Dragon-Blooded against their players without risking bookkeeping hell.<br /> <br /> However, the antagonists section was also being used as a window to Exalt types they weren't going to get to for years (even if things had been on shedule) so expressing them in a way that couldn't be hacked to make player characters would've caused some serious bad blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T12:46:31-08:00","id":1361958,"title":"","content":"So, Exalted: Essence is now out of alpha testing and onto its first draft.<br /> <br /> From the sound of it, it's more Exalted: Simplified than a complete redesign. But that's just my impression.<br /> <br /> Couple more details from the Discord: dice pools max out around 20... which seemed very high to me, but I guess in regular Exalted you can roll 28 dice on a stab if you're maxed out, plus maybe some extra stuff.<br /> Anyway, for anyone hoping to not have to roll so many dice, that's a bit disappointing. They did say they want to reduce the number of steps though.<br /> <br /> Also, the universal charms will often get buffs when used by particulate Exalted types, but normally just 2-3, not all 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T15:06:09-08:00","id":1361998,"title":"","content":"Having less than 20 dice probably doesn\u2019t work well with the massive tower of power that exists in Exalted. There\u2019s unskilled mortals, skilled mortals, spirits, various different exalted. If the difference between focused Solar and unskilled mortal is only 6 there might not be a lot of room for appreciable gradients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T16:05:54-08:00","id":1362007,"title":"","content":"Add successes instead to get a gradation of power. Gradation in power requires gradation in numbers, not gradation in physical things bouncing around on a table. They're not going that way though, so it doesn't really matter as a conversation tangent...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T00:43:56-08:00","id":1362066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1361958#post1361958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Exalted: Essence is now out of alpha testing and onto its first draft.<br /> <br /> From the sound of it, it's more Exalted: Simplified than a complete redesign. But that's just my impression.<br /> <br /> Couple more details from the Discord: dice pools max out around 20... which seemed very high to me, but I guess in regular Exalted you can roll 28 dice on a stab if you're maxed out, plus maybe some extra stuff.<br /> Anyway, for anyone hoping to not have to roll so many dice, that's a bit disappointing. They did say they want to reduce the number of steps though.<br /> <br /> Also, the universal charms will often get buffs when used by particulate Exalted types, but normally just 2-3, not all 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably sensible. I want a simpler set of rules for the existing system, rather than yet another system. This way, OPP also won't cannibalise their own sales and everyone is still playing 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 01-21-2020, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T01:12:27-08:00","id":1362070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1361998#post1361998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having less than 20 dice probably doesn\u2019t work well with the massive tower of power that exists in Exalted. There\u2019s unskilled mortals, skilled mortals, spirits, various different exalted. If the difference between focused Solar and unskilled mortal is only 6 there might not be a lot of room for appreciable gradients.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or have Charms that set the difference not in number of successes or numbers of dice rolled, like Graceful Crane Stance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:02:03-08:00","id":1362109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1361998#post1361998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having less than 20 dice probably doesn\u2019t work well with the massive tower of power that exists in Exalted. There\u2019s unskilled mortals, skilled mortals, spirits, various different exalted. If the difference between focused Solar and unskilled mortal is only 6 there might not be a lot of room for appreciable gradients.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's fine: an unskilled mortal in 3e has 3 dice, a skilled 5-6, and the elite troops in the core have 8-9. If that was reduced to 1, 2 and 3, then an Exalt using charms to get 6 dice to hit and a Defence of 3 would tower over them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:06:47-08:00","id":1362112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1362066#post1362066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is probably sensible. I want a simpler set of rules for the existing system, rather than yet another system. This way, they don't cannibalise their own sales and everyone is still playing 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly seems to be the intention. I'm... mixed on that. It does stay close to the current system, making conversion easy, and generally with Exalted I think &quot;this is good but could really do with being 20% simpler&quot;. Which it sounds like I will get. And obviously I am running/playing Exalted because there's things I like about the system. <br /> <br /> But carrying the legacy of 1st edition Vampire: the Masquerade means I sometimes think certain things would be better if they were redesigned from the ground up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:35:13-08:00","id":1362120,"title":"","content":"Also from the Discord :<br /> <br /> -Exalted : Essence will have less power difference between Exalts (3e already does this to an extent but Essence takes it further still).<br /> <br /> -Charm effects specific to an Exalt type will never make the charm worse (e.g. there will be no &quot;Terrestrial&quot; tag that weakens MA Charms).<br /> <br /> So all in all it sounds like DBs could be getting lots of love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T09:01:04-08:00","id":1362126,"title":"","content":"So they redesign and rewrite Charms as well ? I wasn't sure if it was only Core mechanics with rules on how to adapt Charms from Normal to Essence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T09:22:21-08:00","id":1362133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1362126#post1362126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they redesign and rewrite Charms as well ? I wasn't sure if it was only Core mechanics with rules on how to adapt Charms from Normal to Essence</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, many common Charms will become <u>Universal</u> across all Exalt types (e.g. Ox-Body Technique, Graceful Crane Stance), with <u>Modes</u> that give them something unique for certain Exalts (kinda like Mastery tags).<br /> <br /> so as a made-up example you could have something like this :<br /> <br /> <b>Ox Body Technique (Universal)</b><br /> Gain -1, -2, -4 Health Levels. Can be bought 5 times.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Modes</b></u><br /> <b>Lunar :</b> Gain -1, -2, -4, -4.<br /> <b>Solar :</b> Gain -0, -1, -2.<br /> <b>Dragonblooded : </b>Can buy a 6th stack which grants -0, -4.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T12:52:56-08:00","id":1362202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1362066#post1362066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably sensible. I want a simpler set of rules for the existing system, rather than yet another system. This way, they don't cannibalise their own sales and everyone is still playing 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, I want the opposite, because EX3 <i>but less of it</i> isn't something I'm looking for.<br /> <br /> (Exalted product fails to please everyone; not even out yet; news at eleven.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T12:54:06-08:00","id":1362203,"title":"","content":"Huge, huge thanks to everyone sharing spoiled details here.<br /> <br /> (Discord is a pain to search, and also makes my eyes bleed.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:12:16-08:00","id":1362227,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I only started watching the essence_ruleset part of the Exalted Discord because a)I was already using Discord for a Blood Bowl league, and b)I was unemployed and bored for the last 7 weeks, so had the time to wade through it. It's certainly not the easiest format to search.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T15:18:04-08:00","id":1362249,"title":"","content":"@epitome's last post, it sounds like they think that Ex3 slightly overshoots to get the sort of flavour and balance of conflicts they see in the implies stories?<br /> <br /> I guess it may make sense to reorient universal Charms so they're always building up from a base than adding extra complexity to reduce, in terms of feel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T01:43:32-08:00","id":1362366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1362133#post1362133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, many common Charms will become <u>Universal</u> across all Exalt types (e.g. Ox-Body Technique, Graceful Crane Stance), with <u>Modes</u> that give them something unique for certain Exalts (kinda like Mastery tags).<br /> <br /> so as a made-up example you could have something like this :<br /> <br /> <b>Ox Body Technique (Universal)</b><br /> Gain -1, -2, -4 Health Levels. Can be bought 5 times.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Modes</b></u><br /> <b>Lunar :</b> Gain -1, -2, -4, -4.<br /> <b>Solar :</b> Gain -0, -1, -2.<br /> <b>Dragonblooded : </b>Can buy a 6th stack which grants -0, -4.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T07:39:36-08:00","id":1362404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1362249#post1362249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it may make sense to reorient universal Charms so they're always building up from a base than adding extra complexity to reduce, in terms of feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what the designer said, I think it is a matter of feeling.<br /> <br /> Although I would also prefer it from a reading perspective: it's generally (not always) a bit easier for Solar players to read the charm and edit in their mind to add the buff at the end than it is for Dragonblood players to read the charm and then edit it in their mind to add the nerf at the end.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T07:12:42-08:00","id":1363069,"title":"","content":"About Universal Charms.<br /> <br /> What other Charms do you think will fall under this category? Ox-Body, Graceful Crane, there was an integrity charm... I think Righteous Lion Defense...? But how about combat Charms? Which ones do you think should be a general exalt capacity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T07:30:54-08:00","id":1363070,"title":"","content":"Well Fire and Stones Strike and Crimson Fang Bite are just damage boosters, one contingent on strength the other on overflow successes, you could fuse them. Elsewhere storing charms are pretty common, same with soak boosters. Defense penalty negators like Dipping Swallow and Graceful Flowing Defense. Awareness charms that negate environmental penalties.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately? Fortunately? A lot of charms between splats aren\u2019t very interchangeable. Then again if Essence is supposed to be very streamlined they probably won\u2019t have a lot of charms in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T07:32:03-08:00","id":1363071,"title":"","content":"I think there should be some generic Charms in the following area : Add damage (withering, maybe decisive), Add soak, Counter attack, maybe something about join battle ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T07:38:54-08:00","id":1363072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1363071#post1363071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there should be some generic Charms in the following area : Add damage (withering, maybe decisive), Add soak, Counter attack, maybe something about join battle ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm that might be where the super wide spread starts to get a bit wonky. Solars and Lunars get counterattacks and join battle boosters, but Dragonblooded don\u2019t. It seems a bit of a waste to add bonus DB charms for them missing or on generic ones, but it would also suck if they just have a charm list half the size of everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T07:48:10-08:00","id":1363075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1363072#post1363072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm that might be where the super wide spread starts to get a bit wonky. Solars and Lunars get counterattacks and join battle boosters, but Dragonblooded don\u2019t. It seems a bit of a waste to add bonus DB charms for them missing or on generic ones, but it would also suck if they just have a charm list half the size of everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the possibility (I'm not sure I haven't checked) of Exalted:Essence is that some splats (DB for instance) get Charms they didn't have in the Core in order to simplify and unify the whole. Like maybe they will have a Counterattack but with less bonus than a Solar or a Join Battle with a specific bonus or whatever","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T08:28:26-08:00","id":1363084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1363075#post1363075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one of the possibility (I'm not sure I haven't checked) of Exalted:Essence is that some splats (DB for instance) get Charms they didn't have in the Core in order to simplify and unify the whole. Like maybe they will have a Counterattack but with less bonus than a Solar or a Join Battle with a specific bonus or whatever</div> </div> </div> </div>That would definitely be a good way of doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T08:42:23-08:00","id":1363087,"title":"","content":"DBs can get counterattacks through MAs - the big nerf they usually get is that the counterattack must count as a combat action rather than being a free attack. So that's how I'd expect a native DB counterattack charm to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T09:02:25-08:00","id":1363093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1363087#post1363087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs can get counterattacks through MAs - the big nerf they usually get is that the counterattack must count as a combat action rather than being a free attack. So that's how I'd expect a native DB counterattack charm to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's an example. I think if they don't free themselves of the limitations and expectations of Exalted 3e Core they will only end up making a big home-brew. Which is not necessarily bad, but maybe in a design perspective would not be a total success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T09:27:55-08:00","id":1363099,"title":"","content":"What do we know about Martial Arts in EE? How would they interact with universal charms? If, for eample, there's a general cpacity for counterattacks, what would happen to crane style?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T09:36:54-08:00","id":1363101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1363099#post1363099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do we know about Martial Arts in EE? How would they interact with universal charms? If, for eample, there's a general cpacity for counterattacks, what would happen to crane style?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might branch off the counterattack charm, or just not exist in EE. <br /> <br /> What do we have for charms now?<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Excellency<br /> 2. Withering damage<br /> 3. Defense penalty negator<br /> 4. Soak adder<br /> 5. Counterattack<br /> 6. Ox body<br /> 7. Graceful crane<br /> 8. Decisive multiattack<br /> 9. Intimacy protector<br /> 10. Monkey leap?<br /> 11. Feat of strength enhancer<br /> 12. Stealth penalty negator<br /> 13. Familiar taming charm<br /> 14. Health level recovery<br /> 15. Cypher writing<br /> 16. Finding bartering price<br /> <br /> Outside of combat they often get a lot less generic and applicable, I\u2019m finding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:25:40-08:00","id":1363113,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts are Universal charms in E:E.<br /> <br /> That's all they've said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:28:00-08:00","id":1363115,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, 95% of charms that just represent &quot;do this thing humans can do, but better&quot; (jump higher, run faster, be tougher, play music better) are appropriate for any Exalt type.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure 90% of Solar charms, if nerfed, would be fine (if themeless) charms for other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:34:47-08:00","id":1363118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1363099#post1363099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do we know about Martial Arts in EE? How would they interact with universal charms? If, for example, there's a general capacity for counterattacks, what would happen to crane style?</div> </div> </div> </div>All we know is Martial Arts Charms should work like universal Charms, the Mastery keyword will simply become a &quot;Mode&quot; like any other. To my knowledge they haven't revealed anything of note so far on the interaction between MA and native/universal Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:49:48-08:00","id":1363121,"title":"","content":"That's correct.<br /> <br /> It does make me wonder if, since they said Universal charms aren't generally going to have more than 2 or 3 modes (because it would be too annoying), if there'll be a &quot;Solar+Abyssal+Infernal&quot; mode. Or maybe a &quot;Celestial&quot; Mode.<br /> <br /> I doubt they'll be a &quot;Dragonblood+Liminal&quot; mode though, as they're too different thematically.<br /> <br /> I also wonder how Universal charms will work with Attribute/Ability Exalt types (as the game still has Attributes and Abilities, I assume Liminals/Alchemicals/Lunars are still Attribute-based, while the others use Abilities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T12:31:59-08:00","id":1364005,"title":"","content":"I'm curious what they're doing with xp/costs.<br /> <br /> A lot of issues with Ex3 that are basically rooted in the idea that it's a player's god given right to obtain a new charm every other session and that they should all be useful. This has given rise to bloat, complexity and charms that people consider lacklustre.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T13:32:35-08:00","id":1364018,"title":"","content":"Hmmmmmmmm..............<br /> <br /> It's my experience that low-xp games' players are really keen on getting those charms, but after 300xp, they often leave large chunks of XP on their sheets because they're not sure what to do with it (except the sorcerers, of course).<br /> <br /> So, in the FFG Star Wars (which in many ways is similar to a simplified Exalted, with range bands and ability/attribute and favoured xp costs) each class has 4 talents (kind of like charms) for 5xp, 4 for 10xp, 4 for 15xp, 4 for 20xp. The more expensive ones are either stacks or better, and require cheaper ones.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I think it'd be fine for xp costs for charms to scale the way abilities do. An essence 1 party could get a charm each a session, while an essence 5 could get one every 5 sessions.<br /> <br /> I doubt they'll go for that though.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... I hope, in the attempt to make things simpler, they do make it simpler than 3e's XP system (with Solar xp based on various rp-stuff, which is a bit complicated).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T16:14:43-08:00","id":1364057,"title":"","content":"It's probably too peripheral a subject to really talk about at this stage, but I am wondering what they will do with the three tier structure of Sorcery, and with Sidereal Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T21:09:44-08:00","id":1364097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1364057#post1364057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably too peripheral a subject to really talk about at this stage, but I am wondering what they will do with the three tier structure of Sorcery, and with Sidereal Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery doesn't strike me as something that needs to be simplified.<br /> <br /> The base combat and crafting rules need to be simplified, and the Charm system is going to be simplified to match as well as to cut down on duplicate concepts.<br /> <br /> So maybe combat-level shaping actions might be changed, and some spell mechanics need to change to match the altered base system, but for the most part sorcery seems pretty simple already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T00:47:52-08:00","id":1364113,"title":"","content":"There might be some small bits of simplification, but certainly the three-tier structure is simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T01:23:10-08:00","id":1364115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1364097#post1364097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery doesn't strike me as something that needs to be simplified.<br /> <br /> The base combat and crafting rules need to be simplified, and the Charm system is going to be simplified to match as well as to cut down on duplicate concepts.<br /> <br /> So maybe combat-level shaping actions might be changed, and some spell mechanics need to change to match the altered base system, but for the most part sorcery seems pretty simple already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery's in a good place, but spells could use some work. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T07:21:25-08:00","id":1364155,"title":"","content":"Yeah, to clarify I don't think you really *need* to simplify Sorcery, I just wonder if they'll go for some element of &quot;Flying Guillotine! Flying Guillotine-ara! Flying Guillotine-aga!&quot; (universal spells with different bonuses per sorcerous tier, to use an FF reference for the same thing) as well as the canon spells unique to each tier (in a parallel to what they're doing with universal Charms with tiered power-ups).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T10:28:35-08:00","id":1364187,"title":"","content":"Shaping Rituals seem like something that would need to be massively simplified for this project even if the basics of sorcery itself need minimal attention. Currently they take about 1 page of text each, which is a lot of room being eaten up for some relatively minor character customization (esp. since you can learn multiple).<br /> <br /> I also don't think, again more for space concerns than anything else, you can just rely on a massive spell list (even in more simplified language, most spells would eat up ~1/4 page each). Some sort of &quot;make your own spell&quot; system seems like a far more efficient use of space. The VtR supplement Blood Sorcery has a complete &quot;build you own spells&quot; guide in 14 pages, including incorporating the thematic differences of the different kinds of blood sorcery in the game, and 6 pages of examples with around 5 per page there. So in about the same amount of space, Blood Sorcery covers the same material for its setting, but includes rules for making up spells which Exalted doesn't in the same space (and keep in mind same space as just Ex3 core, not additional stuff from the other books that fall under more spells or more shaping rituals).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T11:13:46-08:00","id":1364196,"title":"","content":"One precise point I'd like to see about sorcery is the moment you accumulate enough motes in Shaping, because it makes for 3 rolls in a turn which is a bit annoying : Accumulating, attacking, damaging. I'm not sure if the First and second roll (which are essentially the same mechanically) could be merged into one roll, and with what consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T11:59:06-08:00","id":1364200,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure merging them is a great idea.<br /> <br /> First, they're not the same. Attack spells don't always use Intelligence (Perception is fairly common) as their base is a direct issue with that premise.<br /> <br /> More importantly though, it makes it much harder on meta-sorcery Charms because adding successes to your shaping rolls is now also adding successes to your attack rolls (if applicable). At the moment, if you want to toss a ton of motes at shaping spells fast, and ensuring an attack spell hits hard, it's very expensive because it's two rolls you have to boost separately.<br /> <br /> If there's going to be any sort of streamlining here, it might not be bad to steal a page from D&amp;D. Get rid of the roll to hit and have that be a static value, with reduced effect if it's not high enough to hit the target appropriate to the spell (esp. since so many of the attack spells are at least descriptively area effects even if they only target one thing mechanically).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T12:25:42-08:00","id":1364205,"title":"","content":"Thing is I believe comparing a static value (your spell attack) against another static value (their Parry or Dodge) seems kinda bori, even though I agree with you that a core idea like this would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T07:34:45-08:00","id":1364343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1364205#post1364205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is I believe comparing a static value (your spell attack) against another static value (their Parry or Dodge) seems kinda bori, even though I agree with you that a core idea like this would be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might make an individual action more boring, but it would make it quicker to resolve a number of actions, potentially allowing you to make more choices as part of a more involved strategy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T08:30:56-08:00","id":1364351,"title":"","content":"What about a spell that deals damage with a linear relation directly between the attacking value (spell attack, perception or something like that) against the parry (or another value like Resistance) ? <br /> <br /> Something along the lines of : A base value + Perception - Target Dodge. If I'm not mistaken <span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"color:#006991\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Unslakable Thirst of the Devil-Maw</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span><br /> already includes this functioning, except for the fact that you have to touch first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T08:44:44-08:00","id":1364356,"title":"","content":"If Essence is going to be drastically simplified they should probably turn damage into 1d10 plus modifiers or something like that, just one die not a pool since it\u2019s faster. Keep the dice pool for attacking though to keep in line with other abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T09:57:41-08:00","id":1364369,"title":"","content":"That makes for a lot of variance in the roll, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T10:17:27-08:00","id":1364371,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you'd want at least 2 dice to create a bell curve of results. It's why I've pondered running DnD with 2d10 instead of a d20. It certainly would help keep the roll simple though if say... equipment and the like added auto-successes instead of dice. Just roll Strength as normal, and add the resulting successes to the static weapon damage, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25921-fffxx","name":"FFFXX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T10:17:31-08:00","id":1364372,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a bit more, and it\u2019s not a nice normally distributed curve, but it\u2019s damn fast. Especially if you ditch adding overflow successes to damage. Then you can look at your dice and if you notice that you totally exploded the attack roll you can pretty confidently just start rolling damage, give the final result, then the ST subtracts soak from it and the damage happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T10:42:27-08:00","id":1364373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FFFXX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1364371#post1364371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you'd want at least 2 dice to create a bell curve of results. It's why I've pondered running DnD with 2d10 instead of a d20. It certainly would help keep the roll simple though if say... equipment and the like added auto-successes instead of dice. Just roll Strength as normal, and add the resulting successes to the static weapon damage, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, rolling Strength wouldn\u2019t be too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T08:00:37-08:00","id":1364537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1364372#post1364372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a bit more, and it\u2019s not a nice normally distributed curve, but it\u2019s damn fast. Especially if you ditch adding overflow successes to damage. Then you can look at your dice and if you notice that you totally exploded the attack roll you can pretty confidently just start rolling damage, give the final result, then the ST subtracts soak from it and the damage happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>If accuracy doesn't add to damage the consideration would be necessary to make sure Soak doesn't get too high, but so long as the math balance is done correctly that could work too to simplify it. It could also, however, maybe benefit from a bonus if you massively exceed the target's Defense, like a critical hit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25921-fffxx","name":"FFFXX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T01:13:05-08:00","id":1364963,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of cutting out the pause after a successful attack where you check extra successes, do a little math, and then roll damage. However, if we're really blue skying with ideas to improve the flow of combat resolution, my best-case would be for attack and damage to be &quot;values,&quot; whilst defense and soak get rolled.<br /> <br /> After all, how many players know what it means to face an Ox-Dragon Smash attack with 19 dice and 12 damage (overwhelming 1)... made by someone in Black Craw Form, and enhanced with Divine Predator Strike, Reed-Breaking Banda, Finding The Needle's Eye, Foe-Driving Attack, and Unerring Fang Technique? I sure wouldn't without looking it up! And most players' intuition will probably mislead them: if they see an expensive attack with fairly low damage and decide to let soak handle it, assorted post-soak bonuses still give the attack a real shot at 4-5 damage... and on an attack with one debuff for 5+ damage and a different one for crashing the target, that could be a big mistake. Alternately, if they do try to boost their defense, &quot;19 dice&quot; doesn't really cover the +1 autosuccess, re-rolling the first three 1s, and getting an extra dice for each 10. Once you've done the math for that, you should also note that you'll be losing 1 defense to a magical onslaught penalty, another to a generic penalty if you're too close to your friends, and in all likelihood, taking away 1 defense from your medium weapon by &quot;ignoring&quot; it, which penalty-negating charms cannot prevent. And don't forget those re-rolled 1s if you (like many Solars) are relying upon low enemy dice to boost your defense after the roll.<br /> <br /> Even for a game as complex as Exalted (and, admittedly, a bit of an extreme example*), that's clearly unreasonable. But it doesn't have to be! You could have exactly the same amount of tactical depth by baking all of the penalties and dice tricks into a static attack value, moving the randomness over to rolls by the defender, and only expecting people to remember all of their own charms, rather than <i>every charm ever printed</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't expect that to happen, since most of what little we know about Essence's mechanics is to emphasize how many things it'll keep from the game's past editions, but if we're dreaming big and they're finally willing to cut into that massive 25-stat array of abilities, then why stop at slightly speeding up the damage roll?<br /> <br /> <br /> * Not, to be clear, the MOST extreme example which could come up in play. This is a combo with a mostly-logical game plan, involving essence 1-2 charms in two attributes, and low-level investment in two reasonably-synergistic MAs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T06:19:45-08:00","id":1364996,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m a bit confused about what you\u2019re saying Kejak. Do you mean to remove all offensive charms from the game as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T15:28:19-08:00","id":1365373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1364996#post1364996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m a bit confused about what you\u2019re saying Kejak. Do you mean to remove all offensive charms from the game as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that explanation needs work.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about removing offensive charms from the game. I just want them to work more like the charms which boost defense and soak (that is, by raising an unrolled number), and have the dice rolling (and thereby, any dice tricks) be on defensive Charms. As it stands, a given number of dice on an attack or damage roll can mean very different things at different times. Since most people know their own charms better than anyone else's, I feel like the tricksy probability stuff should only <i>expect</i> you to know your own charms.<br /> <br /> To backtrack a little from my overly-complex example, here are a few one-charm situations I have seen in play: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Being attacked by a Sidereal with a target number of 4-5, and mistakenly thinking that, say, seven defense was a sure thing against a ten-die decisive attack.</li> <li>A player who often uses Hail-Shattering Practice or Rumor of Form takes a nasty hit because they didn't understand that this attack re-rolled 1s.</li> <li>Incarnated Fury Attack is unblockable and undodgeable - most serious celestial combatants will have some way to defend against it, but that costs extra motes (and you're already crashed if you take an IFA), so they may be tempted to tough out what looks like &quot;only&quot; a withering attack with a light weapon. Since it gives double 7s on damage, this can net a lot more initiative than a player expected when they saved motes by taking the hit.</li> </ol><br /> If those examples said things like &quot;attack value 8&quot; instead of &quot;10 dice, target number 4,&quot; there is less information for players to miss, and no need for people to stop the game and calculate unconventional dice probabilities. In fact, many Exalted players tell me that they don't think in terms of probability at all, and instead follow intuition gained from play. If enemy dice mean different things enemy-by-enemy and action-by-action, that intuition seems very misleading to me, but if it's only dependent on your own abilities, that becomes a much better plan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T15:56:52-08:00","id":1365384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1365373#post1365373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about removing offensive charms from the game. I just want them to work more like the charms which boost defense and soak (that is, by raising an unrolled number), and have the dice rolling (and thereby, any dice tricks) be on defensive Charms.<br /> <br /> As it stands, a given number of dice on an attack or damage roll can mean very different things at different times. Since most people know their own charms better than anyone else's, I feel like the tricksy probability stuff should only <i>expect</i> you to know your own charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you give static values to Attack Charms and dice tricks to Defense Charms, doesn't that just swap the problem around? In that scenario the player won't know his odds of succeeding at an attack because of the dice tricks the NPCs might have for defense.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really feel like there's a way out, short of ruling that PCs get dice tricks while NPCs don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T16:22:01-08:00","id":1365391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1365384#post1365384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you give static values to Attack Charms and dice tricks to Defense Charms, doesn't that just swap the problem around? In that scenario the player won't know his odds of succeeding at an attack because of the dice tricks the NPCs might have for defense.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really feel like there's a way out, short of ruling that PCs get dice tricks while NPCs don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The player won't know anyways, unless they've seen all the defense charms the NPC has <i>and</i> can correctly guess which ones the NPC will use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T18:48:11-08:00","id":1365419,"title":"","content":"Right.<br /> <br /> The way the system works right now, the attacker decides how many resources to put into an attack, then the defender decides how to respond. Usually, this will take one of two forms: either they will make a gamble in which they try to spend as few motes as possible while still preventing the attack, or they will decide they cannot reasonably accomplish that (and can live with the consequences) and spend nothing.<br /> <br /> In other words, the system is built around the attacker making their choices blind, then the defender making an informed choice in reply. My concept keeps that dynamic, but tries to make sure the defender actually has that information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T20:43:23-08:00","id":1365462,"title":"","content":"I think we might be having a bit of a clash of playstyles here.<br /> <br /> One big one is that I as an ST and the other guy who STs Exalted in my group fairly rarely use complex antagonists with dice tricks in general. It's not that we never use them, but generally dice tricks aren't super heavy in any quick character antagonists, and in the past 5 campaigns there's only been 3 fully statted up NPCs that have been built from the books.<br /> <br /> The other thing is barring some odd circumstances we're open about what attacks do what. Like if I'm attacking with a full excellency Deathknight with Savage Shade Style, I'll tell them that a 22 die decisive attack with double 10s on damage is coming their way. Part of that is because I consider it fair, since I know all the charms they're coming at my NPCs with, so nobody gets special treatment in that aspect of the game. The other part is that without that knowledge you could get sucker-punched SO hard. &quot;Yeah this rowdy rough looking dude at the bar is throwing a punch, what do you do? Not spend any essence on defense? Damn shame, he was a Brawl supernal Dawn and he knocked you into that mountain with a 20 mote Heaven Thunder Hammer attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's even worse in social interaction. If somebody is using a Read Intentions on you and you have zero idea about the nature of the read, or even who's doing it, you have no clue what's appropriate to spend on defense.<br /> <br /> It can sometimes sort of spoil a mystery about the identity of a person, but not too often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T00:01:01-08:00","id":1365491,"title":"","content":"I do the same, generally, NPCs probably don't have dice tricks and if they do, the PCs will know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T04:00:36-08:00","id":1365516,"title":"","content":"Oh, I don't believe in keeping that sort of thing a secret. That way lies hurt feelings and dead PCs.<br /> <br /> I just also have not found that most people (myself included) are great at quickly estimating expected successes when it gets much more complicated than dice divided by two. There's a lot to keep track of in an Exalted fight, after all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T04:55:41-08:00","id":1365523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1365462#post1365462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we might be having a bit of a clash of playstyles here.<br /> <br /> One big one is that I as an ST and the other guy who STs Exalted in my group fairly rarely use complex antagonists with dice tricks in general. It's not that we never use them, but generally dice tricks aren't super heavy in any quick character antagonists, and in the past 5 campaigns there's only been 3 fully statted up NPCs that have been built from the books.<br /> <br /> The other thing is barring some odd circumstances we're open about what attacks do what. Like if I'm attacking with a full excellency Deathknight with Savage Shade Style, I'll tell them that a 22 die decisive attack with double 10s on damage is coming their way. Part of that is because I consider it fair, since I know all the charms they're coming at my NPCs with, so nobody gets special treatment in that aspect of the game. The other part is that without that knowledge you could get sucker-punched SO hard. &amp;quot;Yeah this rowdy rough looking dude at the bar is throwing a punch, what do you do? Not spend any essence on defense? Damn shame, he was a Brawl supernal Dawn and he knocked you into that mountain with a 20 mote Heaven Thunder Hammer attack.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> It's even worse in social interaction. If somebody is using a Read Intentions on you and you have zero idea about the nature of the read, or even who's doing it, you have no clue what's appropriate to spend on defense.<br /> <br /> It can sometimes sort of spoil a mystery about the identity of a person, but not too often.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's recommended anyway in the Charm section that everyone announces the Charms they are using","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T07:50:04-08:00","id":1365726,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to doubt that EE will be simple enough to cover my current needs... if things like onslaught penalties are around, I think I'll pass. <br /> <br /> I remember that the original Ex3 developers were somewhat dismissive about suggestions and/or petitions. I really hope that the people behind EE are more open and listen to what the fans want (I would put special attention on what the players who have left said in the past), because otherwise all this project will be pretty useless IMO.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T08:01:02-08:00","id":1365728,"title":"","content":"Are Onslaught penalties still going to be around?<br /> <br /> When I asked the writers about Onslaught, Motes, Initiative, Willpower, etc, etc, they said that they couldn't really answer specific questions, but the amount of things to keep track of was something they were very much bearing in mind.<br /> <br /> Make of that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-06-2020, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T08:06:32-08:00","id":1365730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1365728#post1365728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Overwhelming penalties still going to be around?<br /> <br /> When I asked the writers are Overwhelming, Motes, Initiative, Willpower, etc, etc, they said that they couldn't really answer specific questions, but the amount of things to keep track of was something they were very much bearing in mind.<br /> <br /> Make of that what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talking about Onslaught I guess","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T08:28:01-08:00","id":1365735,"title":"","content":"Sorry, only had half my brain engaged there (long week, not enough sleep). Edited that post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T10:01:06-08:00","id":1365757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1365726#post1365726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that the original Ex3 developers were somewhat dismissive about suggestions and/or petitions. I really hope that the people behind EE are more open and listen to what the fans want (I would put special attention on what the players who have left said in the past), because otherwise all this project will be pretty useless IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, the EE devs' interactions with the Discord community so far have shown a clear openness to fan feedback and a realistic take on the current state and shortcomings of 3e.<br /> <br /> We won't know how good EE will be until we see it, but so far I trust that it won't turn into a pet project disconnected from the fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T11:07:39-08:00","id":1365766,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the whole point if E:E is because of people complaining about the mechanics of Exalted, so they kind of have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T13:53:26-08:00","id":1365831,"title":"","content":"The EE devs are also dealing with a spectrum of fans, not two well defined camps. There's very little they can do to avoid having some fans that feel EE didn't go far enough, and some fans that feel like they're smack in the middle of Ex3 and EE and getting either to work for their group would be an equal amount of work.<br /> <br /> The goal of EE should be to please as many fans as possible, not to please all of them. It sucks to be someone that EE doesn't help have fun with the official books, but there's no reason to put the project down (even after release) if it helps ~60% of the people that aren't feeling Ex3, just because you fall into the ~40% it doesn't. That's still lots of people the book would be making happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T06:10:38-08:00","id":1366751,"title":"","content":"If EE can please 60% of all the fans who are not feeling Ex3e as is, that'd be pretty good mark. More would be better, of course, but probably unrealistic.<br /> <br /> I really hope that (going of Epitome's last sentence) the EE Devs will show their work more openly (and early) than the Ex3e Devs did, so that we know if it is for us or not. That is one of the things I'm still most bitter about the Ex3e Core KS. The &quot;trust us, it's awesome&quot; lines all the time without having anything concrete to show...and then a years long delay because most of it had to be rewritten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25439-mnemon-liranan","name":"Mnemon Liranan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T10:03:42-08:00","id":1366800,"title":"","content":"I think all the current writers know that didn't work well; hence the Discord with the writers of E:E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T11:04:16-08:00","id":1366813,"title":"","content":"There's apparently <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once\">an entire thread right now</a> about how impractical it is to run a five-on-one boss fight in <i>Exalted</i>.<br /> <br /> Is this something you think is crucial for <i>Exalted: Essence</i> to nail?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T13:00:49-08:00","id":1366835,"title":"","content":"Ehhhhhhhhhhhhh...<br /> <br /> The issue with that isn't that the rules are too complex, it's that (some argue) the idea of the game is that 5 combat-orientated Solars are one of the most dangerous groups in the entire world, and so you'd have to be ludicrously powerful to beat them 1 vs 5. Third-Circle Demon level, at least.<br /> Others feel that this idea leads to bad games. I can see both sides, personally.<br /> <br /> So nailing that would be a setting change. Whether that's good or bad... well, you can see the argument about that on that thread.<br /> <br /> Whereas what I really would like it nail is to make it practical to run a 5 on 5 boss fight (say, circle of Solars vs circle of Abyssals) which... well I wouldn't say it's impossible, but it's awkward. Depending on the XP level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T13:05:37-08:00","id":1366837,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t wonder if it might be better for the system to make it harder to casually pick up master levels of excellence in a certain area, combat in particular. I\u2019m not sure though, it is nice not being held down and instead being free to make yourself a great warrior in addition to anything else you might do. On the other hand I\u2019ve played in systems that had a lot of non-combat depth to them before where they DID hold you down and force you to pick, and I didn\u2019t personally feel that was unfair.<br /> <br /> Like if you had ten ability dots to distribute and raising them cost 3 bonus points, to throw out the first thing that came to my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T13:08:22-08:00","id":1366839,"title":"","content":"It would be a lot easier to accomplish functional solo bosses if the system made greater allowances for asymmetric design, and given the people involved and some of their previous works (Storypath, most prominently), I expect at least <i>some</i> of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 02-10-2020, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T14:05:23-08:00","id":1366855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1366835#post1366835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhhhhhhhhhhhh...<br /> <br /> The issue... is that 5 combat-orientated Solars are one of the most dangerous groups in the entire world, and so you'd have to be ludicrously powerful to beat them 1 vs 5. Third-Circle Demon level, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Yeah, that's probably why only one of the Solar Castes is strictly combat-oriented, whereas the non-Fire Aspects of the Dragon-Blooded are more inherently combat-oriented than the non-Dawn Solar Castes.<br /> <br /> And, honestly, I can imagine plenty of purely Dragon-Blooded games where all of the players are Fire Aspects, which is much more likely to happen in Creation than running across a circle of five Dawns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T14:52:29-08:00","id":1366865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1366855#post1366855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. Yeah, that's probably why only one of the Solar Castes is strictly combat-oriented, whereas the non-Fire Aspects of the Dragon-Blooded are more inherently combat-oriented than the non-Dawn Solar Castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's trivially easy for any Solar Caste to start with 5 dots in a Combat Ability (or that +5 dots in Resistance/Dodge). In fact, in my experience 80% of Solars do.<br /> That's not to say they necessarily have a ton of combat charms. Most non-Dawns after all, are played by people who probably don't want Combat to be their number 1 focus (well... most Zenith, Twilight and Eclipse players, after all). But it's often a secondary thing.<br /> <br /> But anyway, if your argument is &quot;most Solar groups have 1 dude who's awesome at combat and a bunch of people who are okay, not great&quot; then... well, I wouldn't quite agree (I wouldn't totally disagree either though, I suspect my group leans more towards that than most groups though), but that's an issue to take up over on the other thread.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't think this is an issue with the Ex3 rules per-se, but rather player attitudes to a character creation that says &quot;you've got 25 abilities to choose, pick X to be good at&quot; and you absolutely can be really good at, say, Crafting, Investigation, Medicine, and still also be pretty decent at cutting people into meaty chunks if you're not that bothered at being terrible at Linguistics/Bureaucracy/Ride/Larceny/Stealth/whatever.<br /> <br /> Now saying that, DrLoveMonkey does raise a good point with this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t wonder if it might be better for the system to make it harder to casually pick up master levels of excellence in a certain area, combat in particular. </div> </div> </div>I often feel like the Combat Abilities (and also probably Presence and Awareness) are... well, kind of more useful for most people than a lot of the Abilities. But they are the same cost.<br /> And often what this means, I think, is that, say your character concept is &quot;brilliant writer&quot;, you put 3 of your starting 28 dots into Linguistics, then 3 into Lore, and then...<br /> Well, you've still got 22 dots left. Where do you put them? It's not really surprising that for a lot of characters, 3 are chucked into Melee just in case, in a way that they're not thrown into Sail or Bureaucracy or Craft (Cooking).<br /> <br /> And then you can put 7 of them from 3 to 5 (and still have an extra merit dot left over). Is it very surprising that so many characters start with 5 in a combat ability?<br /> I mean, I started with Brawl 1... and honestly, it has been a problem. Absolutely that was a sub-optimal decision (which I knew at the time, I was just fed up with Solars who turn up with 5 dots in a Combat Ability).<br /> <br /> I find that... a bit weird I guess (not my Zenith being beaten up, I mean how 75% of Exalts have Melee 5). I mean, I like how flexible Exalted's character creation system. But it does feel a little strange.<br /> I honestly considered just saying &quot;PCs can't start with 5 dots in a combat ability if they're not a Dawn&quot;. Although in the end I just got everyone to play Lunars instead (their character creation is a bit more balanced).<br /> <br /> So that's something that bears thinking about.<br /> <br /> I mean, personally I feel the sheer amount of 5s a Solar can start with (7, if you feel like it. 11 if you include Attributes as well as Abilities) devalues having 5 dots in something. This is partly caused by Solar character creation, and partly because most charms actually need pretty high Abilities to get.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see more spread out Solar characters, and I'd be quite happy if E:E used a slightly different character gen system (or quite different) which facilitated that (or at least, didn't encourage silliness so much). I'm not sure how many other people would feel the same as me though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-10-2020, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T15:18:49-08:00","id":1366868,"title":"","content":"I'd say the problem is partially how broad characters are. I remember seeing a complaint about how people had \u2022\u2022\u2022+ in Abilities that their concept didn't support, and I was <i>very</i> tempted to point out that you can't really avoid that. \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 is a lot! <br /> If you tightly distribute them, you've got \u2022\u2022\u2022 in seven Abilities. Almost 1/3rd of the list! Is there any concept that really supports that? <br /> If you moderately distribute them, you've got \u2022\u2022 in fourteen Abilities. Almost 2/3rds of the list! Is there any concept that really supports that? <br /> If you spread them out, you've got \u2022 in every Ability. Is there any concept that really supports that? <br /> <br /> The opportunity cost of jamming a \u2022\u2022\u2022 into Melee is pretty low. The cost of not having a fighty thing at \u2022\u2022\u2022 is pretty high, since in my experience almost every session of every game has at least one fight. <br /> This is in theory solvable by designing all combat encounters such that non-combat individuals can significantly contribute without exposing themselves to undue harm and by using their non-combat abilities, but that's bloody hard work for the GM so it's not practical. <br /> <br /> A solution I've been toying with in my head is compressing Caste Abilities. The Dawn can buy Dawn \u2022\u2022\u2022, and get swords, bows, troops, the works in a compact package. Everybody else has to pick between Melee, Brawl, Thrown, etc. That would allow for a slashing of the Ability dot budget. &quot;Caste at \u2022\u2022\u2022, then distribute \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022&quot; would result in much tighter characters - assuming that they're hewing tightly to Caste. <br /> <br /> <br /> But really? Unless Essence has a good system of benchmarks and power thresholds, I'm going to be running Exalted in HERO if I run it again. At least there I can say &quot;Alright everyone. This much accuracy, this much evasion, this much defense, this much damage, these limits on skills. Your Caste gives you bonuses that don't count towards this, see the handout.&quot; and have it work nice and tidy. EX3's got good ideas, but the implementation isn't worth slogging through the problems when I can transplant the great bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T22:31:43-08:00","id":1366920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1366868#post1366868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A solution I've been toying with in my head is compressing Caste Abilities. The Dawn can buy Dawn \u2022\u2022\u2022, and get swords, bows, troops, the works in a compact package. Everybody else has to pick between Melee, Brawl, Thrown, etc. That would allow for a slashing of the Ability dot budget. &quot;Caste at \u2022\u2022\u2022, then distribute \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022&quot; would result in much tighter characters - assuming that they're hewing tightly to Caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might enjoy the original Tomb of Five Corners Quickstart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T01:54:13-08:00","id":1366929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1366813#post1366813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's apparently <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once\">an entire thread right now</a> about how impractical it is to run a five-on-one boss fight in <i>Exalted</i>.<br /> <br /> Is this something you think is crucial for <i>Exalted: Essence</i> to nail?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll go a little bit against the usual answers given on this forum by talking about my personal preference : Modular difficulty. When my players want to fight Octavian in an epic fight, I don't care if they are the 5 most dangerous Dawn on the world, or just a simple group with 2 almost good fighters and 1 caster and 1 something else, I want the challenge to adapt to the story we want to tell. So I think what I want is rather simple rules and tools on how to properly and simply balance NPC's for different kind of challenge and group of players.<br /> <br /> for this, I believe the most usual tropes of fighting in the genre that is Exalted are : <br /> - Team vs Team <br /> - Team vs 1<br /> - Team vs Team vs Team <br /> - 1v1 <br /> - Team vs Team in some sort of skill challenge-related fight<br /> <br /> I don't expect all boxes to be checked, but the more the better I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T10:02:13-08:00","id":1367246,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it a bit, I'm not sure this is really an E:E thing to be doing, but addressing the list there, I think there's a relatively simple approach (conceptually): design everything around team vs. team.<br /> <br /> Something that's vaguely present in Ex3 if not really given as much love as it could, is the idea of having single big monsters handled as group of parts. That really just turns big single boss battles into a team vs team design, even if in-universe one team is only one character. But instead a lot of the bigger beasties rely on things like Legendary Size to make them hard to take down (until the PCs get to the point of being able to blow past those bonuses anyway).<br /> <br /> It's already a pretty well defined aspect of the game that Exalted vs. Exalted fights tend to be group affairs. You expect Lunars vs. the Wyld Hunt, or Solars vs. Abyssals to be team fights.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you'd expect minions and battle groups to turn things into team fights. You don't get into a fight with Mask of Winters without getting into a fight with his army.<br /> <br /> 1v1 generally works fine in a team vs.team design paradigm because it's just two small teams.<br /> <br /> More than two teams, and skill related challenge things (I'm guessing that might mean something like Sail fights where there's the sailing part and the boarding part), shouldn't be too hard to layer onto a solid team vs team design.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue is the ST overhead of having to run a team of enemies (esp. since a BG really only counts as one). with the relative complexity each team member is going to have in a 5 on 5 Exalted slugfest. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:26:01-08:00","id":1367502,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> While I'm generally ok with &quot;big boss as a team&quot; design, I think that there is a deeper problem here. As the discussion in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...solars-at-once</a> some people are really attached to Exalted 3e design paradigm that Solars start very near the top of what human-like being can achieve in the setting and it's rather that design decision that seems to be. So the main problem is: expectations differ whether we even want fights against old masters in our game (everyone seems ok to a group fight against an eldritch abomination though).<br /> <br /> As I wrote there, I'm much more attached to the idea that Solars are powerful in the absoulute, not relative sense (I'm ok with them struggling with old arcane sifus), so I'd very interested if the new system allows to make boss fights viable.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a><br /> When I think about it, I think that your division misses some essential distinctions. I'd bring five broad categories of fight participants:<br /> - team<br /> - mooks<br /> - master/nemesis<br /> - monster<br /> - hero/rivals<br /> <br /> Team fights should play out differently against an anti-circle of Abyssals and against a horde of faceless mooks. Similarly, a boss fight with an old sifu (which could be treated as a team) should be different than a fight with Wyld behemoth (I'd be ok with the last one being represented more as series of enviromental threats and some challenges).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-13-2020, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:33:19-08:00","id":1367504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1367502#post1367502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> While I'm generally ok with &quot;big boss as a team&quot; design, I think that there is a deeper problem here. As the discussion in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...solars-at-once</a> some people are really attached to Exalted 3e design paradigm that Solars start very near the top of what human-like being can achieve in the setting and it's rather that design decision that seems to be. So the main problem is: expectations differ whether we even want fights against old masters in our game (everyone seems ok to a group fight against an eldritch abomination though).<br /> <br /> As I wrote there, I'm much more attached to the idea that Solars are powerful in the absoulute, not relative sense (I'm ok with them struggling with old arcane sifus), so I'd very interested if the new system allows to make boss fights viable.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a><br /> When I think about it, I think that your division misses some essential distinctions. I'd bring five broad categories of fight participants:<br /> - team<br /> - mooks<br /> - master/nemesis<br /> - monster<br /> - hero/rivals<br /> <br /> Team fights should play out differently against an anti-circle of Abyssals and against a horde of faceless mooks. Similarly, a boss fight with an old sifu (which could be treated as a team) should be different than a fight with Wyld behemoth (I'd be ok with the last one being represented more as series of enviromental threats and some challenges).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes of course, I didn't list all the tropes and I thank you for listing more. I think going by enemy type is a good idea as well, I actually like the Battle Groups of Exalted as of now (even if they have flaws)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T05:49:17-08:00","id":1368720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1365726#post1365726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to doubt that EE will be simple enough to cover my current needs... if things like onslaught penalties are around, I think I'll pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't said anything about onslaught penalties. What information are you basing your doubts on, precisely?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I remember that the original Ex3 developers were somewhat dismissive about suggestions and/or petitions. I really hope that the people behind EE are more open and listen to what the fans want (I would put special attention on what the players who have left said in the past), because otherwise all this project will be pretty useless IMO. </div> </div> </div>There are people on this project who are new to Exalted with Ex3; there are people who came on board with Ex2; and three of us, including two of the devs, have been with the line since Ex1 (in my case, I pre-ordered the corebook).<br /> <br /> We have been listening to fans and what they don't like about Exalted for a long, long, long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T06:14:01-08:00","id":1368728,"title":"","content":"I found the writers on Discord seemed to take what people said seriously. They didn't actually answer all the questions with &quot;this is what we're going to do&quot;, but I didn't expect them to, but they did take everything seriously, and it sounded like they took the amount of things you have to keep track of in Exalted seriously as a big priority for simplicity. They also said they wanted to reduce the amount of steps you have to go through, which'd be great for speeding up, say, combat.<br /> <br /> Of course, no-one writes a game and tells fans &quot;yeah, it's going to be sh**&quot;, everyone says &quot;my game is going to be great!&quot;, but I found their attitude quite different to Holden and John's, just the fact that you can talk to them a bit on Discord is very different.<br /> <br /> I think if you hate the core mechanic of Exalted (ie Attribute+Ability dice) you're not going to like it, but it does sound like it will be simpler.<br /> (Personally, I want it to be about 20-40% simpler, not completely simplified. But I guess different people will want different things.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-18-2020, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T07:03:37-08:00","id":1368739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1368728#post1368728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you hate the core mechanic of Exalted (ie Attribute+Ability dice) you're not going to like it, but it does sound like it will be simpler.<br /> (Personally, I want it to be about 20-40% simpler, not completely simplified. But I guess different people will want different things.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If it were exalted fourth edition I\u2019d want 20% simpler. For a one-off Exalted: Lite I think closer to 40%-60% just so people who really can\u2019t deal with the complexity can still play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T10:03:58-08:00","id":1368760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1368739#post1368739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it were exalted fourth edition I\u2019d want 20% simpler. For a one-off Exalted: Lite I think closer to 40%-60% just so people who really can\u2019t deal with the complexity can still play.</div> </div> </div> </div>40-60% would suit my group.<br /> <br /> I love Exalted's complexity. My group doesn't. If EE isn't pick-up-and-play then it won't suit us.<br /> <br /> A simplified Exalted doesn't have to appeal <i>to me</i>, but it really does have to cater to people who want a simplified Exalted. 20% won't cut it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T10:24:57-08:00","id":1368764,"title":"","content":"And, as has been discussed, complexity isn't actually something as simple as a percentage to increase or decrease anyway.<br /> <br /> A version of Exalted that barely decreases the complexity on STs, but drastically decreases the complexity on players is going to appeal to a lot of people because a lot of groups already have that sort of dynamic. Meanwhile it's going to turn off a lot of other people because it doesn't matter how fun it is to be an Exalted player if nobody will run the game for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T10:28:23-08:00","id":1368765,"title":"","content":"That's probably true John. While I can (and do) cope with Exalted's complexity, even when it sometimes irritates me, and so just a bit less complexity would be fine with me, there's plenty of others who want a waaaaaaaaaay simpler game. And if E:E is too simple for me, I'll continue playing regular Exalted, while those who want a much more simple game will play E:E.<br /> <br /> Of course, what 20% or 40% or 60% simpler actually looks like might be envisaged differently by different people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-18-2020, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T10:32:01-08:00","id":1368767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1368764#post1368764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A version of Exalted that barely decreases the complexity on STs, but drastically decreases the complexity on players is going to appeal to a lot of people because a lot of groups already have that sort of dynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be mostly fine with that, although I would like it to be much easier to run groups of NPCs in combat. Especially high-essence Dragonblood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T13:41:31-08:00","id":1368795,"title":"","content":"Me as well, but I've STed all three editions of Exalted and while not perfect, I'm capable of handling the complexity without it getting to be unfun for me. While I definitely have players that avoid Exalted for the complexity. So I'm definitely in the camp of people served best if E:E focuses on making things easier on the players.<br /> <br /> It was more of my way of saying the same thing about &quot;X%&quot; not being the same thing to different people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T14:31:17-08:00","id":1368799,"title":"","content":"Oh, definitely.<br /> <br /> And of course, it may put off new STs.<br /> <br /> Although when one of my friends started playing it, with an ST who'd never run games before 3rd ed, that new ST's frustration wasn't complexity, but lack of enemies and challenges for Solars. Which was something I, as an experienced ST, could sympathise with (it's better now, but there was a loooong gap between the Core and anything else).<br /> <br /> Hopefully E:E will face that issue with the fact that there's rules for 10 Exalt types, and hopefully a simpler system will mean it's simpler to make/run a bunch of evil Abyssal/Infernal NPCs, fanatical Dragonblood anathema-hunters, or vile Solar demon-kings for your players to face off against.<br /> (There's also the hope that there'll be lots of much quicker/simpler Quick Character Exalts, so you don't have to make your own, but I'm not very hopeful of that due to space constraints. Still, if there's an experienced and inexperienced example NPC for each type, that'd be 20. I'd like to see some Raksha, Demons, and giant monsters too. Obviously to fit all that in they probably would have to be a lot simpler though.*)<br /> <br /> <br /> *I know they're planning on doing a conversion guide, so you could convert the 2nd circle demons, behemoths, etc, from Hundred Devils, but that's the sort of thing which is fine for the experienced, happy-with-complexity ST with the group that finds Exalted too complex, but not so much for the ST who doesn't want to do so much work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-18-2020, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T15:04:14-08:00","id":1368804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1368799#post1368799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although when one of my friends started playing it, with an ST who'd never run games before 3rd ed, that new ST's frustration wasn't complexity, but lack of enemies and challenges for Solars. Which was something I, as an experienced ST, could sympathise with (it's better now, but there was a loooong gap between the Core and anything else).</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this to be much more a factor of there not being a Storyteller Guide more than anything. Or any non-quickstart-jumpstart-newbie example campaigns. Having no direction about what kinds of challenges I'm supposed to be facing my PCs with, and in what amounts, and with what complications is not good.<br /> <br /> I hope I'm not coming across as angry, but the Exalted 3e system was designed with some kind of idea for how it might function while it was working. It would be good as an ST to be let in on what that was exactly. The DnD DMG is fairly comprehensive about what it expects the challenges of the players to be facing, and if you don't live up to those the system breaks apart. The published campaigns also act as good ways to reinforce that, and give good examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T08:10:49-08:00","id":1369133,"title":"","content":"Essence will have Character Creation templates for Essence 3 and Essence 5 starts.<br /> <br /> I have no strong opinion on that tbh, but it's something that's been previewed, so there you go.<br /> <br /> Oh, and their intention with Craft is that it not be &quot;a mini-game relegated to downtime&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T08:29:17-08:00","id":1369137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369133#post1369133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and their intention with Craft is that it not be &amp;quot;a mini-game relegated to downtime&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be good with some chance there can be ideas to use for the Core rules","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T09:03:13-08:00","id":1369140,"title":"","content":"The Core Craft rules are a mini-game, but they're not relegated to downtime (which is kind of good, but can also be awkward); whereas the 2nd ed rules were straightforward and not a strange point-building mini-game... but they were relegated to downtime for the most part.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Crucible of Legend (the ST Guide) I<i> think*</i> was mentioned to be intended to provide alternate Craft rules anyway. Some people are very happy with the Craft rules actually, others hate them, so it's the sort of thing that having alternate rules works for (it's also something that's very self-contained; you have to rewrite one charm tree per splat. Whereas if you rewrote, say, combat, you'd need to rewrite about 6 charm trees per splat).<br /> <br /> *Not 100% sure on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T19:57:42-08:00","id":1369272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1368720#post1368720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We haven't said anything about onslaught penalties. What information are you basing your doubts on, precisely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant that in the hypothetical case in which things like onslaught penalties are still in the game. In fact I don't know where to look for information about EE outside of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T01:13:57-08:00","id":1369301,"title":"","content":"Discord.<br /> <br /> I'll copy-paste the pinned messages from there in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T07:07:35-08:00","id":1369359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369301#post1369301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discord.<br /> <br /> I'll copy-paste the pinned messages from there in a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do. I struggle to watch stuff on Discord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T08:16:54-08:00","id":1369378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Writers on Discord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Exalted: Essence features streamlined rules for a enw way of playing a classic game, incorerating story-focused action and a presentation designed to appeal to new players and longtime fans alike.<br /> <br /> Featuring multiple classic Exalt types with Charms for each, written to enable ease of play, Exalted: Essence emphasizes story over character, character over mechanics, and mechanics over minutiae in order to drive Exalted toward engaging players.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">It is NOT a new edition</span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">It's planned for one release.</span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Just as a writer on the line, it's pretty self contained; the setting is the same, so if you want a deep dive on, say, the blessed isle and Dragon Blooded you'd go to the existing books.</span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The system itself is still in alpha so I'm gonna not answer any mechanical questions in detail</span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Nothing\u2019s changing [fluff-wise], just how we present it</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The one thing I want to say is that we very carefully assembled this team of veterans to make sure all things are thought of.</span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Of course, we\u2019ve only teased what\u2019s in this book, because this is just the first announcement, but here are a few clarifications from the team on a few things that people have some questions about<b></b>: - A lot of people have been speculating on the system, so we can definitely confirm it\u2019s still a version of the Storyteller System and not Storypath or something else.<br /> <br /> Castes/Aspects, etc. will still come into play, but as variations on the main Exalt types. The 10 Exalt types included will be Solars, Lunars, Dragon-Blooded, Exigents, Sidereals, Getimians, Liminals, Abyssals, Alchemicals, and Infernals.<br /> <br /> There will be some setting information in Essence, enough to run games set across Creation, though players and Storytellers can certainly supplement setting information and history with any of the current and forthcoming Exalted 3e books. - Players and Storytellers won\u2019t need to be familiar with any other Exalted books or editions to run a game of Exalted Essence.<br /> <br /> Our main goal regarding Exalted Essence is to capture the feel of Exalted: the vast, epic-fantasy game that has captured imaginations for almost two decades. Now, I\u2019d also like to step back a bit and go into our impetus for creating a \u201clighter\u201d version of Exalted 3rd. Obviously, Exalted 3rd Edition is a huge book. It has a lot of pages, it\u2019s heavy, and inside, it covers a ton of material with a gigantic Charms chapter, and then several more chapters for other powers. (Obviously, this is a titanic simplification of EX3, but I\u2019m not going into an analysis of everything in there, this is already a long blog post).<br /> <br /> What I\u2019m saying is that EX3 is daunting just to look at when you sit down to play. If you hear about it, and want to get it, it costs a lot to buy, it costs a lot to ship, and the page count pushes the limits of book binding technology. Then we look past that, and the material within is also daunting, even to experienced Exalted players.</span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Each Exalt Type will have a short description talking about who they are, and what they do. If you want dozens of pages or lore and history - you'll have to buy the 3e splatbook (we want you to!) Each Exalt type will also have something we're currently calling Exalt Advantages (name subject to change). Each Exalt has two (currently). An example of this that's far from a spoiler: Lunars get Shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then you get Caste/Aspect Advantages, which (currently) have multiple effects. One passive, the rest active - associated with using your anima. </span></span></div> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>still subject to change</b></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Motes: will be committed or spent. How many motes a character has is being worked out. Committed motes come back after X period of time where X is the duration listed in the charm. Spent motes must be recovered (through stunts, rest, hearthstones, etc). That's about all I can say right now.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Let's make up an example, sure. You have an Awareness Charm where you'd committ 10m for the scene. You'd get those 10m back automatically when the scene is over.</span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You can expect to see overall smaller numbers. How small, TBD</span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">We're sticking with the major places from each direction - classic ones and some new stuff from 3e - and keeping it pretty simple and straightforward, with a focus on how STs can use it and how players can be FROM there. It's meant to be a pick up and play kinda deal</span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Each Exalt type will have Modes on Universal Charms that frame their unique expression of that Charm. These</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> will never be </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>worse</i></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">than the base Charm.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">[On Craft]</span></span></span></span></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">My notes on the outline say &quot;make this not a mini game relegated to downtime&quot; I don't have anything more concrete to spoil there. Sorry to everyone itching to know.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about the formatting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-23-2020, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T08:46:59-08:00","id":1369385,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m glad to hear that the modes will never be worse than the base charm. Some of my players have expressed frustration with the Terrestrial keyword in choosing MA. Like you read the charm, get excited, and then get brought down when you read the terrestrial wording.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T08:55:29-08:00","id":1369386,"title":"","content":"In theory, it makes no difference, but it in terms of how it comes across to players, yeah I can see that.<br /> It's also generally a little easier to remember a charm+upgrade than remember a charm-nerf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T09:50:48-08:00","id":1369397,"title":"","content":"&quot;Exalt Advantages&quot;...<br /> <br /> I would like to humbly suggest introducing the word &quot;Host&quot; to designate a &quot;kind&quot; of Exaltation. The Solar Host is all of the Solar Exalted, the Lunar Host is Lunars, the Celestial Host refers to all kinds of Celestial Exalted, the Terrestrial Host is the Dragon-Blooded...<br /> <br /> The Exigent &quot;Host&quot; would also work, since all Exigents, regardless of patron, owe their Exaltations to the Flame of Exigence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Therefore, instead of &quot;Exalt Advantages&quot;, the phrase could be &quot;Host Advantages&quot;.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, &quot;Patron Advantages&quot; works just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T04:37:58-08:00","id":1369550,"title":"","content":"Where can I find the Discord?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T01:58:28-08:00","id":1369797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369378#post1369378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry about the formatting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you break the lists just before each en-dash? That was really hard on my eyes (not your fault I have migraines/visual snow plus other stuff, and it's worse than usual right now).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T02:38:21-08:00","id":1369800,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a> How is this? (Also thanks for this Wizard.)<br /> <br /> Exalted: Essence features streamlined rules for a enw way of playing a classic game, incorerating story-focused action and a presentation designed to appeal to new players and longtime fans alike. Featuring multiple classic Exalt types with Charms for each, written to enable ease of play, Exalted: Essence emphasizes story over character, character over mechanics, and mechanics over minutiae in order to drive Exalted toward engaging players.<br /> <br /> It is NOT a new edition.<br /> <br /> It's planned for one release.<br /> <br /> Just as a writer on the line, it's pretty self contained; the setting is the same, so if you want a deep dive on, say, the blessed isle and Dragon Blooded you'd go to the existing books.<br /> <br /> The system itself is still in alpha so I'm gonna not answer any mechanical questions in detail. Nothing\u2019s changing [fluff-wise], just how we present it.<br /> <br /> The one thing I want to say is that we very carefully assembled this team of veterans to make sure all things are thought of.<br /> <br /> Of course, we\u2019ve only teased what\u2019s in this book, because this is just the first announcement, but here are a few clarifications from the team on a few things that people have some questions about<b></b>: <br /> <br /> - A lot of people have been speculating on the system, so we can definitely confirm it\u2019s still a version of the Storyteller System and not Storypath or something else. <br /> <br /> - Castes/Aspects, etc. will still come into play, but as variations on the main Exalt types. The 10 Exalt types included will be Solars, Lunars, Dragon-Blooded, Exigents, Sidereals, Getimians, Liminals, Abyssals, Alchemicals, and Infernals. <br /> <br /> - There will be some setting information in Essence, enough to run games set across Creation, though players and Storytellers can certainly supplement setting information and history with any of the current and forthcoming Exalted 3e books. <br /> <br /> - Players and Storytellers won\u2019t need to be familiar with any other Exalted books or editions to run a game of Exalted Essence. <br /> <br /> - Our main goal regarding Exalted Essence is to capture the feel of Exalted: the vast, epic-fantasy game that has captured imaginations for almost two decades. <br /> <br /> Now, I\u2019d also like to step back a bit and go into our impetus for creating a \u201clighter\u201d version of Exalted 3rd. Obviously, Exalted 3rd Edition is a huge book. It has a lot of pages, it\u2019s heavy, and inside, it covers a ton of material with a gigantic Charms chapter, and then several more chapters for other powers. (Obviously, this is a titanic simplification of EX3, but I\u2019m not going into an analysis of everything in there, this is already a long blog post). What I\u2019m saying is that EX3 is daunting just to look at when you sit down to play. If you hear about it, and want to get it, it costs a lot to buy, it costs a lot to ship, and the page count pushes the limits of book binding technology. Then we look past that, and the material within is also daunting, even to experienced Exalted players.<br /> <br /> <br /> Each Exalt Type will have a short description talking about who they are, and what they do. If you want dozens of pages or lore and history - you'll have to buy the 3e splatbook (we want you to!) Each Exalt type will also have something we're currently calling Exalt Advantages (name subject to change). Each Exalt has two (currently). An example of this that's far from a spoiler: Lunars get Shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then you get Caste/Aspect Advantages, which (currently) have multiple effects. One passive, the rest active - associated with using your anima.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still subject to change:-<br /> <br /> Motes: will be committed or spent. How many motes a character has is being worked out. Committed motes come back after X period of time where X is the duration listed in the charm. Spent motes must be recovered (through stunts, rest, hearthstones, etc). That's about all I can say right now.<br /> <br /> Let's make up an example, sure. You have an Awareness Charm where you'd committ 10m for the scene. You'd get those 10m back automatically when the scene is over.<br /> <br /> You can expect to see overall smaller numbers. How small, TBD.<br /> <br /> - We're sticking with the major places from each direction - classic ones and some new stuff from 3e - and keeping it pretty simple and straightforward, with a focus on how STs can use it and how players can be FROM there. It's meant to be a pick up and play kinda deal<br /> <br /> Each Exalt type will have Modes on Universal Charms that frame their unique expression of that Charm. These<br /> will never be worse than the base Charm.<br /> <br /> [On Craft]<br /> My notes on the outline say &quot;make this not a mini game relegated to downtime&quot; I don't have anything more concrete to spoil there. Sorry to everyone itching to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-23-2020, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T05:34:27-08:00","id":1369818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1366839#post1366839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be a lot easier to accomplish functional solo bosses if the system made greater allowances for asymmetric design, and given the people involved and some of their previous works (Storypath, most prominently), I expect at least <i>some</i> of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhhhhh yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T05:49:13-08:00","id":1369820,"title":"","content":"Ex3 talks a good game about asymmetric design but it's still burdened by a lot of legacy code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"li