d 3e books. <br /> <br /> - Players and Storytellers won\u2019t need to be familiar with any other Exalted books or editions to run a game of Exalted Essence. <br /> <br /> - Our main goal regarding Exalted Essence is to capture the feel of Exalted: the vast, epic-fantasy game that has captured imaginations for almost two decades. <br /> <br /> Now, I\u2019d also like to step back a bit and go into our impetus for creating a \u201clighter\u201d version of Exalted 3rd. Obviously, Exalted 3rd Edition is a huge book. It has a lot of pages, it\u2019s heavy, and inside, it covers a ton of material with a gigantic Charms chapter, and then several more chapters for other powers. (Obviously, this is a titanic simplification of EX3, but I\u2019m not going into an analysis of everything in there, this is already a long blog post). What I\u2019m saying is that EX3 is daunting just to look at when you sit down to play. If you hear about it, and want to get it, it costs a lot to buy, it costs a lot to ship, and the page count pushes the limits of book binding technology. Then we look past that, and the material within is also daunting, even to experienced Exalted players.<br /> <br /> <br /> Each Exalt Type will have a short description talking about who they are, and what they do. If you want dozens of pages or lore and history - you'll have to buy the 3e splatbook (we want you to!) Each Exalt type will also have something we're currently calling Exalt Advantages (name subject to change). Each Exalt has two (currently). An example of this that's far from a spoiler: Lunars get Shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then you get Caste/Aspect Advantages, which (currently) have multiple effects. One passive, the rest active - associated with using your anima.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still subject to change:-<br /> <br /> Motes: will be committed or spent. How many motes a character has is being worked out. Committed motes come back after X period of time where X is the duration listed in the charm. Spent motes must be recovered (through stunts, rest, hearthstones, etc). That's about all I can say right now.<br /> <br /> Let's make up an example, sure. You have an Awareness Charm where you'd committ 10m for the scene. You'd get those 10m back automatically when the scene is over.<br /> <br /> You can expect to see overall smaller numbers. How small, TBD.<br /> <br /> - We're sticking with the major places from each direction - classic ones and some new stuff from 3e - and keeping it pretty simple and straightforward, with a focus on how STs can use it and how players can be FROM there. It's meant to be a pick up and play kinda deal<br /> <br /> Each Exalt type will have Modes on Universal Charms that frame their unique expression of that Charm. These<br /> will never be worse than the base Charm.<br /> <br /> [On Craft]<br /> My notes on the outline say &amp;quot;make this not a mini game relegated to downtime&amp;quot; I don't have anything more concrete to spoil there. Sorry to everyone itching to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Reads like poetry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T08:47:48-08:00","id":1369846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369550#post1369550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I find the Discord?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/AaB3t7\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/AaB3t7\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/AaB3t7\" target=\"_blank\"> https://discord.gg/AaB3t7 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T10:10:55-08:00","id":1369854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369831#post1369831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm counting the removal of all the simulationism that was coded into the Dragon-Blooded and Lunar charmsets to make it easier for Solars to bully them like the &amp;quot;fail against Celestial charms&amp;quot; clause and the particular execution of the Solar Bond. Dungeons and Dragons has never really followed mechanics = story like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>IDK. Awful lot of Deeb and Lunar Charms work off your opponent's 1s.<br /> <br /> It's a lot better. A lot better. But... eh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T10:49:05-08:00","id":1369864,"title":"","content":"Solars themselves have Rumor of Form and Iron Kettle Body getting shut down by Excellent Strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T11:11:04-08:00","id":1369874,"title":"","content":"Solars actually have a ton of charms spread across lots of abilities that rely on opponent's 1s to activate. Generally what Solars have that other exalts don't is the ability to reroll 1s, but even then that's not pervasive. Like Solar Brawl just doesn't reroll 1s on the attack roll ever I'm pretty sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T11:18:59-08:00","id":1369877,"title":"","content":"Technically everyone has limited access to reroll 1s. Jewel of the Rabbit Sword - Arms of the Chosen page 137, I remember being in a Sidereals game in 1st edition and 3/5 PCs had one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T11:39:27-08:00","id":1369885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369877#post1369877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically everyone has limited access to reroll 1s. Jewel of the Rabbit Sword - Arms of the Chosen page 137, I remember being in a Sidereals game in 1st edition and 3/5 PCs had one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, true. I also just did a quick check and Melee is the only Solar combat ability that re-rolls 1s. Or if they do they do it without the words &quot;1s&quot; or &quot;reroll&quot;. Agile Beast Defense for Lunars and Flickering Candle Meditation work just fine against Solar archers, brawlers, martial artists, peltasts, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T22:56:57-08:00","id":1369978,"title":"","content":"Can I count on one of you fellow grognards (said with love) to tell me straight up that Exalted: Essence either is or is not a fancy way of saying 3rd Edition's storyteller's guide? Much obliged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T23:03:59-08:00","id":1369980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369978#post1369978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I count on one of you fellow grognards (said with love) to tell me straight up that Exalted: Essence either is or is not a fancy way of saying 3rd Edition's storyteller's guide? Much obliged.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not that.<br /> <br /> That is Crucible of Legends, which is also currently in development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T01:15:20-08:00","id":1369993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369978#post1369978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I count on one of you fellow grognards (said with love) to tell me straight up that Exalted: Essence either is or is not a fancy way of saying 3rd Edition's storyteller's guide? Much obliged.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a rules-lite(r) version of the core rules. Minimal but basic setting info only, plus a full but stripped back core rules system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T05:36:32-08:00","id":1370039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369993#post1369993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a rules-lite(r) version of the core rules. Minimal but basic setting info only, plus a full but stripped back core rules system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say &quot;minimal but basic&quot; setting info only. I'd say it's specifically tailored for brand-new players to the setting and engineered to help emphasize a character's place in the vastness of Creation. We want new players to come to this book, look over a few pages of setting material, and be like, &quot;I'd like to play a priest from Great Forks who became an Exigent&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T08:36:44-08:00","id":1370060,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Crucible of Legends. Got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T20:48:43-08:00","id":1370222,"title":"","content":"Only just learned of Essence. Given that I love the setting of Exalted<i>, </i>butthe system of every edition so far has been too crunchy for my tastes, an official streamlined version has me optimistic. I've been working with some, admittedly very well put together, fan conversions for other systems so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T00:27:08-08:00","id":1370264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370039#post1370039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say &amp;quot;minimal but basic&amp;quot; setting info only. I'd say it's specifically tailored for brand-new players to the setting and engineered to help emphasize a character's place in the vastness of Creation. We want new players to come to this book, look over a few pages of setting material, and be like, &amp;quot;I'd like to play a priest from Great Forks who became an Exigent&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even better!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T05:26:13-08:00","id":1370319,"title":"","content":"De-Lurk:<br /> <br /> Developers and writers: I would like to know whether special considerations have been taken regarding solo or duo PC play, as opposed to groups of 3 or more. For example, is there an option to play say, a more general Solar exaltation rather than one with a specific caste? Even the Eclipse caste, who are supposed to fill in the gaps, has a specific character and set of abilities that a player may not want, even if they're playing a jack of all trades.<br /> <br /> Now, I can already hear the questions some people might have like &quot;why don't you just talk to your ST about customizing the campaign&quot; and &quot;why don't you just play an Exigent.&quot; And in answer to those questions, I say:<br /> <br /> Look, just humor me, all right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 02-25-2020, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T06:04:47-08:00","id":1370331,"title":"","content":"Nothing has been said about that, tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T10:37:24-08:00","id":1370397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370331#post1370331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing has been said about that, tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's still too early in the process I suppose. It's probably just a thing only I was concerned about anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T10:51:30-08:00","id":1370402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370397#post1370397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it's still too early in the process I suppose. It's probably just a thing only I was concerned about anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just out of curiosity, why is it not good to have castes when running a solo game? Even solo characters have a kind of identity other than master-of-all-trades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T11:46:04-08:00","id":1370415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370402#post1370402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just out of curiosity, why is it not good to have castes when running a solo game? Even solo characters have a kind of identity other than master-of-all-trades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it's perfectly fine and dandy to have castes in a solo game; it can narrow down precisely what a player wants to be doing. You play a solo game and pick a Dawn caste, the ST is probably safe in assuming you want to kick butt most of the time.<br /> <br /> My line of thinking was that since this side(?) edition was focused on making things simpler and more accessible, you might want to take the opportunity to open up character creation more. Since there's less ground to cover, you can let the player roam around more, mix and match things that would be nailed down with strict Caste choice.<br /> <br /> For example: suppose I want to make a solar that combines elements from Dawn, Zenith, and Night castes. I get intimidation bonuses from Dawn, the ability to sanctify corpses from Zenith, and the stealth bonuses from Night. I'm not exactly any one of them specifically, but I have elements from all of them.<br /> <br /> Now that I'm thinking about it, my way is probably not as well thought out as it should be, because specific usually beat general when it comes to making things interesting. But what piqued my curiosity was this quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castes/Aspects, etc. will still come into play, but as variations on the main Exalt types.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Variations? What does that mean? Is it possible they might have some sort of baseline template you can customize to your liking? Will taking a Caste or Aspect still be mandatory?&quot;<br /> <br /> Then this got me to thinking about what kind of play experience having more of a clean slate Exalt would be good for, and thought maybe 1-2 PC groups would appreciate the freedom. 3 or more PCs would probably be better served by having specific roles within the group.<br /> <br /> ...I just realized how much of a logical leap I've taken from just one tiny quote out of context. I really should go lie down. At this rate, I'll qualify for the baseless speculation olympics in no time.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wait, I just read that blurb again and noticed them talking about Caste/Aspect advantages. Implying you get those with every character, ergo every character picks a caste.<br /> <br /> I really need to take a nap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 02-25-2020, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T12:05:27-08:00","id":1370418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370415#post1370415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, it's perfectly fine and dandy to have castes in a solo game; it can narrow down precisely what a player wants to be doing. You play a solo game and pick a Dawn caste, the ST is probably safe in assuming you want to kick butt most of the time.<br /> <br /> My line of thinking was that since this side(?) edition was focused on making things simpler and more accessible, you might want to take the opportunity to open up character creation more. Since there's less ground to cover, you can let the player roam around more, mix and match things that would be nailed down with strict Caste choice.<br /> <br /> For example: suppose I want to make a solar that combines elements from Dawn, Zenith, and Night castes. I get intimidation bonuses from Dawn, the ability to sanctify corpses from Zenith, and the stealth bonuses from Night. I'm not exactly any one of them specifically, but I have elements from all of them.<br /> <br /> Now that I'm thinking about it, my way is probably not as well thought out as it should be, because specific usually beat general when it comes to making things interesting. But what piqued my curiosity was this quote:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Variations? What does that mean? Is it possible they might have some sort of baseline template you can customize to your liking? Will taking a Caste or Aspect still be mandatory?&quot;<br /> <br /> Then this got me to thinking about what kind of play experience having more of a clean slate Exalt would be good for, and thought maybe 1-2 PC groups would appreciate the freedom. 3 or more PCs would probably be better served by having specific roles within the group.<br /> <br /> ...I just realized how much of a logical leap I've taken from just one tiny quote out of context. I really should go lie down. At this rate, I'll qualify for the baseless speculation olympics in no time.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wait, I just read that blurb again and noticed them talking about Caste/Aspect advantages. Implying you get those with every character, ergo every character picks a caste.<br /> <br /> I really need to take a nap.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Caste choice in no way nails anything down. You can make a Dawn with no dots in any combat-relevant Abilities and garbage combat-relevant Attributes. You can make a Twilight god-blending sword-machine. Caste helps you go in a particular direction, it doesn't lock out the other directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T12:14:05-08:00","id":1370422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370418#post1370418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Caste choice in no way nails anything down. You can make a Dawn with no dots in any combat-relevant Abilities and garbage combat-relevant Attributes. You can make a Twilight god-blending sword-machine. Caste helps you go in a particular direction, it doesn't lock out the other directions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah yeah, I know. I'm just being stupid. Never mind me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T12:18:36-08:00","id":1370423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370415#post1370415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My line of thinking was that since this side(?) edition was focused on making things simpler and more accessible, you might want to take the opportunity to open up character creation more. Since there's less ground to cover, you can let the player roam around more, mix and match things that would be nailed down with strict Caste choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I wasn\u2019t even thinking about the caste anima abilities. Everything else in 3e is pretty well wide open. I very much doubt they\u2019ll go that way though, it\u2019s a fairly niche rules variation which is otherwise really easy to houserule.<br /> <br /> Something more likely is ditching exalt types all together and making the whole thing more of a generic system. So there\u2019s no Solar/Lunar/DB divide. If you want to be a glowing golden sunchild who shapeshifts into a bear and breathes fire that\u2019s all good. At which point there\u2019s probably not going to be castes either, except for just choose what you want from a list of all caste abilities.<br /> <br /> That will need some doing for balance though, some anima powers are much more powerful than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T13:30:41-08:00","id":1370434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370319#post1370319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">De-Lurk:<br /> <br /> Developers and writers: I would like to know whether special considerations have been taken regarding solo or duo PC play, as opposed to groups of 3 or more. For example, is there an option to play say, a more general Solar exaltation rather than one with a specific caste? Even the Eclipse caste, who are supposed to fill in the gaps, has a specific character and set of abilities that a player may not want, even if they're playing a jack of all trades.<br /> <br /> Now, I can already hear the questions some people might have like &quot;why don't you just talk to your ST about customizing the campaign&quot; and &quot;why don't you just play an Exigent.&quot; And in answer to those questions, I say:<br /> <br /> Look, just humor me, all right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess this is something that woudl be more for <b>Crucible of Legends</b> than <b>Exalted Essence</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T06:03:24-08:00","id":1370540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370319#post1370319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">De-Lurk:<br /> <br /> Developers and writers: I would like to know whether special considerations have been taken regarding solo or duo PC play, as opposed to groups of 3 or more. For example, is there an option to play say, a more general Solar exaltation rather than one with a specific caste? Even the Eclipse caste, who are supposed to fill in the gaps, has a specific character and set of abilities that a player may not want, even if they're playing a jack of all trades.<br /> <br /> Look, just humor me, all right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The primary focus of play is on single-type and multiple-types; in other words, we're including explicit support for multiple Exalt types running around together. As for a &quot;generic&quot; Solar Exaltation, the biggest element of caste or aspect is in the anima powers, and it might be possible to mix-and-match some of those to your own content.<br /> <br /> And I mean, yes, an Exigent of the Golden Lord would look very much like a generic Solar.<br /> <br /> (I have <i>opinions </i>about wanting to have an out-of-caste Supernal, but even that expression of caste won't be in play in Essence.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 02-26-2020, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:16:28-08:00","id":1370561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1369978#post1369978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I count on one of you fellow grognards (said with love) to tell me straight up that Exalted: Essence either is or is not a fancy way of saying 3rd Edition's storyteller's guide? Much obliged.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Third Edition's &quot;Power Combat&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyone else remember First Edition's &quot;Power Combat&quot;?<br /> <br /> Most of you might instead remember Second Edition's &quot;Dawn Solution&quot; and the &quot;Raksha Fix&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm being facetious, of course. EE sounds a lot more ambitious and promising than any of those other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T09:30:05-08:00","id":1370583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370561#post1370561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Third Edition's &amp;quot;Power Combat&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyone else remember First Edition's &amp;quot;Power Combat&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> Most of you might instead remember Second Edition's &amp;quot;Dawn Solution&amp;quot; and the &amp;quot;Raksha Fix&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm being facetious, of course. EE sounds a lot more ambitious and promising than any of those other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont so please feed me some tales of ancient times !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T12:00:12-08:00","id":1370617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370583#post1370583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont so please feed me some tales of ancient times !</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't do the story justice. I think I found Exalted after Power Combat came to be. But I'll try.<br /> <br /> Maybe 20 years ago, the First Edition system of Exalted had issues. Bugs, that led to unintended styles of play. Listing them would take longer than I care right now, but Power Combat sought to address at least a few of the flaws that were actually considered flaws, especially with the statistics of weapons. So, weapons were rebalanced.<br /> <br /> But since White Wolf didn't want to alienate people who liked the old balance, every character statblock in the game now HAD to include TWO different set of numbers. One for the old system, and one for the new system. It seemed to be a terrible waste of word count, and ugly besides. Certainly I don't imagine it inspired confidence in people considering getting into the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Second Edition inherited a problem from First Edition, whereby the Dawn Caste of the Solar Exalted were not actually more effective at combat than Twilight and Night Castes, who could favor just one &quot;attack Ability&quot; and do just as well as a Dawn, and still have four other Favored Abilities to assist their combat prowess AND supplement their Caste Abilities for doing anything other than fighting.<br /> <br /> Third Edition handily solved this problem with the introduction of Supernal Abilities and giving Dawns the option of picking just one or two &quot;attack Abilities&quot; as Caste Abilities, using their remaining Caste Abilities to supplement those choices with things like Resistance, Dodge, Awareness, and then having Favored Abilities to maybe do something other than fighting. New Anima Abilities sealed the deal.<br /> <br /> But the Dawn Solution happened before that simple solution, and it sought to address the problem by rewarding Dawns for investing in multiple &quot;attack Abilities&quot; (and War) by giving many of those Charms cross-compatibility with other attack Abilities, so that investing in Thrown could make you better with Melee, and War could make you better with the other four Abilities that let you actually hit people. It was much more complicated.<br /> <br /> The Fae Solution was equally ambitious, but far less complicated. It not only involved errata for all of the raksha Charms that could be used in Creation using the normal system, it also basically doubled the raksha Charmset by taking every Charm that COULDN'T be used in Creation, and giving each of them a whole new function that ONLY worked in Creation. (Because NO ONE played the raksha out in the Wyld, because no one gives a shit about the Wyld and the raksha's fairy-only games of make-believe.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T12:13:23-08:00","id":1370619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370540#post1370540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in other words, we're including explicit support for multiple Exalt types running around together.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I'm very much looking forward to, increasing player options from 3 to 10.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but even that expression of caste won't be in play in Essence.) </div> </div> </div>Just checking; you're saying there's no Supernal in Essence?<br /> <br /> (Not that this means the same thing it would in regular 3e, of course, as it's a different system and maybe power levels, charm acquisition, etc, works differently. I'm just interested.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T20:31:59-08:00","id":1370692,"title":"","content":"Off-topic, but I want to share some life-wisdom with y'all.<br /> <br /> You never get older. The world gets younger.<br /> <br /> I can remember the days when I first started paying attention to <i>Exalted</i> like they were last week, but I just had to use the words &quot;20 years ago&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are probably some of you today who weren't even BORN yet.<br /> <br /> I'm still me. I'm not &quot;one of the old people&quot;, because the people I think are older got older along with me. Even if some of them are dead now, most of them are still around.<br /> <br /> But here you are! People younger than me. People like you didn't exist in my world, once. But now there are more people younger than me, and fewer people older.<br /> <br /> It's human nature to notice the changes in the world more than in yourself.<br /> <br /> And just the other day, I was telling a little second-cousin that if she wanted to use the trampoline, she needed to ask the adults, and she asked me, and I realized that from her point of view, I was indistinguishable from any other adult. (So I had to change tactics and inform her that it wasn't my home or trampoline; she had to ask the adults who owned those.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T21:26:30-08:00","id":1370698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370692#post1370692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here you are! People younger than me. People like you didn't exist in my world, once. But now there are more people younger than me, and fewer people older.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also think it's our job to make sure we don't carry any of the crappy frustrating ideas and practices that ruined a lot of previous Exalted games forward with us. Absurd Chungian combat, trying to extrapolate the world from the rules as opposed to the other way around, marginalization of the setting, lava-lamp Wyld, etc. Those can all stay dead in the past and never revived again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T07:50:57-08:00","id":1370759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370698#post1370698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think it's our job to make sure we don't carry any of the crappy frustrating ideas and practices that ruined a lot of previous Exalted games forward with us. Absurd Chungian combat, trying to extrapolate the world from the rules as opposed to the other way around, marginalization of the setting, lava-lamp Wyld, etc. Those can all stay dead in the past and never revived again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, now. Lava-lamp Wyld was exactly what the art, the lore, and the rules framed for us to believe. If something far less extreme was the intent, that's no one's fault but White Wolf.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Yes to all that other stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T08:16:30-08:00","id":1370763,"title":"","content":"What's this lava-lamp ? Btw thanks Sunder The Gold it's really hard when you are new to Exalted (as I am) to realize the legacy some people bears when coming from precedent editions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T08:21:17-08:00","id":1370764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370763#post1370763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's this lava-lamp ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava_lamp\" target=\"_blank\">Lava Lamp</a> uses an incandescent bulb to heat the water in a glass tube to a temperature where the wax submerged in it warms, distorts and rises, cools, and descends back down to start warming up again.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Wyld as it's been described <i>at times</i> seems kind of pointless to interact with beyond scourging it out of existence via Lore Charms, because even when it's <i>not</i> in a state of flux, its details could be changed almost trivially by an interested raksha.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike, would you want to go to Disney World if <i>in the time it took for you to get there</i>, it could be invaded by hordes of walking teeth, the teeth being overthrown by Mickey (who'd been disguising himself as an animatronic), Mickey turning to crystal after his ceaseless crushing of his competitors have left him with no conflict, and then the whole thing becoming a Scooby-Doo theme park in his absence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-27-2020, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T08:36:45-08:00","id":1370766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370764#post1370764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bLike, would you want to go to Disney World if <i>in the time it took for you to get there</i>, it could be invaded by hordes of walking teeth, the teeth being overthrown by Mickey (who'd been disguising himself as an animatronic), Mickey turning to crystal after his ceaseless crushing of his competitors have left him with no conflict, and then the whole thing becoming a Scooby-Doo theme park in his absence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I don't see who wouldn't go to Disney World in these conditions this seems totally awesome !<br /> <br /> I got your point though, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T09:04:17-08:00","id":1370772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370766#post1370766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I don't see who wouldn't go to Disney World in these conditions this seems totally awesome !</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you wouldn't be going to Disney World, though - you'd be going to a Scooby-Doo theme park littered with a suspicious quantity of broken teeth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T09:17:38-08:00","id":1370775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370764#post1370764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe Wyld as it's been described <i>at times</i> seems kind of pointless to interact with beyond scourging it out of existence via Lore Charms, because even when it's <i>not</i> in a state of flux, its details could be changed almost trivially by an interested raksha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> The deepest Wyld is defined by its lack of definition and meaning. Things are so formless that they don't actually exist (Greek Kaos was &quot;nothingness&quot;), and closer to Creation, things only take forms briefly before becoming else so quickly that there's no rhyme or reason; a riot of sound and fury, as told by an idiot, signifying nothing.<br /> <br /> Creation is the most meaningful place in the universe of <i>Exalted</i> in every sense of the word, which is what makes it the most interesting and rewarding of investment by the people in the setting, by the people who write it, and the people who play in it.<br /> <br /> The Wyld is only meaningful or interesting to the extent that it's just a region of vanilla Creation that was twisted just slightly weird by the Wyld, so that you can tell a story that would otherwise be impossible in normal Creation. But the region isn't still in flux; the change happened and then stopped, so that any further change is the result of characters or of natural phenomenon (even if that phenomenon is only natural to that region, it still follows self-consistent laws).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T10:04:08-08:00","id":1370788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370775#post1370775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld is only meaningful or interesting to the extent that it's just a region of vanilla Creation that was twisted just slightly weird by the Wyld, so that you can tell a story that would otherwise be impossible in normal Creation. But the region isn't still in flux; the change happened and then stopped, so that any further change is the result of characters or of natural phenomenon (even if that phenomenon is only natural to that region, it still follows self-consistent laws).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I think that boarder marches or lands tainted by the Wyld are way more interesting. Rockagators are cool, I want some rockagator soup. I also like fyreflies, who can be pretty and luminous, or swarm a village and burn the whole thing to the ground.<br /> <br /> What I'm not a fan of is going out into the Wyld and seeing an army 100,000 strong of fey creatures headed towards Creation, only to have those soldiers shrink and become toy soldiers, only to have them become cats, who then run up a giant tree that's rapidly growing and hang there by their tails, making a cat tree, who then start to drop, and as they drop they become shooting stars, the shooting stars form a person, I ask them who they are, but before I can finish speaking they melt into a puddle, the puddle grows into an ocean, the ocean dries up into a salt flat, a great mouth splits open on the flat, I ask if it's the same creature as it was before, it says it's the only thing that's ever existed, the flat granulates into a desert.<br /> <br /> Wacky fun and imaginative? Oh yes indeed. Just not something I care to experience for more than a few minutes. Rather, give me the 100,000 strong army of various fey creatures from the Wyld, and make them a rag-tag band with their own unique desires and cultures that I can interact with without them changing on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T11:32:10-08:00","id":1370803,"title":"","content":"While we're talking about baggage from the past, tangent, something I would consider if I were helping write a hypothetical Exalted 4th Edition (in 2040 after all the Ex3 books come out)?<br /> <br /> I don't think Exalted needs the Great Curse, really. Limit is said to be part of it, but Occasional Emotional Outbursts don't seem to fit the Slow But Steady Fall From Grace the Great Curse is described as.<br /> <br /> So, hypothetically, how would I describe Limit in an Exaltrd where it's not part of the Curse?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Exalted are people, but greater. Their abilities, their power, their ambitions, and their emotions are far beyond than they were before their Second Breath. Sometimes, their control slips, and their emotions run rampant and wild. This process is called Limit Break.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah. Sometimes Exalts just have too many Feelings. And I'd probably try to mimic something like Strife in the newest edition of Legend of the Five Rings.<br /> <br /> Now, what of the other part of the Great Curse? The decadence and mania of the Solars of the High First Age that led to the Usurpation? Well this may just be me, but I personally don't see a need to blame an external curse for why some people who were blessed with an absurd amount of power, a life span in the thousands of years, and with growing ambitions and desires in a sociopolitical environment that gently approved of them following their whims could have produced enough bad eggs for the Sidereals to go &quot;Right, we should fix this problem&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 02-27-2020, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T12:57:48-08:00","id":1370823,"title":"","content":"I love your idea. It totally fits my vision of Exalted, even better than the Great Curse. It is the nature of the Exalted to go into a greater passion, not some curse. Good suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:07:53-08:00","id":1370827,"title":"","content":"Yeah me too, even if the mechanics stay the same the source being the Exalt themselves might be better. That why the fall and the failings aren't made external to the character. I've had a lot of fun with Limit Breaks in the past, they can really change a story, and they're one of the ways that the different Exalted can have different advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:20:10-08:00","id":1370829,"title":"","content":"I almost completely disagree. I understand the idea, but the problem is that it makes the kind of decadent fall of the First Age feel like an unavoidable inevitability, a critical and unquestionable flaw that makes the Sidereals completely justified in their action. It's hard to feel like a hero when you're part of the problem and there's nothing anybody can do about it except off you when the time is right. It's too negative an assessment of human nature and I don't buy into it.<br /> <br /> I'm all for the mechanic enhancing a game, but as far as world building is concerned, I prefer limit to be external in origin purely because I hate what it says about humanity or the exalted if it is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25921-fffxx","name":"FFFXX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:23:22-08:00","id":1370831,"title":"","content":"I think it's too soon to say. Ex3 hasn't explored the Great Curse much yet because the splats that spend the most time addressing the question of if there really is something seriously wrong with the Solar Exalted and history might be doomed to repeat itself, aren't out yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:25:53-08:00","id":1370833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FFFXX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370829#post1370829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I almost completely disagree. I understand the idea, but the problem is that it makes the kind of decadent fall of the First Age feel like an unavoidable inevitability, a critical and unquestionable flaw that makes the Sidereals completely justified in their action. It's hard to feel like a hero when you're part of the problem and there's nothing anybody can do about it except off you when the time is right. It's too negative an assessment of human nature and I don't buy into it.<br /> <br /> I'm all for the mechanic enhancing a game, but as far as world building is concerned, I prefer limit to be external in origin purely because I hate what it says about humanity or the exalted if it is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I understand your disagreement, I don't see what it changes to specific part of &quot;The Sidereals were right&quot;. I mean the Solar Exalted are already cursed and prone to tremendous actions that can threaten creation, the source of it being an invisible and immutable curse landed by the Primordials or in the inextricable nature of the Exaltation is not relevant to this topic I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:34:57-08:00","id":1370835,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I ponder having Stress instead of Limit, kind of like Darkest Dungeon. Mortals also get a Stress bar, and suffer psychological issues at five dots, and severe physiological ones at 10. Exalted have to be taken to 10 to suffer the psychological effect and aren't in danger of suffering a sudden loss of health from the toll taken on the body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FFFXX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370829#post1370829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I almost completely disagree. I understand the idea, but the problem is that it makes the kind of decadent fall of the First Age feel like an unavoidable inevitability, a critical and unquestionable flaw that makes the Sidereals completely justified in their action. It's hard to feel like a hero when you're part of the problem and there's nothing anybody can do about it except off you when the time is right. It's too negative an assessment of human nature and I don't buy into it.<br /> <br /> I'm all for the mechanic enhancing a game, but as far as world building is concerned, I prefer limit to be external in origin purely because I hate what it says about humanity or the exalted if it is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not human nature that's the problem, though humans can be extra-irrational in the face of losing standing and power. It's the entrenched system of privilege that the ruling order builds up; that's going to start showing cracks in itself as an inevitability. It doesn't need to exist, though, even if the successors are convinced that they need to have the same kind of thing, only on a slightly smaller scale. Surely, it'll work out this time...<br /> <br /> (Narrator: It would not, in fact, work out this time, or any other.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:42:56-08:00","id":1370837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370833#post1370833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although I understand your disagreement, I don't see what it changes to specific part of &quot;The Sidereals were right&quot;. I mean the Solar Exalted are already cursed and prone to tremendous actions that can threaten creation, the source of it being an invisible and immutable curse landed by the Primordials or in the inextricable nature of the Exaltation is not relevant to this topic I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less about them having been right, and more about them continuing to be right. You are correct, it is a bit off topic, so something Essence related:<br /> <br /> I am very excited to see simplified takes on various subsystems (or the removal of them almost entirely? Not sure how they plan to do stuff there). Either way, if a particular mechanic isn't getting a lot of play in a campaign, I could see myself trying to port the Essence version of the subsystem in to keep it simple whenever it does come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25921-fffxx","name":"FFFXX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:18:32-08:00","id":1371001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FFFXX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370837#post1370837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less about them having been right, and more about them continuing to be right. You are correct, it is a bit off topic, so something Essence related:<br /> <br /> I am very excited to see simplified takes on various subsystems (or the removal of them almost entirely? Not sure how they plan to do stuff there). Either way, if a particular mechanic isn't getting a lot of play in a campaign, I could see myself trying to port the Essence version of the subsystem in to keep it simple whenever it does come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry I just realized you misunderstood my post : I didn't mean that you &quot;were off topic&quot;, but that I think your argument had a flaw (but I find the topic interesting). I didn't mean to prevent you talking about it all !<br /> <br /> English is not my first language so my post may have come as agressive, I'm sorry for that.<br /> <br /> I also think that if some simple subsystems of Essence can be used instead of existing systems of Exalted 3e Core it'd be useful, I look forward to see if this is possible or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T11:34:19-08:00","id":1371059,"title":"","content":"Hm. I hadn't considered using Essence systems in place of more complex Ex3 systems but using the rest of Ex3 in the game.<br /> <br /> I figured that most alternate rulesets would be in the Crucible of Legends","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T12:47:27-08:00","id":1371072,"title":"","content":"The main issue is probably character gen and charms.<br /> <br /> It'd be easy to use the base combat system from one game and the Craft system from another, but if character building is very different, it might be awkward in terms of XP investment into the two different systems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T14:16:49-08:00","id":1371088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370692#post1370692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can remember the days when I first started paying attention to <i>Exalted</i> like they were last week, but I just had to use the words &quot;20 years ago&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop making me feel old!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1370692#post1370692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off-topic, but I want to share some life-wisdom with y'all.<br /> <br /> You never get older. The world gets younger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright then... stop making everyone else feel young!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T15:06:41-08:00","id":1371096,"title":"","content":"Personally, I will always dig my heels in to speak for it being a great concept to have the Great Curse as &quot;Great heroes undone by a moment of extreme pride or rigidity (of moral principle, of belief, of behaviour) that they cannot undo and which has terrible consequences&quot; and for this to affect PCs right from the point of starting play (as opposed to *just* creeping moral decline at some point in the future).<br /> <br /> If you're making a game that is *about* heroism (and I think Exalted actually and rarely among rpgs aspires to be about heroism and virtue in a somewhat critically thinking and questioning way which helps its players think better about this topic, beyond just being &quot;White Wolf's Heroic Fantasy Game&quot;, and this is really cool and unique among heroic fantasy rpgs), then it seems pretty good to have some element in that of thinking critically about the dangers of great power invested in heroes who ultimately all too human and flawed (that heroes are worthy of admiration, but never unthinking deference without concern for their potential for flaws). And dramatically it inspires high and noble feelings of tragedy in us and all this stuff.<br /> <br /> (To add, it's even better to tie this into the perhaps-deservedly wrought death curse of Primordials, tying it into the cycle of heroism and violence in the world and getting us to think about those cycles of usurpation and revolution and the questionable legitimacy of each of those!)<br /> <br /> But I think it is hard to get people to buy into it...! Exalted started as like 70% golden reborn heroes making the world better, and 30% great heroes with feet of clay, and is now as of 3e probably something like 90:10(?).<br /> <br /> The Great Curse really hasn't been front-loaded in much of the Exalted material. Do we know when any Age of Sorrows NPC Solars have had Limit Break and how it has affected their story? As far as I can tell after 20 years, we actually really do not (either at all, or at least often). Do we really get any advice subtly wainscotted through the books giving STs Storytelling hooks for the Great Curse, advice how to use it, reminders that it should be integral to their storytelling? Is it really in any chapter fiction?<br /> <br /> And in that situation, I absolutely am not surprised that people kind of see The Great Curse as a somewhat inexplicable facet or something to get to for Elder Solars.<br /> <br /> If we really wanted it to work, it should be in a lot of places; hooks through the text, NPC biographies, Solar Caste Book subjective experiences, Storytelling advice. And I think the authors have generally somewhat shyed away from it, perhaps sensing it as a divisive element, which lends a bit of a feel of &quot;Oh, you can have it, but you totally don't have to include any of this Epic Tragedy stuff if you don't want&quot;. And because it is not often mentioned, it functionally isn't present in a lot of people's Exalted as experienced, rather than woven integrally into stories, and the audience can't really blamed at this point for just going the remaining 10-30% into 100% golden reborn heroes (and in a sense maybe that's the more functional thing and I am being a hopeless romantic here). So if you had a 4th edition, maybe you should either front-load it a lot more in prominence, or take a different stance on it entirely...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T17:13:21-08:00","id":1371118,"title":"","content":"I am also hopelessly romantic about the Great Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T04:00:48-08:00","id":1371220,"title":"","content":"Just don't do Hunger Dice Mk II (V5) and I'll be fine with more Great Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:20:23-08:00","id":1372014,"title":"","content":"I really hope the combat system will be <u>way</u> simpler than what it is in 3E. That's my only wish concearning Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>Inevitable Meerkat Style</b></i><br /> <i>The Student Sutra of Spotlight Hoging: Once, there was a maiden, but who cares about those? Let's talk about Lunars.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8863-slulura","name":"Slulura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T14:23:29-08:00","id":1372034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slulura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1372014#post1372014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope the combat system will be <u>way</u> simpler than what it is in 3E. That's my only wish concearning Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can live with that, but frankly I think Ex3's combat is one of its best points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T15:19:04-08:00","id":1372044,"title":"","content":"I agree. I wouldn't mind it being a bit pared-down for essence (the combat charms definitely need to be, and it'd be nice if there was less to keep track of), but the basic ideas behind the combat are fairly original, work well, are reasonably quick as complex rpg combat goes, and are quite fun and interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T21:31:16-08:00","id":1372094,"title":"","content":"I think the Sidereal book will give us a lot more information on the 3e incarnation of the Great Curse and the role it played for two reasons.<br /> <br /> The first is that it's always been the primary reason the Sidereals launched the Usurpation, even if they didn't know about it at the time or ever. And a lot of their background information was written from a neutral perspective, providing information about the Great Curse to the players that the Sidereals did not have in setting.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the Sidereals themselves have been said to have a different relationship with the Great Curse than the other Exalted. In 1e they didn't have a standard Curse mechanic, relying on roleplaying to get it across, and instead dealt with Pattern Spider Bite as a mechanical balance. While 2e, attempting to ease complaints about them not having a mechanical Curse, gave them a fairly weak one. And 3e... well while I've long been outside the discussion circles for Exalted altogether, last I knew the prevailing school of thought was that Pattern Spider bite should be done away with altogether, so that Sidereal players would no longer be deterred from using one of their splat powers because they periodically get punished for it. If so, then a mechanical Great Curse flaw would be called for to keep them 'in line' with the other splat mechanics (at least, those are my initial thoughts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T23:22:44-08:00","id":1372100,"title":"","content":"I mean that's not really related to Exalted Essence (though I figure Sidereals in Ex3 will get Limit of a sort, and actual Limit Breaks)<br /> <br /> ... Though I wonder if/how Essence is gonna handle Limit Break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T06:03:26-08:00","id":1372138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1372044#post1372044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. I wouldn't mind it being a bit pared-down for essence (the combat charms definitely need to be, and it'd be nice if there was less to keep track of), but the basic ideas behind the combat are fairly original, work well, are reasonably quick as complex rpg combat goes, and are quite fun and interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting but there are too many things to track at once (initiative, essence, penalties (wounds, etc.), charms timing, ...) and the numerous options tend to provoke analysis paralysis. This tends to make combats take a really long time unless everyone around the table is very invested in the system.<br /> Not what I'd call an ideal entry point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>Inevitable Meerkat Style</b></i><br /> <i>The Student Sutra of Spotlight Hoging: Once, there was a maiden, but who cares about those? Let's talk about Lunars.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8863-slulura","name":"Slulura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T09:27:57-08:00","id":1372159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1372100#post1372100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that's not really related to Exalted Essence</div> </div> </div> </div>People were talking about the Great Curse, mostly about how they wish it didn't exist. Yet we don't really know much about it in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T11:09:08-08:00","id":1372172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broken Masque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1372159#post1372159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People were talking about the Great Curse, mostly about how they wish it didn't exist. Yet we don't really know much about it in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I was the one who started the tangent. And from what I saw it seemed like it was a mix of opinions with some people liking it and some people not seeing the major point of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T05:36:08-08:00","id":1372258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1371096#post1371096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I will always dig my heels in to speak for it being a great concept to have the Great Curse as &quot;Great heroes undone by a moment of extreme pride or rigidity (of moral principle, of belief, of behaviour) that they cannot undo and which has terrible consequences&quot; and for this to affect PCs right from the point of starting play (as opposed to *just* creeping moral decline at some point in the future).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been an Exalted fan since you could pre-order the limited edition 1e corebook, which I did. I've seen a lot of people argue against the Great Curse in that time, and not once have I heard a compelling argument for how you generate epic tragedy without some kind of external mechanic like the Curse. Granted, I think the mechanics haven't been great - the Curse has always been more stick than carrot - but I that's a failure of implementation, not a failure of imagination, and the whole point of iterative design in successive editions is to improve on implementation. A proper Curse influences both player <i>and </i>Storyteller. It's been my experience that players will dig in their heels to keep anything bad from happening to their character and will only rarely sulk like Achilles in his tent, much less drag Hector's body around the walls - and it's even more rare that the Storyteller will have those decisions come back to haunt them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T06:14:17-08:00","id":1372261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1372258#post1372258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been an Exalted fan since you could pre-order the limited edition 1e corebook, which I did. I've seen a lot of people argue against the Great Curse in that time, and not once have I heard a compelling argument for how you generate epic tragedy without some kind of external mechanic like the Curse. Granted, I think the mechanics haven't been great - the Curse has always been more stick than carrot - but I that's a failure of implementation, not a failure of imagination, and the whole point of iterative design in successive editions is to improve on implementation. A proper Curse influences both player <i>and </i>Storyteller. It's been my experience that players will dig in their heels to keep anything bad from happening to their character and will only rarely sulk like Achilles in his tent, much less drag Hector's body around the walls - and it's even more rare that the Storyteller will have those decisions come back to haunt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting because I noticed the exact opposite in my games : The mechanics of The Great Curse really acted as a kind of psychological release there the players could go all in, and usually they had a very strong relation to it following the Limit Break where I didn't hesitate to use it as a narrative tools to make them go forward. I must say that after each Great Curse I ask my player to change most of their intimacies, and make sure that they have at least a new Major intimacy that integrates somehow what happened during The Great Curse (and obviously I don't accept something floppy like &quot;I must keep control next time&quot;).<br /> <br /> But yes it's true that players will still be the most reluctant to lose things for their character, that's why I think as a ST you have to present The Great Curse as a tool to make the character progress in some way and clearly establish it with the player. That's why in another thread I explained that I'm for a &quot;Let's discuss a specific dramatic situation we want to happen&quot; rather than &quot;You now have X emotion deal with it and let's see the consequences later&quot;.<br /> <br /> For example, a Limit Break of one player was that we discussed how she could assassinate her superior because she considered she didn't take the good decisions. Of course if you present it like this, it's not engaging and the rather pacific character would have a strange evolution. So we discussed the deeper reasons she would do this : With her leader dead, she could take power and take the hard decisions that must be done, so it's also a consensus with the other players to let her take the power in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T08:02:03-08:00","id":1372276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1372258#post1372258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Curse has always been more stick than carrot - but I that's a failure of implementation, not a failure of imagination, and the whole point of iterative design in successive editions is to improve on implementation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Limit imposed penalties on characters, that would match the idea that Limit represents a supernatural form of stress, and gaining Limit would represent becoming more distressed, and Limit Break would feel more like the euphoric moment in which your character returns to full power and in which the player has no choice (or the perfect excuse) to take that power and run wild.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, a designer could avoid penalties and simply design Celestial Exalted so that their default power level is represented by a full Limit gauge, and that the euphoric freedom from distress is exceptional enough to be represented with bonuses.<br /> <br /> These bonuses would gradually decrease as your character gains more Limit, which thus powerfully incentivizes players/characters either to construct scenarios in which they never gain limit (the super-empathetic Hierophant and his metaphorical ivory tower in the First Age), or else to seek out ways to actually GAIN MORE Limit as quickly as possible in order to achieve the rush of Limit Break. (And possibly even both in sequence; tea-totalling until you fall off the wagon, then going on a raging bender.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Under either model, characters might have the ability to Limit Break at ANY TIME, by default.<br /> <br /> So if you ever gain one point of Limit, and psychologically you just cannot stand suffering any penalty or losing the power of your full bonus, at ANY TIME you could have your character go mad in order to return to full power.<br /> <br /> An evocative balancing act of selfless suffering versus selfish indulgence. Is your own freedom and power worth more to you than the people you would hurt?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-02-2020, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T08:44:28-08:00","id":1372285,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with the Great Curse. Like some others, I like the idea of it being an inherent problem to Exalted or a human trait magnified, rather than something externally imposed upon the Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T09:33:16-08:00","id":1372293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1372285#post1372285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problem with the Great Curse. Like some others, I like the idea of it being an inherent problem to Exalted or a human trait magnified, rather than something externally imposed upon the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of my view. I actually think 3e has the best implementation of the Great Curse even. I just am not as keen of it being a thing imposed on the Exalted over it being a side-effect of Exaltation and something that is not quite as &quot;real&quot; ICly. I think it could have been given the same treatment of Solar Charms in being a narrative representation of how Exalted power interacts with human limits.<br /> <br /> I think it's worth noting though that since <b>Exalted Essence</b> is meant to distill a lot and I think give ag ood idea of things linked to the 3e setting, I would expect it to show up in some fomr in the book, even if purely in a descriptive sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T13:25:57-08:00","id":1372324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1372258#post1372258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been my experience that players will dig in their heels to keep anything bad from happening to their character and will only rarely sulk like Achilles in his tent, much less drag Hector's body around the walls - and it's even more rare that the Storyteller will have those decisions come back to haunt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>We must have been hanging around with different circles. Granted, I have a relatively small group of regular friends that I have games with (and I recognize that I'm blessed in that regard) but we've had a great deal of Drama, often at the PC's own hands, without a Limit Meter showing up. Granted we're kind of atypical-<br /> <br /> Also, Achilles sulking in his tent may not be the BEST example of things to try and emulate, because it's easy to think of that as &quot;There's a WICKED AWESOME BATTLE and I'm forced to sit here and MISS IT because my Limit Meter went <i>ding</i>&quot; which... I don't think that's a good way to use Limit Break. It should make things more interesting and fun, which yes, can involve disrupting plans and moments of self-sabotage...<br /> <br /> But in my experience, if someone stats up a Fighter Exalt, they're not gonna want to spend a scene NOT fighting unless they're doing something equally engaging. And &quot;Sitting in this tent while the fight goes on&quot; isn't exactly fun to play through for most people.<br /> <br /> I'll also say that I actually like the Limit Breaks of Ex3 (even if I don't think the Limit METER is a good way to do it, and instead would give the PCs chances to enter Limit Break and disrupt a scene for Bonus XP) but they never really FELT like they matched what the Great Curse said it was. A slow and steady slide from hero to villainy that can sometimes take decades or centuries to manifest may not be something that can be easily represented in most tabletop games. Let alone &quot;Occasionally you just flip out, but it usually goes away&quot; as a manifestation thereof. It just didn't ever quite mix for me.<br /> <br /> Thus my thought of &quot;Limit Break feels more natural to me when explained not as a result of a Curse, but as a sense of <i>Sometimes Exalts have too many Feelings</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, as for &quot;Most players dig in their heels to keep anything bad from happening-&quot; This is why I liked the DB version of Limit so much, because heck yeah, give players some bonus XP (with the rider that it has to make the game more fun or interesting) and I'm sure Limit Break would go over so much smoother. The base Limit Meter rules even say &quot;Limit Break doesn't have to occur exactly when the meter fills, but can instead just happen later at a dramatic point&quot; seems only a quarter-step away from just going &quot;Limit Break when the GM offers to gain Splat XP for the session&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 03-02-2020, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T14:56:35-08:00","id":1372339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1372324#post1372324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Achilles sulking in his tent may not be the BEST example of things to try and emulate, because it's easy to think of that as &quot;There's a WICKED AWESOME BATTLE and I'm forced to sit here and MISS IT because my Limit Meter went <i>ding</i>&quot; which... I don't think that's a good way to use Limit Break. It should make things more interesting and fun, which yes, can involve disrupting plans and moments of self-sabotage...</div> </div> </div> </div>It can work under either of the models I proposed.<br /> <br /> Achilles' player has gained so much Limit that he's crippled by penalties or has lost most of his bonus strength (depending on the model you use). Then Achilles receives the latest insult and gains one more point of Limit than his player is willing to put up with. He can either choose to go into battle under-strength, or he can choose to have Achilles give into his stress and Limit Break.<br /> <br /> (&quot;Limit Break&quot; would need a new name if entering a psychotic fit is a matter of choice.)<br /> <br /> Because Achilles and his player are confident his allies cannot win the battle without him, they decide Achilles will sulk in his tent, reasoning that the battle will still be there when he's done and ready to fight at full power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T06:54:13-07:00","id":1376540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">If anything, I think Martial Arts in Essence are particularly cool, especially since it's not a separate skill. So the Charms are really about enhancing a highly specific method of fighting.<br /> &quot;Do I use Melee to hit him with my daiklaive or MA with Violet Bier of Sorrows Style&quot; is not a question you'll have to ask. More properly, your Charms would modify your attack action, or grant you a special attack with your voice.<br /> <br /> The divide between formal MA and Brawl/Melee/Archery/Thrown has always been weird. 2e tried to solve it by making everything MA except those abilities, and it was kind of a half measure Folding in Brawl</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Makes sense for a simpler system.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T08:58:59-07:00","id":1377746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1376540#post1376540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Makes sense for a simpler system.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds promising.<br /> <br /> Is there any word about what Martial Arts Styles might be in the book?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/184941301859\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/17a0569c16cc89ad9e32d5fd53bf1fc9/tumblr_ppprvtwJyJ1y3v0d8o1_540.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/184941301859\" target=\"_blank\"> My RWBY Blog </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/184941301859\" target=\"_blank\"> https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/184941301859 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> swords,reference,resource,skills,fighting </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This tumblr post has a number of animated pictures displaying European swordsmanship techniques, some of which involve grappling the opponent. It seems like neat fodder for a new Martial Art using straight swords.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it reminds me of how swordsman can and would just casually lash out with a kick if their opponent focused too much on their sword and left an opening.<br /> <br /> In a system like <i>Burn Legend</i>, a kick could be a self-contained technique, or just the Basic Strike technique fluffed as a kick. You wouldn't learn to learn the entire style of Kickboxing to incorporate one kick into your swordsman's skills.<br /> <br /> But in the Storyteller System, you never kick, because your Dexterity+Brawl total is vastly inferior to your Dexterity+Melee total. Though I suppose you could always Stunt a Melee attack by saying that you kicked the opponent to throw them off-guard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T09:07:01-07:00","id":1377748,"title":"","content":"No, they haven't said what MA will be included.<br /> <br /> But here are some more spoilers:<br /> All splat types advance at the same speed.<br /> Intimacies still exist.<br /> Character creation does not use BP.<br /> They're &quot;trying to avoid order of operation issues from character generation and advancement.&quot; which I <i>assume</i> means about how buying things in different orders is better or worse. But I'm not sure if that's what they mean or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-01-2020, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:24:26-07:00","id":1378027,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Ascendant Caste:</b></u><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Prophets, messiahs, and revolutionaries, these Infernals are chosen from those told that they are worthless, impure, or abominations. Chosen by the Demon Princes, they now see through these lies, and return to the world clothed in righteousness to depose wicked gods, reform unjust laws, and show Creation the magnificence and munificence of the Infernal Exalted.<br /> <br /> Technically that's an Exalted: Essence spoiler... but I guess really it's an Infernal spoiler.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and sorcerous initiations are in for Essence.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:27:16-07:00","id":1378031,"title":"","content":"Also, Getimians are resonant with Starmetal. Alchemicals are resonant with the material of their caste.<br /> <br /> And while Essence has Resonant and... normal level, I guess, it doesn't bother with Dissonant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:28:49-07:00","id":1378033,"title":"","content":"Looks like the Zenith analogue.<br /> <br /> Also seems just as capable as including those unfairly oppressed by corrupt societies as those properly scorned by healthy societies. You can play an Infernal who brings justice to a twisted society... or who twists a functioning society into a madhouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:56:35-07:00","id":1378039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378027#post1378027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Ascendant Caste:</b></u><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Prophets, messiahs, and revolutionaries, these Infernals are chosen from those told that they are worthless, impure, or abominations. Chosen by the Demon Princes, they now see through these lies, and return to the world clothed in righteousness to depose wicked gods, reform unjust laws, and show Creation the magnificence and munificence of the Infernal Exalted.<br /> <br /> Technically that's an Exalted: Essence spoiler... but I guess really it's an Infernal spoiler.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Further, the Infernal Castes have been confirmed as Azimuth, Ascendant, Horizon, Nadir and Penumbra (the Dawn, Zenith, Twilight, Night and Eclipse analogues, respectively).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T10:16:53-07:00","id":1378301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378033#post1378033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like the Zenith analogue.<br /> <br /> Also seems just as capable as including those unfairly oppressed by corrupt societies as those properly scorned by healthy societies. You can play an Infernal who brings justice to a twisted society... or who twists a functioning society into a madhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Don't talk like one of them, you're not! Even if you'd like to be. To them, you're just a freak; like me! They need you right now, but when they don't... they'll cast you out. Like a leper! See, their morals, their code? It's a bad joke. Dropped at the first sign of trouble. They're only as good as the world allows them to be. I'll show ya'. When the chips are down, these uh, these<i> civilized</i> people?<br /> <br /> They'll <b>eat</b> each other.<br /> <br /> See, I'm not a monster!<br /> <br /> <b><i>I'm just ahead of the curve.</i></b>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> (That quote might be more appropriate for the Night or Eclipse analogue, but we'll see.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T14:25:58-07:00","id":1378354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378301#post1378301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(That quote might be more appropriate for the Night or Eclipse analogue, but we'll see.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably more of a Nadir Caste who invested into Presence, but the Joker isn't interested in building anything like an Ascendant would be.<br /> <br /> The Joker doesn't have any vision of a society to replace the one he's destroying. He just wants to destroy <i>all </i>society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T22:21:14-07:00","id":1378474,"title":"","content":"Well, <i>that</i> Joker, anyway.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">I prefer my comic book villains to <b>not</b> be written to justify the Bush administration\u2019s actions.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T09:31:26-07:00","id":1378564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378474#post1378474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, <i>that</i> Joker, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unaware of any Joker that sought to reform any society.<br /> <br /> Originally, he was just a bank robber with a clown theme. Whenever he's not a nihilistic psychopath who wants to watch the world burn, he's still just a bank robber with a clown theme, plus an obsessive fixation with Batman.<br /> <br /> The Scourge Caste was most associated with Adjoran in Second Edition, with clear nods to the Joker, especially in their laughing mental defense Charm. The new Nadir Caste seems to be more independent of Adjoran, but I doubt they've lost all association.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I prefer my comic book villains to <b>not</b> be written to justify the Bush administration\u2019s actions. </div> </div> </div>You won't see me defending either Bush.<br /> <br /> The difference between Bush and Batman is that Batman nuked his spying tool after using it once, but Bush's &quot;Patriot&quot; Act is still very unpatriotically being used to spy on us all, using &quot;The Hammer&quot;. So I wouldn't say that the movie justified Bush so much as subtly condemned him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:07:59-07:00","id":1378572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378564#post1378564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unaware of any Joker that sought to reform any society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're shifting the goalposts - you <i>said</i> &quot;He just wants to destroy all society.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bNot wanting to destroy a society, is not the same as wanting to reform it. Sometimes you just wanna rob banks or <a href=\"https://batman.fandom.com/wiki/Batman_Issue_66\" target=\"_blank\">have the &quot;biggest boner&quot; on record</a>, without any particular care to what happens to society as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-04-2020, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:22:57-07:00","id":1378576,"title":"","content":"Right, lighter topic. Seeing as how there is another thread up of a guy <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1378553-exalted-to-m-m-relative-power-levels\">converting Exalted to Mutants and Masterminds because 3e is just too much to handle</a>, how many folks here want to predict Essence supplanting standard 3rd edition rules as the preferred way to play the game? 'Cause I know what my money's on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:37:37-07:00","id":1378579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378572#post1378572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you're shifting the goalposts - you <i>said</i> &quot;He just wants to destroy all society.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bNot wanting to destroy a society, is not the same as wanting to reform it. Sometimes you just wanna rob banks or <a href=\"https://batman.fandom.com/wiki/Batman_Issue_66\" target=\"_blank\">have the &quot;biggest boner&quot; on record</a>, without any particular care to what happens to society as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think I was arguing against Joker being an Exalt, or against him being the Zenith Caste equivalent instead of the Night Caste equivalent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:37:38-07:00","id":1378580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">how many folks here want to predict Essence supplanting standard 3rd edition rules as the preferred way to play the game? 'Cause I know what my money's on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, I wouldn't be shocked if it becomes more common than the &quot;normal&quot; way, but I don't think it'll be, like, 80%. There are people who like crunchy systems.<br /> Also, due to having 10 Exalt types in one book (not to mention antagonists), I'm guessing they will be a bit more similar to each other than across the Splat Books, and there will be less options, less spells, less martial arts, less artefacts, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One key thing is that the writers of Essence can look at 3rd edition, see what works and people like, see what doesn't work so well and people aren't so keen on, and think about that accordingly. Also... edit it properly.<br /> <br /> Which means that, just by dint of experience and hindsight, it's likely to be better than Ex3. Same as if they wrote an Ex3.5. It's just easier to improve on something than to make something that's revolutionary (and Ex3 is a big change from Ex2 in so many ways that it was kind of revolutionary, even if the basic mechanics seem similar).<br /> <br /> But I can see a lot of people just using Essence+Across the Eight Directions.<br /> <br /> I can also see people trying to combine Essence and the main books.<br /> <br /> Still, it depends. Essence might be rubbish. It might be great. Exigents and Sidereals (the next two splatbooks) might be rubbish, or great. Can't really say for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> I suspect in some ways Essence is a bit of an experiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:54:27-07:00","id":1378583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378579#post1378579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think I was arguing against Joker being an Exalt, or against him being the Zenith Caste equivalent instead of the Night Caste equivalent?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter.<br /> <br /> And I can understand that; I'm a bit on the fence about whether a person who would tear something down <i>can even be</i> a revolutionary if they don't have something in mind to replace it afterward. But all I was getting at, is that this is just <i>one </i>version of the Joker, and there's been <i>a lot of</i> takes on the guy, showing the concept of the Clown Prince of Crime is nothing if not malleable. I just figure concepts one is trying to gel, &quot;criminal clown,&quot; and &quot;prophetic revolutionary&quot; are not <i>that</i> incompatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-04-2020, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T11:01:16-07:00","id":1378584,"title":"","content":"I must say I just did my first game of Exalted in solo during the quarantine and her first reaction was &quot;I really like the setting and the story but the game seems veyr complicated&quot; and I remembered that, yes, it's very complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T13:07:14-07:00","id":1378606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378576#post1378576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, lighter topic. Seeing as how there is another thread up of a guy <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1378553-exalted-to-m-m-relative-power-levels\">converting Exalted to Mutants and Masterminds because 3e is just too much to handle</a>, how many folks here want to predict Essence supplanting standard 3rd edition rules as the preferred way to play the game? 'Cause I know what my money's on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short-term I can't see there not being a really strong start for Exalted: Essence because it's providing people with the ability to play splats that otherwise won't be available for years.<br /> Long-term, it depends on how they simplify and what the product's objectives are- I don't think Onyx Path wants to deliver an Exalted lite at the expense of Third Edition so much as create a gateway version of the game that's like a delicious sampler plate of what's coming in the years to come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T13:21:03-07:00","id":1378607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378606#post1378606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short-term I can't see there not being a really strong start for Exalted: Essence because it's providing people with the ability to play splats that otherwise won't be available for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T13:26:50-07:00","id":1378608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378576#post1378576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, lighter topic. Seeing as how there is another thread up of a guy <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1378553-exalted-to-m-m-relative-power-levels\">converting Exalted to Mutants and Masterminds because 3e is just too much to handle</a>, how many folks here want to predict Essence supplanting standard 3rd edition rules as the preferred way to play the game? 'Cause I know what my money's on.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Exalted: Essence is what I want ti to be, I don't think it will be the preferred way to play. Like, there's some people out there who think that 5e is kind of simple enough, but tracking spell slots, if you get advantage or not, temporary HP, that can get to be a bit overwhelming. Those people should have an Exalted to play too, but that's drastically too simple for me to play regularly. Also it will be nice if that version clamps down a bit on &quot;Well this artifact, plus this spell, plus this MA and this native charm is the only halfway decent way to play a swordsman&quot; kinds of things.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I think Exalted could stand to be a bit simpler, but when that happens I want it to be like, Exalted 4th edition. If Essence is just a bit simpler, then it's still way too complex for some people, and that's no good for them, and won't be enough to draw me away from the line that already has a huge amount of content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T16:12:09-07:00","id":1378625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378583#post1378583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I can understand that; I'm a bit on the fence about whether a person who would tear something down <i>can even be</i> a revolutionary if they don't have something in mind to replace it afterward. But all I was getting at, is that this is just <i>one </i>version of the Joker, and there's been <i>a lot of</i> takes on the guy, showing the concept of the Clown Prince of Crime is nothing if not malleable. I just figure concepts one is trying to gel, &quot;criminal clown,&quot; and &quot;prophetic revolutionary&quot; are not <i>that</i> incompatible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll repeat that, even ignoring Heath Ledger's version of the Joker, there has never been a Joker who wanted to build a new society or reform an existing one. (If he ever tried it, he probably got bored and quit shortly afterwards.)<br /> <br /> I'll add that I don't think doing so could fit within the Joker's broad concept: &quot;The Clown Prince of Crime&quot;.<br /> <br /> For one thing, he models himself after a clown, and clowns are meant to tear things down. To mock persons, institutions, and customs. To break unspoken tensions, point out contradictions, draw attention to vanities.<br /> <br /> Clowns do not exist to build anything up.<br /> <br /> A clown might be the leader of a revolt or a riot or some other reactionary, destructive movement, but no one elects a clown to govern public affairs after the dust settles. Especially because most people want to know the true face and name of the person they put in charge, not the stage persona of someone who paints their face and only answers to a title.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T20:02:14-07:00","id":1378663,"title":"","content":"You and I must have had some very different clowns entertain us as kids. Mine just taught me how to make balloon animals; she didn\u2019t try to tear down society.<br /> <br /> (Well, there was also Ronald McDonald I guess, but aside from his complicity in the obesity epidemic, he didn\u2019t seem especially malicious either.)<br /> <br /> But even if the clowns I\u2019ve seen are the exceptions that prove the rule, you\u2019re focusing so much on the Clown part that you\u2019re disregarding the rest. Princes are, in fact, part of a structured hierarchy.<br /> <br /> All that said, this is really off-topic, does anyone have Exalted essence spoilers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-04-2020, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T20:43:46-07:00","id":1378668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378663#post1378663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that said, this is really off-topic, does anyone have Exalted essence spoilers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Today was spoiler heavy on the Discord. Here's what I got :<br /> <br /> <u>general spoilers</u><br /> <br /> -Essence has a <b>Virtue </b>system. Virtues provide the umbrella under which Intimacies are defined. There are 7 Virtues. There are old Virtues and brand new ones. One of the Virtues is Ambition.<br /> <br /> -One of the <b>Exalted Advantages</b> (a splat wide benefit, such as Lunar Shapeshifting) for Infernals is<b> Unwoven Coadjutor</b>, which allows you to, once per session, ask your Demon for info on a topic and the ST must give you an important or story relevant fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Lots of spoilers on <b>Charm modes</b> (splat-specific addon to universal charms) :</u><br /> <br /> -Abyssals, Infernals, and Solars can all learn <b>SMA </b>with a tutor. However, in Essence's paradigm, SMA Charms have Sidereal (and occasionally Getimian) modes - they do not have Celestial or Solar, Infernal, or Abyssal Modes.<br /> <br /> -Some Charm modes cover multiple splats : <b>Celestial </b>covers Solars, Abyssals, Infernals, Getimians, Sidereals, Lunars; <b>Terrestrial </b>is Liminals, Dragon-Blooded, Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> -<b>Dragon Styles</b> have Dragon-Blooded Modes, Solars don't get as much benefit from them.<br /> <br /> -Modes are alterations to the existing mechanics. They always have a tangible mechanical effect, but they do not add completely new features to Charms. As an example, a Mode might cause an attack charm to gain armor piercing qualities, but it would not change the Charm into a multi-attack charm or an AoE.<br /> <br /> -Modes do not have to be activated when you use the Charm. You can always choose not to take its benefits. Why you would do this was not explained.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Unclear quotes that might or might not mean anything :</u><br /> <br /> -Dex isn't a God Stat. Or even a thing.<br /> <br /> -DBs become stronger when working together (Might be one of their Exalted Advantages?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T20:48:36-07:00","id":1378669,"title":"","content":"Infernals get Unwoven Coadjutor which allows you to, once per session, ask your Demon for info on a topic and the ST must give you an important or story relevant fact","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T02:14:42-07:00","id":1378705,"title":"","content":"There's a lot making me feel Interested here, and one of them is how apparently Alchemicals will be classified as Terrestrials for effects that care.<br /> <br /> Which... Frankly? Makes sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T02:38:15-07:00","id":1378709,"title":"","content":"When you've already got 6 types of Celestial, I think it makes sense for them to be at the top of Terrestrial rather than the bottom of Celestial.<br /> <br /> Tbh though, as Modes are always advantageous, I wonder if the Terrestrial keyword (as opposed to the DB keyword, Alchemical keyword, etc) will be pretty rare. Whereas I expect to see the Celestial keyword a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T05:43:34-07:00","id":1378735,"title":"","content":"The devs have mentionned that the power curve between exalts is greatly flattened in Essence. Solars remain the top dogs, but they dominate in subtle ways rather than beat up the other exalts and take their lunch money. A DB can win against a Solar if that's the way things go. That being said, a Solar can still take on an entire Wyld Hunt eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T07:55:06-07:00","id":1378758,"title":"","content":"I wrinkled my nose at the &quot;Seven Virtues&quot; thing. It probably won't be anything like the Seven Virtues and Vices of New World of Darkness... but that's the immediate comparison I draw.<br /> <br /> If they are what defines Intimacies, does that mean the distinction between Principles and Ties has been subsumed by this new feature, replaced by this new feature, or both features exist together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T10:36:38-07:00","id":1378791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=