nnot take on the appearance of a galaxy-dragon, especially as part of an Inspire/Instill or Threaten action? Or that it might not have been his original, preferred face?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T11:26:47-07:00","id":1378809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378807#post1378807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s not to say that he cannot take on the appearance of a galaxy-dragon, especially as part of an Inspire/Instill or Threaten action? Or that it might not have been his original, preferred face?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would he do that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T11:33:51-07:00","id":1378813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378809#post1378809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would he do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it\u2019s his original face, before he became the god of the Dragon-Kings (and thus assumed his four-armed but Tyrannosaurus-headed appearance) or the patron of the Solar Exalted (and thus assumed a human appearance), then it would be a very personal thing to reveal.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it\u2019s just very impressive and impactful.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-05-2020, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T12:00:06-07:00","id":1378820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378668#post1378668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> -Dex isn't a God Stat. Or even a thing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some Attributes should never have been. It is just work removing them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Intelligence, I'd be looking at you next, but I don't make those calls.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T13:22:23-07:00","id":1378830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378668#post1378668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-One of the <b>Exalted Advantages</b> (a splat wide benefit, such as Lunar Shapeshifting) for Infernals is<b> Unwoven Coadjutor</b>, which allows you to, once per session, ask your Demon for info on a topic and the ST must give you an important or story relevant fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is weird. I have seen exactly one Green Sun Prince who actively interacted with their Coadjutor and a lot of First Circle Demons are a poor choice for someone supplying you relevant information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T13:32:24-07:00","id":1378831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378830#post1378830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is weird. I have seen exactly one Green Sun Prince who actively interacted with their Coadjutor and a lot of First Circle Demons are a poor choice for someone supplying you relevant information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emiya Shirou is getting a lot of mileage out of Senbreck, a Blood Ape who lived so long in the Demon City that his whole pelt had turned white, in the fanfic &quot;<a href=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/skipping-all-the-steps-exalted-fsn.298622/\" target=\"_blank\">Skipping All The Steps</a>&quot;, because he's stranded in Creation alone with no one else to talk to and plenty of questions that need answering.<br /> <br /> But, in &quot;<a href=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/miracles-of-ancient-wonder-rwby-exalted.389319/unread\" target=\"_blank\">Miracles of Ancient Wonder</a>&quot;, Yang Xiao Long so seldom talks with or about her Coadjutor that we still don't even know what it <i>was</i>, because she already has plenty of conversational company with her teammates, and generally isn't interested in asking it any questions. It just sort of sulks in the back of her mind except when it hits the Limit Button as punishment for acting against her Urge.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from that, &quot;Exalted Advantages&quot; sounds too much like &quot;Advantages enjoyed by all Exalted&quot;, and I'm really hoping that they go with &quot;Host Advantages&quot; or &quot;Patron Advantages&quot;, because obviously all Exalted are Exalted, but each Exalt belongs to a single specific Host of Exalted, or their Exaltation comes from a single specific Patron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T13:45:44-07:00","id":1378837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378668#post1378668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Dex isn't a God Stat. Or even a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I think I might know what this means. In the original First Edition Quickstart, there were only five Attributes, and no Abilities. Everything was folded into Fighting, Magnetism, Scholarship, Stealth, and Embassy.<br /> <br /> Could be something like that, maybe not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T13:55:42-07:00","id":1378838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378831#post1378831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emiya Shirou is getting a lot of mileage out of Senbreck, a Blood Ape who lived so long in the Demon City that his whole pelt had turned white, in the fanfic &quot;<a href=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/skipping-all-the-steps-exalted-fsn.298622/\" target=\"_blank\">Skipping All The Steps</a>&quot;, because he's stranded in Creation alone with no one else to talk to and plenty of questions that need answering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, see that sounds like a useful framing device for a story with one character, but not something that jumps out to me as important to Infernals like shapeshifting is to Lunars. Relevant/useful knowledge once per session honestly sounds like a better fit for Whispers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T13:58:49-07:00","id":1378839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378830#post1378830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is weird. I have seen exactly one Green Sun Prince who actively interacted with their Coadjutor and a lot of First Circle Demons are a poor choice for someone supplying you relevant information.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Alright, I'm stumped, I'm going to ask my Coadjutor.&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;there are no BABIES here they are ADORABLE though did you know that BABIES are ADORABLE also those trees would look better as a HOUSE i can make a HOUSE out of them if you want wait where is my body i really need to build a HOUSE right now-&quot;</i><br /> <br /> More seriously, communing with the demon/symbiote inside of you is a classic trope, and it would be a complete waste to just... not make it a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T16:24:53-07:00","id":1378875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378838#post1378838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, see that sounds like a useful framing device for a story with one character, but not something that jumps out to me as important to Infernals like shapeshifting is to Lunars. Relevant/useful knowledge once per session honestly sounds like a better fit for Whispers.</div> </div> </div> </div>No argument!<br /> <br /> I meant the example as a way to point out that even some unlikely species of demons (the brutish Blood Apes) could be a surprising font of relevant knowledge.<br /> <br /> But as you allude, it's most useful when the Infernal is alone and has no one else to dialogue with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T16:59:28-07:00","id":1378882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378837#post1378837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I think I might know what this means. In the original First Edition Quickstart, there were only five Attributes, and no Abilities. Everything was folded into Fighting, Magnetism, Scholarship, Stealth, and Embassy.<br /> <br /> Could be something like that, maybe not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Essence devs did mention Embassy once, saying it could be a means of achieving political change within the Realm. Plus they have said that a lot was built from the perspective of the 5 Solar archetypes. So my guess is you are right on the money and those will be the 5 Attributes in Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 04-06-2020, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T00:24:22-07:00","id":1378943,"title":"","content":"Hm. I wonder... If Alchemicals are Terrestrials for purposes that care, does that mean that they'll be Orichalcum and Jade <i>ASPECTS</i> rather than <i>CASTES?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T03:09:34-07:00","id":1378962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378839#post1378839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More seriously, communing with the demon/symbiote inside of you is a classic trope, and it would be a complete waste to just... not make it a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind Infernals as Venom, however in that context I take issue with the frequency it can be communed with and the expectation on the storyteller to provide good information.<br /> <br /> That seems likely to push against how myopic demons in Exalted are typically portrayed in order to show their alien mindset. Being expected to filter ideas on how to say... blackmail the duke, through a Blood Ape or Hopping Puppeteer seems like some significant characterisation will get lost in the shuffle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T05:14:09-07:00","id":1378973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378943#post1378943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I wonder... If Alchemicals are Terrestrials for purposes that care, does that mean that they'll be Orichalcum and Jade <i>ASPECTS</i> rather than <i>CASTES?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Aspects indicates that Dragon-Blooded and Liminals are elemental in character - they all possess all of their elements within them, they just lean towards one more than the others. Castes indicates role and purpose. I realize that's a distinction without a difference - it's basically saying there's really only one type of Liminal or Dragon-Blooded, sort of similar to saying how Sidereals don't have castes since they're each Chosen by a different Incarna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T05:29:57-07:00","id":1378976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378973#post1378973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. Aspects indicates that Dragon-Blooded and Liminals are elemental in character - they all possess all of their elements within them, they just lean towards one more than the others. Castes indicates role and purpose. I realize that's a distinction without a difference - it's basically saying there's really only one type of Liminal or Dragon-Blooded, sort of similar to saying how Sidereals don't have castes since they're each Chosen by a different Incarna.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really noticed that the Sidereals don't use castes till now. I've been calling them Chosen of blank but it never seemed odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T06:08:15-07:00","id":1378978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378976#post1378976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really noticed that the Sidereals don't use castes till now. I've been calling them Chosen of blank but it never seemed odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do have castes. They just tend to call themselves Chosen of Whichever Maiden because their <i>caste marks</i> clearly label them as such whenever their anima is burning.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T06:15:22-07:00","id":1378979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378962#post1378962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can get behind Infernals as Venom, however in that context I take issue with the frequency it can be communed with and the expectation on the storyteller to provide good information.<br /> <br /> That seems likely to push against how myopic demons in Exalted are typically portrayed in order to show their alien mindset. Being expected to filter ideas on how to say... blackmail the duke, through a Blood Ape or Hopping Puppeteer seems like some significant characterisation will get lost in the shuffle.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've been debating how to handle this behind the scenes (like, say, the coadjutor serving as a connection to a patron Yozi).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T09:33:15-07:00","id":1379007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378973#post1378973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. Aspects indicates that Dragon-Blooded and Liminals are elemental in character - they all possess all of their elements within them, they just lean towards one more than the others. Castes indicates role and purpose. I realize that's a distinction without a difference - it's basically saying there's really only one type of Liminal or Dragon-Blooded, sort of similar to saying how Sidereals don't have castes since they're each Chosen by a different Incarna.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the easier criteria to understand and accept is that CHOICE is involved with Caste, and determinism is involved with Aspect.<br /> <br /> For Solar Exalted, the Sun chose you to be a Dawn, rather than any other Exaltation that might have been available.<br /> <br /> For Sidereals, a specific Maiden decided to Choose you.<br /> <br /> For Lunars, they choose their own Castes. <br /> <br /> For Alchemical Exalted, the people building them chose them and chose what Caste they would have.<br /> <br /> But there's no such choice involved with Dragon-Blooded; whoever takes the Second Breath is reborn with the Aspect of one of their Dragon-Blooded ancestors. It's automatic and deterministic, even if the determining mechanisms are so minute and finicky that possibly only the god who monitors Terrestrial Exalted could predict it.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Dark Mother doesn't get to choose what sort of Liminal she breathes into. Their Aspect is determined by the creator of their physical body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T14:27:25-07:00","id":1379060,"title":"","content":"Fresh spoilers from the Discord :<br /> <br /> #1<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Some Sort of Dragon King</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charm cascades.<br /> So! They're minimal and most Charms don't use them. There are some places they're more common (ie, Martial Arts), and occasionally linked sets of Charms will have them, but that's to a pretty hard limit of 3. You're more likely to see Charms that have upgrades on a second purchase or get better as Essence increases, and you will not see sprawling charm trees.<br /> We are also looking really hard at character generation, and ways not to overwhelm new players with a sea of choices.<br /> <br /> But yeah, since charm trees won't exceed 3, you probably won't see diagrams of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>#2<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall, Exalted Essence Somelier</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getimians are still Attribute-based</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T15:04:27-07:00","id":1379069,"title":"","content":"Huh. That is interesting. It's likely to lead to/be the cause of some pretty serious simplification.<br /> Which is good, but it's likely to mean less finesse in terms of options, which some may not like. I'm probably fine with it personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T16:48:30-07:00","id":1379097,"title":"","content":"Not much in the way of huge charm trees and cascades? Y'know what? I can live with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:13:07-07:00","id":1379116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378943#post1378943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I wonder... If Alchemicals are Terrestrials for purposes that care, does that mean that they'll be Orichalcum and Jade <i>ASPECTS</i> rather than <i>CASTES?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>To add to comments on this, Caste and Aspect are not, inherently, linked with being Celestial or Terrestrail Exalted. While the division is the way it's been <i>so far</i>, it's not necessarily the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T05:43:03-07:00","id":1379461,"title":"","content":"Essence is now in Redlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T11:54:03-07:00","id":1379508,"title":"","content":"Imagine this was a game about Baseball, and every player had this particular bonus related to what team they were part of or what college team they'd been drafted out of.<br /> <br /> But instead of calling this something sensible like Team Advantage or Origin Advantage, the game called it Baseball-Player Advantage. When <i>every </i>player-character the game is meant to model is a Baseball player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T12:27:35-07:00","id":1379511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379508#post1379508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine this was a game about Baseball, and every player had this particular bonus related to what team they were part of or what college team they'd been drafted out of.<br /> <br /> But instead of calling this something sensible like Team Advantage or Origin Advantage, the game called it Baseball-Player Advantage. When <i>every </i>player-character the game is meant to model is a Baseball player.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted Advantage isn't perfect, but the thing is there's no word for [all-the-exalts-of-1-type]. What would you suggest instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T12:36:57-07:00","id":1379514,"title":"","content":"Going to be honest... I don't really care. Seems like a dull name, but it's no big problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T13:02:36-07:00","id":1379518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379511#post1379511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted Advantage isn't perfect, but the thing is there's no word for [all-the-exalts-of-1-type]. What would you suggest instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>The two other times that I complained about this, I did offer simple alternatives.<br /> <br /> Patron Advantage is simplest, as it doesn't quite introduce a new Proper Term into the lexicon, while still clearly saying that this specific advantage has its roots in your specific patron.<br /> <br /> Host Advantage works better in the sense that it does introduce a new Proper Term, and one that I feel the lexicon has been missing from the beginning, though it's maybe almost come up before with phrases like &quot;Celestial Host&quot; (referring to all Celestial Exalted), &quot;Terrestrial Host&quot; (referring to the Dragon-Blooded, or &quot;Exalted Host&quot; (referring to all Exalted).<br /> <br /> &quot;Host&quot; also works better than Patron in the sense that most Exalted &quot;Patrons&quot; are actually female, even when Luna feels like being male.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T13:05:12-07:00","id":1379519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379514#post1379514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to be honest... I don't really care. Seems like a dull name, but it's no big problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse than being dull, it's confusing. &quot;Exalted&quot; refers to all of the Exalted, but &quot;Exalted Advantage&quot; is not an advantage one gets simply for being Exalted, but for being a specific kind of Exalt.<br /> <br /> And there's still no better name for &quot;kind of Exalt&quot; than &quot;kind&quot; or &quot;type&quot; or &quot;splat&quot;, and there really should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T14:31:21-07:00","id":1379523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379519#post1379519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worse than being dull, it's confusing. &quot;Exalted&quot; refers to all of the Exalted, but &quot;Exalted Advantage&quot; is not an advantage one gets simply for being Exalted, but for being a specific kind of Exalt.<br /> <br /> And there's still no better name for &quot;kind of Exalt&quot; than &quot;kind&quot; or &quot;type&quot; or &quot;splat&quot;, and there really should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be confusing to you. It's an Advantage that applies to some kind of Exalt, Exalted Advantage or Exalt Advantage works <i>enough</i> that I'm not gonna waste anymore brainpower on giving it thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T15:39:40-07:00","id":1379529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378830#post1378830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is weird. I have seen exactly one Green Sun Prince who actively interacted with their Coadjutor and a lot of First Circle Demons are a poor choice for someone supplying you relevant information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of late to this (and the AG already responded pretty well I think) but: A) It's still presumably subject to &quot;My 1CD would actually kind of know about this stuff&quot; (aka, you can't ask them what the Empress had for dinner last week and expect it to work, and should you choose a 1CD who don't know nuthin' about nuthin', that's kind of still your prerogative, though slightly more disincentived) and B) Nothing to stop you playing your demon so they're actually snowing you with irrelevant and delusional tosh 90% of the time.<br /> <br /> It seems pretty cool though; in terms of &quot;Mechanics which actually require character interaction and encourage you to role-play it out and establish character and story&quot;. Which is surely pretty much exactly what we'd expect or hope them to do when their a brief / sales pitch is &quot;emphasizes story over character, character over mechanics, and mechanics over minutiae in order to drive Exalted toward engaging players with the myriad stories they can tell in the world of Creation&quot;. (So my takeaway is that it seems like a cool sign that they actually have some inventive ways to do this).<br /> <br /> (It also reminded me of Vampire Hunter D: Bloodlust, and I am easy to please by being reminded of Vampire Hunter D: Bloodlust).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T16:04:43-07:00","id":1379538,"title":"","content":"Sunder, I agree with you that there's no good name for type-of-exalt.<br /> <br /> Patron Advantage I think doesn't work great because Sidereals have different Patrons, the Dragons aren't really Patrons the way that the Sun is, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Host Advantage I guess could work. Don't love it, but it's okay. But I don't really have any big problem with Exalt Advantage, other than it's dull. But that's actually more the word &quot;Advantage&quot; than the Exalt part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T16:11:46-07:00","id":1379541,"title":"","content":"Exalted advantage sounds like the tagline for an insurance company. &quot;We guarantee you'll save at least 10% if you bundle home and auto with Exalted Insurance, because that's the Exalted advantage!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T16:18:25-07:00","id":1379543,"title":"","content":"It may just be a working title. There's surely a more evocative, fantastical and exotic term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T16:49:29-07:00","id":1379550,"title":"","content":"Exalt Edge?<br /> <br /> Because it gives you the <i>edge</i> that being this kind of Exalt has over others. The <i>edge</i> that Lunars have over other Exalts is their Shapeshifting. The <i>edge</i> that Dragonbloods get is their cooperative themes and elemental powers.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's alliteration. Bonus points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T19:05:30-07:00","id":1379571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379550#post1379550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalt Edge?<br /> <br /> Because it gives you the <i>edge</i> that being this kind of Exalt has over others. The <i>edge</i> that Lunars have over other Exalts is their Shapeshifting. The <i>edge</i> that Dragonbloods get is their cooperative themes and elemental powers.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's alliteration. Bonus points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely think it's an improvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:09:36-07:00","id":1379679,"title":"","content":"I like it, but don't love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:58:13-07:00","id":1379698,"title":"","content":"Exalted Advantage is fine. It's not the hill I'd choose to die on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T02:58:57-07:00","id":1379715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379550#post1379550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalt Edge?</div> </div> </div> </div> But only Abyssals have edge!<br /> Well, and Infernals.<br /> ...Probably Liminals too.<br /> Soulsteel Castes...<br /> Chosen of Endings, of course.<br /> <br /> Alright, it's not half bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T03:05:04-07:00","id":1379716,"title":"","content":"I think folks will find a lot of the interesting naming conventions of Exalted Advantage come out of the specific Advantages and Caste powers rather than a system topic, which - by virtue of necessity and ease of understanding - has more virtue in being boringly-named than being interestingly-but-obscurely-named. <i>Ten Thousand Forms, Living Artifact, Undying</i>...you can be evocative and functional at the same time, but there's a point where you get diminishing returns.<br /> <br /> <b>Exalted: Essence</b> needs to appeal to new players. I think we'll reexamine system topic names if playtesting reveals some fundamental confusion as to their purpose and over their use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 04-09-2020, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T06:13:04-07:00","id":1379740,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Liminal stuff today:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">The aspects are Blood, Breath, Flesh, Marrow, and Soil<br /> <br /> Blood Aspects are born from lust, greed, and ambition. Breaths stem from regret or penitence. Flesh is rage and vengeance. Marrow is curiosity and obsession. Soil is sorrow and yearning.<br /> <br /> Liminals are aspected beings; they contain all of their elements within them, even if they favor one.<br /> <br /> Liminals have to anchor themselves with a Major Intimacy to a mortal, although later Charms might modify this to enable an Exalt-to-Exalt connection; we're still talking about it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">If the mortal dies, or if the Intimacy breaks otherwise, the Liminal begins to decompose. Within a Lunar cycle, they're nothing but dirt and forgotten memories. Tears in the rain.<br /> <br /> They can forge a connection to a new mortal, but it's not easy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The emotion is what defines your Aspect</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> I<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">n Essence, Liminals are neutral to all magical materials, but they may upgrade to resonant with soulsteel if they take a body part from someone who is resonant to soulsteel.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">Liminals have been around since the Shogunate</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">Late, </span><i>late</i><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"> Shogunate<br /> <br /> The basic function of Liminals is to hold fast the line between the living and the dead, to fight for peace and the tranquility of death, and to stop the dead from predating upon the quick.<br /> <br /> They're </span><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">not going to delve too deeply into the Dark Mother's origins in Crucible or Essence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">The process that produces a Liminal is the Dark Mother conferring the Exaltation through the vehicle of a failed resurrection attempt, in the space between the living and the dead<br /> <br /> She chooses when the Exaltation occurs</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">Liminals are not the people whose flesh they inhabit, though some memories remain<br /> <br /> <br /> On the Great Curse, which not all Exalt types have...</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">They all do in Essence, for simplicity's sake. Every Exalt type has something that causes them to wig out spectacularly in response to stress.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">That should not be extrapolated to the rest of Ex3.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">Your Major Virtue is a potential Great Curse trigger, yes. (If you're a Solar, your Minor is too)<br /> <br /> And Virtues are just Major and Minor, no dots.<br /> <br /> Other random bits:<br /> One Getimian anima power is called Better World Proposition<br /> <br /> Stunt bonuses exist, but are a bit different.<br /> 1. It's a flat rate. A &quot;Stunt bonus&quot; - full stop 2. You can share them with your teammates</span></span> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If you're really blown away by someone's Stunt you can always reward them an additional bonus, but no more judging your friends ability to describe things.</span></span></span></span></span></span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">There is a charm called Divine Mantle. It doesn't work mechanically the same as in 3e (thankfully).<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">&quot;Supernal&quot; isn't quite the same thing in Essence. It's there, but it's taking a slightly different form - because it's tied directly into your Anima powers</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T06:27:49-07:00","id":1379742,"title":"","content":"Oh, and there will be rules for necromancy as well as sorcery.<br /> <br /> Experience got a big rework and is still being tested (I assume related to changes to character generation issues), so no details on that yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T06:33:24-07:00","id":1379746,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Anima Effects have three discrete abilities, but broken down into Passive/Active/Iconic.<br /> Passive effects are an always-on bonus. Active effects happen when you have any Anima at all Iconic effects go off when your Anima is maxed out</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"d