neutral to all magical materials, but they may upgrade to resonant with soulsteel if they take a body part from someone who is resonant to soulsteel.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">Liminals have been around since the Shogunate</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">Late, </span><i>late</i><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"> Shogunate<br /> <br /> The basic function of Liminals is to hold fast the line between the living and the dead, to fight for peace and the tranquility of death, and to stop the dead from predating upon the quick.<br /> <br /> They're </span><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">not going to delve too deeply into the Dark Mother's origins in Crucible or Essence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">The process that produces a Liminal is the Dark Mother conferring the Exaltation through the vehicle of a failed resurrection attempt, in the space between the living and the dead<br /> <br /> She chooses when the Exaltation occurs</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">Liminals are not the people whose flesh they inhabit, though some memories remain<br /> <br /> <br /> On the Great Curse, which not all Exalt types have...</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">They all do in Essence, for simplicity's sake. Every Exalt type has something that causes them to wig out spectacularly in response to stress.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">That should not be extrapolated to the rest of Ex3.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">Your Major Virtue is a potential Great Curse trigger, yes. (If you're a Solar, your Minor is too)<br /> <br /> And Virtues are just Major and Minor, no dots.<br /> <br /> Other random bits:<br /> One Getimian anima power is called Better World Proposition<br /> <br /> Stunt bonuses exist, but are a bit different.<br /> 1. It's a flat rate. A &amp;quot;Stunt bonus&amp;quot; - full stop 2. You can share them with your teammates</span></span> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If you're really blown away by someone's Stunt you can always reward them an additional bonus, but no more judging your friends ability to describe things.</span></span></span></span></span></span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">There is a charm called Divine Mantle. It doesn't work mechanically the same as in 3e (thankfully).<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">&amp;quot;Supernal&amp;quot; isn't quite the same thing in Essence. It's there, but it's taking a slightly different form - because it's tied directly into your Anima powers</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>...nice!<br /> <br /> Liminals sound really fun to play, and have a neat unique trait. I also love how the undead hunter Exalts have a very practical reason to hunt vampire Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:02:36-07:00","id":1379789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379746#post1379746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Anima Effects have three discrete abilities, but broken down into Passive/Active/Iconic.<br /> Passive effects are an always-on bonus. Active effects happen when you have any Anima at all Iconic effects go off when your Anima is maxed out</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I very much like the direction these anima powers are going. Maybe because the structured look is appealing, it interacts with Anima in a way where it's not you spending Anima for cool effects, but it's the rising of the Anima that brings the cool like powerups, or that we have confirmed that all of them will have some awesome names.<br /> <br /> Overall it's all very appealing to me and I'm looking forward on seeing them more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:19:33-07:00","id":1379858,"title":"","content":"Well okay NOW I'm somewhat interested in Liminals. Which is a bit of a change, NGL, but sure, I'll give them a shake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:51:22-07:00","id":1379868,"title":"","content":"None of the Liminal stuff is actually new, except for the specific mechanics of their bond (and the fact that leads to death, which is... a thing, certainly<sup>1</sup>).<br /> <br /> <sup>1: Actually it sounds like it could pretty poignant.</sup>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:58:29-07:00","id":1379871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379868#post1379868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the Liminal stuff is actually new, except for the specific mechanics of their bond (and the fact that leads to death, which is... a thing, certainly<sup>1</sup>).<br /> <br /> <sup>1: Actually it sounds like it could pretty poignant.</sup></div> </div> </div> </div>It looks harrowing.<br /> <br /> To avoid dying, these magical zombie-people need to have SOMEONE about whom they are Amorally Curious (Marrow), Violently Loathing (Flesh), or Lustfully Obsessed (Blood)...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:47:25-07:00","id":1379882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379871#post1379871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks harrowing.<br /> <br /> To avoid dying, these magical zombie-people need to have SOMEONE about whom they are Amorally Curious (Marrow), Violently Loathing (Flesh), or Lustfully Obsessed (Blood)...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not seeing an issue here. It sounds like a potential horror story, and Liminals are horror stories about resurrection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:49:32-07:00","id":1379884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379871#post1379871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks harrowing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, the one month time limit feels crazy punishing, but under the right circumstances it could make for a cool story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:59:39-07:00","id":1379886,"title":"","content":"Presumably they still have the thing that they come back to life unless they die by fire or whatever (I forget exactly).<br /> <br /> So the interesting thing is that to kill them, you have to kill someone else. It's a lich's phylactery, or a horcrux, or whatever, but it's a person. And is it morally okay to kill that person to kill the Liminal?<br /> So the Liminal Villain is quite interesting.<br /> <br /> I don't know how well it'd work for a PC though. I guess in practice you'd be able to find another person unless your ST is being mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:05:01-07:00","id":1379889,"title":"","content":"Only by destroying their brain or by drowning can a Liminal die. Everything else even when incapacitated they will come back from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:08:39-07:00","id":1379891,"title":"","content":"Sure. Which is... ridiculously OP (though interesting!). That is not a power you would let a Celestial have. So this seems like a fair balancing reason, though it does make your character very focused on one NPC, which can at times be awkward for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-09-2020, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:12:21-07:00","id":1379893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379891#post1379891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Which is... ridiculous. That is not a power you would let a Celestial have. So this seems like a fair balancing reason, though it does make your character very focused on one NPC, which can at times be awkward for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, you'd be surprised how many things &quot;stab 'em in the brain&quot; will kill.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:15:35-07:00","id":1379895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379893#post1379893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, you'd be surprised how many things &quot;stab 'em in the brain&quot; will kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;How do we kill a vampire, specifically?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Stab them in the heart with a stake, then cut off the head.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But that kills everything!'<br /> <br /> &quot;I know! That's why we do it!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:32:10-07:00","id":1379899,"title":"","content":"I really want to see how they make having a mortal person to whom they must have an intimacy *not* an Escort Mission. Because I'm fairly certain that they're faaar smarter than me on this and they *will* have thought of a clever way to make it *not* like an Escort Mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:48:26-07:00","id":1379905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379891#post1379891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not a power you would let a Celestial have. So this seems like a fair balancing reason, though it does make your character very focused on one NPC, which can at times be awkward for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I don't know about <i>fair</i>. The more I think about it, the more heavy-handed it feels.<br /> <br /> Having a mandatory connection to a person to keep yourself together is pretty cool, though making that tie mortal-only feels very CofD (and not in a good way). Having the failure state of that connection be <i>death</i> feels... clumsy.<br /> <br /> My mind goes to <i>Deviant: the Renegades</i>, the most recent CofD gameline. It, too, has mandatory NPC connections, and likely for similar reasons (as anchors against alienation and to ground the PCs), complete with bad shit if all of these Touchstones crumble away.<br /> Thing is, in Deviant, your Touchstones don't need to be baseline humans (though that's recommended for genre reasons), and can include buildings, items, and places. You get more than one, too, so the failure state is rarer, and a portion to your Touchstones are dedicated to your hatred and unyielding need for vengeance. Finally, and more importantly, if you do run out of Touchstones, your doom is further out than <i>a month</i>, and you always have the option of turning back the clock by letting yourself get more monstrous, more burdened, more inhuman.<br /> (This is not to say that being a Deviant without Touchstones doesn't suck. It sucks <i>bad</i>, and its a downward spiral to your inevitable, messy, likely massively destructive death.)<br /> <br /> Hmm. I suppose that, back when I first heard about Liminals needing connections, I expected something more like that. Less of a replicant's time limit, and more Guts falling to his Beast of Darkness without his companions to ground him; slow and horrible and dehumanizing, not an urgent countdown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:49:16-07:00","id":1379906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379899#post1379899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want to see how they make having a mortal person to whom they must have an intimacy *not* an Escort Mission. Because I'm fairly certain that they're faaar smarter than me on this and they *will* have thought of a clever way to make it *not* like an Escort Mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least, the escort needs to move at the Liminal's walking speed, since it's pretty unrealistic to expect them to run as fast as any Liminal's running speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:47:25-07:00","id":1379935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379906#post1379906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, the escort needs to move at the Liminal's walking speed, since it's pretty unrealistic to expect them to run as fast as any Liminal's running speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I DO understand that not everybody can just stitch on a pair of legs that belonged to a man who ran like the wind, and they're also limited to just one pair of legs-&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:19:24-07:00","id":1379957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379891#post1379891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Which is... ridiculously OP (though interesting!). That is not a power you would let a Celestial have.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, as was pointed out to me, it turns out Celestials <i>do</i> have that. They just have to build towards it.<br /> <br /> The most prominent example would be the notorious <b>D</b>ual <b>M</b>agnus <b>P</b>rana, in which a dedicated Solar crafter can just decide that a death didn't count, no matter how absolute it seemed. Less contentious examples are Soul Reprisal and the Lunar Charms Form-Shedding Sacrifice and Soul Beyond Shape.<br /> <br /> Beyond this, I don't think &quot;OP&quot; is a meaningful word when it comes to these things. A Liminal who dies in a fight, however temporarily, still <i>lost the fight.</i> That she can pick herself up and shove her spilled guts back inside doesn't mean much if the raiders still massacred her village, if the rebellion against the Realm was still crushed, or if the vengeful spirit still broke free of its bonds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:09:11-07:00","id":1379980,"title":"","content":"I am coming in to this discussion with nothing but this page to go by, through a combination of this being an incredibly dense thread and being very wary of information from Heirs. I beg pardon if this renders me a bit obtuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379905#post1379905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, I don't know about <i>fair</i>. The more I think about it, the more heavy-handed it feels.<br /> <br /> Having a mandatory connection to a person to keep yourself together is pretty cool, though making that tie mortal-only feels very CofD (and not in a good way). Having the failure state of that connection be <i>death</i> feels... clumsy.<br /> <br /> My mind goes to <i>Deviant: the Renegades</i>, the most recent CofD gameline. It, too, has mandatory NPC connections, and likely for similar reasons (as anchors against alienation and to ground the PCs), complete with bad shit if all of these Touchstones crumble away.<br /> Thing is, in Deviant, your Touchstones don't need to be baseline humans (though that's recommended for genre reasons), and can include buildings, items, and places. You get more than one, too, so the failure state is rarer, and a portion to your Touchstones are dedicated to your hatred and unyielding need for vengeance. Finally, and more importantly, if you do run out of Touchstones, your doom is further out than <i>a month</i>, and you always have the option of turning back the clock by letting yourself get more monstrous, more burdened, more inhuman.<br /> (This is not to say that being a Deviant without Touchstones doesn't suck. It sucks <i>bad</i>, and its a downward spiral to your inevitable, messy, likely massively destructive death.)<br /> <br /> Hmm. I suppose that, back when I first heard about Liminals needing connections, I expected something more like that. Less of a replicant's time limit, and more Guts falling to his Beast of Darkness without his companions to ground him; slow and horrible and dehumanizing, not an urgent countdown.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm feeling as though a tension about the possibility of becoming monstrous leads Liminals off on tangents away from the fact that they're animated corpses.<br /> <br /> That does after all seem to be what the core conceit of them is. And not just the literal implications, it's that whole connotation of &quot;this is an imitation of life that is being powered solely by the miracle of Exaltation&quot;. Given the setting's complicated relationship with death I think that's an interesting and unique place to put them in, and I think that's the side that should be dived more deeply into.<br /> <br /> And to my mind a lot of significance can come out of the fact that they're not immortal, they're just running on borrowed time that they can keep trying to push back indefinitely.<br /> <br /> Heck, one thing I think is interesting about them is to imagine that despite being such an imitation, the Liminals are very human. They might even be... pretty normal. Perhaps even more so than the other Exalted. I think that could lend a lot of pathos to the idea that they sincerely want to connect to other people, but there's always a bit of a gulf because something about them doesn't quite belong. I think that pathos would be weakened by the prospect of becoming monstrous, whether that be perceived as a dread outcome or a way out of a dilemma.<br /> <br /> After all, literally the only reason that they're moving around at all is because somebody else really wanted that corpse to do so. I think the idea that the right disconnect from others causes those strings to be cut is both metaphysically logical and a consistent form of compelling drama.<br /> <br /> I know nothing about Deviant, but I suspect this is another point where attempts to draw parallels between Chronicles of Darkness and Exalted falters in the face of key differences such as the figures of the former being monsters and the fact that they're buried down in the substrata of their world, compared to the loftier position that the Chosen hold. It's like the weakness in people suggesting Beast as an inspiration for Lunars, hanging around in your spooky lair all the time cultivating sources of the fear juice isn't really a narrative space for any of the Exalted. If Deviant lets them get by with things other than humans I expect that's because the Chronicles of Darkness have a very different thematic significance to their big old subculture of monsters, freaks and weirdos than Exalted does.<br /> <br /> \u2026. Does Dame Crimson's backstory still work at all? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:11:01-07:00","id":1379981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379893#post1379893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, you'd be surprised how many things &quot;stab 'em in the brain&quot; will kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah, &quot;stab 'em in the brain&quot; has on several occasions failed to even kill normal humans! One guy gets stabbed through the brain by a railway spike, he not only lives for years after it he starts carrying that spike around everywhere as though it's his best damn friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:23:19-07:00","id":1379984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379905#post1379905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a mandatory connection to a person to keep yourself together is pretty cool, though making that tie mortal-only feels very CofD (and not in a good way). Having the failure state of that connection be <i>death</i> feels... clumsy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death isn't the only failure state of the thread of life. And it doesn't have to be a mortal, although that's delving into some design space Essence may not necessarily get into. Dame Crimson is still a canon Liminal, and she was made by a jerkass Wood elemental - but note that her current connection is a mortal in the Guild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T19:27:22-07:00","id":1379997,"title":"","content":"Also is there any real confirmation as to whether the Liminal's Bonded needs to be within easy glomping distance at all times? From the tidbits I see it could very well be that we have an entirely mortal Magistrate doing paperwork most of the day, and the Liminal that works solving Spooky Ghost Problems in the city drops by with food every so often. The mortal may not need to be on-screen at all times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T20:13:10-07:00","id":1380008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379997#post1379997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also is there any real confirmation as to whether the Liminal's Bonded needs to be within easy glomping distance at all times?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that would make things too difficult for the vengeance-crazed Flesh Aspects, who probably tend to kill their Bonded target as soon as they get close enough, while most such targets do their best to maintain distance.<br /> <br /> Once again, I think of Alex Mercer as a powerful Flesh Aspect on a rampage. &quot;Nothing will keep you safe from me! Not soldiers! Not tanks!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T20:17:38-07:00","id":1380009,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say Flesh Aspects are murder craze. Their Essence influences their emotions, but only in so far as Elemental Essence influences DBs. So it is something they can control. It just informs their personality a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T21:08:17-07:00","id":1380019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380008#post1380008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that would make things too difficult for the vengeance-crazed Flesh Aspects, who probably tend to kill their Bonded target as soon as they get close enough, while most such targets do their best to maintain distance.<br /> <br /> Once again, I think of Alex Mercer as a powerful Flesh Aspect on a rampage. &quot;Nothing will keep you safe from me! Not soldiers! Not tanks!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Psh, killing them is too easy.<br /> <br /> You have to ruin them.<br /> <br /> Destroy what they love. Tear down their ambitions. Drive their life to ruin. Tear asunder all those that they care about.<br /> <br /> And when their dreams lie in a pile of ash, and all they have wanted is but a memory... Then, and only then, will they have your permission to die.<br /> <br /> Oh huh turned that into an entire Storyline, lookit that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-10-2020, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:33:14-07:00","id":1380132,"title":"","content":"On Liminals, I'd also note that the spoilers have <i>not</i> said that the Intimacy a Liminal needs to their &quot;creator&quot; needs to have a context of the emotion that inspired the failed resurrection that was empowered and gave rise to them. Frankenstein has been cited as a Liminal inspiration, and while the Creature in that is pretty clearly a Marrow Aspect, created because of Victor Frankenstein's curiosity and obsession, I would describe the Creature's Intimacy towards him as being much more one of &quot;Anger due to abandonment&quot;. And I <i>really</i> doubt that Blood Aspects will all be forced to love or lust for their creators - that would be both creepy, and far too restrictive, cutting off quite a lot of interesting stories. Like, what if a Blood Aspect was created when a woman wanted to resurrect her dead wife, but the new Liminal is asexual, and just wants to be friends with her? Or is obsessed with figuring out her &quot;past life&quot;, and only views the woman who tried the resurrection as a link to someone who knew &quot;herself&quot;?<br /> <br /> Point is, I doubt very much they're going to be so restrictive on the Intimacy Liminals need to have to a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T20:26:51-07:00","id":1380290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380132#post1380132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Liminals, I'd also note that the spoilers have <i>not</i> said that the Intimacy a Liminal needs to their &quot;creator&quot; needs to have a context of the emotion that inspired the failed resurrection that was empowered and gave rise to them. Frankenstein has been cited as a Liminal inspiration, and while the Creature in that is pretty clearly a Marrow Aspect, created because of Victor Frankenstein's curiosity and obsession, I would describe the Creature's Intimacy towards him as being much more one of &quot;Anger due to abandonment&quot;. And I <i>really</i> doubt that Blood Aspects will all be forced to love or lust for their creators - that would be both creepy, and far too restrictive, cutting off quite a lot of interesting stories. Like, what if a Blood Aspect was created when a woman wanted to resurrect her dead wife, but the new Liminal is asexual, and just wants to be friends with her? Or is obsessed with figuring out her &quot;past life&quot;, and only views the woman who tried the resurrection as a link to someone who knew &quot;herself&quot;?<br /> <br /> Point is, I doubt very much they're going to be so restrictive on the Intimacy Liminals need to have to a person.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given how it's explicit the thread can be regenerated if lost, it just has a time limit, I figured. Still, I'm thankful a Liminal can have more than their Aspect emotion for their thread, and even if not, I like the implication Liminals can change Aspect; if a Blood Aspect's passion cools, they simply cease to be a Blood Aspect and explore being, say, a Soil for a bit.<br /> <br /> I'm especially interested in how Liminals are children of the Shogunate; it shows Exaltation is a living process, not bound to the Primordial Age and what Autochthon made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T20:38:40-07:00","id":1380292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380290#post1380290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how it's explicit the thread can be regenerated if lost, it just has a time limit, I figured. Still, I'm thankful a Liminal can have more than their Aspect emotion for their thread, and even if not, I like the implication Liminals can change Aspect; if a Blood Aspect's passion cools, they simply cease to be a Blood Aspect and explore being, say, a Soil for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that the context of the Liminal's Intimacy to their creator simply doesn't need to have the context of the motivation that created them <i>at all</i>. A Blood Aspect's creator may have been experiencing an emotion of &quot;lust, greed, and ambition&quot;, but the Blood Aspect <i>themselves</i> could have a context toward the creator of &quot;troubled suspicion&quot; or &quot;furious resentment&quot; or something. And while I don't know this for sure, I'm willing to wager that the Liminal changing the context of their Intimacy, or changing its target, won't change their Aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:05:42-07:00","id":1380296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380290#post1380290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given how it's explicit the thread can be regenerated if lost, it just has a time limit, I figured. Still, I'm thankful a Liminal can have more than their Aspect emotion for their thread, and even if not, I like the implication Liminals can change Aspect; if a Blood Aspect's passion cools, they simply cease to be a Blood Aspect and explore being, say, a Soil for a bit.<br /> <br /> I'm especially interested in how Liminals are children of the Shogunate; it shows Exaltation is a living process, not bound to the Primordial Age and what Autochthon made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liminals aren't so much children of the Shogunate or well, we got confirmation that appeared pretty late into it......specifically which is the interesting part, either right before or during when the Great Contagion hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T00:17:06-07:00","id":1380331,"title":"","content":"Have anyone heard anything about whether Essence will contain dice trick Charms, such as 1s that counteract successes, or 6s being rerolled, etc?<br /> <br /> And whether cooldown (reset conditions, if you will) Charms is a thing?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T01:16:32-07:00","id":1380335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379984#post1379984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death isn't the only failure state of the thread of life. And it doesn't have to be a mortal, although that's delving into some design space Essence may not necessarily get into. Dame Crimson is still a canon Liminal, and she was made by a jerkass Wood elemental - but note that her current connection is a mortal in the Guild.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, the bit Wizard quoted said mortals only and &quot;one Lunar cycle&quot; before you're dirt and memories, but if that's not actually <i>accurate</i>, then I'm down with the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T05:26:48-07:00","id":1380362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379740#post1379740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're [/FONT]<span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">not going to delve too deeply into the Dark Mother's origins in Crucible or Essence.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I hope we at least learn a little more about her.<br /> <br /> A lot of people with antipathy to the idea of new exalt types have asked why Frankenstein's Monster needs to be it's own Exalt type with five distinct flavours of Frakenstein if they're just going to explore their humanity and fight ghosts, there's nothing wrong with the concept but on the surface it feels like the sort of unique character that the Exigents book should facilitate.<br /> <br /> Obviously the Dark Mother is what connects them and gives them common identity, but these days I can't help but expect mystery boxes to be empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T05:47:48-07:00","id":1380366,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... tbh, if they were one of four or five kinds, I'd maybe agree, but with 10 different kind of Exalts I think there's enough there. Certainly in Essence at least. And I'm more interested in being a horrifying flesh golem trying to fit in to a band of more human Exalts than in a mysterious underworld patron. There's plenty of mysterious underworld patrons to go around.<br /> <br /> I maybe wouldn't expect the Liminals book, when it comes out in 3 years or so, to be as long as the Dragonblood or Lunars books of course. But I think there's more to them than just a kind of Exigent.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... I wonder about release schedules and Essence/Storyteller's Companion.<br /> <br /> What I mean is, the next book is Exigents, and after that Sidereals. What comes next? I wonder if it'll depend on what people think of the new/changed Exalt types in Essence and the ST Companion. If suddenly everyone's raving about Getimians, maybe that'll come next, whereas if they're raving about the new Infernals that might be next.<br /> <br /> Still, quite a long way away, I think Exigents is only in 2nd draft(?) and they haven't started Sidereals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T06:01:11-07:00","id":1380367,"title":"","content":"I guess I'd say that the reason to be a splat rather than a one-off is... if they want them to be a group that forms a society with a clear role in the world, where interaction with each other matters, and other characters in the world have clear opinions them.<br /> <br /> (My reservation about Liminals is that though the forms of Exaltation can be adapted to fit lots of stuff (just slap on some Charms, Castes, animas, etc), I'm not sure how the spirit of them really meshes with Exalted. At root, you're descending from a story in Shelley's Frankenstein of an alienated creation, misbegotten by science, marked by a sorrowful and haunting tone, tending to self-destruction, marked by jerky, unnatural and discomforting, ugly movements and separated from society by nature, not just by persecution or being &quot;spirited away&quot;. How do we really mesh that, in spirit, with the themes of Exalted being born from uplifting magical forces that bestow upon humans beautifully stylish kung fu and the weighty questions of heroism? Are the writers really trying to be a bit too-clever-for-their-good and relying on their skill to make something work, that ultimately doesn't work that well, without many more changes than is apparent so far? Well, let's find out soon!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T06:26:55-07:00","id":1380372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380367#post1380367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(My reservation about Liminals is that though the forms of Exaltation can be adapted to fit lots of stuff (just slap on some Charms, Castes, animas, etc), I'm not sure how the spirit of them really meshes with Exalted. At root, you're descending from a story in Shelley's Frankenstein of an alienated creation, misbegotten by science, marked by a sorrowful and haunting tone, tending to self-destruction, marked by jerky, unnatural and discomforting, ugly movements and separated from society by nature, not just by persecution or being &amp;quot;spirited away&amp;quot;. How do we really mesh that, in spirit, with the themes of Exalted being born from uplifting magical forces that bestow upon humans beautifully stylish kung fu and the weighty questions of heroism? Are the writers really trying to be a bit too-clever-for-their-good and relying on their skill to make something work, that ultimately doesn't work that well, without many more changes than is apparent so far? Well, let's find out soon!).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not believe that any of the features you point out in Frankenstein are incompatible with how you summarize Exalted.<br /> <br /> I for one anticipate the Liminal Exalted as existing in a space of &quot;there's something spiritually profound in us being the Chosen created by an inhabitant of the depths of the Underworld bearing the more gritty, visceral aspects of death and loss, but we still kind of lack the pomp and the glamour&quot;. I think there's something distinct and interesting in them being... let's say Exalted who don't quite wear being cool and impressive on their sleeve, while still carrying something the others do not that is quite evocative and almost universally resonant.<br /> <br /> I find they've still got just enough of the spiritually significant and heroic inclination to fall short of a concern of &quot;just build a CofD splat and call it Exalted&quot;. The closest they might get is with the need for a Bond, but I think the specifics make that sufficiently mythic rather than postmodern folklore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T06:36:17-07:00","id":1380373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380367#post1380367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the weighty questions of heroism?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's probably a lot you can do with the weighty questions of heroism when the hero (or antihero) is a twisted monster born of obsession.<br /> <br /> I do see your overall point that they're different in tone from other splats, but I think that's good because sometimes one player (or the ST) wants to have a very different kind of tone, and this is a way for them to do so in a manner that feels less anti-tonal than doing it with a Solar, perhaps.<br /> <br /> Probably it would be awkward if there were thousands of them, but I think there's only supposed to be like 50.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T07:01:33-07:00","id":1380377,"title":"","content":"You both make a good positive case. Honestly, let's just see how it works out! Maybe it could work really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T07:09:08-07:00","id":1380378,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we'll have to wait and see.<br /> <br /> With 10 different kinds of Exalts available for play (each of which has 4-5 variants), I can well imagine STs will want to think carefully about the themes they want to explore in game, and therefore which Exalt types to allow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T08:08:07-07:00","id":1380383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380366#post1380366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And I'm more interested in being a horrifying flesh golem trying to fit in to a band of more human Exalts than in a mysterious underworld patron.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, but do you envision your horrifying flesh golem having total antipathy towards their creator?<br /> <br /> &quot;I exist because the Dark Mother breathed life into a failed resurrection attempt making me one of her Chosen. Why did she do that and deliver me to this half-alive existence? Who the fuck cares! Wanna see me take out my eyeballs?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not asking for Glories: Dark Mother but some answers would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-11-2020, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:09:06-07:00","id":1380409,"title":"","content":"This actually makes me wonder how much Liminals know about their creator. How does a Liminal know they were given life by the Dark Mother?<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder how it complicates their themes and relationships; they are created by the obsession of some mad scientist or necromancer, defined by their own connection to a mortal (who presumably often is their creator, at least at the beginning, but it wasn't clear if it had to be?). Only actually, it was really the Dark Mother who created them via that process?<br /> What changes if Frankenstein's creation realises that his &quot;father's&quot; experiment would have done nothing, had it not been for the intervention of a mysterious &quot;mother&quot; from the Underworld?<br /> <br /> Anyway. I don't really find the Dark Mother a very compelling part of Liminals so far. She feels to me like she's thrown on because every Exalt type needs a patron. I'd have been fine with them actually just being created by botched resurrections. But it does probably require some information; and I see your point about pointless mysteries. (Sometimes I find those give the ST flexibility. Generally... I don't.)<br /> And perhaps more info on her will make her more compelling to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:34:27-07:00","id":1380446,"title":"","content":"Liminals as their own Exalt type I think over just an Exigent I think is in part because Liminals were conceputlaized first (they were origianlly gonna be pitched for a book in 2e) and because there is some setting exploration they can do with their source of Exaltation being from the Underworld and they themsleves having the Alchemical/Promtehan-style &quot;new being&quot; thing going with their bodies.<br /> <br /> I also have felt that Liminals do a lot of helping Abyssals focus, interestingly. It kind of reminds me a bit of Lunars acutally. In 1e, Lunars while having a lot of flaws, were a <i>particular kind</i> of shapeshifter. This got lost in 2e where nearly any shapeshfiting nich epossible was put into the Knack system in part well, due to the Knack system needing to justify itself mroe and their Charms felt diluted. 3e notably goes ab it back to 1e's focus, but with a lot better idea of how to implement that. Lunars are a partiuclar kind of shapeshifter means other Exalts get a bit of shapeshifting and it not feeling like it steps on Lunar toes. An Exigent who can turn into a fox isn't weird if they're patron was a fox spirit and that was just a subset of what htey do. Abyssals doing swarms of vermin all vampire style or Infernal shintai similarly don't feel like they attack Lunars as much as those are again, <i>particular kinds</i> of shapeshifting,r ather htan giving Lunars the whole thing cart blanche and anything else doing that being infringing.<br /> <br /> Abyssals to some extent had this too. In 1e and 2e, they were the splat obviously inspired by vampires, but there was also a lot of body horror, ghoulishness, and zombie aesthetics too. This isn't bad in itself, some of WW's own vampires did that, but it kind of meant Abyssals were at the same time presented as what is often teh apex undead in a lot of fantasy and anime while at the same time also ahving a lot of the &quot;base&quot; undead stuff. It also meant that nearly anything Underworld realted was assumed to be Abyssal playground, resulting in their themes being stretched thin since well, there was no where else to put it. Liminals kind of allow Abyssals to focus on a particular sort of undead, namely the vampire, lich, or necromancer-king. Liminals pick up a lot more of the body horror and corporeal undead elements I think.<br /> <br /> The different relationship with power also stands out. Abyssals being Death's Lawgivers has a very different route for powers than the Liminal focus on being well, liminal beings. Being Lord of the Dead is different than being a being on the threshold of life and death, which Abyssals were kind of had forced on them in a way in 1e and 2e. It just gives more focus I think and helps also explore parts of the Underworld thematically that were kind of at times limtited to the power-based themes of Abyssal Exalted.<br /> <br /> I think also that the writers feel just there's confidence in fleshing them out. That they have Asepcts at all, thsoe Aspects could be on themes that aren't just the corpse-elements of previous editions Abyssal books, and that they can explore a kind of dark anti-heroism in a way that Abyssals do differently to me seems to imply there is at least enough interest to give them that. Much like how Getimains got full Castes and Attribute Charms because the writers thought, &quot;You could tell a story with just a Circle of these guys&quot;, I think that the same happened with Liminals in a way that felt bigger than an Exigent or an Essence-only optional splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 04-11-2020, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T15:01:23-07:00","id":1380499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380409#post1380409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually makes me wonder how much Liminals know about their creator. How does a Liminal know they were given life by the Dark Mother?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, the old Kickstarter preview (or possibly a dev comment; I can't double check right now) noted that a newborn Liminal could feel the receding touch of their Mother, and the first Liminal ever mentioned (in <i>Masters of Jade</i>) descended into the Underworld to &quot;face the judgment of his dark mother,&quot; so maybe she's actually a presence in their lives.<br /> <br /> This is of course based on old, old information, and can't be taken as gospel.<br /> <br /> As for Mother herself I'm with you in that I don't particularly care who or what she is. I already have what I personally need from her: an ominous name to invoke in narration when you need to hype up your Berserk-Frankenstein-Claymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T17:42:58-07:00","id":1380522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380409#post1380409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they are created by the obsession of some mad scientist or necromancer</div> </div> </div> </div>Or lovestruck poets. What you're describing sounds like it'll really only make the Marrow Aspects.<br /> <br /> See, that's the other thing that I think will make the Chernozem work in Exalted; that the literary and mythological basis for people grappling against mortality runs the gamut. It features in what is probably the oldest surviving piece of pen to paper, there remain shades of it in every person that is still taken in by a cold reader passing themselves off as a spirit medium. In a world like Creation where supernatural powers provably exist? Take everybody in reality who has a difficult time processing loss and let them proactively grasp for <i>something</i> to let them overcome it, or be taken in by confidence tricksters who'll pull off a scheme with a paralysed cat in an indigenous burial ground for a fee*. I can readily imagine vast numbers of people trying that stuff, more than enough to let the Dark Mother take her pick.<br /> <br /> That and every asshole who wants to play God by carving up a bunch of people with particular qualities they value and trying to mix the bits up together to create a supreme example of the type.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only actually, it was really the Dark Mother who created them via that process?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you not think that it can be both? That the driving emotions behind the desperation are a necessary conduit or component of the process? The Liminal Exalted aren't like the others, every one is apparently custom made, I think that can be kind of read as meaning that each instance requires something as big as whatever allowed the first Celestial Exaltations.<br /> <br /> Either that or the essential principles are no different than any other assignment of Exaltation; the Unconquered Sun cannot or will not choose people as Dawn Caste Solars who do not fit the type, and that comes down to the person that you were before. The Dark Mother might bestow Exaltation, but the Aspect comes from... somewhere else in order to create the new person wholecloth. Similar to but different from all other Exalted.<br /> <br /> I personally am interested in the Dark Mother only insofar as I'm intrigued at being provided with... implications for a deity whose need for Chosen is expressed in such a manner, and is motivated enough to experience Diminishment with every one that is new. I don't need it to be much, just enough to create a compelling bit of background for them any maybe a personification of some of the driving themes and activities.<br /> <br /> * Ahh darn it, now I need to acknowledge that the possibility of becoming monstrous actually does have a legitimate place insofar as their personhood is provisional and tenuous and there's valid drama in dealing with the possibility of losing it or not wanting it. That they're not just animated corpses but the hijacked (and from one perspective, partially fulfilled) attempt to create a new human, and that question of humanity can lead towards other interpretations of &quot;dead is better&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:21:12-07:00","id":1380532,"title":"","content":"Ah damn it, I shouldn't have gone back to read the Kickstarter preview. That has reminded me that for every single Liminal, there's a brief moment where the person responsible for them gets to believe that the thing worked.<br /> <br /> I'm sad now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:36:45-07:00","id":1380534,"title":"","content":"That's basically my view. Liminals are much more then Frankenstein, the Aspects listing the emotions while simple, allows for so many hooks on why someone would mess with a corpse and try to make it live again. Where Abyssals teeter at the edge of death and make a deal to survive, forever changed, Liminals are pretty much the other way around. It also helps the fact we have been confirmed that the methods of preparing the Liminal body is totally up to the creator, meaning anything can work as long as they believe it can bring the dead back. This could be ritual necromancy, or it could be hasty bargain with a spirit, a journey to dump the body into a stagnant pond in a Shadowland, use a artifact to cut off some years off their life for it or even as so much as crying onto the body's chest, just begging and begging for them to open their eyes. The emotion is central there, regardless of the used method, an absolute belief that the body will breath once more. I think that kinda stories are very evocative, and have to make Liminals very interesting as they have to deal with said expectations and wishes for when they do arise. More then just them being rigged-up Fraken projects(Really I only see them potentially being made of different bodies after they are already alive, as they go through life and replace parts for their Charms.)<br /> <br /> For the Dark Mother, I agree with Levi that I find her interesting on the view of a shady figure literally ripping pieces of her soul out each time to make Liminals, that even with such a cost to herself she doesn't care but continue on to accomplish whatever it is she wants to fix, whether the Underworld or Death itself, i'm interested in learning more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T02:21:49-07:00","id":1380605,"title":"","content":"So I remembered why I got it into my head that the unbound Liminal would turn monstrous:<br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/294219437203128322/698821923056123944/Screenshot_20200412-110644210_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/294219437203128322/698821923706110032/Screenshot_20200412-110653630_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T05:17:29-07:00","id":1380623,"title":"","content":"Indeed, although it bears noting that small details in the corebook can be provisional. There things about Lunars I expected, even looked forward to, based on the core that were dummied out for their own book. Such things happen.<br /> <br /> On the note of the Dark Mother, published information this far does indeed describe her as intermittently speaking to the Chernozem. I think this can have potential even if playing one interested in policing the veil, and not just for being pressured. A distant voice to offer commentary on your actions, with whom you can have certain short conversations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:37:41-07:00","id":1380657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380605#post1380605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I remembered why I got it into my head that the unbound Liminal would turn monstrous</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it makes sense to me that they'd have their own version of Centimani. Perhaps it was a casualty of the previous developers leaving?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:38:31-07:00","id":1380658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380335#post1380335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, the bit Wizard quoted said mortals only and &quot;one Lunar cycle&quot; before you're dirt and memories, but if that's not actually <i>accurate</i>, then I'm down with the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can walk that back slightly. We're simplifying it for Essence but there's room for some greater nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:49:51-07:00","id":1380665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379754#post1379754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">They can forge a connection to a new mortal, but it's not easy.</span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The emotion is what defines your Aspect</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></i></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is what gave me the impression that the Liminal's sentiments for their creator or the next anchor HAD to be defined by their Aspect, which is defined by their creator's motivations for making them.<br /> <br /> Looking again, it seems Leliel MIGHT have pasted two different articles back-to-back, and there was no connection intended with these two sentences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:58:28-07:00","id":1380666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380665#post1380665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking again, it seems Leliel MIGHT have pasted two different articles back-to-back, and there was no connection intended with these two sentences.</div> </div> </div> </div>That be it yeah, I recall it being from two different discord posts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T16:35:13-07:00","id":1380787,"title":"","content":"...Wow, those screenshots weren't supposed to be that big.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380657#post1380657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it makes sense to me that they'd have their own version of Centimani. Perhaps it was a casualty of the previous developers leaving?</div> </div> </div> </div> Hopefully not. It's not just a Promethean thing, it's a classic &quot;enhanced monster hunter&quot; trope.<br /> <br /> It also ties well into the idea of Liminals as people who <i>came back wrong</i>, allowing them to veer into more traditional territory in that vein, when they usually touch upon it by just... not being what their creators intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 04-12-2020, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:57:11-07:00","id":1380808,"title":"","content":"One thing that annoys me with &quot;Frankenstein monster&quot; creatures is how some authors try to have their cake and eat it too with regards to how &quot;dead&quot; they are.<br /> <br /> If you're dealing with a creature made only (or at least primarily) with actual human flesh and organs, and its heart beats and its neurons are firing, then it's alive. It shouldn't be suffering from necrosis and decay; it shouldn't need formaldehyde or other preservatives for blood. It should heal on its own from injuries without needing a specialist necromancer to repair it. Hell, it should actually be capable of sexual reproduction as long as it has the proper organs.<br /> <br /> You know; like the actual, original Frankenstein's Monster.<br /> <br /> Either they're alive because of scientifically-understood biological processes, or they're just advanced zombies animated by necromantic magic.<br /> <br /> <i>Exalted</i>, at least, can and will lean on &quot;they're animated through divine magic&quot;. That's sufficient to explain why Liminals may not be able to sexually reproduce (soul mumbo-jumbo) and why they can regenerate from &quot;fatal&quot; damage, and why they can crumble into dirt if they don't have emotional sustenance.<br /> <br /> But ironically, it seems that they're actually going to lean on biology for things like &quot;they can heal on their own, they don't need chemical preservatives, and they bleed actual blood&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T20:39:30-07:00","id":1380844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380666#post1380666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That be it yeah, I recall it being from two different discord posts</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I didn't get that, myself. And it's all in one post, so I assumed it was all from the same Discord post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:33:18-07:00","id":1380968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379716#post1379716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think folks will find a lot of the interesting naming conventions of Exalted Advantage come out of the specific Advantages and Caste powers rather than a system topic, which - by virtue of necessity and ease of understanding - has more virtue in being boringly-named than being interestingly-but-obscurely-named. <i>Ten Thousand Forms, Living Artifact, Undying</i>...you can be evocative and functional at the same time, but there's a point where you get diminishing returns.<br /> <br /> <b>Exalted: Essence</b> needs to appeal to new players. I think we'll reexamine system topic names if playtesting reveals some fundamental confusion as to their purpose and over their use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta say, I wasn't a fan of the name &quot;Exalted Advantage&quot; but having listened to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview\">The Story Told</a> interview, I am absolutely hyped about it.<br /> <br /> Exalted Advantage is literally the thing that excites me most about Essence now. It seems absolutely epic.<br /> <br /> Now that said... any plans to have playable gods/demons/Fair Folk? I wasn't a fan of Graceful Wicked Masks, but only because the elements that made Fair Folk interesting PCs were really clunky. But if they could be rendered down into Exalted Advantage the way you've handled Sidereal Astrology... that'd be epic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:30:33-07:00","id":1380991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380968#post1380968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that said... any plans to have playable gods/demons/Fair Folk? I wasn't a fan of Graceful Wicked Masks, but only because the elements that made Fair Folk interesting PCs were really clunky. But if they could be rendered down into Exalted Advantage the way you've handled Sidereal Astrology... that'd be epic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the Essence core as of right now (10 Exalt types take up a lot of space), but I can't say right now if/when we might have any support books, or what they'll contain. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>In-House Developer for <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> and <b>Exalted </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23832-dixiecyanide","name":"DixieCyanide","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:08:06-07:00","id":1381007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1380968#post1380968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gotta say, I wasn't a fan of the name &amp;quot;Exalted Advantage&amp;quot; but having listened to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380917-exalted-essence-dev-interview\">The Story Told</a> interview, I am absolutely hyped about it.<br /> <br /> Exalted Advantage is literally the thing that excites me most about Essence now. It seems absolutely epic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep I find Exalt Advantages so cool!! I feel they are a perfect way of capturing Exalted and their different vibes and niches. And frankly just having all these powers condensed to one paragraph is interesting seeing, especially for Sidereals.<br /> <br /> For those who don't know, I think this is the current list of Exalt Advantages that was revealed and what they do, though know it's all subject to change.<br /> <br /> Infernals <br /> Devil-Body. For a scene Infernals may change into a demon form, causing the effects of some of their charms to go differently or have cheaper costs.<br /> <br /> Unwoven Cuadjutor: the Infernal may once per session ask the Dm a question and they must answer.<br /> <br /> Sidereals <br /> Arcane Fate: after leaving the scene people start to forget about the Sidereal, explaining their actions as the work of passing strangers as they forget all details of the Sidereal. For Exalts this may be contested by a Diff 5 Intergrity roll or if they have an Intimacy to the Sidereal. If so they always remember.<br /> <br /> Weaving Destiny: the Sidereal may weave a Destiny modeled after an archetype, profession, or social roll and give it to another character with a touch. When attempting a task which resonates with that archetype the target may transfer dice for automatic successes up to the Sidereals Essence. A destiny lasts for 5 years up to the Sidereals discretion. They may only be subject to one destiny at a time. A Sidereal may apply a Destiny to themselves and with it they lose access to Arcane Fate, allowing people to remember their fake destiny.<br /> <br /> Solars<br /> Supremacy of Ability: Solars do not pay the mote cost to use Excellencies<br /> <br /> First Among Equals: Solars always win ties, Solar PCs win against Solar NPCs<br /> <br /> Liminals<br /> Undying: Liminals are able to get up and can't be incapacitated as long as their brain remains intact.<br /> <br /> Child of Death: may interact with Incorporeal ghosts as if they were corporeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:33:59-07:00","id":1381014,"title":"","content":"Yeah, those are actually great. Fitting, simple, easy to remember.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:18:50-07:00","id":1381034,"title":"","content":"Don't forget about Lunar shapeshifting either, that's a big one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:40:32-07:00","id":1381041,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure, but that's a more obvious one. (I wonder what their other advantage will be?)<br /> <br /> I'm quite curious as to how they'll do shapeshifting in a simple way. It's never been simple... but I think it could be. Each animal could just give 1 or 2 bonuses, rather than a bunch of complex stats. Or there might just be, say, a few possible bonuses (tough hide, flying, being small, being big, water breathing, poison), and you get 1-3 as appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-13-2020, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T12:03:30-07:00","id":1381053,"title":"","content":"The other thing I like about those Exalt Advantages is that the level of rules looks about right; it's proper rules, not narrative, but it's simple and straightforward. And doesn't involve any calculations (Solars get free excellencies, not -2m cost or something).<br /> That's the kind of mechanical level I'm hoping for generally.<br /> <br /> Very interesting that Sidereals turn (Essence) dice into successes. I wonder if that's a common effect for Essence? Or just a Sidereal thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-13-2020, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T12:41:31-07:00","id":1381062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Exalts this may be contested by a Diff 5 Intergrity roll </div> </div> </div>I notice that this is an Integrity roll, not a Wits+Integrity roll, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T13:27:49-07:00","id":1381076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1381041#post1381041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite curious as to how they'll do shapeshifting in a simple way. It's never been simple... but I think it could be. Each animal could just give 1 or 2 bonuses, rather than a bunch of complex stats. Or there might just be, say, a few possible bonuses (tough hide, flying, being small, being big, water breathing, poison), and you get 1-3 as appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div> Scion 2e did an interesting thing with this in the Greek gods' ability to transform people.<br /> <br /> Put simply, the cursed target uses their own traits, but gains automatic successes on rolls that capitalize on their new form, while rolls that go against the form's nature suffer drawbacks. This doesn't actually make success less likely, but makes successful rolls more complicated unless you get a lot of extra successes (this mechanic, Complications, is the best part of Storypath).<br /> <br /> The rules for personal shapeshifting are marginally more complex, without any drawbacks, but I like the simpler setup. Add special abilities, as you suggest, and it'd be golden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T13:35:09-07:00","id":1381079,"title":"","content":"Honestly, 90% of the time, I find shapechanging is for a)fast travel, or b)sneaking. 5% of the time it's for coping with certain environments; being warm, breathing water, etc, or for better senses. And then 5% of the time it's to make a character better at combat via better soak, better dice pools, or merits. That's... not very much, and I think can definitely be simplified. And the rest of it can be simple anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:28:50-07:00","id":1381166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1381041#post1381041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, sure, but that's a more obvious one. (I wonder what their other advantage will be?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Range Advantage relating to Lunar tattoos? Of course Casteless don't have them but maybe their will be a clause and a benefit when they dont. Maybe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:10:41-07:00","id":1381178,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Alchemical Charm slots/loadouts are represented in any way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1381007#post1381007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Child of Death: may interact with Incorporeal ghosts as if they were corporeal.</div> </div> </div> </div> How I hope that this is an actual Liminal trait rather than a simplification just for <i>Essence</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:43:21-07:00","id":1381187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1381178#post1381178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Alchemical Charm slots/loadouts are represented in any way.<br /> <br /> How I hope that this is an actual Liminal trait rather than a simplification just for <i>Essence</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same, allows for earlier and cooler expansion onto &quot;Incorperal attack&quot; charms. I wouldn't mind that becoming their gimmick","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 04-13-2020, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T10:25:48-07:00","id":1381360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1381178#post1381178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Alchemical Charm slots/loadouts are represented in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>From Neall on the Discord earlier:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alchemicals can I think - currently, before playtesting - take any number of Universal Charms they want but have a limited amount of room for Modes and proprietary Charms </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T15:53:26-07:00","id":1381459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1381187#post1381187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same, allows for earlier and cooler expansion onto &quot;Incorperal attack&quot; charms. I wouldn't mind that becoming their gimmick</div> </div> </div> </div> It also means any Liminal can be a ghost hunter or medium without having to spec for it, because you just... see ghosts, and can fight them, at all times. On top of that, Liminals would always be <i>aware </i>of ghosts whether they want to or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T15:59:51-07:00","id":1381461,"title":"","content":"If they're all supposed to be policing the line between life and death, then yeah, why not give them all that basic power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T18:12:17-07:00","id":1381489,"title":"","content":"Especially if it makes them more VULNERABLE to ghosts, which gives them a LOT more reason to care about ghosts and the threat monstrous ghosts pose to mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T23:52:08-07:00","id":1381542,"title":"","content":"One thing I\u2019m curious about is how well Essence is going to support the \u201cNon-combat\u201d stuff, like social influence, crafting, and all that. I suspect that Social Influence will stick around, but I\u2019m concerned that my preference for \u201cthinky\u201d type characters will be left by the wayside save for the bits that involve punching people with your brain.<br /> <br /> (Granted, they\u2019re not necessarily all that well supported in base 3e as is, but I could easily imagine cutting things all the way back to \u201ceh, just have it be a basic die roll, we don\u2019t really need to waste wordcount on it\u201d in the name of simplifying things.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 04-15-2020, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T00:45:46-07:00","id":1381552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1381542#post1381542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I\u2019m curious about is how well Essence is going to support the \u201cNon-combat\u201d stuff, like social influence, crafting, and all that. I suspect that Social Influence will stick around, but I\u2019m concerned that my preference for \u201cthinky\u201d type characters will be left by the wayside save for the bits that involve punching people with your brain.<br /> <br /> (Granted, they\u2019re not necessarily all that well supported in base 3e as is, but I could easily imagine cutting things all the way back to \u201ceh, just have it be a basic die roll, we don\u2019t really need to waste wordcount on it\u201d in the name of simplifying things.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I somehow doubt that. It may not be SUPER robust but I doubt that Social and Mental avenues will be neglected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T00:50:35-07:00","id":1381554,"title":"","content":"Go look at \u201cwhat I love about exalted\u201d the thread. I think the developers would be foolish to ignore how many people love exalted specifically because they can play epic socialites and loremasters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T01:20:19-07:00","id":1381561,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/294219437203128322/699880337081368616/1586876995844.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> So I'm told that these are the Getimian Caste marks. I don't know if that's true, since I got them from a second-hand source, but if so... I think I like them.<br /> <br /> They clearly invoke the Eight Trigrams, specifically the ones associated with the solstices and equinoxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T01:37:55-07:00","id":1381564,"title":"","content":"I now imagine that the Getimian Exaltations were locked inside something that looked like the Pan'ku Box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T01:50:10-07:00","id":1381569,"title":"","content":"Those DO look neat, but if the imagery of the Trigrams makes me a bit uncertain, as last I heard there were deliberate efforts to move away from Orientalism when not appropriate in some parts of Exalted, like the Getimian Mote Pools not being called &quot;Yin&quot; and &quot;Yang&quot; motes anymore.<br /> <br /> I mean if they are, Neat. Those look really cool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T04:42:40-07:00","id":1381605,"title":"","content":"Those are the first draft of the marks, posted on the Discord.<br /> <br /> If they do feel odd to you, just ask yourselves what are the Sidereal Caste marks are and there position IRL. I'd think they serve as a nice parallel no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T15:06:26-07:00","id":1382390,"title":"","content":"Immaculte Styles are in Essence. I don't think anyone's shocked by that.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of charms aren't in trees, but there's more repurchases. When there are trees, they're quite short. This includes Martial Arts (which aren't their own Ability). Looks like 3, 4, 5ish maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T07:45:04-07:00","id":1383366,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">2) withering/decisive still exist as this is still built on 3e's framework<br /> 3) there's a dice cap</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">3.5) there's also a success cap</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T07:33:04-07:00","id":1384190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1383366#post1383366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) withering/decisive still exist as this is still built on 3e's framework</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. That's a big plus for <i>Essence</i>, which I expected to have a less dynamic combat system.<br /> <br /> But what was <i>1)</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T09:04:38-07:00","id":1384199,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Something irrelevant. It was just something about that conversation, not a preview/spoiler.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-27-2020, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T09:08:37-07:00","id":1384200,"title":"","content":"On Withering/Decisive...<br /> <br /> I think that you can actually simplify the Exalted combat system a lot while still keeping withering/decisive. The idea of it modifying your initiative is quite a radical one, and has a lot of interesting strategy. But if you take out different dice pools, maybe simplify the way damage is done to create a 1-step (rather than 2-step attack), simplify Stealth, take out Clashes, simplify gambits (especially grapple!), simplify the movement rules, take out Onslaught penalties, take out mote regen, simplify battle groups, simplify being crashed, have everything use double 10s, etc, etc...<br /> I reckon you could end up with a reasonably simple system that still has attacks that change your initiative, and attacks that do damage but are based on your initiative, and has some kind of tactics. Of course, each thing you remove reduces possible tactics, so it's a question of what best to remove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-27-2020, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:04:14-07:00","id":1384222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384200#post1384200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Withering/Decisive...<br /> <br /> I think that you can actually simplify the Exalted combat system a lot while still keeping withering/decisive. The idea of it modifying your initiative is quite a radical one, and has a lot of interesting strategy. But if you take out different dice pools, maybe simplify the way damage is done to create a 1-step (rather than 2-step attack), simplify Stealth, take out Clashes, simplify gambits (especially grapple!), simplify the movement rules, take out Onslaught penalties, take out mote regen, simplify battle groups, simplify being crashed, have everything use double 10s, etc, etc...<br /> I reckon you could end up with a reasonably simple system that still has attacks that change your initiative, and attacks that do damage but are based on your initiative, and has some kind of tactics. Of course, each thing you remove reduces possible tactics, so it's a question of what best to remove.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really have the feeling that Exalted 3e didn't use the Initiative system to it's full potential, especially for the ST. I'd really like they have gotten farther to represent what Initiative abstracts than just &quot;martial advantage&quot;, as least for the ST, and I think it could go for players as well to a certain extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:16:42-07:00","id":1384226,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... what do you mean?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:38:54-07:00","id":1384231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384226#post1384226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm... what do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a dev so my designing skills suxx. Here's an example of a &quot;ST Charm&quot; I wrote once to try out some ideas. <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Will you stop me, or save the children ?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost : 5init</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type : Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword : But.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The luck every villain gets when the hero finally close on him. The ST designates something a PC care for deeply or has a positive intimacy toward. The designated object or person find itself in a terrible situation, usually through the confusion of the fight : the close walls start crumbling around it and threaten to smash it, a close magical relic activates and starts contaminating it with Wyld influence or Strange powers, a group of innocent bystanders get thrown in the middle of the confusion need protection else their fate sealed, etc \u2026</span></span><br /> <br /> (I've used the shortest and simplest one as an example, you can find the others I did <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12AIsDCFk7uZnbiBz1Y09oaOlwbyDbGVwkHVoB0SHGkg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>)<br /> <br /> As you can see, my perspective (which is not everyone's perspective but I'M defending my opinion) is that Initiative can be used to abstract so much more about the flow of combat rather than just &quot;I can strike you dead&quot;, at least from the ST perspective. I'm the kind of ST that doesn't care if the PC's win or loses as long as I was able to come up with reversals and unique situations, and I think an Initiative system could be one of the best thing ever to implement it in a &quot;tactical fighting game&quot;. I think it's a shame they didn't go this way with the core, and I hope Essence will give some replacement/ideas for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T22:39:24-07:00","id":1384360,"title":"","content":"So I am WAY behind the times, as I just now even heard of Essence. Is there a solid place to review information regarding it, other than reading through all 45 pages? And, any news/timeline/guess on a Kickstarter, or if there won't be one? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T22:44:45-07:00","id":1384363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384360#post1384360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am WAY behind the times, as I just now even heard of Essence. Is there a solid place to review information regarding it, other than reading through all 45 pages? And, any news/timeline/guess on a Kickstarter, or if there won't be one? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>There'll be a Kickstarter. As for where to read up on it... Well, it's either mine through Discord Statement Teasers, or read through these pages. :P This is probably less painful.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/exalted-essence-dev-team-interview\" target=\"_blank\">This podcast does have a lot of intel and may be easier to digest</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T12:00:08-07:00","id":1384678,"title":"","content":"Everything I've heard about the mechanics has gotten me really pumped for Essence. Except... I don't like the idea of flattening the curve. I think the different roles for the exalt types are a key part of the lore of the world and the fun of the game. Having solars be generally the best but the other celestials shining through with their special thing makes it interesting to me.<br /> <br /> I am very concerned about the change in power dynamics between the dragon blooded and solars. The return of the solars (and abyssals and infernals) is supposed to be a world changing event. The future of Creation is up for grabs as the powers of oblivion and hell stake their claim on the world meanwhile individual people who stand up against the darkness are being invested with perfection from the sun. But if each solar (or equivalent) is only worth two dragon blooded... that's not important. That's the equivalent of 600 new dragon blooded when the Realm alone has 10,000 and all the entrenched artifacts and power that come with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13508-necrobotany","name":"necrobotany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T12:16:06-07:00","id":1384681,"title":"","content":"I guess it depends how much they flatten the curve? And in what way? (I mean, measuring the power of a Solar PC compared to that of a Dragonblood PC is tricky. I play a game with 3 Solars and 2 DBs, and the DBs do feel weaker, but in quite a complex way, such that I couldn't really say how much they're weaker.)<br /> <br /> It may be relatively easy to change of course; if a 3rd ed ST says &quot;guys, I want to flatten the differences, so the Solar PCs are only starting with 10 charms not 15&quot; players will be very unhappy. But if an Essence ST says &quot;I've decided Solars aren't powerful enough, so you can all have 10 charms instead of Essence's normal 5&quot; they'll be delighted.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're running a Solar game, Solars will absolutely be more powerful because of PCs' insane XP-gain. And if you're not running Solars, I guess you could still give Solar NPCs more xp than expected for their age.<br /> <br /> Although it's not always that simple, of course, since a character with 100xp isn't twice as powerful as one with 50xp, and having more charms isn't always better than having more powerful charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T12:56:41-07:00","id":1384685,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about that a lot too and I'm still undecided. On the one hand yes as outlined there's a lot of issues with stuff, I've posted about that before.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, in my not inconsiderable experience, a lot of new players kind of struggle with the idea. They struggle with the idea that as a Solar they are feared and reviled as demons, they are hunted by the greatest nations in the world, and sometimes they struggle with the power disparity that their characters have.<br /> <br /> So maybe if they tone down/back on all of those things a bit it can be friendlier to newer players? That way new people coming to it can be like &quot;Oh cool, sun-heroes, I wanna be one of them. You like the Water guys? Sweet, lets team up and have adventures!&quot; without getting too caught up over the fact that the water guy is way weaker but the sun hero is a demon. It's not like you need to be 10x more badass than the DBs to overthrow the Realm. Dragonblooded themselves can overthrow the Realm.<br /> <br /> Then again that asymmetric balance and different styles of play can be fun...then again-again so many people are excited for Essence because they want mixed groups, and that's why they won't buy a single book of 3e for the next ten years because to them Exalted is about an Alchemical, an Abyssal, a Sidereal and a DB bombing around Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:09:00-07:00","id":1384717,"title":"","content":"To add to DrLoveMonkey's point :<br /> <br /> Exalted is a game which offers the possibility of playing completely overpowered characters, but which does nothing to educate players/STs about the dangers inherent to playing OP PCs, or to warn them about what specific builds/setups are likely to break their games.<br /> <br /> Players are handed dozens of different ways to derail their own campaigns and spoil the fun at their table, and are then expected to have both the system mastery and the personal maturity to thread the fine line carefully on their own.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I love this freedom that 3e offers to be as balanced or as broken as you like... but that is definitely something that can lead to terrible new player experiences. So in that respect, I think that flattening the curve should help limit these sorts of power disparities that can create problems at the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:59:21-07:00","id":1384731,"title":"","content":"Also due to the complexity Ex3 it just as often leaves players wondering what people are talking about with mega OP Solars who can battle Alhat and Octavian with their pinkies. Like if their melee charm list looks like:<br /> <br /> Call the Blade<br /> Summoning the Loyal Steel<br /> Glorious Solar Saber<br /> Dipping Swallow<br /> Excellent Strike<br /> Iron Raptor Technique<br /> Sandstorm Wind Attack<br /> Solar Counterattack<br /> Bulwark Stance<br /> Fire and Stones Strike<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I think that might be a pretty fun Solar to play, not a lot of big powerhouse charms but you've got a lot of utility and variety.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also the &quot;oops I made my character invincible&quot; or &quot;my player made a character who's invincible&quot; is made a lot worse for not having an ST guide. It's like trying to design daily encounters without the DMG in DnD. It really doesn't work well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T01:10:25-07:00","id":1384801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>necrobotany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384678#post1384678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything I've heard about the mechanics has gotten me really pumped for Essence. Except... I don't like the idea of flattening the curve. I think the different roles for the exalt types are a key part of the lore of the world and the fun of the game. Having solars be generally the best but the other celestials shining through with their special thing makes it interesting to me.<br /> <br /> I am very concerned about the change in power dynamics between the dragon blooded and solars. The return of the solars (and abyssals and infernals) is supposed to be a world changing event. The future of Creation is up for grabs as the powers of oblivion and hell stake their claim on the world meanwhile individual people who stand up against the darkness are being invested with perfection from the sun. But if each solar (or equivalent) is only worth two dragon blooded... that's not important. That's the equivalent of 600 new dragon blooded when the Realm alone has 10,000 and all the entrenched artifacts and power that come with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned this a bit earlier, but there's few things at work ehre to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> The first is that equality for PCs doesn't mean equality for NPCs. Dragon-Blooded NPCs probably just dont's cale quite as fast or as often as PCs, and this is shown in the example QCs we have for regular Exalted, where htey're still fightable and approachable as the game rules are not a long term physics engine. This goes the other way with other Exalts, who are as powerful or not as need be. PCs in general are able to beat eachother doens't mean that NPCs work on teh same logic. Dragon-Blooded PCs are exceptional people. Solars are next to them doing thier thing too. That's a conceit the game has currently really that needs to be kept in midn with the flattened curve. The system is trying ot be simple and foster cross-splat play. But the system also assumes NPCs don't use PC rules, and don't have to weaken PCs to a point of crippling to make up for the in-setting numbers advantages or no that the setting has.<br /> <br /> Second, I actually tink in 3e there's a general feel I get that had the united Realm of the Scarlet Empress had tried, they probably <i>could </i>fend-off all the Solars and other shit showing up. Not like, completely. The empire can't last forever, there were cracks a long time forming that Lunars and over-extension had shown, and so on. The Realm <i>is</i> a juggernaught of thousands of Dragon-Blooded who have put it sboot on the neck of the world despite hundreds of Celestial Exalted working against htem. It's also one who's leader is gone, and which quickly falls apart as being able to be that when it collapses and drags the rest of the global structure down with it. If the Empress were still there, the Realm very likely probably could carry along for a few more centuries, although dozens of Solar dominions and other things all over the map showed up as the influence shirnks. Think the Eastern Roman Empire and how it kind of slowly just withered away with the encorachment of Arabs, Persians, Armenians, Mongols, and eventually Turks. What the Realm is in now though is something more akin to the 5th Century Western Empire and is straignt-up falling apart and going to change hte world as a result. <br /> <br /> That said, the way Solar magic at least in the base system manifests, the edges come in acces to magic the Dragon-Blooded just can't (higher sorcery, Evocations, unique artifact creation, exptertise in some leements of leading armies and statescraft their magic expresses). Solars also ahve Supernal Ability in 3e, which means you get out of the gate pulling bullshit fast, creating wonders unseen in centuries and often not doable by most characters ins etting (Essence 5 is rare afterall but every SOlar has Supernal). Basically, Solars leverage resrouces better, they can get them better, and so on. But they and thier dervitives are still in the end of the day a huge extra side-swipe in a world that was already trying to capitalize on the Empress being gone. It's less that Solars won't matter, it's just that they're not (to me at least) the Number One Crisis in the world (Realm hegemony collapsing is) and happen to be pretty damned good in their nature in exploting it and making it worse.<br /> <br /> Kind of how I see it, had the Realm been united, they might have been able to put Solars in a similar situation Lunars have been for a while, while still losing stuff like Thorns or some other satrapies. As it is now, I kind of doubt they can survive with the Blessed Isle as a united polity, let alone a lot of satrapies not gobbled-up by new Solar empires and dominions about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T01:24:57-07:00","id":1384803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384731#post1384731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also due to the complexity Ex3 it just as often leaves players wondering what people are talking about with mega OP Solars who can battle Alhat and Octavian with their pinkies. Like if their melee charm list looks like:<br /> <br /> Call the Blade<br /> Summoning the Loyal Steel<br /> Glorious Solar Saber<br /> Dipping Swallow<br /> Excellent Strike<br /> Iron Raptor Technique<br /> Sandstorm Wind Attack<br /> Solar Counterattack<br /> Bulwark Stance<br /> Fire and Stones Strike<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I think that might be a pretty fun Solar to play, not a lot of big powerhouse charms but you've got a lot of utility and variety.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also the &quot;oops I made my character invincible&quot; or &quot;my player made a character who's invincible&quot; is made a lot worse for not having an ST guide. It's like trying to design daily encounters without the DMG in DnD. It really doesn't work well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fun because summoning your weapon is usually a go to for many players when they discover Solar Melee 3e (because it's cool and fluffy), but then compared to &quot;optimized content&quot; yeahs it seems so far behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T01:27:29-07:00","id":1384804,"title":"","content":"Kind of a TLDR as I reread my post a bit: There's more to the Solar impact on the world than just raw power and that raw power doesn't override that the world is going through some things to enact it on. That therea re a lot of DBs who are powerful deosn't change the fact that Solar power manifests in a different way that still maeks them impactful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T01:34:34-07:00","id":1384805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384804#post1384804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of a TLDR as I reread my post a bit: There's more to the Solar impact on the world than just raw power and that raw power doesn't override that the world is going through some things to enact it on. That therea re a lot of DBs who are powerful deosn't change the fact that Solar power manifests in a different way that still maeks them impactful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you, it's actually written in the Core Book presenting all kind of Exalts : Solars are in particular master of Evocations and Sorcery, that are domains that impact the world in a quite specific fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T01:56:50-07:00","id":1384808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384805#post1384805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with you, it's actually written in the Core Book presenting all kind of Exalts : Solars are in particular master of Evocations and Sorcery, that are domains that impact the world in a quite specific fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Craft. Making it so only Solars can realistically maintain the artifice of the First Age is far more impactful to the Status Quo than just &quot;I killed 10,000 Dragon Bloods with a dull spoon&quot;<br /> <br /> Now granted I don't mind Solars still having advantages, but i'm one of those who feels that a single battle-specced Dragonblood and a Dawn getting in a fight shouldn't be a certain result.<br /> <br /> Sure, it may be 70:30 or even 60:40 in favor of the Dawn, but I find it boring if the fight is 100:0 in the Solar's favor.<br /> <br /> Solars don't need everyone to be chumps in order to be the nominal &quot;best&quot; or to represent a major upheaval to the status quo.<br /> <br /> Hell, in our world, we get people who change the status quo with something as simple as realizing that milkmaids who get cowpox don't get smallpox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T02:08:55-07:00","id":1384809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384808#post1384808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Craft. Making it so only Solars can realistically maintain the artifice of the First Age is far more impactful to the Status Quo than just &quot;I killed 10,000 Dragon Bloods with a dull spoon&quot;<br /> <br /> Now granted I don't mind Solars still having advantages, but i'm one of those who feels that a single battle-specced Dragonblood and a Dawn getting in a fight shouldn't be a certain result.<br /> <br /> Sure, it may be 70:30 or even 60:40 in favor of the Dawn, but I find it boring if the fight is 100:0 in the Solar's favor.<br /> <br /> Solars don't need everyone to be chumps in order to be the nominal &quot;best&quot; or to represent a major upheaval to the status quo.<br /> <br /> Hell, in our world, we get people who change the status quo with something as simple as realizing that milkmaids who get cowpox don't get smallpox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah sure I didn't talk about Craft but it's true as well.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm fine with combat either way. I'm okay with Solars dominating teams of Dragon-Blooded just as much as I'm okay with Solars fighting almost on-par with 1 Dragon-Blooded. Both premises work for me, it's only about how you and your players want the game to feel at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T04:11:47-07:00","id":1384820,"title":"","content":"I agree that &quot;advantage&quot; should never mean &quot;utterly overwhelm&quot; - but it should mean that a lower-tier Exalt should be at a disadvantage against a higher-tier Exalt (assuming equal investment in that area of skill, and excluding niche powers like flying air aspects out-jumping any Solar which).<br /> <br /> But based on comments in the interview along the lines of &quot;no Mode being more potent than any other Mode&quot;, and &quot;Celestial's having Charms that are more broadly applicable, but not more powerful&quot;, it looks to me like the Devs are aiming for it to be 50:50. <br /> <br /> Sure you could give lower-tier NPC Exalts less charms to put their power at an appropriate level to celestial PCs, but if those charms are just as potent I don't really see it working very well - they'll have a few less tricks up their sleeve, but the ones they have will let them go toe-to-toe with no disadvantage whatsoever. The reverse argument for Celestial NPCs is just as valid.<br /> <br /> On another note restricting the Solar power advantage to Sorcery and Evocations is limiting - not every character is a Solar/Celestial level sorceror, and coming up with unique evocations for every Solar's artifacts defeats the object of a fast-play system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4972-hurum","name":"hurum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T04:35:34-07:00","id":1384822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hurum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384820#post1384820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that &quot;advantage&quot; should never mean &quot;utterly overwhelm&quot; - but it should mean that a lower-tier Exalt should be at a disadvantage against a higher-tier Exalt (assuming equal investment in that area of skill, and excluding niche powers like flying air aspects out-jumping any Solar which).</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I'm happy with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;no Mode being more potent than any other Mode&quot; </div> </div> </div> Did they say that? I don't remember it (not saying you're wrong).<br /> Though of course, if 40% of universal charms have a Mode that buffs Solars, 70% of universal charms have a Mode that buffs all Celestials (including Solars), and 30% have a Mode that buffs Dragonblood, then Dragonblood are weaker overall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Celestial's having Charms that are more broadly applicable, but not more powerful&quot;, it looks to me like the Devs are aiming for it to be 50:50. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... maybe. But a Solar charm that gives double 9s on social rolls and a Dragonblood charm that gives double 9s on Inspire rolls is exactly that (the Solar charm is more broadly applicable, but not more powerful per-se), and that's often how 3rd ed works between Solars and DBs. (Dragonblood are good at inspiring and okay at other social stuff, Lunars are good at lying/seduction/intimidation/doing stuff related to cultures and okay at other stuff, Solars are just good generally in social stuff.)<br /> <br /> Having more broadly applicable powers <i>is</i> more powerful, even if the charms themselves give a similar buff.<br /> My Dragonblood can see and fight spirits, same as a Solar, except they can do it even without a mirror. My Dragonblood is good at making friends... at drinking parties. Solars can do it everywhere. My Dragonblood is good with terrestrial elemental-themed spells, especially Wood and Earth-based ones. Solars are good at all spells. My Dragonblood is good at crafting things from earth or wood. Solars are good at crafting regardless of material. Etc.<br /> <br /> Also, of course, that's Celestials overall. It might be talking mostly about Lunars, Sidereals, Getimians, Abyssals, Infernals... there's a lot. Solars get free excellencies, and if they still have bigger mote pools (which they may or may not) they'd still be using a lot more charms at a higher power for longer.<br /> <br /> Not to say that they're not intending to reduce the power disparity, they clearly intend to, but I don't think that makes it 50:50. My impression was more like taking it from 70:30 to 60:40.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure you could give lower-tier NPC Exalts less charms to put their power at an appropriate level to celestial PCs, but if those charms are just as potent I don't really see it working very well - they'll have a few less tricks up their sleeve, but the ones they have will let them go toe-to-toe with no disadvantage whatsoever. The reverse argument for Celestial NPCs is just as valid. </div> </div> </div>Huh... that'd certainly make it a very different experience. My general experience is that Solars are throwing down great power at a couple of things, but most have a lot less tricks up their sleeve than the less-powerful Lunars, or Sidereals, or Infernals, and a bit less than Dragonblood (though Dragonblood are way behind in power). So Solars tend to do amazingly when it's their focus, and not well when they get caught in a kind of situation they're bad at (for example, our Dawn is a rock-hard tank and brilliant general, but doesn't cope well with mobile snipers, or politics, or getting on with people, or being a moral person. Our Zenith is amazing at preaching, and little else. Our Eclipse is good at gathering intelligence, but poor at combat. Whereas Lunars can deal okay if not great with almost everything).<br /> So if DBs and Solars had similar powers but DBs had far less... yeah, that'd be a very different Solar experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note restricting the Solar power advantage to Sorcery and Evocations is limiting - not every character is a Solar/Celestial level sorceror, and coming up with unique evocations for every Solar's artifacts defeats the object of a fast-play system. </div> </div> </div>Very true. Our 485xp game has an Eclipse with Solar sorcery and no evocations, a Dawn with a few evocations and no sorcery, and a Zenith and Eclipse with no sorcery or evocations. Making Solar Sorcerers or Solars with magic weapons the best is basically saying &quot;all Solars are supposed to be sorcerers or wield magic items.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-30-2020, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T05:09:32-07:00","id":1384824,"title":"","content":"Yeah, First Age Craft and Sorcery projects are important for Solars.<br /> <br /> On a level of Creation's narrative, I do think I'd caveat that a lot with &quot;In those instances where the First Solars dealt with pure elemental forces, with Fate and with protean essence, they rarely got really exceptional results *without* cooperation with master-artificer Dragonblooded, Sidereals, Lunars...&quot; (with either party in the driving seat). (I wouldn't want to go back to &quot;If you weren't a Solar, you were an unnecessary bystander to First Age artifice&quot;, which was an impression which came up in 2e era discussions). But that's a narrative thing and would probably be mechanically clumsy to implement too mechanically.<br /> <br /> It's of course not totally the only way to establish Solar importance - I'm very sympathetic to those complaints that they don't just want Solars to be &quot;just&quot; Celestials, with Twilights alone being super-Celestial, or to over-emphasize rulership such that leadership focused Zeniths or War focused Dawns alone are super-Celestial, and so on.<br /> <br /> But I do think the way I'd like to frame Solars is that we get the impression that they mattered, and still do matter, because there were and are really important situations where having the best and most skilled to do heroic deeds and provide inspiration, which couldn't just be substituted by huge numbers of Dragonblooded. Aka, that sheer quality has a quality of its own that quantity just can't match. Sometimes you *need* the mightiest duelist or the best spy and you can't match it by vast amounts of less capable appointments (&quot;I don't want more. I want fewer and better&quot;), and that's why the Solars were important. Rather than, y'know, Solars must be completely resistant to and evenly matched with overwhelming numbers of DBs in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T06:10:30-07:00","id":1384828,"title":"","content":"I have to say, having the Solar being the most important Exalted during the First Age, and the decline of Creation since their disappearance, being measured in 'how many DB you can defeat at the same time' is the most boring thing you can do.<br /> <br /> Personal combat is the least meaningful way the Solar Host could possibly have to influence Creation as a whole. Bureaucracy, law, crafting, sorcery, directing troops in war are all methods that make them much bigger than any other Host.<br /> <br /> So, I welcome the flattening of the curve. Solars don't need bigger pools. What they need is bigger magnitude. And they have it. The rest are just details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T06:27:22-07:00","id":1384831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384685#post1384685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, in my not inconsiderable experience, a lot of new players kind of struggle with the idea. They struggle with the idea that as a Solar they are feared and reviled as demons, they are hunted by the greatest nations in the world, and sometimes they struggle with the power disparity that their characters have.<br /> <br /> So maybe if they tone down/back on all of those things a bit it can be friendlier to newer players? That way new people coming to it can be like &quot;Oh cool, sun-heroes, I wanna be one of them. You like the Water guys? Sweet, lets team up and have adventures!&quot; without getting too caught up over the fact that the water guy is way weaker but the sun hero is a demon. It's not like you need to be 10x more badass than the DBs to overthrow the Realm. Dragonblooded themselves can overthrow the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would be terribly lame. Being Anathema is one of the few <i>actual</i> limits on Solar power, and it's basically the reason they <i>have</i> animas to begin with.<br /> <br /> I've played in games where revealing your anima was a big deal, and games where it wasn't, and things got a lot more interesting when you were incentivized to conserve motes and avoid the blatant SFX.<br /> <br /> The kind of KoC-style crossover groups people lust after should be supported, but they shouldn't be <i>easy</i>. If anything, the role of such PCs as potential bridgebuilders who can see past the ancestral vendettas and cycles of violence, as opposed to just being a ragtag group of weirdos going uncommented on, should be emphasized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T06:33:51-07:00","id":1384832,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the fact that the world thinks they're demons although they're not (but, potentially, could be a Nobunaga-style &quot;Demon&quot;) is one of the most interesting things to me about Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T06:37:39-07:00","id":1384833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384832#post1384832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the fact that the world thinks they're demons although they're not (but, potentially, could be a Nobunaga-style &quot;Demon&quot;) is one of the most interesting things to me about Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I had some players asking me for NPC's to be nicer with them but ... well sorry you are one of the demons who destroyed the world, dude","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T07:45:10-07:00","id":1384841,"title":"","content":"I sometimes think I make NPCs too friendly, honestly, but &quot;aaagh demon run for it&quot; gets boring after a while. But then, while they're not perfect at hiding their nature, most of the PCs in games I play/run do put some decent effort into seeming, at least, to be ambiguous powerful entities but not demons. Actually one Lunar PC has been a woman for 3 months so as to not give the game away to the NPCs they're travelling with, which they might realise if she turned back into a he.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-30-2020, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T11:03:28-07:00","id":1384874,"title":"","content":"I honestly think some of the advantages Solars are said to have in Essence are actually nothing to socff at either. I mean just a short break down they have:<br /> <br /> <b>First Among Equals: </b>Always winning ties is one of those subtle, but kind of powerful effects depending on soem things. It means if you're smart on how you manage your pools, you can overwelm and you basically get &quot;For free&quot; that extra success against everyone. This might matter in combat, sneakinga bout, social things, competitions like racing and projects, and so on. This one feels like it adds up pretty quick.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Abiltiy</b> giving free Excellencies depends, mind. I dobut Solars get +dice pool dice in Essence as they're tyring to constrain pools. But just inherently rolling more and doing better adds up wihtout being &quot;I'm effectively immune to everyone.&quot; And it also expresses Solar Ability to just churn out bullshit when no one is stopping htem, be it trianing troops, artifacts, large scale projects, and so on.<br /> <br /> They also have just good access to anything anyone else can get. Full Evocation access, three Circles of sorcery, two of necromancy, and Sidereal Martial Arts are pretty effing solid powers that give a lot of flexiblity.<br /> <br /> Due to their innate powers, plus likely Caste Advantages, there seems to be this theme of <i>subtle</i> power for Solars. THey have a lot built-in before Charms that make them strong and interesing. You likely roll more dice, win all ties, and have more things out of native Charms to work with as options. And with Universal CHarms, likely effects that are again, sublte-yet-powerful. You see this inb ase 3e a bit I think. THere's some raw power inherent in giving folks mutations ala making beastfolk for Lunars. I'm not quite sure those are <i>as good</i> as what Solars do with Tiger Warriors. And the Solar can make the Tiger Warriors out of the gate. But it's not so much better that the Lunar might as well not have ever tried.<br /> <br /> And this is before actual native Charms, which might end up with things again, just options no on eelse gets that are impactful. I imagine for instance Wyld-Shaping Technique being one, and hta tin itself opens a lot of avenues for Solars to be Surprise Truck of Plot ot everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:03:23-07:00","id":1384885,"title":"","content":"I've never liked the whole sunshine Ubermensch thing. It's like the Ultramarines in Warhammer 40K. I get that they are dangerous and hunted, but I don't need anyone at the table sitting in golden smugness and looking down on everyone else. Levelling the playing field is something I find really appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:07:48-07:00","id":1384888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384831#post1384831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That would be terribly lame. Being Anathema is one of the few <i>actual</i> limits on Solar power, and it's basically the reason they <i>have</i> animas to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why flattening the power curve would have to be in conjunction with reducing the insistence that Solars are wretched spiteful demons. Otherwise you're just both not stronger than the DBs and not a divine saint.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384831#post1384831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kind of KoC-style crossover groups people lust after should be supported, but they shouldn't be <i>easy</i>. If anything, the role of such PCs as potential bridgebuilders who can see past the ancestral vendettas and cycles of violence, as opposed to just being a ragtag group of weirdos going uncommented on, should be emphasized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I know where you're coming from, but the difficulty here isn't in the characters ability to see past historical violence, it's in the players ability to feel like a complete chump next to the other player. If your awesome Dragonblooded swordmaster is super weak compared to the Solar guy who's just dabbling a bit into Brawl, that sucks, and lots of people might end up thinking this whole <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XXOOGsgTQr0\" target=\"_blank\">water swordsman thing</a> is really super cool, but if I have to play a level 5 character when all the other guys in the group are playing level 15 characters then no I'm not going to do it. Why do I have to be half as strong if I want to be an elemental hero, or 3/4 as strong if I want to be a fate ninja? DnD doesn't punish me for wanting to be a Druid instead of a Fighter. Sounds to me like this game isn't so much Exalted as &quot;Solars and their sidekicks.&quot;<br /> <br /> Balancing that with the power disparity is really hard, and also not intuitive to people coming into Exalted from almost any other system, or even into RPGs for the first time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384841#post1384841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sometimes think I make NPCs too friendly, honestly, but &quot;aaagh demon run for it&quot; gets boring after a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can be a bit of another problem as well. It can be frustrating to players, and definitely feel punitive especially to new players. One might flare their anima in the middle of the Lap and think if they just use their powers to save somebody from falling off a cliff or something everyone will realize that they were wrong to think Solars were demons and they can all get on with being a proper loved hero.<br /> <br /> That exact sentiment is something I've run into a lot with new players actually. I've even had players just want to sort this whole thing out, so even without needing to flare their anima they walk up to a Dynast, flare their castemark and try to make friends.<br /> <br /> On the flipside I've also seen STs just brush past the whole thing and say &quot;Yeah okay that Immaculate Monk saw you fighting the fey creatures so he decides that you're not so bad and the rest of the town agrees.&quot; just so they don't have to deal with all the players feeling like they're being punished for picking the sun hero guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:35:02-07:00","id":1384910,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I don't think I've ever seen that, except by characters who didn't know about the Immaculate Order or whatever (so the <i>players</i> knew what could happen). But maybe the ST just explained it clearly that the Solars are hated by the Evil Empire.<br /> <br /> Not saying your players are stupid or doing it wrong or whatever, just not something I've really seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T14:56:02-07:00","id":1384929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384910#post1384910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, I don't think I've ever seen that, except by characters who didn't know about the Immaculate Order or whatever (so the <i>players</i> knew what could happen). But maybe the ST just explained it clearly that the Solars are hated by the Evil Empire.<br /> <br /> Not saying your players are stupid or doing it wrong or whatever, just not something I've really seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see every new player do it, but it has happened to me more than once. I think maybe the direct &quot;Oh they hate us? That's just because they're wrong about us though right? So we'll go say hello and they'll realize their mistake.&quot; has only happened once.<br /> <br /> What I have seen happen a ton of times, even with experienced players though is &quot;Aw, fuck it, TIME TO FLARE TOTEMIC! WOOOOO POOOWWWAAAAAA!&quot; at the slightest provocation, and then get either really annoyed when those actions have less than ideal consequences, or go kind of crazy to avoid them. Several times where people exploded multiple animas, they then just used sorcery to flee thousands of miles and hid for several months for a timeskip until the heat died down, and then went on their way.<br /> <br /> One campaign I played in even had that as kind of a running theme. Meet up, go to a place, do one thing, inevitably everyone can't help themselves so we throw around Total Annihilation spells and stuff, and then we scatter and timeskip several months, then meet back up somewhere else and do something else. All so that we could use our awesome Solar might without regard and not have to deal with the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even in 3e the one game I ran in a Realm Satrapy had maybe 2 sessions in before both Dawns flared totemic fighting a small group of mortal saboteurs. They could have easily beaten them with just personal motes, but when you have a giant button that makes you win so hard the universe feels it, it's hard not to push it. Especially when you designed the button.<br /> <br /> If you're going to do that I think you really need to hammer home the point, like the sidebar on page 21 of the 1e Exalted core.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> HIGH AND LOW<br /> The life of one of the Solar Exalted is a whirl of cataclysmic ups and downs. Suddenly, an individual who was merely gifted is Exalted to tremendous stature. The Chosen are unaging and of unfailing health. They possess tremendous physical stamina and can quickly heal from even the most grievous wounds. In all things, they are excellent, and in that which they favor, they are unexcelled. No mortal could hope to best one in combat, and the Solars may challenge the mettle of the Celestial Exalted or bring the tyrannical Realm to its knees. In these individuals is the power to change history and remake the world.<br /> <br /> Yet, they are hunted creatures. Regarded as akin to demon princes in many regions, the reborn Solars must live like shadows. Cosmic beings, they must work their plans among men subtly and walk unseen if they are able. The Wyld Hunt of the Dragon-Blooded is hardly their only fear. They might be stoned or ridden down \u2014 no matter how mighty the hero, enough men with bows will eventually wear him down. Also, countless are the snares of those who would involve the newly reborn Solars in their schemes. From the Gold Faction\u2019s training of Sidereals to oppose the Realm and the Deathlords to the political schemes of the Dragon-Blooded houses and the spirit courts, there are countless powers and interests who would gladly use the Solars as their agents and puppets. Young Solar Exalted who wish to prosper must carefully balance the amount of patronage they receive with the magnitude of the obligations they develop in return to those who tutor them in their infancy.<br /> <br /> Thus goes the existence of the Solar Exalted \u2014 to wield the power of the Sun but to do so with the greatest economy possible, showing their true mighty only when the need is great. Traveling the roads as mendicants, pilgrims and fugitives, they tread lightly and fight when they have no choice or when their consciences compel them to. Some have crowned themselves kings and queens, but so far, their reigns have been brief and ended by the knives of the Wyld Hunt or by some regional power fearful of competition. Those Solars who wish to survive the maturity of their power must play a game of high and low \u2014 living as vagabonds, bandits and troubadours while they master their great power and learn the secrets of their Exalted state.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:18:06-07:00","id":1384934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384888#post1384888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's why flattening the power curve would have to be in conjunction with reducing the insistence that Solars are wretched spiteful demons. Otherwise you're just both not stronger than the DBs and not a divine saint.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think power curve has anything to do with it. Again, Solars can be able to just do shit that DBs can't at scales which quickly undermine DB rule to be villainized. We on Earth seem pretty capable of demonizing groups with religious motivationw ithout having to have them actually be super-powered. Solar Exalted ahving different and still powerful magic seems to be something worth in itself for the view of them by the Immauclte Order wihtout that power bieng &quot;Can mow down armies of DBs single-handeldy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I know where you're coming from, but the difficulty here isn't in the characters ability to see past historical violence, it's in the players ability to feel like a complete chump next to the other player. If your awesome Dragonblooded swordmaster is super weak compared to the Solar guy who's just dabbling a bit into Brawl, that sucks, and lots of people might end up thinking this whole <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XXOOGsgTQr0\" target=\"_blank\">water swordsman thing</a> is really super cool, but if I have to play a level 5 character when all the other guys in the group are playing level 15 characters then no I'm not going to do it. Why do I have to be half as strong if I want to be an elemental hero, or 3/4 as strong if I want to be a fate ninja? DnD doesn't punish me for wanting to be a Druid instead of a Fighter. Sounds to me like this game isn't so much Exalted as &quot;Solars and their sidekicks.&quot;<br /> <br /> Balancing that with the power disparity is really hard, and also not intuitive to people coming into Exalted from almost any other system, or even into RPGs for the first time. ... </div> </div> </div>Seconding this entirely. Setting needs are good, but should not override what a table should use. Going all-in on NPCs don't use PC rules as-written does a lot in this. DBs are as weak and Solars as strong in the world as need be. <i>Your characters</i> are as weak or as strong as the group needs. They don't need to be mirrored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:23:08-07:00","id":1384938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384888#post1384888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's why flattening the power curve would have to be in conjunction with reducing the insistence that Solars are wretched spiteful demons. Otherwise you're just both not stronger than the DBs and not a divine saint.</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems like there should be *some* moderation in the setting for this though, as it would actually work in practice in mixed groups? <br /> <br /> If you're playing a DB who is in a party with Solars (and other Anathema), you'd probably be seen as *somewhat* of a teensy-bit heretical by half of civilization, and the other half (and the rest of Creation) probably sees you as a jumped up imperialist. You certainly don't have the family connections in play, and any Realm you meet may well make a point of making an example of you. If you're a Dynast, and not too much better or worse than that if you're an Outcaste. <br /> <br /> While if you're playing Lunar in that party, we're back to &quot;terrible demon&quot; again, and for Sidereal ronin/Gold it's &quot;.... and who now?&quot;. (Though true, they'd probably have a bit of network access).<br /> <br /> I get the distinction you're making but does seem a bit like, in practice, you'd perhaps really going to get actual members of the same group in this situation quite as extremely. It's a bit less with all the social disadvantages loaded on the Solar side of things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T19:53:57-07:00","id":1384991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384938#post1384938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There seems like there should be *some* moderation in the setting for this though, as it would actually work in practice in mixed groups?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of...but it still gets a bit difficult if Solars are zealously hunted and DBs aren't.<br /> <br /> If you're going by that sidebar that I posted, then the Solars are working in the shadows, walking hidden through society trying to balance their interests against enemies who hunt them and those who would use their power for their own ends. In that setting by proudly proclaiming yourself as being allied with these anathema, you just blew their cover. Or you could hide yourself as well along with them, but why would you want to do that? Unless you're a Dynast you're not an imperial bastard, there's tons of non-imperial outcaste groups, like Lookshy or Heaven's Dragons or the Forest Witches.<br /> <br /> You'd have to present the setting in such a way that being openly anathema isn't actually that big of a problem, which in the current one it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T09:25:57-07:00","id":1385086,"title":"","content":"Sure, that's true, though 3e is different from this than &quot;pure core&quot; 1e: there are a lot more options to pretend &quot;I'm someone a bit powerful but not really a Exalted&quot; that are about. (In early 1e it's like Solars could pretend to be some sort of Scavenger Lord, but options are really limited beyond that.)<br /> <br /> Definitely don't dispute your general point here, it's just that it seemed worth pointing out that in 3e, the actual scenario is seeming to be less like in the same circle, &quot;Dynast held up as the lord-prince of Creation, loved by all, with all access to the Realm's goodies vs guy who has to pretend to be an unassuming mortal&quot;, as much as &quot;Outcaste vs guy who is likely known to be some of supernaturally empowered and potent hero, at least a sorceror... but has to be careful not to flare anima unless he really needs to&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T10:54:13-07:00","id":1385091,"title":"","content":"I think it depends as well on where the game is set. If you're in, say, Jiara or Cherak or the Lap, there's a Realm garrison right there, and even if the locals aren't Immaculate believers they've heard a lot about how awful the Anathema are (plus older traditions from the Shogunate, plus the fact that everyone knows that barbarian armies led by face-eating shapeshifters do, indeed, sometimes attack satrapies).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you're in Skullstone, or Volivat, or Iscomay, attitudes may be quite different. Not &quot;Hooray, a Solar, let us bow down before them!&quot; But not &quot;Aaargh a demon, we must kill it or die trying!&quot;<br /> <br /> So the game I'm playing is set in Sukhmet, an Egypt-expy in the Summer Mountains. I am playing a Dragonblood who believes himself to be, like all Dragonblood in Sukhmet, a descendant of the River God, Sukhmet. Hence his plant-, earth- and water-based powers.<br /> <br /> Then there's Prince Meek, the Chosen of Sukhmet. Obviously, he must be an Exigent, because it's well known that he is Chosen by Sukhmet. Hence his great toughness, mighty strength, ability to heal the sick, and the fact that the sacred crocodiles like him (and didn't eat him). Sun aura? Well, he hasn't shown it much, but that's probably due to his connection with the sun god Ra (who is connected to the River God Sukhmet, as Gods are, they syncretise).<br /> <br /> There's also his foreign witch-wife, who may or may not shapechange. She's got in trouble several times with the government, because everyone suspects of being, you know, a foreign witch. She does, after all, have red hair. Some say she's the Chosen of Set. I've recently learned that she can, in fact, shapechange. So she is indeed a Set-witch. But Set, while tricksome, does sometimes work with the river Gods, using his knowledge of evil to help fight evil, and it makes sense that the Chosen of Sukhmet is married to the Chosen of Set. We just have to watch her to make sure she doesn't go too far.<br /> <br /> Then there's Akhenaten, a mysterious and stealthy noble... my old character thought he might be a shapeshifting witch. Very dodgy. Trying to cover up the Pharoah's kidnapping. Might be some kind of demon, like those Anathema I heard about on my travels... but that seems unlikely. They apparently have an evil mark that appears on their head, haven't seen that.<br /> <br /> Then we've got Penitent Gift, an Immaculate Monk who was in the Wyld Hunt, but got sick of the killing, had a crisis of faith, and has decided to actually hang out with some Solars, Lunars, etc, and see if they're as bad as he was always told. So far his conclusions have been... mixed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway. The point is that this is an isolated part of the world, far from Prasad's Wyld Hunt (although the monks of the kingdom next door got very upset with my previous character and his anathema-ness, but what could they do?) so it works okay.<br /> Obviously it's quite different in Realm Satrapies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T13:09:59-07:00","id":1385127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385086#post1385086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, that's true, though 3e is different from this than &quot;pure core&quot; 1e: there are a lot more options to pretend &quot;I'm someone a bit powerful but not really a Exalted&quot; that are about. (In early 1e it's like Solars could pretend to be some sort of Scavenger Lord, but options are really limited beyond that.)<br /> <br /> Definitely don't dispute your general point here, it's just that it seemed worth pointing out that in 3e, the actual scenario is seeming to be less like in the same circle, &quot;Dynast held up as the lord-prince of Creation, loved by all, with all access to the Realm's goodies vs guy who has to pretend to be an unassuming mortal&quot;, as much as &quot;Outcaste vs guy who is likely known to be some of supernaturally empowered and potent hero, at least a sorceror... but has to be careful not to flare anima unless he really needs to&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and as Wizard points out there's room in the setting for places that don't immediately call down a Wyld Hunt on you the second they suspect you're anathema. You might want a lot more places that are like that if you're going to sell the setting as a place where groups can just freely mix whenever, and tone down the Dragonblooded Wyld Hunts fervor a bit.<br /> <br /> In 3e as it is now the Wyld Hunt is a globally recognized Dragonblooded institution that supersedes the boundaries of politics and law. It's unites Dragonblooded of the Realm, Lookshy, and Outcaste groups worldwide, so that when a Hunt is called all nearby terrestrials put aside their differences and answer. Not literally 100% of the time, that's boring, but it's a pretty big deal either way.<br /> <br /> It's also why the Silver Pact prioritizes going after newly Exalted Lunars so much. If the Wyld Hunt didn't have the reach it did most Lunars who Exalt would just be safe where they are.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not just one way either. From one side, if you're going to flatten the power curve, you should make the setting more agnostic towards what kind of Exalt you are, and from the flip side if you're going to make the setting more agnostic to what kind of Exalt you are you'd better flatten the power curve.<br /> <br /> If you did that I would recharacterize the Realm/Lookshy/Outcastes in the setting. I'd put more of the focus on Threshold kingdoms that have nothing to do the Immaculate Faith whatsoever, and instead of the Realm being a global superpower casting its shadow long out into the edges of Creation, I'd have it be a more a smaller self-contained nation that has the Immaculate Order as one of its local setting quirks. Like have it be &quot;This nation, that calls it self the Realm, has a state religion that demonizes all non-dragonblooded Exalted. Most Celestial Exalted avoid it for this reason. Now, onto Vaneha in the East...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T13:23:55-07:00","id":1385129,"title":"","content":"That makes sense, that you might want to do that, if we're talking about if you *really* flattened it out way more than Essence seems to be. But that's seems a bit more of an abstract argument of y'know &quot;If you dramatically changed things more than my impression of Essence is&quot; I guess... <br /> <br /> In the context of the sort of level of flattening that are seems to be in play in Essence - where Solars still have Solar sorcery and Charm benefits and some significant edges - and the sort of latitude that groups have and setting to actually play up and adjust the salience of social disadvantages so it doesn't cause group friction, I guess my point is, in that situation, don't think there'd be any need to change any setting assumptions at all and there wouldn't be any problems without any setting changes at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T13:57:00-07:00","id":1385135,"title":"","content":"Maybe not in the way some areas are presented, but in the way the setting is presented as a whole. In the 2e Compass Direction South the major cities that got chapters were Chiaroscuro, Paragon, The Lap, Gem, Varangia, Harbourhead, and An-Teng, and all but Varangia are satrapies of the Realm. Even then Varangia is full of Immaculate missionaries.<br /> <br /> If I'm running a 3e group where my Solar players aren't supposed to feel like they're being hemmed in and shouldn't flare their animas, and I pick up Compass Book: South, I have almost no places I can base my campaign on where public flare doesn't equal immediate risk of a Wyld Hunt. That's not good for me as an ST who wants to basically ignore the social advantage/disadvantages of DB vs Solar characters, or downplay them to the point where they're pretty small.<br /> <br /> Even in 3e the power curve is pretty flat, and what we know so far about Essence is that the universal charms are the same for all Exalted, and that Solar specific charms might be more widely applicable or versatile, but not really more powerful. At that point the horrible disadvantages of being labeled Anathema and enemy #1 of all Dragonblooded worldwide would, I think, be too punishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T15:18:24-07:00","id":1385141,"title":"","content":"Maybe you would have to tone down the &quot;Nobody expects the Wyld Hunt!&quot; a bit more back to 1e-2e levels? Well short of &quot;The Realm is just this one distant nation, y'know&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Slight digression, I don't know if this is some dissonance for me; the whole thing of &quot;Solars flare animas, this attracts attention&quot; always seemed to me like a device to set games up such that the action in a story progresses to a big fight scene where Solars flare their animas and do lots of extreme stuff, and then need to move on like the wandering heroes they are, before trouble catches up to them (in ways that evoke David Banner, the A-Team, Vash The Stampede and such hunted hero types). Rather than the Wyld Hunt generally being right there, right then and if you flare you have to deal with it right now. It's somewhat overworked and underfunded and it's not hard to for an ST to either invoke or pass over in any game, for the most part. It's there to establish some genre emulating story logic as to why Solar games establish players as roving heroes, without just going &quot;because&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Ultimately this as a discussion gets to the difficult bit that we're trying to weight something totally unseen (how much Ex:Essence flattens out power), against something which we can talk know about but which is inherently a bit more subject to a fair bit of shifts from game-to-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T01:52:54-07:00","id":1385216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385135#post1385135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Even in 3e the power curve is pretty flat, and what we know so far about Essence is that the universal charms are the same for all Exalted, and that Solar specific charms might be more widely applicable or versatile, but not really more powerful. At that point the horrible disadvantages of being labeled Anathema and enemy #1 of all Dragonblooded worldwide would, I think, be too punishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, NPCs don't use PC scales of power or rules and re adjustable as needed. And things being flat doesn't mean that Solar Exalted aren't able to have great effect on the setting. It' just that it's not apparently in making a career of murdering DBs by the score single-handeldly for free for being a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T02:46:27-07:00","id":1385223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385141#post1385141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the whole thing of &quot;Solars flare animas, this attracts attention&quot; always seemed to me like a device to set games up such that the action in a story progresses to a big fight scene where Solars flare their animas and do lots of extreme stuff, and then need to move on like the wandering heroes they are, before trouble catches up to them</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. It worked like that in our very first Solar game, but I haven't really seen it work like that since. Still, you don't want every game to be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T03:04:33-07:00","id":1385227,"title":"","content":"Wizard, yeah, I think that is admittedly the caveat to that. Even if that's the chief function that the Wyld Hunt serves, you *kind* of don't want it to be a sort of obvious, toothless, plot device thing that players don't believe in and makes every game feel the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T03:19:06-07:00","id":1385228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385216#post1385216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, NPCs don't use PC scales of power or rules and re adjustable as needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boo!<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I have nothing against the average mortal having 3 dice, and PCs playing Heroic Mortals with 11 dice. I have nothing against the powers of QCs being simplified to make them easier to run. I have nothing against DB PCs starting play as established heroes with more &quot;XP&quot; than the average Dynast.<br /> <br /> But, fundamentally, I want there to be a presumption of fairness.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't do that because you're not an NPC!&quot; Goes against the basic premise of what Exalted is about for me. Sure I'm not a mile high volcano monster, but I want my Solar PC to be able to do what a Solar NPC can.<br /> <br /> &quot;NPCs can't do this because you are a Mary Sue!&quot; Well... to some extent, sure. PCs gain XP faster as they go off on adventures. They're the protagonists in their story. But I don't want it to be a pivotal part of how the game works. Other characters should matter, and putting PCs on an untouchable tier doesn't sit well with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T03:41:29-07:00","id":1385229,"title":"","content":"I agree, and I think that it breaks versimilitude. In addition, it makes PCs' achievements less meaningful if the presumption is that, as PCs, they'll breeze past everything.<br /> <br /> PCs with their enormous amount of XP are generally going to do much better than NPCs who've been exalted for a similar time, and I think that's enough. Maybe reinforce this by having NPCs laugh at how a Solar who's been exalted for 3 years could ever dare take them on, before the Solar PC cuts off the 100-year old Lunar's head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T15:51:49-07:00","id":1385313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385228#post1385228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boo!<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I have nothing against the average mortal having 3 dice, and PCs playing Heroic Mortals with 11 dice. I have nothing against the powers of QCs being simplified to make them easier to run. I have nothing against DB PCs starting play as established heroes with more &quot;XP&quot; than the average Dynast.<br /> <br /> But, fundamentally, I want there to be a presumption of fairness.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't do that because you're not an NPC!&quot; Goes against the basic premise of what Exalted is about for me. Sure I'm not a mile high volcano monster, but I want my Solar PC to be able to do what a Solar NPC can.<br /> <br /> &quot;NPCs can't do this because you are a Mary Sue!&quot; Well... to some extent, sure. PCs gain XP faster as they go off on adventures. They're the protagonists in their story. But I don't want it to be a pivotal part of how the game works. Other characters should matter, and putting PCs on an untouchable tier doesn't sit well with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Verisimilitude I think takes a back seat in thsi case to you know, runnability. NPCs invariably aren't going ot ahve complete Charmsets with xp histories as STs in general don't wanna do that shit. Youg ive your NPCs what you think is needed for your group and so on. This means as weak as need be so you don't feel DBs overwelm Solars, or as strong as they need to be so they're an actual challenge to your playgroup. To my understanding, ExEss is leaning ahrd on the QC stuff, and I&quot;m of a view base Exalted 3e probably would have een better had it done so too.<br /> <br /> In the end, many of the mechanics that make Exalted interesting but complex are player-facing and controlled. This is good since one person is managing each character and can handle the complexity. An issue Exalted has always had before was that NPCs used thsoe same rules, but the ST was supposed to handle basically an entire player's toolset single-handedly multiple times. This has lead to issues of over-pwoerful singular entities, or just plain ST overload. Solar NPCs having the full suite of powers your PC has is neat. Expecting that single character to then stand up to a circle of PCs means you are either 1) Cheating anyhow in favor of the NPC using things the PCs can't to even stand-up or 2) Basically just giving your PCs wins anyhow.<br /> <br /> LIke, this is my view having ran Exalted from September 2001. Combat for the ST kind of fucking sucks. And in 3e, I pretty much go whole hog on QCs because each NPC is really going ot ever use probably six to ten things in a fight anyhow, and I think making them jus timpactful for the group is going to b emore something I can manage than trying to make a cast of twenty beings each as complex as my PCs for the cast. And if I got there, I might as well let hteir power or weakness be what enforces setting rather than making the tosy fo rPCs ot interact with the game define thos elines.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T22:57:23-07:00","id":1385355,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m all for asymmetry, but I want it to be balanced asymmetry. I don\u2019t want to run a team of DBs against my team of Dolars and have to remember 60+ charms across all of them, but I also don\u2019t want Cathak Cainen to have 50 health levels just because he\u2019s a boss guy in the campaign and thus is more powerful than the equivalent Essence 5 PC. <br /> <br /> QCs have better stats and abilities to make up for their lack of massive charm combos and stuff, it\u2019s not a perfectly balanced trade off, but it\u2019s pretty close sometimes, and in the right ways usually. In Exalted a player actually can become Hallaster Blackcloak if they work at it.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s also said with the knowledge that the Exalted are not the be-all end-all of night in the world of Creation, and there are things that there do exist things that players can\u2019t really hope to become, but that\u2019s because there\u2019s a fundamental in-universe distinction between a Solar and a third circle demon or behemoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T22:10:36-07:00","id":1385538,"title":"","content":"Have we heard anything about the great curse? That\u2019s another thing that in the game helps balance out the different characters and campaign styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T23:02:14-07:00","id":1385547,"title":"","content":"Quibbling about power levels and which splat can hit the hardest is the most boring part of the different splats in Exalted. The interesting things to compare are like, how a Solar archer lands a clear shot on a Dragon-blooded who can control the wind. I'm glad Essence seems to be focusing more on the latter than the former.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1384888#post1384888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Balancing that with the power disparity is really hard, and also not intuitive to people coming into Exalted from almost any other system, or even into RPGs for the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean here? Do you mean 'people coming into Exalted from other RPGs won't understand how some types of Exalted are more or less powerful than others? Because I don't think that's true. There are other RPGs that allow for wild disparity in power between characters in a group, and do it elegantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T00:41:29-07:00","id":1385556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385538#post1385538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we heard anything about the great curse? That\u2019s another thing that in the game helps balance out the different characters and campaign styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all we know so far is that Solars are more susceptible to it. More specifically, going against your Major Virtue is a trigger for the curse for all Exalts, but for Solars this is also true when going against your Minor Virtue (All Exalts have 1 Major and 1 Minor Virtue out of a pool of 7 possible Virtues).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T07:42:27-07:00","id":1385603,"title":"","content":"Currently, there are going to be 7 Virtues, including the original 4 and also &quot;Ambition&quot;. That leaves 2 unknowns.<br /> <br /> I'm really skeptical, because I felt that Principles and Ties were superior to the four Virtues in terms of function and verisimilitude.<br /> <br /> Valor had nothing to do with courage and everything to do with self-assertiveness, aggression, and establishing one's place in a hierarchy of dominance and authority. But while we could argue about the definition of courage, at least no one was confused about what Valor looked like.<br /> <br /> Conviction and Temperance, on the other hand...<br /> <br /> And &quot;Stupid Useless Compassion&quot; was a meme for a reason.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how they plan to keep Valor and Ambition distinct enough from each other such that you don't feel punished for having high Ambition without the Valor to see it through, or high Valor without enough Ambition to think of DOING anything with your position of dominance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T08:22:03-07:00","id":1385606,"title":"","content":"Have they said that the original 4 are included? I remember they said there'll be Virtues, but not that Conviction, Compassion, Temperance and Valour are included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T13:48:20-07:00","id":1385648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385606#post1385606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have they said that the original 4 are included? I remember they said there'll be Virtues, but not that Conviction, Compassion, Temperance and Valour are included.</div> </div> </div> </div>I checked, and the exact wording was that that old Virtues would be returning, but no mention of how many of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> The seven Virtues are supposed to define or categorize Intimacies in some way, which I remembered. I also remembered how Neall couldn't answer what this meant for the distinctions of &quot;Ties and Principles&quot;, but I suppose the seven Virtues replace those two categories.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Ambition Intimacies&quot; makes some sense. They could take the place of Principles which reflect goals you want to achieve in the world, and a general strength of Ambition would make it easier to form and keep Intimacies representing grand Ambitions.<br /> <br /> &quot;Temperance Intimacies&quot; could take the place of Principles which reflect the creeds by which you live, such as &quot;Honesty is the best policy&quot;. Again, the more Temperate you are, the easier you find to structure your life according to strong principles, and to not waver from them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Compassion Intimacies&quot; could take the place of Ties, specifically positive Ties to people or beasts. The more Compassionate you are habitually, the easier you find it to care about other creatures in general, even when you've just met them, but especially if they're already big parts of your life.<br /> <br /> &quot;Passion/Lust Intimacies&quot; could take the place of positive Ties for objects and activities, reflecting a character's favorite possessions like manses or artifact weapons, and favorite pleasures like exploration, battle, gambling, sex, or food. The more lusty you are, the more you seek to enjoy life to the fullest.<br /> <br /> &quot;Conviction Intimacies&quot; could take the place of negative Ties in general. The Virtue of Conviction represents your rejection of everything you fear, and your commitment to avoiding or destroying those things you perceive as aberrations and detriments to the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, fear and hatred aren't backed by any Virtue at all, which would be an interesting commentary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-04-2020, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T14:48:25-07:00","id":1385659,"title":"","content":"It came up that Robert Vance, who as I gather along with Eric Minton have veto power over such things, was one of the earlier advocates for cutting Virtues in 3e out entirely due to the Intiamcy system taking them on. They seems on board with the Virtues as they are in Essence, so my guess is they're for sure not the 1e and 2e takes. If only since if theywere, they'd not justify being in a simpler systme than the one that canned them in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 05-04-2020, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T19:00:38-07:00","id":1385705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385603#post1385603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And &quot;Stupid Useless Compassion&quot; was a meme for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>As-written, Compassion was actually pretty good because it was easily channeled in support of others. Which, as a PC supporting others was something you could be expected to do a lot of.<br /> <br /> The problem was a lot of tables interpreted of Conviction as the &quot;do what you want&quot; virtue rather than the enduring hardship virtue which totally muscled out the good part of Compassion and left it the sucker virtue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T20:28:58-07:00","id":1385724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385705#post1385705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As-written, Compassion was actually pretty good because it was easily channeled in support of others. Which, as a PC supporting others was something you could be expected to do a lot of.<br /> <br /> The problem was a lot of tables interpreted of Conviction as the &quot;do what you want&quot; virtue rather than the enduring hardship virtue which totally muscled out the good part of Compassion and left it the sucker virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it's an example of how introducing multiple &quot;Virtues&quot; into a game is a hazardous balancing act.<br /> <br /> That's why I wrinkled my nose at the idea that they're introducing seven; because previous Editions failed to properly balance a mere FOUR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:17:04-07:00","id":1385733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385547#post1385547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean here? Do you mean 'people coming into Exalted from other RPGs won't understand how some types of Exalted are more or less powerful than others? Because I don't think that's true. There are other RPGs that allow for wild disparity in power between characters in a group, and do it elegantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I think most people are not going to assume that as a default. What I'm picturing is something like this...<br /> <br /> <br /> Storyteller: Okay, everyone get a chance to flip through Exalted Essence? Got an idea for a character?<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded Archer Player: Oh yeah, I was flipping through and saw this red haired warrior woman using her bow as a vine-grapple hook and, yeah, she hooked me. I'm going to hookshot all over the place.<br /> <br /> Storyteller: At least until you get all giddy and shoot it off ten times and run out of motes. That works out with your character though since I think you said you wanted close ties with your powerful grandmother?<br /> <br /> Solar Swordsman: Ten times? What it costs two motes or something?<br /> <br /> DB: No? We get ten motes, it costs one mote each.<br /> <br /> So: Oh, weird, I actually get 20 motes it looks like.<br /> <br /> DB: That's a weird way to do things, are your charms more expensive or something?<br /> <br /> So: Maybe, that would explain why I get a free excellency. Like I've got this one that lets me attack five times for three motes and a willpower.<br /> <br /> DB: That can't be it, I've got one that lets me attack three times for six motes and a willpower, and only after I spend a round aiming. Maybe Dragonblooded are like the social guys then, with Exalted's big social system and all that.<br /> <br /> So: Hmmm, not...really? From what I see all my social powers are just stronger too.<br /> <br /> ST: Yeah actually I've been looking through it and it looks like Solars are just like that, they're just the best in all the areas.<br /> <br /> DB: Okay, that's kind of messed up. I guess they're dull and straightforward so they get to be the strongest? You can be cool or you can be really powerful.<br /> <br /> ST: They're not really dull at all, they've got a ton of cool powers, like being able to form a sword out of sunlight, or shoot a massive explosive arrow that leaves the whole area burning like a bonfire, or even leap into people's souls and do literal battle with their inner demons.<br /> <br /> DB: Alright, so what's the point of playing a Dragonblood then?<br /> <br /> ST: Well you get access to these other cool powers.<br /> <br /> DB: But they're not actually as good as the Solar ones, like my vine grapple is just worse than that Monkey Leap charm that the Solars have, and I can use it less, and all my other abilities are just worse as well?<br /> <br /> ST: Yeah, but a Solar can't do the vine grapple thing without evocations or sorcery or the like.<br /> <br /> DB: What's an 'evocation'?<br /> <br /> ST: It's like if the Solar had a green jade bow, he could get it to shoot a grapple vine, or if he was wearing a blue jade breastplate he could protect himself with a whirlwind.<br /> <br /> DB: Okay I'm just going to be that then. Why'd they make friggin' NINE other kinds of exalts if the Solars are just so much better in every way? That's like if we were playing DnD and the Wizard got the same HP as a barbarian, the same attacks as a fighter, the skills and feats as a rogue, sorcerer's metamagic and divine casting. Then say &quot;yeah, but they didn't get wyld shape, so that's the reason to play a druid.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:16:21-07:00","id":1385761,"title":"","content":"This is a textbook example of why representing the power and excellence of the Solar Exalted by making their math the best is one of the worst design choices in the game. Here's hoping Essence changes that.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as your D&amp;D example goes - wizards can summon monsters collectively tougher than the barbarian, can far outpace the fighter's attacks with their AoE spells, can replicate entire class features of the rogue with a handful of low-level spells and shapeshift like druids, on top of a million other things like teleportation etc that are unique to them.<br /> <br /> Dungeons and Dragons has been very poorly balanced throughout all of its editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:33:05-07:00","id":1385763,"title":"","content":"I honestly think they should just have a sidebar saying &quot;Celestials are stronger, Terrestrials are weaker, if you don't like it don't play a Terrestrial in a mixed game&quot; (but maybe said in a nicer way).<br /> <br /> The alternative is to balance them all, which kind of wrecks the fluff where 400 Lunars have been just about beating 10,000 Dragonblood (and Sidereals) for centuries.<br /> <br /> (Balancing Solars, Abyssals and Infernals with each other, the Lunars and the Sidereals is fine.)<br /> <br /> Or make it clear that DB PCs are unusual. But with word count constraints, most likely DB NPCs will need to base their powers on the same charms as PCs, so it can't be done via charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:35:32-07:00","id":1385764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385761#post1385761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dungeons and Dragons has been very poorly balanced throughout all of its editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd disagree a bit concerning DD4, but I don't want to make this topic about DD so I'll not argue further <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Concerning Solar perfection through Maths, I think it's a complicated topic though. RPG like Exalted have math included in them, if you want to make something out of one Exalted being the best, you most likely need to make it concrete through the maths of the system (what Wizard refers as verisimilitude). I'm not saying this was done well, but I think the problem is complicated from a dev point of view because you have to deliver on some premises that are not simple to &quot;math out&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:46:39-07:00","id":1385767,"title":"","content":"I'll be frank. Solars are the best at things a human can do. Ie things any character can potentially do via rolling dice. &quot;Roll more dice&quot; is a pretty boring way, IMO, to simulate this, but it's also the easiest and most accurate way. There's also &quot;don't bother rolling for small stuff&quot;, like Graceful Crane Stance, but in Essence the advice is that you do that for everyone. <br /> <br /> Anyway. Hopefully, as Solars already get free excellencies and win draws, and I imagine Universal charms will cover lift more, jump higher, dodge faster, etc, with modes covering the extra dice, the actual Solar charms will be more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:55:24-07:00","id":1385769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385764#post1385764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd disagree a bit concerning DD4, but I don't want to make this topic about DD so I'll not argue further <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wholeheartedly agree with you. As far as a team-based tactical wargame goes, DD4 has a pretty good balance between player characters.<br /> <br /> Also, one thing that ought to be said here is that balance between player characters doesn't exist in a vaccum. People play RPGs like Exalted in groups, and in groups characters occupy certain niches. You might have a party consisting of a Solar scholar, a Lunar socialite, a Dragon-Blooded priest, and a Sidereal martial artist - in this case, the fact that the Solar could be a better socialite than the Lunar, a better priest than the Dragon-Blooded, or a better fighter than the Sidereal are totally irrelevant, because that player has no desire to outclass his friend's characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T01:37:16-07:00","id":1385777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385769#post1385769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wholeheartedly agree with you. As far as a team-based tactical wargame goes, DD4 has a pretty good balance between player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, compared to every other edition, it's very well balanced. I'm enjoying 5th ed, and I think it's better balanced than 2nd or 3rd edition, but I suspect that while my 2nd-level cleric runs out of spells quickly and does hardly any damage, and my 6th level wizard is a strong member of the team but squishy and fragile, at high levels the spellcasters will be stronger than the rogues and fighters.<br /> <br /> Still, comparing 4th and 5th edition is like combaring oranges and books. They're completely different things.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I still think 4th edition has the best combat system of any roleplaying game, although maybe not the most amusing (Dark Heresy I always found a hoot, with all the limbs being blown off, horrible burn scars from fire, etc. Oh, we did so love saying &quot;Death from shock and blood loss is instantaneous&quot;!) and certainly not one for a low-combat game where you want the combats to be quick.<br /> <br /> But one particular thing I found interesting is how they did Fighters and Rogues, ie the people fighting with skill rather than magic (which is relevant to Solars). At high levels, they had a lot of different 1/encounter or 1/day powers powers representing combat skill. Doing damage, recovering health, moving around the battlefield, attacking multiple people, etc. Powerful, skilled, more interesting than just &quot;bigger numbers&quot; (well, there were a few that just did that), and without much in the way of book-keeping.<br /> I also found the way at high-levels you swapped your low-level techniques out for higher-level ones quite useful, rather than remembering the 20 different skills you had. I do find the 40+ charms an Essence 5 character has in Exalted to be a bit irritating (though it really depends on the build, my new Lunar's much better for this than my old one).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, one thing that ought to be said here is that balance between player characters doesn't exist in a vaccum. People play RPGs like Exalted in groups, and in groups characters occupy certain niches. You might have a party consisting of a Solar scholar, a Lunar socialite, a Dragon-Blooded priest, and a Sidereal martial artist - in this case, the fact that the Solar could be a better socialite than the Lunar, a better priest than the Dragon-Blooded, or a better fighter than the Sidereal are totally irrelevant, because that player has no desire to outclass his friend's characters. </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Neall was very keen on presenting most kinds of Exalts' castes through the lense of the same five archetypes (he didn't say what they were, but referred back to Scroll of Heroes and the mortal section, which IIRC he wrote. That had Warrior, Priest, Savant, Criminal and Broker).<br /> <br /> I wonder if part of that idea is for the Storyteller section to encourage the group to have a Chosen of Battles, Zenith, No Moon, Moonsilver Alchemical and Moonshadow, at which point you really don't have to worry that your Sidereal isn't very good at combat by comparison. As opposed to, say, a Zenith, an Earth, a Chosen of Serenity, a Midnight and a Jade Caste, at which point the Earth's player might get frustrated if the Zenith is tougher, harder to influence, and better at commanding troops than her character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T01:38:46-07:00","id":1385778,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>, well, I think if you do have that one player who hasn't really read what any of the splats are about in the setting and isn't excited by the role playing that each of their backgrounds presents and their different &quot;feel&quot;, isn't too interested in the detail of powers and how they feel, just what they should accomplish in the end, and thinks it's kinda bullshit to have different 'strength' player options, that person should probably not be playing a DB in a Solar game! Even if Essence flattens things out. I have no clue about how commonly you'd get players like that or not is though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T02:06:39-07:00","id":1385781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385777#post1385777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... Neall was very keen on presenting most kinds of Exalts' castes through the lense of the same five archetypes (he didn't say what they were, but referred back to Scroll of Heroes and the mortal section, which IIRC he wrote. That had Warrior, Priest, Savant, Criminal and Broker).<br /> <br /> I wonder if part of that idea is for the Storyteller section to encourage the group to have a Chosen of Battles, Zenith, No Moon, Moonsilver Alchemical and Moonshadow, at which point you really don't have to worry that your Sidereal isn't very good at combat by comparison. As opposed to, say, a Zenith, an Earth, a Chosen of Serenity, a Midnight and a Jade Caste, at which point the Earth's player might get frustrated if the Zenith is tougher, harder to influence, and better at commanding troops than her character.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a ton of sense. I guess more ambiguous Exalt types could simply have multiple associated archetypes, e.g.<br /> <br /> Fire = Fighting, Magnetism<br /> Air = Scholarship, Stealth<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378837#post1378837\">Based on</a> Dawn = Fighting, Zenith = Magnetism, Twilight = Scholarship, Night = Stealth, Eclipse = Embassy)<br /> <br /> So at character creation everyone can pick an Archetype first, and then once everyone has their Archetype they can go through the list of Castes/Aspects to see what they can play as that Archetype, making the process of picking an Exalt type a lot less overwhelming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T02:06:58-07:00","id":1385782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385769#post1385769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, one thing that ought to be said here is that balance between player characters doesn't exist in a vaccum. People play RPGs like Exalted in groups, and in groups characters occupy certain niches. You might have a party consisting of a Solar scholar, a Lunar socialite, a Dragon-Blooded priest, and a Sidereal martial artist - in this case, the fact that the Solar could be a better socialite than the Lunar, a better priest than the Dragon-Blooded, or a better fighter than the Sidereal are totally irrelevant, because that player has no desire to outclass his friend's characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then when you factor in 3E's Character Creation mini-game... an optimized Solar Scholar could be a better better priest, socailite AND fighter, and be a renown scholar who can speak her will into existence, as well as a returning god-like, rightful ruler of Creation.<br /> <br /> Like, it's not hard to do that <i>accidently</i>, and you just picked Solars because they're the vanilla splat. Never mind if you actually <i>do</i> want to outclass the other PCs and picked Solars deliberately to try and be the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T02:19:31-07:00","id":1385783,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... I see your point Ghosthead, and certainly anyone I thought was a bit of a power gamer I'd say &quot;you should play a Solar, they're the strongest&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I don't think it's unreasonable or uncommon for players to assume all options are roughly equal. Or that they can choose something based on how cool they think it is and it'll probably be a similar power level to everyone else.*<br /> <br /> *This has actually been an issue with Exalted even when all the players are playing Solars, because character building can be done in so many different ways. I'chan the tyrant-lizard-riding Djala archer/medicine-man was, while super cool, frankly one of the weaker characters in my 2nd edition group, hence his untimely death in a fight between the circle and some Sidereals (the only other PCs who ever died, died fighting alone against multiple NPCs. Or in one case killed himself).<br /> <br /> <br /> In my DnD game, everyone chose their character based on something they thought would be fun and they'd enjoy, and no-one dislikes the idea of their character. But sometimes players (especially newer ones) get disgruntled when it seems their character isn't very good. Bruno was a bit disgruntled when he saw how much damage my lighnting bolt can do (8d6) compared to his sneak attack (4d6+4 I think? Maybe 5d6+4 once a day). Steffie was a bit disgruntled when she realised that Barbarians actually don't do that much damage, she thought being a giant Dragon-woman with a giant axe would be doing tons of damage (which I don't think is a stupid assumption), but they're really a tank with okay damage.<br /> And these, frankly, are characters who are intended to be balanced.<br /> If I was playing a Solar and Bruno and Steffie were playing Dragonblood, the answer wouldn't be &quot;oh, I can do more damage but only twice a day, and I have AC12 and the smallest number of HP in the party, so while I can do the most damage in one turn we're actually balanced&quot; the answer would be &quot;yeah, my character is better than yours because I've played the game longer and knew to pick the best class, sucks to be you.&quot;<br /> <br /> When new players pick something they think is interesting and cool, and after several sessions go &quot;hey, why is my awesome fire-swordsman who fights ON FIRE and shoots fireballs and went to the world's greatest military school just not as good as Shiny Peasant McSolar the self-taught swordswoman who fights by stabbing people with the pointy end? I mean, I'm not demanding to be better than her, but it seems I'm a bit lame compared to her?&quot;... well, I don't want to be the ST who has to say &quot;Yeah, his character is just better than yours. You get to be cool, she gets to be good.&quot; Because players want characters who are cool <i>and</i> good.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd probably solve this by, during character creation, going &quot;okay, you can play a classic superhuman demi-god like Hercules or something, or a were-beast-monster, or a secret agent of Heaven, or an undead-antihero, or a demonic anti-hero. Check out these pages and pictures.<br /> Oh, and also you could play a frankenstein monster or elemental aristocrat or robo-golem if you want, but please be aware that those are weaker characters and so you would playing on Hard Mode. I don't recommend Hard Mode for your first character.&quot;<br /> <br /> Although even the ST may not realise this (our DnD DM's never played a barbarian, so didn't know to make sure Steffie knew barbarians don't do loads of damage compared to arcane casters), so I think the book possibly needs to clearly divide Celestials and Terrestrials, and say &quot;STs and players, be aware that Celestials are more powerful than Terrestrials.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T02:32:47-07:00","id":1385785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385782#post1385782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then when you factor in 3E's Character Creation mini-game... an optimized Solar Scholar could be a better better priest, socailite AND fighter, and be a renown scholar who can speak her will into existence, as well as a returning god-like, rightful ruler of Creation.<br /> <br /> Like, it's not hard to do that <i>accidently</i>, and you just picked Solars because they're the vanilla splat. Never mind if you actually <i>do</i> want to outclass the other PCs and picked Solars deliberately to try and be the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. I hope Essence's character creation system is different enough that this isn't really an issue.*<br /> <br /> *I actually wonder if every single Exalt type will use the exact same character creation system. Though to solve this issue, you also need a character gen system that can't be &quot;won&quot; the way 3rd ed's can be. As I said, I've found similar issues with different PC's Solars.<br /> <br /> I'm currently playing a fairly new DB in a 325xp game, because I reckoned I could just straight-up optimise my character with ridiculous stats and that'd make up half the difference between me and the Solars. But if you had a Solar built that way and a DB built normally, the difference would be pretty drastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T03:07:54-07:00","id":1385789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385782#post1385782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But then when you factor in 3E's Character Creation mini-game... an optimized Solar Scholar could be a better better priest, socailite AND fighter, and be a renown scholar who can speak her will into existence, as well as a returning god-like, rightful ruler of Creation.<br /> Like, it's not hard to do that <i>accidently</i>, and you just picked Solars because they're the vanilla splat.</div> </div> </div> </div> That seems like a mark of poor design to me. When a player builds a character in an RPG there shouldn\u2019t be gotchas or unintended consequences built into the process.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385782#post1385782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never mind if you actually <i>do</i> want to outclass the other PCs and picked Solars deliberately to try and be the best.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, if their desire to outclass all of their party members is making the game worse I\u2019d probably talk to them out of game and come to some sort of resolution.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385783#post1385783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When new players pick something they think is interesting and cool, and after several sessions go &quot;hey, why is my awesome fire-swordsman who fights ON FIRE and shoots fireballs and went to the world's greatest military school just not as good as Shiny Peasant McSolar the self-taught swordswoman who fights by stabbing people with the pointy end? I mean, I'm not demanding to be better than her, but it seems I'm a bit lame compared to her?&quot;... well, I don't want to be the ST who has to say &quot;Yeah, his character is just better than yours. You get to be cool, she gets to be good.&quot; Because players want characters who are cool <i>and</i> good.<br /> Personally, I'd probably solve this by, during character creation, going &quot;okay, you can play a classic superhuman demi-god like Hercules or something, or a were-beast-monster, or a secret agent of Heaven, or an undead-antihero, or a demonic anti-hero. Check out these pages and pictures.<br /> Oh, and also you could play a frankenstein monster or elemental aristocrat or robo-golem if you want, but please be aware that those are weaker characters and so you would playing on Hard Mode. I don't recommend Hard Mode for your first character.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Were I designing a game about powerful demigods pursuing their ambitions and changing the world, I\u2019d solve this problem by highlighting that the differences between Exalt \u2018type\u2019 are narrative, and that in a game intended to tell a story there need be no separation between narrative and mechanics.<br /> In your two swordsman examples, both should have strengths and weaknesses befitting their fictional positioning. The fire-swordsman\u2019s world-class training, fiery aura, and ranged blasts of flame would certainly make them a potent warrior. Of course a self-taught peasant swordsman who only knows to stick people with their weapon\u2019s pointy end would seem oafish in comparison, but this is overlooking the Solar magic that suffuses them. What does it look like? When they swing their sword does golden light wash around them like a wave, blinding their foes and shoring up their poor defense with a blast of force that accompanies every strike? Does their sun-magic suffuse their sword-arm such that a single swing can take the roof off a house or cut the head off a tyrant lizard? Does their magic come in the form of instinct, allowing them to anticipate every strike aimed their way and, when the time comes, answer with a perfect attack of their own? Does their sun-magic take the form of a bond with a weapon of Orichalcum with such odious strength that creatures of darkness flee from its unsheathed blade, and even gods bow in fear of a weapon that can cut their divine flesh?<br /> <br /> It's a damn shame that the game represents this Dragon-Blooded's training and flame skills through boosts to their Withering and Decisive damage, and represents whatever powers this Solar calls upon by <i>better </i>boosts to their Withering and Decisive damage. Again, here's to hoping that Essence will change this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T04:16:16-07:00","id":1385792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385724#post1385724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it's an example of how introducing multiple &quot;Virtues&quot; into a game is a hazardous balancing act.<br /> <br /> That's why I wrinkled my nose at the idea that they're introducing seven; because previous Editions failed to properly balance a mere FOUR.</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtues as they existed in 1st and 2nd edition had pretty specific problems with their execution that I doubt we'll see a repeat of unless there's an active desire to be retro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T04:26:30-07:00","id":1385797,"title":"","content":"I suppose it depends how important they are. The more important and significant, the harder they are to balance.<br /> <br /> I also suspect different people had quite different experience with how balanced they were. Some people on the forums complained about Compassion being more of a hindrance than a help (and probably in our Dynastic game that was true), but in our Solar game, it was a pretty useful virtue to channel to help people. Temperance was very useful in games where PCs faced, say, sexy incubi trying to seduce you to the dark side, not so useful in a game where your opponents are Immaculate Monks. Valour was probably something a lot of groups found very powerful, but refusing to turn down challenges could be a big hindrance if the ST wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T04:54:30-07:00","id":1385799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385789#post1385789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like a mark of poor design to me. When a player builds a character in an RPG there shouldn\u2019t be gotchas or unintended consequences built into the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> 3rd ed's character creation system is (besides charm picks) actually a good and simple one for new players in the sense that it's very quick to make your Solar Dawn Caste compared to making a Level 10 Fighter in Pathfinder. Actually even with charm bloat it may be quicker, probably depends. That's because it's based on OWoD, and I ran both Vampire and Mage with completely new players able to make their character in 10 minutes.<br /> It's just that it has these kind of optimisation tricks that aren't obvious to new players. So it's easy to make a character, but it's not easy for a new player to make a character who is as good as an experienced player.<br /> I do remember people (myself included) arguing with Holden, one of the original 3rd ed Devs, about this, some people said for example it'd be better to use an XP-based system (I tried this one time, it didn't actually work that well IMO, essentially it solved some issues but created others). And he basically felt that, at the end of the day, for most groups it was more important for character creation to be quick and easy than to be perfectly balanced. And I know some of my players agree, and I can see where he's coming from.<br /> <br /> But I do feel it's probably not that hard to make a reasonably balanced character creation system that's also fairly quick and easy, for Exalted. Mostly to do with how freebies work, which could easily be changed, and also a bit about attributes (which I suspect Essence is going to do quite differently anyway).<br /> You can also change how XP works radically, but personally that would not be my preference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Were I designing a game about powerful demigods pursuing their ambitions and changing the world, I\u2019d solve this problem by highlighting that the differences between Exalt \u2018type\u2019 are narrative, and that in a game intended to tell a story there need be no separation between narrative and mechanics. </div> </div> </div>The issue is that the PCs are also NPCs. What I mean is, if a goblin is rubbish compared to an elven wizard, this is fine because your elven wizard PC is supposed to beat a goblin without much difficulty. If your PCs do face a wizard, he's probably a boss fight, so if an NPC wizard is pretty hard that's fine.<br /> <br /> But inexperienced Solars are supposed to be a match for experienced Dragonblood. I mean, for your group of five Solars who've been exalted for about six months, a group of experienced Dragonblood warriors is supposed to be a significant encounter, but it's probably not the story's finale. You certainly don't expect to be completely outmatched the way you would be if you were a group of new Dragonblood against a group of experienced Dragonblood, or a group of new Solars against a group of experienced Lunars.<br /> <br /> If the writers are keen on ensuring all PCs are roughly equal overall (which is a laudable goal), there's probably ways to deal with this, like saying Dragonblood PCs represent very experienced Dragonblood while Solar PCs do not, because they are shonen protagonists. Just that it's worth the writers putting some thought into it, rather than just saying &quot;yeah, DBs and Solars are the same strength mechanically but we'll say in fluff that Solars are better&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In your two swordsman examples, both should have strengths and weaknesses befitting their fictional positioning. The fire-swordsman\u2019s world-class training, fiery aura, and ranged blasts of flame would certainly make them a potent warrior. Of course a self-taught peasant swordsman who only knows to stick people with their weapon\u2019s pointy end would seem oafish in comparison, but this is overlooking the Solar magic that suffuses them. What does it look like? When they swing their sword does golden light wash around them like a wave, blinding their foes and shoring up their poor defense with a blast of force that accompanies every strike? Does their sun-magic suffuse their sword-arm such that a single swing can take the roof off a house or cut the head off a tyrant lizard? Does their magic come in the form of instinct, allowing them to anticipate every strike aimed their way and, when the time comes, answer with a perfect attack of their own? Does their sun-magic take the form of a bond with a weapon of Orichalcum with such odious strength that creatures of darkness flee from its unsheathed blade, and even gods bow in fear of a weapon that can cut their divine flesh?<br /> <br /> It's a damn shame that the game represents this Dragon-Blooded's training and flame skills through boosts to their Withering and Decisive damage, and represents whatever powers this Solar calls upon by <i>better </i>boosts to their Withering and Decisive damage. </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Dragonblood melee-ists do get to do stuff like blind their opponent, set them on fire, make a sword out of fire if they're unarmed, etc. It's just not all that powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, here's to hoping that Essence will change this. </div> </div> </div>I am always up for charms that are not just bonus dice, because if you want more dice you can just buy more abilities (though the current character gen system doesn't do that great, but hopefully you get what I mean), and excellencies already do that. And I find having more interesting powers/options is a lot more fun (and less frustrating sometimes) than just more dice/stats.<br /> (Which is why I don't like playing Solars as much as other splats in 3rd ed. Or 2nd ed, although that's also because the Solar combat meta was dull.)<br /> But I'll admit, for various reasons that's a bit harder to design for Solars than it is for... pretty much everyone else. I mean &quot;their sun-magic suffuses their sword-arm such that a single swing can cut the head off a Tyrant Lizard&quot; is a fancy way to say &quot;+more damage&quot;. Instinct that allows them to anticipate every blow, is mechanically &quot;+defence&quot;. I mean, I guess a DB attacking with a sword that's on fire is probably also +damage, but it might work in a few other ways than that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think, with Universal charms being around, it's quite likely tbh that everyone will be using mostly the same &quot;add more damage, defend better, ignore penalty X, run faster&quot; etc charms, and the individual charmsets are more likely to have your interesting powers and options; Solars radiating light that scares off ghosts, Sidereal foresight, Lunars growing to 30 foot tall, Abyssals regaining health by eating corpses, Alchemicals growing essence cannons from their arms, Infernals spawning demon servants, Dragonblood sinking beneath the earth, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T05:30:11-07:00","id":1385803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385789#post1385789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were I designing a game about powerful demigods pursuing their ambitions and changing the world, I\u2019d solve this problem by highlighting that the differences between Exalt \u2018type\u2019 are narrative, and that in a game intended to tell a story there need be no separation between narrative and mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I want to come back to this.<br /> <br /> First, small point, surely in that idea there<i> is </i>a seperation between narrative and mechanics? I assume you mean that the narrative says &quot;Solars change the world with their great power which is more than individual Dragonblood have&quot; but that this doesn't mean you have to reflect that mechanically, because it'd be lame for DB players to have worse mechanics than Solar mechanics?<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, the main point: if I was designing a game about powerful demigods pursuing their ambitions and changing the world, I think I'd solve this problem by not having a core conceit of the game in the first place be that 300 returning sun-king heroes of ancient times, disparate, disunited, far from each other and with little self-knowledge are a serious challenge to the rule of 20-30,000 aristocratic element-benders mostly orgaised in a massive empire with huge armies, who've also been seriously challenged and in a massive war against 3-400 shapeshifters, and also the 20-30,000 aristocratic element-benders are secretly controlled by 80 secret agents.<br /> <br /> (I'm not saying Solars don't make sense unless each Solar can easily kill 100 Dragonblood by themselves, or even 5. After all, your Solar PC is with 4 or 5 others, they're probably in somewhere that's awkward for the Realm to reach, while the Realm is collapsing in a civil war. And the Bronze Faction has always been more worried about what a Solar could become if you leave them alone for a few years or decades rather than when they're newly-exalted, which you can't do much about anyway as they reincarnate. But I am saying Celestials don't make sense in Exalted's fluff unless they're at least <i>somewhat</i> more powerful than Terrestrials. Especially as your band of young inexperienced Solar heroes without much influence or magical equipment is much more likely, setting-wise, to encounter a group of experienced and well-armed Dragonblood carrying their ancestral magic swords, than to encounter a bunch of young inexperienced Dragonblood nobles without much influence or magical equipment. Except maybe on An-Teng's beaches.)<br /> <br /> It's like... if I made a DnD campaign where there's a massive empire of 10,000 wizards, and they've been fighting 400 warlocks for 1500 years without defeating them, and while they used to be winning now they're losing and in fact their empire is collapsing, you'd assume those warlocks must be much higher level than the wizards. Which does actually work for Lunars if you point out that some of them are 1-2 thousand years old (so they are epic level) whereas the oldest wizards are a few hundred. But it doesn't really work for Solars, who are basically pretty much all Level 1, except maybe Yurgen and Samea who are like level 10.<br /> <br /> But if you want to change it so that the Solars and DBs are pretty level in power, I think you have to seriously change the fluff, the same way (or rather, the opposite way) 3rd ed went straight in and tackled people complaining about how little Lunars did by rewriting the setting so that Lunars are a much bigger deal. By making Solars less of a big deal, and also (as I guess was DrLoveMonkey's argument) minimising the Wyld Hunt, so that bands of experienced Dragonblood only bother turning up to ambush very experienced Solar PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which, possibly, they are actually doing in Essence. I think one of the writers in Discord said that the only changes they're making to fluff is to slightly de-emphasise Solars. I'd still argue that without a complete change in fluff Solars and Lunars kind of need to be, say, 10% more powerful than an equivalent Dragonblood*, but for PCs that's small enough that a DB could make up for it with his free dots of Resources, Influence, and magic sword.**<br /> Present the Realm as sliding into Civil War (ie the biggest threats to the Dragonblood are each other), while facing numerous threats, their main threat being several hundred coordinated Lunars and their beastmen armies, 13 Deathlords each with a band of Abyssals, and also the new Solars who aren't really a big threat but maybe could be in the future (when your PC has loads of XP).<br /> This would be fine with me.***<br /> <br /> <br /> *Tbh, assuming excellencies are still pretty good even if they're, say, everyone can add a few dice and its the same for all splats, the Solar free excellencies and auto-win Ties may actually be enough for that.<br /> <br /> **The Exalt advantages I think are designed to immediately make it clear to players the differences. If Solars get free excellencies, which we'll assume for now are some kind of dice-adders, and auto-win ties, and Dragonblood get say X extra dots of merits, I think that immediately tells you that Solars are the splat of &quot;roll more dice better&quot; and DBs are the splat of &quot;have more equipment and money and contacts&quot;. And I can absolutely see some players picking &quot;have a free magic sword and more money and contacts&quot; rather than &quot;be more min-maxed&quot; and being happy with that.<br /> <br /> ***I may be biased here of course, because I don't think the Solars are very interesting as a part of the setting as a whole. I used Solar NPCs as antagonists in 3rd ed because it was pretty much all I had to challenge the PCs, and I knew a couple of players would be very motivated to go up against people claiming to be god-kings with an inherent right to rule. But essentially, as far as I'm concerned, the job of Solars is to be PCs, and outside of being PCs or the occasional deconstruction of Chosen One tropes, there's not much point to them. I don't really have Solars in my game at all; there's essentially just Lunars, Dragonblood and slightly toned-down Infernals.<br /> So I wouldn't really be bothered if Essence downplayed the importance of Solars to the setting, but I know there's lots of Solar fans who would be really shocked by that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T05:35:41-07:00","id":1385804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385797#post1385797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also suspect different people had quite different experience with how balanced they were. Some people on the forums complained about Compassion being more of a hindrance than a help (and probably in our Dynastic game that was true), but in our Solar game, it was a pretty useful virtue to channel to help people. Temperance was very useful in games where PCs faced, say, sexy incubi trying to seduce you to the dark side, not so useful in a game where your opponents are Immaculate Monks. Valour was probably something a lot of groups found very powerful, but refusing to turn down challenges could be a big hindrance if the ST wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was another problem at play here.<br /> The mindset of the paranoia combo helped cultivate an adversarial relationship between player and storyteller - when people are conditioned to view their demigod character getting murdered in their sleep as a real possibility if they don't buy certain charms, it's much easier to see the situations certain virtues could put you in as a totally unacceptable shortcoming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T05:47:45-07:00","id":1385805,"title":"","content":"I didn't really see that with virtues generally, but I think it certainly came up with Virtue Flaws for Perfect Defences, where people wouldn't often choose the most characterful because they could see it as being too easily exploited I guess.<br /> <br /> (Tbh, I never really felt that the ST was out to murder us in our sleep or whatever. Not like Vampire Larp! The only of my PCs I remember dying were a Fire Aspect bureaucrat who another PC with a grand goremaul killed without meaning to, as he didn't assume that a single hit from a grand goremaul on an unarmoured bureaucrat would insta-kill him, and an Air Aspect who Walker in Darkness killed after she grappled him for 3 turns, which was pretty much expected. And when other PCs died, it was generally a surprise to the ST rather than it felt like the ST had gone out of their way to come up with a bull**** assassination method. But that was us, and one player did mention he thought my Wyld Hunts were being unrealistically unintelligent in finding ways to kill PCs, so maybe other groups were much more adversarial.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T06:28:52-07:00","id":1385809,"title":"","content":"My groups have never been adversarial, but I occasionally crossed paths with players who were shaped by negative experiences with groups that were or had their expectations informed by forum memes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:56:51-07:00","id":1385835,"title":"","content":"On the spirit of rampant speculation for bored locked-down people, as per Sunder's thread:<br /> <br /> Have I mentioned these?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Currently, [Getimians] are <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attribute</span></span> Exalts, but that doesn't mean much in Essence's paradigm</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You won't see [Getimian's] Attributes in Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica Speca</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">maybe there aren't 9 <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">attributes</span></span> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica Speca</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dex</span></span> isn't a God Stat. Or even a thing.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I note that Sidereals Arcane Fate is a difficulty 5 Integrity roll to resist... <i>not </i>a difficulty 5 Perception+Integrity roll, or whatever.<br /> (Unless they were just describing it in a short way. But it did sound like they were reading from the book. Though I sure hope that Sidereal fate-weaving has a limit on how many people you can use it on, or how long it lasts, or costs a resource, etc, so you don't use it on literally everyone you meet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T08:04:02-07:00","id":1385836,"title":"","content":"Honestly, all this would make me wonder if there even <i>were</i> Attributes in Exalted.<br /> <br /> But right at the beginning, we got this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica Speca</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Yes, the dice basics are exactly the same. TN 7, double 10s, <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attribute</span></span> + <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ability</span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>So, there are still attributes. But there's probably less than 9. And Dexterity isn't one of them.<br /> <br /> So commence your rampant speculation!<br /> <br /> I could definitely see Charisma and Appearance being combined. Or Appearance just being a merit (hot or not. Or scary of course).<br /> I could similarly see Strength and Stamina being combined. And possibly Perception+Wits.<br /> <br /> Not really sure what you'd do with Dexterity. You could split it, but that would make even more stats.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's just three Attributes; Physical, Mental and Social (maybe different names of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T08:18:38-07:00","id":1385837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385761#post1385761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as far as your D&amp;D example goes - wizards can summon monsters collectively tougher than the barbarian, can far outpace the fighter's attacks with their AoE spells, can replicate entire class features of the rogue with a handful of low-level spells and shapeshift like druids, on top of a million other things like teleportation etc that are unique to them.<br /> <br /> Dungeons and Dragons has been very poorly balanced throughout all of its editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of the biggest, maybe even the single biggest, complaint about DnD though isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385789#post1385789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a damn shame that the game represents this Dragon-Blooded's training and flame skills through boosts to their Withering and Decisive damage, and represents whatever powers this Solar calls upon by <i>better </i>boosts to their Withering and Decisive damage. Again, here's to hoping that Essence will change this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s why I think it might be a good idea for Essence to flatten things out. If the Fire swordsman has an attack that costs 5 motes and sets their enemy ablaze, burning them in magical red flame for 1 die of lethal damage every round for (Essence) rounds, and the Solar has a charm that for 2 motes tripled the final rolled damage of any attack as their golden destruction wave annihilates all before it, the two charms have a vastly different feel, but the DB swordsman comes out of it looking like a chump.<br /> <br /> Also even if you don\u2019t have two fighters in the same group, the guy playing the fire swordsman when he was making his character had to choose between what he thought felt cool, the burning foes in a bonfire, vs being way way stronger. So then every time they come up against an enemy who\u2019s a bit too strong, or if they have to run he might think \u201cyou know, if I was a Solar I\u2019d beat this monster in like one round instead of running away with my tail between my legs...\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T09:55:53-07:00","id":1385853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385837#post1385837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one of the biggest, maybe even the single biggest, complaint about DnD though isn\u2019t it?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Star Wars</i> is honest about this. I don't know of any <i>Star Wars</i> game where you can play as a Jedi <i>and</i> as someone who can't use the Force and swinging around an armor-shredding plasma-cutter for a sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T10:02:06-07:00","id":1385857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385853#post1385853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Star Wars</i> is honest about this. I don't know of any <i>Star Wars</i> game where you can play as a Jedi <i>and</i> as someone who can't use the Force and swinging around an armor-shredding plasma-cutter for a sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>IDK. The FFG line (Force and Destiny, Edge of the Empire, Age of Rebellion) kinda lets you do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T10:18:13-07:00","id":1385860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385853#post1385853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Star Wars</i> is honest about this. I don't know of any <i>Star Wars</i> game where you can play as a Jedi <i>and</i> as someone who can't use the Force and swinging around an armor-shredding plasma-cutter for a sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, what do you mean? Like there\u2019s no SW game that lets you mix force users and non-force users?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T10:20:11-07:00","id":1385861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385860#post1385860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, what do you mean? Like there\u2019s no SW game that lets you mix force users and non-force users?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's more there is no game that let you mix them and expect the same results from both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T10:25:01-07:00","id":1385864,"title":"","content":"I've never played any Star Wars video game, so I probably made an overbroad generalization.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385861#post1385861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it's more there is no game that let you mix them and expect the same results from both.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this seems like it should be pretty accurate.<br /> <br /> In Star Wars, when you want a single character to challenge a Jedi, generally that antagonist is another Jedi, or a Sith.<br /> <br /> Space Wizard versus Space Wizard, with plasma-cutter swords on both sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T10:28:49-07:00","id":1385866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385837#post1385837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one of the biggest, maybe even the single biggest, complaint about DnD though isn\u2019t it?</div> </div> </div> </div>When they <i>did </i>perfectly balance the classes against one another in 4e, people complained. Oh, how they complained!<br /> <br /> 5e at least acknowledges the asymmetric power curve compared to the level curve and builds upon that as a feature, not a bug. If you're <i>aware </i>of the Linear Fighter, Quadratic Wizard problem, you can put in compensation mechanics or elements to highlight the positive aspects of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T11:31:56-07:00","id":1385878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385864#post1385864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Star Wars, when you want a single character to challenge a Jedi, generally that antagonist is another Jedi, or a Sith.<br /> <br /> Space Wizard versus Space Wizard, with plasma-cutter swords on both sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are definitely SW games out there like that, but there\u2019s also ones where being a Jedi can give you incredible powers like telekinesis, super speed, lightsaber combat, but other characters are just buried under an avalanche of skills and gadgets and other stuff.<br /> <br /> So like your Jedi with Force Throw and Force Jump is being compared to the bounty hunter with a jetpack, sleep darts, cloaking field, equally proficient in blaster combat as vibroblades and hand-to-hand, and skills in hacking, engineering, chemistry and eight different languages. Maybe a bit of an exaggeration but there are definitely ways to make it feel like your character is sitting at the kids table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385866#post1385866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they <i>did </i>perfectly balance the classes against one another in 4e, people complained. Oh, how they complained!<br /> <br /> 5e at least acknowledges the asymmetric power curve compared to the level curve and builds upon that as a feature, not a bug. If you're <i>aware </i>of the Linear Fighter, Quadratic Wizard problem, you can put in compensation mechanics or elements to highlight the positive aspects of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The writers may have been aware of that but the books definitely are not. The DMG\u2019s tier section maybe hints at it in a really subtle or tongue-in-cheek way, but nowhere does it say \u201cSo you might notice here that by level 17 the wizard can shift planes, create miles wide real-not illusions, destroy small armies with one spell, and warp reality to their will by uttering the words \u2018 I Wish...\u2019 along with cheating death with Clones and completely ending a fight with clever spell application, while the fighter can attack three times and the rogue has a +4 bonus to her skill checks compared to ten levels ago. This is intentional design, but one that may leave some players feeling like the sidekick to the wizard\u2019s main character. Here are some ways to help those players still feel relevant next to the demigods that are their full caster friends.\u201d, or alternatively you can suggest running a party of characters who all roughly have the same capabilities.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T11:34:40-07:00","id":1385881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385866#post1385866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they <i>did </i>perfectly balance the classes against one another in 4e, people complained. Oh, how they complained!<br /> <br /> 5e at least acknowledges the asymmetric power curve compared to the level curve and builds upon that as a feature, not a bug. If you're <i>aware </i>of the Linear Fighter, Quadratic Wizard problem, you can put in compensation mechanics or elements to highlight the positive aspects of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compensation mechanics like Dragon-Blooded cooperative powers, perhaps.<br /> <br /> Or Liminals being really hard to kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:23:54-07:00","id":1385914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385866#post1385866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they <i>did </i>perfectly balance the classes against one another in 4e, people complained. Oh, how they complained!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh indeed! Though I think most people complained about other things than that. (Some, I'm sure, complained about how their 20th level wizards were severely nerfed.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5e at least acknowledges the asymmetric power curve compared to the level curve and builds upon that as a feature, not a bug. If you're <i>aware </i>of the Linear Fighter, Quadratic Wizard problem, you can put in compensation mechanics or elements to highlight the positive aspects of that. </div> </div> </div>Does it? I'll be honest, I've not played above level 8 with 5th ed, or read the DMG.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, Star Wars. So the thing of course is that yes, Jedi are better than non-Jedi. Some SW roleplaying games say &quot;you can't play a Jedi&quot;. Some SW roleplaying games say &quot;you can play a young inexperienced Jedi or a skilled bounty hunter/smuggler/scout/pilot/soldier with a bunch of skills in all sorts of areas.&quot; And in a small number of those, that's actually balanced!<br /> (In a lot of games, it's <i>supposed</i> to be balanced, but isn't.)<br /> With computer games, you generally either play a bounty hunter/smuggler/scout/pilot/soldier with a ton of equipment, a Jedi/Sith, or an inexperienced bounty hunter/smuggler/scout/pilot/soldier who then becomes a Jedi.<br /> Often you are a Jedi, and your companions are smugglers, Wookies, Droids, younger Jedi, etc. PC and NPC companions don't need to be balanced though.<br /> <br /> That is, of course, how the films work. Luke is a farmboy with a bit of force power who is a good pilot, Han is an experienced fast-talking smuggler and awesome shot and a great pilot. Chewbacca is really strong and tough, has a laser-crossbow, and is a great mechanic and decent pilot. C3PO speaks 6 billion languages, R2D2 is a brilliant hacker and mechanic. Kinobi is an OP DMPC, but the DM quickly kills him off so it's fine.<br /> So, the guy with the force is the weakest character in every other way (least money, least skills, also if he uses his powers he'll give himself away to the evil empire who hunts those like him), so it's kind of balanced.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you can use that as an example of how to balance a Solar with other splats. But certainly it's worth bearing in mind that while some SW game effectively balance this, most try and fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-06-2020, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T19:33:41-07:00","id":1385993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385881#post1385881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compensation mechanics like Dragon-Blooded cooperative powers, perhaps.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Like the dragon blooded being inherently better at teamwork making a group of them exponentially more dangerous than any number of them individually?<br /> <br /> That seems to be where they are going with this, Solars get all the awesome modes that hit harder and make you more badass, DBs get the elemental powers and the exponential teamwork gains, a minor solar may be able to fight an experienced DB and win but a team of solars vs a team of DBs may be more of an even fight. I don't think we're giving enough credit to the advantages the exalted have and that DBs not only have the numbers but the means to exploit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 05-05-2020, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T03:16:51-07:00","id":1386031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385993#post1385993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like the dragon blooded being inherently better at teamwork making a group of them exponentially more dangerous than any number of them individually?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea.......................<br /> <br /> But it doesn't really solve the issue of how to make a PC competitive with a Solar PC, while still having a world where Dragonblood are weaker than Solars.<br /> <br /> At least the exponential teamwork.<br /> However, if the Dragonblood are the &quot;buffer&quot; splat, with lots of buffing teamwork powers, then (as long as this is made clear in their write-up) actually that does work. Like, in my DnD group the Bard does the worst damage, has the 2nd worst defence, etc. But the player's never said she feels the character is weak, because she has very good buffs that buff other PCs.<br /> But if you had a group of Bards... well, a group of fighters or wizards would probably beat them without a lot of trouble.<br /> <br /> So, as long as players know that picking a Dragonblood is the buffer, they would be very useful in a party (best at buffing other characters, much better at it than the Solar or Lunar characters), but a group of Solars fighting a group of Dragonblood probably still has the advantage. So that kind of works? Wouldn't want to go over the top there (there's a reason Clerics and Bards don't<i> only</i> do buffing), but an element of that could work.<br /> (It also leans into the idea that honestly, the world's 20,000+ Dragonblood probably could beat the Lunars, Solars, Abyssals, etc, if they'd just bloody work together.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T08:07:08-07:00","id":1386077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386031#post1386031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this idea.......................<br /> <br /> But it doesn't really solve the issue of how to make a PC competitive with a Solar PC, while still having a world where Dragonblood are weaker than Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Blaque said this already, but I really believe this is where &quot;NPC's scales don't need to be the same as PC's and can be re adjustable&quot;. Just put cool and powerful power for Solar and DB PC's, and give tools for the ST to adjust the difficulty according to what they want the experience to feel like. <br /> <br /> The system is not a description of the world as it functions, it is our interface to make said world move into narrative action. The Dragonblooded of the setting can be weaker than the Solar and at the same time the Dragon Blooded of the player can compete with the Solar if the system recognizes that these situations are different and thus can be resolved differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T08:33:00-07:00","id":1386089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386077#post1386077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Blaque said this already, but I really believe this is where &quot;NPC's scales don't need to be the same as PC's and can be re adjustable&quot;. Just put cool and powerful power for Solar and DB PC's, and give tools for the ST to adjust the difficulty according to what they want the experience to feel like.<br /> <br /> The system is not a description of the world as it functions, it is our interface to make said world move into narrative action. The Dragonblooded of the setting can be weaker than the Solar and at the same time the Dragon Blooded of the player can compete with the Solar if the system recognizes that these situations are different and thus can be resolved differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think like four times in this thread. I gave up trying to restate it. -_-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T08:41:48-07:00","id":1386090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386031#post1386031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it doesn't really solve the issue of how to make a PC competitive with a Solar PC, while still having a world where Dragonblood are weaker than Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't injurious to the setting at all if a Fire Aspect can kill a Dawn Caste in a fair fight. Maybe the odds are on the latter, but the idea that it could go either way and you shouldn't put ten down on the Fire Aspect to be safe doesn't hurt things. Solars have access to way more nuanced and subtle advantages and high-power effects that make their absence from the setting noticeable, but that's not the same as talking about PC parity and PC usefulness.<br /> <br /> And as others have said, that has <i>no relation </i>to the effectiveness of PCs vs. NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T09:20:10-07:00","id":1386099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386090#post1386090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't injurious to the setting at all if a Fire Aspect can kill a Dawn Caste in a fair fight. Maybe the odds are on the latter, but the idea that it could go either way and you shouldn't put ten down on the Fire Aspect to be safe doesn't hurt things. Solars have access to way more nuanced and subtle advantages and high-power effects that make their absence from the setting noticeable, but that's not the same as talking about PC parity and PC usefulness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I often think about things like how the setting is affected by details such as Solars having fighting capabilities to offset the advantages of Legendary Size that Dragon Blooded do not, while those aren't exactly advantages that help you in a fight with some Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Which, sure, they still do have, of a different kind, but I'm definitely on board with the idea that those advantages are something that can be weathered with struggle and ingenuity even within the scope of a single character/group concept, and responded to with proper alignment of one's own advantages to hit back hard enough to kill.<br /> <br /> And I certainly think the range of narratives widens considerably if there's player and gameplay support for a wider range of win conditions than having killed the opponent. You know, it's like barring the correct Medicine or Resistance Charms, an attack that does three health levels of lethal damage is going to take somewhere between three days and a weak to recover from. Has the Fire Aspect not come out well if they managed to get in a stab that took a decent chunk out of the Dawn Caste while holding off on taking a blow in kind and being able to fall back, leaving the Solar needing to make decisions about what they want their next fight to be? Do you go where you're needed right now, faced with needing less powerful decisive attacks to finish you off as well as possibly the choice between dedicating motes to offsetting your wound penalties or letting those keep down you attack and defence capabilities, or do you go to ground to return to 100% while removing your combat strength from whatever else you were doing?<br /> <br /> Also during that fight, did you light yourself up so much that a Wyld Hunt in a widely dispersed search pattern can now start closing the noose around you? It takes, what, an hour for that glare to die down?<br /> <br /> Those seem as though they should be considerations that let the Dragon Blooded swordfighter be a legitimate threat to the Solar swordfighter in a straightforward duel that doesn't fall back on &quot;figure out the Solar's weak area and hit them from that angle instead&quot;. Well, I... guess the lack of improved healing is technically still that, but you get what I mean, it's different from saying that the Melee Solar needs to be fought in the court room. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T09:27:01-07:00","id":1386101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386089#post1386089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think like four times in this thread. I gave up trying to restate it. -_-</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't mind, since I'm French I rarely have the opportunity to use this expression, so I'll take this one.<br /> <br /> <i>I feel you, dude</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T09:31:36-07:00","id":1386102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1385914#post1385914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the thing of course is that yes, Jedi are better than non-Jedi.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this is a kind of power creep that has its frustrations but at least makes a modicum of sense when comparing different types of Exalted, but I find totally absurd in Star Wars fandom and game design when it seems to be present in no other form of Star Wars media.<br /> <br /> Nowhere are the Jedi portrayed as people who develop a highly broad array of skills, and Force powers are very uncommonly powerful enough to overwhelm all forms of opposition.<br /> <br /> &quot;Jedi are better than non-Jedi&quot;, unless you want to fly off of Tattooine, I suppose. Then you need to go trawling through bars for somebody who knows how to fly a fucking ship, because it seems as though that's a skill you didn't have the time to develop in addition to knowing the ways of the Force and honing your fencing.<br /> <br /> Remember the Clone Wars cartoon? The one Genndy Tartakofsky did? That was pretty cool, wasn't it. The most recent Honest Trailer recapped it, people should check that out if they want a reacquaintance.<br /> <br /> Remember how that cartoon depicted an alien bounty hunter whose unique physiology made him an enormous hassle to deal with and portrayed General Grievous as an absolute killing machine even in the face of multiple Jedi?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:41:06-07:00","id":1386116,"title":"","content":"Again, I strongly feel the FFG games hit a great balance point here for Star Wars. It's literally the current gameline.<br /> <br /> And, again, I'm not opposed to assymetric PC/NPC rules out of hand. But I am concerned about how Essence will present its super special PC classes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-06-2020, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:43:48-07:00","id":1386118,"title":"","content":"Anakin being an excellent general, great pilot, and prodigal droid-builder not-withstanding, yes, as I touched on in the rest of that very post, pointing out that the other characters are all better than Luke at other things, more experienced in various areas than he is, and this is a way to balance people with more mystic power than others in the same game. A feat most Star Wars games attempt, but a fair few fail at in practice.<br /> <br /> So you could perhaps balance, say, a Solar and Dragonblood by giving the Dragonblood more abilities (as 2nd ed did), more experience (as 3rd ed kind of does) and/or more Merits (as both 2nd and 3rd ed do; I forget about 1st ed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:47:37-07:00","id":1386119,"title":"","content":"Yeah, to be fair, much of Star Wars is about how Luke/Anakin/Rey are very quickly the best pilots at flying ships because they are &quot;in touch with the force&quot; (this is the whole point of the first movie's climatic scene, after all! Han Solo *had* the Millennium Falcon at the start of Ep IV, he wasn't necessarily the best *at* Millennium Falconing)... but yeah, in general the point that non-Jedi are good at leadership and social stuff does stand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:58:52-07:00","id":1386123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386116#post1386116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I strongly feel the FFG games hit a great balance point here for Star Wars. It's literally the current gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seemed well-balanced to me, because the force powers cost a lot of XP, but I only ran Edge of the Empire, not Force and Destiny. I don't know how balanced a Force and Destiny character is with an Edge of the Empire or Age of Rebellion character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, again, I'm not opposed to assymetric PC/NPC rules out of hand. But I am concerned about how Essence will present its super special PC classes. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think it's fine if you just acknowledge it and present it sensibly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T11:02:21-07:00","id":1386124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386118#post1386118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anakin being an excellent general, great pilot, and prodigal droid-builder not-withstanding, yes, as I touched on in the rest of that very post, pointing out that the other characters are all better than Luke at other things, more experienced in various areas than he is, and this is a way to balance people with more mystic power than others in the same game. A feat most Star Wars games attempt, but a fair few fail at in practice.<br /> <br /> So you could perhaps balance, say, a Solar and Dragonblood by giving the Dragonblood more abilities (as 2nd ed did), more experience (as 3rd ed kind of does) and/or more Merits (as both 2nd and 3rd ed do; I forget about 1st ed).</div> </div> </div> </div>1E:<br /> Fewer Attributes, more Abilities, more Backgrounds, same Freebie Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T11:17:37-07:00","id":1386130,"title":"","content":"That sounds the same as 2nd ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:05:46-07:00","id":1386155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386089#post1386089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think like four times in this thread. I gave up trying to restate it. -_-</div> </div> </div> </div>I acknowledge that this is a solution to the particular problem, but I think it creates too many other problems. In-universe my PC isn't special to the point of being twice as strong as the strongest DB right off chargen. Or at least not to the point where I feel like my character is just a completely different thing from what the NPCs are. I can 100% deal with it if my character is stronger than most other DBs, if I built them to be the best at something there shouldn't be a lot of others who match them there, but they should be drastically better than people who are supposedly their peers, or at least close.<br /> <br /> Maybe there could be something introduced like...concentrated dragon blood or something? So like, some DBs are just boosted like that? So the Empress could be one along with a few other people maybe? I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:21:30-07:00","id":1386163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386130#post1386130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds the same as 2nd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Trait minimums were generic for Dynasts rather than tied to Secondary School. But, yeah, reasonably similiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:43:57-07:00","id":1386168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386155#post1386155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I acknowledge that this is a solution to the particular problem, but I think it creates too many other problems. In-universe my PC isn't special to the point of being twice as strong as the strongest DB right off chargen. Or at least not to the point where I feel like my character is just a completely different thing from what the NPCs are. I can 100% deal with it if my character is stronger than most other DBs, if I built them to be the best at something there shouldn't be a lot of others who match them there, but they should be drastically better than people who are supposedly their peers, or at least close.<br /> <br /> Maybe there could be something introduced like...concentrated dragon blood or something? So like, some DBs are just boosted like that? So the Empress could be one along with a few other people maybe? I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm to sure we understand each other. What do you think we mean when we say &quot;the NPC's can be re adjustable&quot; ? Because my proposition is to have the ST adjusting the difficulty depending on the context.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure it will not make us have an agreement, but I remember we argued over &quot;Is it possible to give more actions to an Elder Sidereal in order to make him a solo Circle boss ?&quot;. I think it's a bit of the same case. I don't think a Sidereal Elder should always be a Solo Circle Boss for Solars. I think it's good if the Exalted system allows you to do it for the specific occurrences where you want to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:51:00-07:00","id":1386169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386155#post1386155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I acknowledge that this is a solution to the particular problem, but I think it creates too many other problems. In-universe my PC isn't special to the point of being twice as strong as the strongest DB right off chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I don't think that's an issue because I don't think starting Solars are twice as strong as the strongest Dragonblood. I think they're, like, 20% stronger than a starting Dragonblood, or some such.<br /> <br /> So I think it's okay to say &quot;your Dragonblood is unusually strong for a Dragonblood, feel free to claim she was top in his class at the House of Bells*, is V'neef's own son with amazing blood purity**, is a retired Immaculate Master***, is a famous hero/explorer/sorcerer who recently returned from a trip to the Dreaming Sea where he had all kinds of amazing pulp adventures****.<br /> <br /> *Two PCs in the Dragonblood game I played.<br /> **One PC in the same game<br /> ***One PC in my current mixed game<br /> ****My PC in my current mixed game.<br /> (Contrast these with 16 year-old Solar street kid, and 17-year old Fox-Lunar from the poor part of Nexus. And they're in the same game as retired Immaculate Master.)<br /> <br /> And maybe have a sidebar for a more &quot;average&quot; Dragonblood.<br /> Ie all Exalted PCs get 6 dots of attributes, 20 dots of abilities, 10 charms, etc. However, if you want to do a lower-powered game, perhaps young Dragonblood, statting a pretty average DB NPC, etc, etc, then start with 5 dots of attributes, 15 dots of abilities, 5 charms, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T14:35:20-07:00","id":1386179,"title":"","content":"Even like, by 3e's default rules, your PCs will likely be more powerful than some NPCs unless you adjust things. It's not hard for a starting DB to have pools and stuff similar to Ragara's since he doens't have some super secret higher traits for being old. (His attack dice pool with Blood Zenith is a confirmed typo, just t ontoe.) The system already more or less lets your PCs in short time outstrip NPCs on things like Essence and thus Charm capability. V'Neef is old enough to be your grandma, but you could have higher Essence than her. This is a conceit of the system already letting PCs be exceptional to NPCs.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm just also not sympathetic to the idea that if there are DBs about equal to other Exalts in personal power, that this means other Exalts can't be relevant or a threat to the setting. As I noted before, other Exalts just <i>do shit</i> that DBs can't. This ranges from access to general magic (notably evocations, sorcery, necromancy, and martial arts), long lifespans allowing for particualrly potent long term power bases (this is implied a big thing with the Empress' power this editon is that she stayed in power long enough to be an instiution in herself), and at times probably just the nature fo their magic. Lunar Exalted are a bitch to actually put down. Solar Exalted have what looks to be an effect on their enviornment and followers which is multiplied in a way DBs don't get (nothing like Tiger Warrior Training exists so far for other Exalts we've seen, and that's like, a signature Solar <i>thing</i>).<br /> <br /> I dunno, I just look at things and think that Solars don't need that much to be notably a problem fo the Realm and its myraid DBs. And I think a lot of this comes from folks feeling that the gap between Exalts needs to be greater than necssary to achieve the setting as it is presented.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:26:50-07:00","id":1386184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386102#post1386102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, this is a kind of power creep that has its frustrations but at least makes a modicum of sense when comparing different types of Exalted, but I find totally absurd in Star Wars fandom and game design when it seems to be present in no other form of Star Wars media.<br /> <br /> Nowhere are the Jedi portrayed as people who develop a highly broad array of skills, and Force powers are very uncommonly powerful enough to overwhelm all forms of opposition.<br /> <br /> &quot;Jedi are better than non-Jedi&quot;, unless you want to fly off of Tattooine, I suppose. Then you need to go trawling through bars for somebody who knows how to fly a fucking ship, because it seems as though that's a skill you didn't have the time to develop in addition to knowing the ways of the Force and honing your fencing.<br /> <br /> Remember the Clone Wars cartoon? The one Genndy Tartakofsky did? That was pretty cool, wasn't it. The most recent Honest Trailer recapped it, people should check that out if they want a reacquaintance.<br /> <br /> Remember how that cartoon depicted an alien bounty hunter whose unique physiology made him an enormous hassle to deal with and portrayed General Grievous as an absolute killing machine even in the face of multiple Jedi?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hard to fly off a planet when you don't own a space craft, and hiring an experienced smuggler crew and their specialized ship to get you somewhere while you are in a situation where you will probably need to evade the law to get there isn't exactly the same thing as hiring a generic space taxi. In general they were actually portrayed as having a fairly broad set of mundane skills they were supposed to learn to be considered competent enough to be a knight (Personal combat skills unrelated to lightsabers like how to use blasters, diplomacy, military strategy, how to dog fight in star fighters, how to investigate for a variety of crimes, enough familiarity with technology to know uncommon knowledge like the fact that starships have a separate computer for tracking fuel that erasing your navigation computer to hide where you have traveled doesn't touch) in TCW on top of learning force powers. At one point an undercover jedi who has to completely avoid using force powers still managed to be one of the most competent people present among a group consisting of people considered to be among the best bounty hunters in the galaxy. So it is definitely not just games where they are portrayed as being vastly more competent then all but the most elite of normies decked out in a bunch of high tech goodies to equalize against the edge they get from the force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T16:04:28-07:00","id":1386200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386155#post1386155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I acknowledge that this is a solution to the particular problem, but I think it creates too many other problems. In-universe my PC isn't special to the point of being twice as strong as the strongest DB right off chargen. Or at least not to the point where I feel like my character is just a completely different thing from what the NPCs are. I can 100% deal with it if my character is stronger than most other DBs, if I built them to be the best at something there shouldn't be a lot of others who match them there, but they should be drastically better than people who are supposedly their peers, or at least close.<br /> <br /> Maybe there could be something introduced like...concentrated dragon blood or something? So like, some DBs are just boosted like that? So the Empress could be one along with a few other people maybe? I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>Double-Dragon-Blooded, or &quot;Exalted of Exalted&quot; sounds as bad as Terrestrial Half-Castes.<br /> <br /> Either you ARE Chosen of the Dragons, or you AREN'T. No halfsies. No double-Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T16:13:20-07:00","id":1386202,"title":"","content":"I think also it's too big a fluff change for Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T20:56:44-07:00","id":1386238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386118#post1386118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anakin being an excellent general, <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious if the Clone Wars series depicted Jedi military leadership as anything more sophisticated than being the tip of the spear.<br /> <br /> What would have been Anakin's Battle of Austerlitz, the thing that shows his Jedi superiority over Ackbar or Holdo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T21:29:56-07:00","id":1386245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386238#post1386238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious if the Clone Wars series depicted Jedi military leadership as anything more sophisticated than being the tip of the spear.<br /> <br /> What would have been Anakin's Battle of Austerlitz, the thing that shows his Jedi superiority over Ackbar or Holdo?</div> </div> </div> </div>The best thing he did was probably the time he ambushed Grievous in an asteroid field via the unorthodox tactic of hiding a bunch of AT-TEs on asteroids opposite of his fleet and having them blast the undefended rears of Grievous's capital ships once the focused energy into their forward shields to defend against Anakin's visible forces. It let him take out a fleet that was superior to his own in terms of power without that much in the way of loses for a fight that was basically 2 on 1 in numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ywBZNZEr8q8\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ywBZNZEr8q8\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ywBZNZEr8q8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ywBZNZEr8q8 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-07-2020, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T21:41:49-07:00","id":1386249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386168#post1386168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm to sure we understand each other. What do you think we mean when we say &quot;the NPC's can be re adjustable&quot; ? Because my proposition is to have the ST adjusting the difficulty depending on the context.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure it will not make us have an agreement, but I remember we argued over &quot;Is it possible to give more actions to an Elder Sidereal in order to make him a solo Circle boss ?&quot;. I think it's a bit of the same case. I don't think a Sidereal Elder should always be a Solo Circle Boss for Solars. I think it's good if the Exalted system allows you to do it for the specific occurrences where you want to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of thing, for me, messes with the verisimilitude of the setting or story. Like say you were running a mortals game where one of the character's father was challenged to a duel by a powerful Solar warrior for some great prize, and lost. A way that character could progress with his vendetta is to go after that Solar, challenge them to single combat, and beat them in a classic, iconic cycle of revenge/violence family honour kind of story.<br /> <br /> If I was running that though, the last thing I'd want to do is completely gimp this supposedly exceptionally powerful Dawn caste down to the point where the mortal player could just beat them down in a fair fight. Just because it's the narrative arc that might take doesn't mean that it doesn't really make sense? Without some kind of in-universe explanation to help balance the scales, anyway.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather the setting be changed and presented in a different way so as to have a flat power curve and have it make sense, than to give the PCs or certain NPCs a special status that made them very different. Or at least if you have to do that lampshade it somehow, like somehow x-person fused their souls with a powerful demon to warrant them being set apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T00:19:16-07:00","id":1386299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386249#post1386249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kind of thing, for me, messes with the verisimilitude of the setting or story. Like say you were running a mortals game where one of the character's father was challenged to a duel by a powerful Solar warrior for some great prize, and lost. A way that character could progress with his vendetta is to go after that Solar, challenge them to single combat, and beat them in a classic, iconic cycle of revenge/violence family honour kind of story.<br /> <br /> If I was running that though, the last thing I'd want to do is completely gimp this supposedly exceptionally powerful Dawn caste down to the point where the mortal player could just beat them down in a fair fight. Just because it's the narrative arc that might take doesn't mean that it doesn't really make sense? Without some kind of in-universe explanation to help balance the scales, anyway.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather the setting be changed and presented in a different way so as to have a flat power curve and have it make sense, than to give the PCs or certain NPCs a special status that made them very different. Or at least if you have to do that lampshade it somehow, like somehow x-person fused their souls with a powerful demon to warrant them being set apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we'll convince each other much at that point because we already had a discussion on this topic, and I think we each have our own reasons to stay by our position. <br /> <br /> I'm just going to argue 2 things :<br /> <br /> 1) I'm not arguing to change the system every time there is a possible character arc. I'm arguing having multiple resolution system that can fit different kind of narration would help solve the whole topic debated over many pages of &quot;How do we make DB PC's fun to play with Solar PC's if the DB are much weaker than the Solar&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) This kind of things already exist in the core system. The Battlegroup system is literally this kind of feature, that helps the ST adjust the system to whatever the challenge the PC are facing. And while people argue over the quality of the implementation of this feature, I think most people who played Ex3 are happy that this feature exist, and I don't think it breaks that much verisimilitude. Because this feature has already been used doesn't necessarily mean it's a good idea to re-use it on every other aspect of the system, but I think it's an option worth considering with discussions that goes into &quot;How could it feel like and how would it accomplish what we want it to accomplish ?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:02:54-07:00","id":1386307,"title":"","content":"Battle Groups is a good example, though it's a somewhat specific thing that builds on genre-tropes, and also the fact that people are somewhat aware of the fact that 1 Solar vs 100 mortal spods is unrunnable.<br /> <br /> Still, I see your point.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I think that this kind of thing is potentially viable, it just has to be done quite carefully. Which is a point JohnDoe made earlier; there's somewhat of an issue around presentation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T04:58:41-07:00","id":1386354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386249#post1386249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd much rather the setting be changed and presented in a different way so as to have a flat power curve and have it make sense, than to give the PCs or certain NPCs a special status that made them very different. Or at least if you have to do that lampshade it somehow, like somehow x-person fused their souls with a powerful demon to warrant them being set apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, maybe I need to phrase this differently: if you place the Exalted on a relatively level playing field for certain things, such as duels, it doesn't break the setting or the lore. If you give them a rough degree of parity in capability, it doesn't break the setting or the lore.<br /> <br /> Look, I'm coming at this from 2e. Dragon-Blooded were completely weaksauce against Solars and totally at their mercy; the lore actually changed to fit this, to the point where the Usurpation didn't make any damn sense. 3e avoided this, largely by making Dragon-Blooded highly competent and taking advantage of the swinginess of the dice pools. But even though a Dragon-Blooded can kill a Solar now - Tepet Arada has done so twice in the fiction, and I personally saw a DB with his stats kill an Essence 2 Solar, then watched an Essence 1 DB go toe-to-toe with an Essence 1 Solar - Solars still have access to top-tier sorcery and crafting, to Wyld-Shaping, to vast capabilities with Evocations. Solars have <i>so many </i>advantages that parity in this one area - even if the Exalted Host as a whole matches or exceeds them on certain areas - doesn't hurt them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:05:32-07:00","id":1386358,"title":"","content":"Being Exalted is the baseline in <b>Exalted</b>. You cannot ever ignore another Exalt as a threat, period.<br /> <br /> And if we assume only Exalts are PCs, rather than going from an assumption of mortals and then the Exalted systematically ignoring parts of the mechanical engine, certain things change and parity in the party becomes way easier to achieve. If you divorce NPCs from that power curve and from using PC mechanics, you can do a <i>lot </i>more to help Storytellers match conflicts to the party and reduce cognitive load.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-07-2020, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:31:40-07:00","id":1386364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386358#post1386358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if we assume only Exalts are PCs, rather than going from an assumption of mortals and then the Exalted systematically ignoring parts of the mechanical engine, certain things change and parity in the party becomes way easier to achieve. If you divorce NPCs from that power curve and from using PC mechanics, you can do a <i>lot </i>more to help Storytellers match conflicts to the party and reduce cognitive load.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really seems like a clever approach. I like 3e's idea of building the entire world and then making your heroes break the rules to show how awesome they are, but I think from a design perspective this puts many limitations and contradictions on the game.<br /> <br /> I don't know how this will go, but I'm curious and positive to see how this will work out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 05-07-2020, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:39:20-07:00","id":1386367,"title":"","content":"My ideal would be for it to be like 4th ed DnD, where a powerful wizard or warrior NPC used completely different rules to your PC (and rules designed to be a fun encounter rather than be for someone who fights 20 combats and is run by a player doing nothing else*), but still felt appropriate thematically for what they were; I think players actually find it easier to accept than for NPCs to be kinda-based on the PC rules but cheat with extra rules-breaking stuff to make up for the fact they've got a third of the charms.<br /> Personally, I feel much more comfortable using a completely-different-rules-NPC from the book than make a character kinda-but-not-quite based on the PC character creation system.<br /> <br /> But that's just me, maybe other people would actually much more prefer things quite close.<br /> Also, close is maybe easier to make NPCs yourself.<br /> Also the book may not have room.<br /> <br /> Probably saying flat-out &quot;NPCs do not use the same rules, this is a conceit necessary to have a good game, suspend your disbelief&quot; (which people don't seem bothered with in DnD) is 80% of the issue, but traditionally Exalted hasn't wanted to do.<br /> <br /> *Neall's comment makes me optimistic, because I did find running high-level NPC Exalts in groups in 3rd ed to have a lot of cognitive load, compared to running a CR15 Wizard with 5 spells and his two CR12 Demons with 3 abilities each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-07-2020, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:45:29-07:00","id":1386396,"title":"","content":"To be honest, the more I hear, the less I like.<br /> <br /> It feels like this thing is an attempt to force game balance into this setting, which is absolute nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:51:15-07:00","id":1386398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386396#post1386396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, the more I hear, the less I like.<br /> <br /> It feels like this thing is an attempt to force game balance into this setting, which is absolute nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would have been very unexpected of a lite-Exalted version to keep or increase &quot;game imbalance&quot;, so I'm sorry for you but sadly I don't think this should come as a surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 05-07-2020, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T11:22:48-07:00","id":1386439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386396#post1386396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, the more I hear, the less I like.<br /> <br /> It feels like this thing is an attempt to force game balance into this setting, which is absolute nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I don't understand the sentiment unless again, there's a particualr dictate on what the power curve is even supposed to be that's being flattened, or we assume that the setting shoudl be reflective of PC mechanics toa a T.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:48:28-07:00","id":1386501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386354#post1386354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I'm coming at this from 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh okay, I'm coming at this from 3e where it's already been flattened down a bit. Barring some weird outlier craziness that I'm pretty sure wasn't actually intentional design, a group of 4 DBs can totally beat down the one Solar in their group if she goes completely insane with a Limit Break and decides to butcher the surrendering enemy army or whatever. I look forward to seeing what you guys come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:13:20-07:00","id":1386510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386358#post1386358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being Exalted is the baseline in <b>Exalted</b>. You cannot ever ignore another Exalt as a threat, period.<br /> <br /> And if we assume only Exalts are PCs, rather than going from an assumption of mortals and then the Exalted systematically ignoring parts of the mechanical engine, certain things change and parity in the party becomes way easier to achieve. If you divorce NPCs from that power curve and from using PC mechanics, you can do a <i>lot </i>more to help Storytellers match conflicts to the party and reduce cognitive load.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like what a game named &quot;Exalted&quot; should have tried from the beginning. But setting that potential argument aside, I'm eager to see the attempt made now.<br /> <br /> Playing an unExalted mortal seems like it should be niche enough that the system shouldn't be built around unExalted mortals.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't even seem complicated to play a mortal in Essence. No motes, no Exalted Advantages, no Excellencies, no Charms, possibly lower dice pools, and as many penalties from the storyteller as seems necessary to reflect a mortal's greater mortality in the face of injury and disease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:00:28-07:00","id":1386522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386090#post1386090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't injurious to the setting at all if a Fire Aspect can kill a Dawn Caste in a fair fight. Maybe the odds are on the latter, but the idea that it could go either way and you shouldn't put ten down on the Fire Aspect to be safe doesn't hurt things. Solars have access to way more nuanced and subtle advantages and high-power effects that make their absence from the setting noticeable, but that's not the same as talking about PC parity and PC usefulness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I'm dipping a bit far back in the conversation, but I have to say, this comment killed my enthusiasm for Exalted Essence stone dead. I <i>do</i> think that's injurious to the setting. Isn't one of the central themes of Exalted that Creation is going to shit precisely because the Solars have been missing? Why would that be the case if the Solars are scarcely more capable than the DBs that outnumber them 33 to 1? I'm assuming this comment is about a Fire Aspect and a Dawn Caste that are sitting at equal XP levels, of course- I have no problem with an experienced DB killing an inexperienced Solar, or a combat-focused DB killing a non-combat-focused Solar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386354#post1386354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars still have access to top-tier sorcery and crafting, to Wyld-Shaping, to vast capabilities with Evocations. Solars have <i>so many </i>advantages that parity in this one area - even if the Exalted Host as a whole matches or exceeds them on certain areas - doesn't hurt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this comment did not reassure me at all. Do you know how many players I've had that wanted to focus on Wyld-Shaping, crafting, or Evocations? None, ever. Exalted has always been a very combat-focused game, and having the Solars hang their hats on such tertiary parts of the system seems like a bad choice to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/794-el-pinko-grande","name":"el pinko grande","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:15:23-07:00","id":1386530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386522#post1386522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't one of the central themes of Exalted that Creation is going to shit precisely because the Solars have been missing? Why would that be the case if the Solars are scarcely more capable than the DBs that outnumber them 33 to 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all capability is combat capability. The absence of Solar circle sorcery, Wyld-Shaping Technique, and the highest tiers of Solar artifice is <i>plenty</i> to justify a fall from a glorious golden age.<br /> <br /> \u200b- The absence of Solar circle sorcery means the greatest workings can only be achieved haphazardly and at great cost.<br /> \u200b- The absence of Solar artifice means that the greatest manses and artifacts, once lost, will probably never be seen again.<br /> - The absence of Wyld-Shaping Technique means that any land lost to the Wyld is gone forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-07-2020, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:24:41-07:00","id":1386534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386530#post1386530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all capability is combat capability. The absence of Solar circle sorcery, Wyld-Shaping Technique, and the highest tiers of Solar artifice is <i>plenty</i> to justify a fall from a glorious golden age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but when has Exalted ever been a game focused on artifice or Wyld-Shaping? The issue I have is that the core areas of competence for Solars all appear to be in tertiary aspects of the game, and I find that choice to be a massive turn-off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/794-el-pinko-grande","name":"el pinko grande","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:27:48-07:00","id":1386536,"title":"","content":"(I realise the post he's replying to of Neall's is a post Neall made in response to me, but I missed it as more people replied to other things I said so I didn't reply. Sorry to ignore you Neall.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I think the setting works fine with Solars being the best in leadership roles, Solar sorcery, generalship, curing the Great Contagion, convincing nations to follow them, cutting mountains in half; stuff that has a big setting impact and so the fluff of 150 Solars, that's not the same as being the best at combat.<br /> (What I want from Solars is essentially to change the world; not to make it difficult for me to supply them with challenging combat characters, which I found a big challenge when I ran an E4 Solar game when 3rd ed first came out. I want them to be able to chop a castle in two, not thrash a high-essence god at combat in a system where they're clearly going to win but it takes 2 hours of rolling. I'd rather a Solar can destroy a Shadowland with a week-long ritual than get 10 more dice than an Abyssal.<br /> Of course, in Essence Solars will be able to get free excellencies and auto-win ties vs Abyssals anyway...)<br /> <br /> But then, I can get that if for you playing Solars is about being the best at combat (in my current E5 game, we've got a combat-Dawn, a social-Zenith, a social-Eclipse, a Solar-Sorcery eclipse, and we previously had a Night with a warstrider and evocations and a craft/medicine-Twilight, so our characters are combat-capable but it's not a combat-orientated game; the Lunars game I run I'd say has 2 combat-focused characters out of 6, and only one is very combat-forced), then saying they're going for more parity between a Solar melee-ist and a Fire melee-ist, well, it doesn't bother me but I can see why it bothers you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-07-2020, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:30:15-07:00","id":1386537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right, but when has Exalted ever been a game focused on artifice or Wyld-Shaping? </div> </div> </div>Tbh, I found in 2nd ed that the idea of Solars and how great they were in the First Age was pretty much mostly focused on Craft: Magitek, and Sorcery (the High First Age very much felt like the glorious achievement of the Twilights, with the rest being a little subsidary). Certainly a lot of people seemed to see it that way.<br /> <br /> Not saying that's a good or bad thing, just that it was a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:36:49-07:00","id":1386544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386537#post1386537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tbh, I found in 2nd ed that the idea of Solars and how great they were in the First Age was pretty much mostly focused on Craft: Magitek, and Sorcery (the High First Age very much felt like the glorious achievement of the Twilights, with the rest being a little subsidary).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but we're talking about the fiction there. How often was crafting Magitek or crazy sorcerous workings the focus of games people actually played? Hell, how many campaigns were either long enough or high level enough for PCs to have access to Solar Circle Sorcery? Certainly I imagine lots of groups had characters running around with crazy gear from Oadenol's Codex, but that's not quite the same thing as saying the game is focused on PCs building their own Magitek gadgets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/794-el-pinko-grande","name":"el pinko grande","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:43:00-07:00","id":1386547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386534#post1386534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but when has Exalted ever been a game focused on artifice or Wyld-Shaping?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least once, considering the longest-running game I played in 2e had us doing that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:44:18-07:00","id":1386548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386534#post1386534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but when has Exalted ever been a game focused on artifice or Wyld-Shaping? The issue I have is that the core areas of competence for Solars all appear to be in tertiary aspects of the game, and I find that choice to be a massive turn-off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see your point here; we discussed this a while back in this thread (it's a long thread).<br /> If Lunars' &quot;thing&quot; is shapechanging, Dragonblood's &quot;thing&quot; is teamwork, Sidereals &quot;thing&quot; is Martial Arts, and Solars' &quot;thing&quot; is sorcery, Craft and evocations... why bother playing a Solar if you're not playing a Twilight? Why bother playing a Dawn Martial Artist, because what's good about being a Dawn?<br /> <br /> But I think that being a Martial Artist who's 10% more punchy than another splat is fine for a Dawn in play or as an NPC. He doesn't need to be able to kill 10 Dragonblood by himself to be the best Martial Artist around (this makes for a boring game, IMO. Being able to kill 1000 mortals is fine though.)<br /> And other things can explain the overal significance of Solars, such as the fact that some could cast Benediction of Archgenesis, or cure the Great Contagion, or alter the weather with powers learnt from gods, or be a general whose army of 1000 men could defeat an army of 10000 Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> But again, these to me seem the defining features of Solars, or at least the interesting ones (any splat can be built to be &quot;good at combat&quot;), whereas you consider them tertiary. Which sounds to me like your play group has had quite a different experience to mine (and your play is no less valid than ours).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:47:57-07:00","id":1386552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386544#post1386544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but we're talking about the fiction there. How often was crafting Magitek or crazy sorcerous workings the focus of games people actually played? Hell, how many campaigns were either long enough or high level enough for PCs to have access to Solar Circle Sorcery? Certainly I imagine lots of groups had characters running around with crazy gear from Oadenol's Codex, but that's not quite the same thing as saying the game is focused on PCs building their own Magitek gadgets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, by the end of my game the Eclipse was a Solar Sorcerer who Wyld-Shaped his own society (of three-eyed winged lizardmen), and the Twilight engineered a mutagenic retro-virus in his lab that gave all Djala (and some other mortals) Exalted Healing and Enlightened Essence.<br /> <br /> But in the other game I played the Solars didn't do anything like that. Oh... actually the Twilight made a floating city, but that was while he was away, not near the other PCs. They mostly just bumbled around in one country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:04:38-07:00","id":1386556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386548#post1386548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think that being a Martial Artist who's 10% more punchy than another splat is fine for a Dawn in play or as an NPC. He doesn't need to be able to kill 10 Dragonblood by himself to be the best Martial Artist around (this makes for a boring game, IMO. Being able to kill 1000 mortals is fine though.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually fine with that, too, and I'm fine with Punchy Dawn losing a fight to an Immaculate because the Immaculate is decked out in all sorts of cool artifact gear to which the Solar doesn't have access.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386548#post1386548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And other things can explain the overal significance of Solars, such as the fact that some could cast Benediction of Archgenesis, or cure the Great Contagion, or alter the weather with powers learnt from gods, or be a general whose army of 1000 men could defeat an army of 10000 Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> But again, these to me seem the defining features of Solars, or at least the interesting ones (any splat can be built to be &quot;good at combat&quot;), whereas you consider them tertiary. Which sounds to me like your play group has had quite a different experience to mine (and your play is no less valid than ours).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all that stuff is cool, too, the issue is that it's actually quite high level, and hence something my games rarely reach. That might change with Exalted Essence, since higher powered games should be less daunting to run. But regardless, I think it's worth noting that if you start a game at the normal power level, it's going to be quite a long time before a lot of the stuff that makes Solars distinct comes online, unless things are changed so that Solar Circle Sorcery can be reached earlier. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/794-el-pinko-grande","name":"el pinko grande","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:12:38-07:00","id":1386559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386556#post1386556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think all that stuff is cool, too, the issue is that it's actually quite high level, and hence something my games rarely reach. That might change with Exalted Essence, since higher powered games should be less daunting to run. But regardless, I think it's worth noting that if you start a game at the normal power level, it's going to be quite a long time before a lot of the stuff that makes Solars distinct comes online, unless things are changed so that Solar Circle Sorcery can be reached earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Infinite free excellencies should be quite noticeable from session 1, especially in a mixed Circle where everyone else is counting motes. Also Exalted: Essence pumps more power into the Caste powers (to make up for each splat having less unique Charms), which should be noticeable from the get go. A Dawn going iconic should feel a serious combat power boost, and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:12:59-07:00","id":1386560,"title":"","content":"That's a good point el Pinko Grande, but I think Neall was addressing a point about Solar power level, rather than distinctiveness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:14:53-07:00","id":1386562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386559#post1386559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like Infinite free excellencies should be quite noticeable from session 1, especially in a mixed Circle where everyone else is counting motes. Also Exalted: Essence pumps more power into the Caste powers (to make up for each splat having less unique Charms), which should be noticeable from the get go. A Dawn going iconic should feel a serious combat power boost, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like that to be the case, but do we know how Excellencies work yet? I was under the impression they would be quite different than the Excellencies to which we've become accustomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/794-el-pinko-grande","name":"el pinko grande","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:20:00-07:00","id":1386563,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if they'll be very different, I think they might still be dice adders (since there's a dice cap), but Monica said that free excellencies isn't as good as it would be in regular 3rd edition. But that it's still powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:26:55-07:00","id":1386566,"title":"","content":"Well, that might mollify my concerns somewhat, and if that leads us to Dawns that are 10% more punchy/swordy than their counterparts among other types of Exalts, I'll be content. <br /> <br /> Neall's comment still really concerns me, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/794-el-pinko-grande","name":"el pinko grande","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:12:22-07:00","id":1386574,"title":"","content":"A dev quote on roll difficulties and what they mean, which mentions excellencies near the end :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Difficulty 7 pushes the limits on what the Exalted can accomplish without aid of magic. Difficulty 7 actions might include: instantly punching through a fortified stone wall, sneaking past a vigilant guardian of Heaven, or translating a text in a language lost to time.<br /> Difficulty 10, most of the time, will not be achievable without Charms. To perform a Difficulty 10 feat without magic borderlines on impossible. This might be [...] swimming through the Wyld and coming out unaltered, or successfully recreating an artifact from a fragment of a First Age manual.<br /> [...]<br /> Essence does its level best to keep dice pools at 20 or less<br /> which is why 10 is where it is (note: an Excellency is using magic)<br /> [...]<br /> So like yeah 15 dice is pretty easy to come by if you max out everything and drop an Excellency on it and yes you probably will see 10 succesess by doing so - but you're still using magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:19:38-07:00","id":1386575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386530#post1386530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all capability is combat capability. The absence of Solar circle sorcery, Wyld-Shaping Technique, and the highest tiers of Solar artifice is <i>plenty</i> to justify a fall from a glorious golden age.<br /> <br /> \u200b- The absence of Solar circle sorcery means the greatest workings can only be achieved haphazardly and at great cost.<br /> \u200b- The absence of Solar artifice means that the greatest manses and artifacts, once lost, will probably never be seen again.<br /> - The absence of Wyld-Shaping Technique means that any land lost to the Wyld is gone forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are major factors for sure, but the absence of the Solar Exalted isn't the whole story.<br /> <br /> Another factor behind the fall of the First Age is that the Solar Exalted and Terrestrial Exalted now existed in a state of total war against each other. Previously, any conflict between these Hosts was specific and personal to the Chosen involved, and they were just as likely to gladly work together.<br /> <br /> The First Age wasn't built by the Solar Exalted alone. It was made by the Solars, Lunars, Sidereals, and Terrestrials all working together.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation brought that cooperation to an end. Now Terrestrial and Sidereal Exalted hunt Solars and Lunars like animals, and Solars and Lunars work to tear down everything that Terrestrials and Sidereals build up.<br /> <br /> The fall of the First Age wouldn't have been nearly so bad if all of the Solars and Lunars had just... disappeared. The Second Age has been greatly shaped by the Silver Pact's long guerrilla war against the Realm, and many First Age wonders must have been lost in final acts of vengeance from the Solar Exalted before they died (and when their next incarnations came back for revenge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:24:39-07:00","id":1386578,"title":"","content":"We can't say for sure until we see the system but it seems like free excellencies and always winning ties are going to be pretty great in terms of being the best at something like sword fighting or whatever you focus in. But you can be the best without being so good that you basically just hit an 'I win' button at the start of the fight instead of other people being able to give you a run for your money and even win if you get cocky and screw around or are fighting under some sort of handicap like them poisoning your drink before the fight. Solars don't have to be able to beat the 10 thousand dragons of the realm in a 10K vs 300 fight in a white room to be the strongest exalts (or, you know, be able to beat them 10K on 1 like they used to be able to do in 2nd edition).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-07-2020, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:26:10-07:00","id":1386579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386575#post1386575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Usurpation brought that cooperation to an end. Now Terrestrial and Sidereal Exalted hunt Solars and Lunars like animals, and Solars and Lunars work to tear down everything that Terrestrials and Sidereals build up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the Sidereals, who were previously the great advisors of all, had to retreat from the world after the breaking of the mask caused their arcane fate, and Creation became so dangerous what with the Lunars and all. That would be a pretty big deal.<br /> <br /> Even the the Shogunate was less epic than the high first age, but it wasn't totally fallen either. Also the Shogunate was an age of constant infighting among the terrestrials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T20:53:09-07:00","id":1386605,"title":"","content":"Yeah I agree that in a fight between a Fire Aspect and a Dawn (assuming similar XP levels, PC rules, and the like)... Like I still think the Dawn should win most often.<br /> <br /> But I think it should be like, 30:70 or 40:60 rather than 0:100. Like, you can have ONE have an advantage without the other being a chump who's a dumbass for even trying.<br /> <br /> I'll also echo the people saying that measuring Solar Power Levels in units of Dead Dragonbloods per Round (DDR) is the <i>least</i> interesting metric by which to measure overall competence. <i>You can be good at what you do without making other Exalts be irrelevant and suckers.</i> &quot;Oh, sorry you suck at literally everything, you should have played a REAL Exalt&quot; isn't a good message to send.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386534#post1386534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but when has Exalted ever been a game focused on artifice or Wyld-Shaping? The issue I have is that the core areas of competence for Solars all appear to be in tertiary aspects of the game, and I find that choice to be a massive turn-off.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the time, honestly. I've had a lot more Builders, Shapers, Loremasters, Spymasters, and Diplomancers than I have Straight Up Fighters. Both as a player and having had to GM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-07-2020, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T22:47:26-07:00","id":1386618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386544#post1386544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but we're talking about the fiction there. How often was crafting Magitek or crazy sorcerous workings the focus of games people actually played? Hell, how many campaigns were either long enough or high level enough for PCs to have access to Solar Circle Sorcery? Certainly I imagine lots of groups had characters running around with crazy gear from Oadenol's Codex, but that's not quite the same thing as saying the game is focused on PCs building their own Magitek gadgets.</div> </div> </div> </div>My longest running Exalted game, which has just hit its 40th session, is one-hundred-percent about crazy sorcerous workings and artifice. The Twilight in my game allied with Lookshy and basically overnight got their airships and warstriders back to full functionality and built something like 20 new suits of Gunzosha armor from scratch. Solars, at least in some respects, have the power to usher in a new golden age for Creation.<br /> <br /> As of right now that Solar is focused on creating a beautiful perfect city with running water, automatically replenishing food stores, etc. She has, by her Solar nature, the power to change the world for the better and she's doing so.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T01:51:08-07:00","id":1386644,"title":"","content":"Kind of a thing to point out too is that the return of the Solar Exalted isn't the only single problem in the world right now. The gist I get, especialy with 3e's presentation, is the big issue wiht Solars coming back is absolutely no one expected Solars to matter again for the last fifteen centuries and had largley moved on from the Usurpation. Their return, timed with the rise of the Abyssal and Infenral Exlated along htem, the return of Exigents, and renewed pushes to the Center are kinda all happening at once, right hwen the instituion that historiclaly <i>could</i> fend this all off, the Realm, is on the brink of collapse due to a succession crisis.<br /> <br /> In previous editions, I think the world's eminant &quot;Everything is gong to get fucked and sucks&quot; would probably have been more on Solars...as they were the last thing standing between the world dying to new Balorian Crusade, the Dead, or Yozi invasion. The existential nature of threats side-lined the Realm and focused on uniquely Solar powerful magic as that's all that could stop the eminatn Thousand Dooms.<br /> <br /> I think in 3e, the Realm collapsing is probably actually the singular most important event right now. That the Realm is collapsing <i>at the same time</i> as the Solars and their derivatives returning, is kind of more a feedback loop. The smaller curve of 3e kind of empahsizes this. A Dawn can't just blender her way through a Realm Legion and all its officers. The Bull needed a Circle, allies beyond them, and sabotage on the Tepet side...and got a Pyrric victory out of it. There's no Primordial return coming. The Fair Folk aren't going to invade the world in a second Crusade. The Deathlords aren't going Omnicidal on the universe. The singular axial power is collapsing, dragging the rest of the world with it, and hundreds of forgotten or new wild cards got flung into the board while at it.<br /> <br /> I just kind of feel in this context, Solar Exalted don't need some &quot;Beat X number of DBs in a fight&quot; to matter. THere's a lot for oom of generally being a badass, generally having the edges where it counts (via Excellencies and even just ties), access to things lost for ages (sorcery, artifice, unique Solar Charm stuff, even just deals/contracts/obligtions left void since the Usurpation with weird allies), and not a lot of the mechanism of the Empire to squish this from getting out of hand. They have a combination of just enough edge and especially significant circumstances that add up to thier importance. Remember, the Realm's fall was always supposed to be a big factor fo Solar upheaval to follow.<br /> <br /> If just the Solars returned but the Empress were still there, I would see Solars put in a similar situation as Lunars. At the edge, tyring ot survive, eeking out a living in teh Threshold. Likely they'd eat away at the Realm, and it would loose a lot of key satrapies, but it woudl stand, and like be the central axis of the world still, though weakned wiht a lot more ocmpition from Solar Kingdoms along the Lunar Dominions. Had just the Empress disappeared, the Realm's succession crisis would go to hell, and we would probably be in a new era of strife regardless, maybe a new Realm repalces it. Again, likley diminished, Lunars taking cuts about, and mabye a disunified Blessed Isle or a weaker Throne. A world in cahos, but one more predictable.<br /> <br /> I think <u><b>both</b></u>happening is a lot of what makes for the current Time of Tumult. I dunno, I just don't see that the upehaval has to be &quot;The Solar could take on the Realm anyways.&quot; The Realm's decay is to me actually kind of pointless if the Solars had pretty much a sure win regardless of its current succession state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T01:52:07-07:00","id":1386645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386522#post1386522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this comment did not reassure me at all. Do you know how many players I've had that wanted to focus on Wyld-Shaping, crafting, or Evocations? None, ever. Exalted has always been a very combat-focused game, and having the Solars hang their hats on such tertiary parts of the system seems like a bad choice to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all I want to say that I totally respect your experience and expectation of gameplay. <br /> <br /> That said, the reason I have been so much into Exalted the last 3 years was precisely because all campaigns were less focused on combat and included more aspects of everything else. <br /> <br /> So I guess it's going to be very hard for Essence to deal with this kind of different expectation because if it went down your road (ie more combat focused) I'd be as disappointed as you seem to be","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T02:26:24-07:00","id":1386648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386605#post1386605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I agree that in a fight between a Fire Aspect and a Dawn (assuming similar XP levels, PC rules, and the like)... Like I still think the Dawn should win most often.<br /> <br /> But I think it should be like, 30:70 or 40:60 rather than 0:100. Like, you can have ONE have an advantage without the other being a chump who's a dumbass for even trying.</div> </div> </div> </div>So while I agree, etc, etc... is anyone actually disagreeing with this? Or at least many people.<br /> <br /> 2nd ed was (if built fairly optimally) maybe 90:10 between a Solar and a Dragonblood in a fight. I'd say 3rd ed is about 70:30 (looking at the Arena, it seems pretty swingy, but depends a lot on the character's stats. As it should really).<br /> <br /> Neall wants to flatten that to make mixed games more viable.<br /> <br /> So, let's say in Essence a fight is 60:40 between a Dawn and a Fire Aspect. The Dawn after all, has free excellencies and wins ties, so in this straight fight between the two of them she has the advantage. Overall, though, the Dragonblood is better at socialising (because he's a Fire Aspect so gets Presence, and because he's the second son of a Kingdom's ruling family, and knows all the local nobles in this part of the world), and has teamwork buffs which are useful to the party. So they're roughly equal in overall power, even though Solars are best at straight competitions (like a fight).<br /> <br /> Is anyone here actually arguing against that?<br /> <br /> I think El Pinko Grande is worried that there will be nothing significant, interesting or distinctive about Solar fighters (which is most Solars they see), but I think we can all agree that you don't need to be able to kill 10 DBs by yourself to be those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T05:41:38-07:00","id":1386663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386522#post1386522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm dipping a bit far back in the conversation, but I have to say, this comment killed my enthusiasm for Exalted Essence stone dead. I <i>do</i> think that's injurious to the setting. Isn't one of the central themes of Exalted that Creation is going to shit precisely because the Solars have been missing? Why would that be the case if the Solars are scarcely more capable than the DBs that outnumber them 33 to 1? I'm assuming this comment is about a Fire Aspect and a Dawn Caste that are sitting at equal XP levels, of course- I have no problem with an experienced DB killing an inexperienced Solar, or a combat-focused DB killing a non-combat-focused Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue here is that &quot;scarcely more capable&quot; is not a viable metric. The Solar Exalted - and the accompanying Abyssal and Infernal Exalted, it should be noted - have capabilities to rapidly change the setting. It's just that those capabilities aren't simply outclassing and shutting down other Exalts, partly due to the Universal Charms and partly due to the scaling of Solar capability. Right now Dawns demolish whole armies like nobody's business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:03:53-07:00","id":1386692,"title":"","content":"Charms can be written such that a Solar fighter has a noticeable but not overwhelming advantage over a Dragon-Blooded fighter, while the Solar enjoys more advantages against armies and giants than the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Dragon-Blooded might enjoy more advantages when fighting together with other Exalted or similarly important/powerful allies. Advantages that would apply against a single Solar they're all fighting together, as well as against an army or a giant.<br /> <br /> <br /> Interestingly, this could lead to such a scenario:<br /> <br /> If you have a mixed party of a Solar fighter and two Dragon-Blooded fighters, and you are challenged by a Raksha lord accompanied by a fae dragon, the Solar fighter might fight the giant dragon by himself while the two Dragon-Blooded team up against the Raksha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:33:45-07:00","id":1386702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386644#post1386644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of a thing to point out too is that the return of the Solar Exalted isn't the only single problem in the world right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this whole post.<br /> <br /> I feel your post is the flipside of the coin from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386575#post1386575\">my own post in this thread</a> about how the banishment of the Solar Exalted wasn't the only reason for why the Second Age sucked so much even before the Empress disappeared and everything else started happening at once.<br /> <br /> Both sides of the coin are conducive to the idea that the Solar Exalted are really powerful and influential and important all on their own, but just on their own they're not actually such a huge deal that every story has to revolve around them.<br /> <br /> Just as not every story should revolve around ANY threat in Creation, like the Deathlords or the Autochthonians or the Yozi or the Fair Folk... and certainly none of these dooms should be written to be immediate threats that must be handled within a year Lest The World Shall End.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:52:38-07:00","id":1386764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378973#post1378973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. Aspects indicates that Dragon-Blooded and Liminals are elemental in character - they all possess all of their elements within them, they just lean towards one more than the others. Castes indicates role and purpose. I realize that's a distinction without a difference - it's basically saying there's really only one type of Liminal or Dragon-Blooded, sort of similar to saying how Sidereals don't have castes since they're each Chosen by a different Incarna.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1379007#post1379007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the easier criteria to understand and accept is that CHOICE is involved with Caste, and determinism is involved with Aspect.<br /> <br /> For Solar Exalted, the Sun chose you to be a Dawn, rather than any other Exaltation that might have been available.<br /> <br /> For Sidereals, a specific Maiden decided to Choose you.<br /> <br /> For Lunars, they choose their own Castes.<br /> <br /> For Alchemical Exalted, the people building them chose them and chose what Caste they would have.<br /> <br /> But there's no such choice involved with Dragon-Blooded; whoever takes the Second Breath is reborn with the Aspect of one of their Dragon-Blooded ancestors. It's automatic and deterministic, even if the determining mechanisms are so minute and finicky that possibly only the god who monitors Terrestrial Exalted could predict it.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Dark Mother doesn't get to choose what sort of Liminal she breathes into. Their Aspect is determined by the creator of their physical body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revisiting this.<br /> <br /> The other reason I offered an alternative explanation for the &quot;Caste / Aspect&quot; divide is because I didn't think &quot;possess all of their elements within them&quot; worked as an explanation.<br /> <br /> Each Sidereal Exaltation comes from one specific goddess the same way each Terrestrial Aspect comes from one specific dragon, yet each Sidereal contains the Essence of the four other Maidens as well. A Chosen of Battles can still learn the Charms of Secrets, Journeys, Serenity, and Endings, and even Favor them as much as the Charms of Battles.<br /> <br /> Alchemical Exalted are either made with a little of all six metals from the start, or they could end up incorporating all six through their Charms.<br /> <br /> Certainly, Solars and Lunars possess all of their &quot;elements&quot; within them, to whatever extent the Caste Abilities of the Dawn Caste are associated to &quot;Dawn&quot;, while a Dawn Caste could also learn and Favor areas of Solar magic associated with the other four Castes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, but CHOICE. Choice is what distinguishes the purposefulness of Castes against the serendipity of Aspect.<br /> <br /> While each Caste is associated with certain personalities, mostly they're associated with duties and responsibilities, with the potential for personalities which would normally be at odds with such roles.<br /> <br /> But Aspects reverse this. They are primarily about associated personalities, with roles and responsibilities arising organically from those.<br /> <br /> If Caste is top-down and deliberate, then Aspect is bottom-up and emergent.<br /> <br /> <br /> There was a faction of Raksha in Second Edition who were trying to become human -- or at least Creationborn -- by somehow plugging themselves into the reincarnation system. If they succeeded and ended up becoming a new form of Exalted in the process, they would be good candidates for Aspects rather than Castes. Perhaps the Aspects reflect the sort of Raksha they used to be, but while that Raksha was shaped by their choices, the reborn human didn't make those choices anymore than a Fire Aspect made choices for Hesiesh.<br /> <br /> <br /> I forget if Getimians are supposed to have Castes or Aspects, but you could make a case for either. They chose <i>how </i>they changed the worlds-that-never-were, so their Castes could arise from their choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T14:45:14-07:00","id":1386782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386764#post1386764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget if Getimians are supposed to have Castes or Aspects, but you could make a case for either. They chose <i>how </i>they changed the worlds-that-never-were, so their Castes could arise from their choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is precisely the case. Getimians have Castes, which are attributed based on their approach to changing the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Spring</b><br /> The Vernals are heroic dreamers, warrior poets, and guardians. They helped make their world beautiful \u2014 and now Creation will benefit from their bold vision.<br /> <br /> <b>Summer</b><br /> The Estivals are conquerors, mad prophets, and iconoclasts who upend the old orders. They come from worlds of upheaval, ready to shatter the old ways of Creation.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn</b><br /> The Autumnals are inspirational war-leaders, healers, and saviors. They come from worlds redeemed by their sacrifices; now they will redeem Creation, as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Winter</b><br /> The Hibernals are magicians, demiurges, and powerbrokers who transform society. They come from worlds made orderly and grand, with the strength of will to make whole what Creation has set asunder. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T22:18:15-07:00","id":1387418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1386522#post1386522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know I'm dipping a bit far back in the conversation, but I have to say, this comment killed my enthusiasm for Exalted Essence stone dead. I <i>do</i> think that's injurious to the setting. Isn't one of the central themes of Exalted that Creation is going to shit precisely because the Solars have been missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Scarlet Empress explicitly made things better for a while, and things went to shit because of the Great Contagion happening at the worst possible time. The central theme is &quot;things can go to shit if people in charge forget their humanity and succumb to hubris.&quot;<br /> <br /> And to all of you so upset that Solars only have a <i>surmountable </i>advantage: what about those of us who, I dunno, like to play Exalted other than Solars and would like to play them in a mixed game with Solars? Wouldn't being constantly upstaged by the guys with a sun disc be kind of unfun for us, for some strange 2E idea of &quot;Solaroids over all&quot; that doesn't even make sense in the backstory, given the Usurpation happened?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T14:17:56-07:00","id":1387589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1387418#post1387418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. The Scarlet Empress explicitly made things better for a while, and things went to shit because of the Great Contagion happening at the worst possible time. The central theme is &quot;things can go to shit if people in charge forget their humanity and succumb to hubris.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Empress was after the Contagion. Also, her efforts even then were blind in application; Scavenger Sons (which is still a relevant source for 3e) noted that the act of using the Imperial Manse was impersonal and often inflicted massive amounts of damage on locations far away from the Blessed Isle, such that the Scavenger Lands didn't feel particularly grateful for being &quot;saved&quot;, and justifiably so. It's a hell of a thing when you start out your rule with hubris and just build from there.<br /> <br /> Solars have a legacy of wonders built across Creation - sometimes including portions of Creation - and those things aren't practically kept up by others' efforts. So, on some level, the Solars are required to have setting bits not go to shit, but that's the genre-breaking stuff that fits on top of the basic swords and sorcery world. If you want the flying machines and automatons to last for more than a few more centuries at best, and you want to restore them to what they were before they began to slide into ruin, then yes, Solars are quite necessary. If you prefer a swords and sandals experience, then they are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T14:47:20-07:00","id":1387812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">I think I'll just go ahead and confirm that the only difference between Withering and decisive is the way they interact with damage (and some Charms)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I'm sure you can guess that decisive is the way you do health levels of damage</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">That's not even a spoiler that's just 3e rules lol</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You know how default withering attacks damage intitative? It's like that still, but using a slightly different resource</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T19:03:43-07:00","id":1387862,"title":"","content":"If withering attacks damage/steal a different resource than Initiative, I don't have a clue what that might be.<br /> <br /> Obviously not Health, and likely not motes or Willpower.<br /> <br /> Unless it is Motes, and Motes work VERY differently from before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T22:21:31-07:00","id":1387907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1387862#post1387862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If withering attacks damage/steal a different resource than Initiative, I don't have a clue what that might be.<br /> <br /> Obviously not Health, and likely not motes or Willpower.<br /> <br /> Unless it is Motes, and Motes work VERY differently from before.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what the devs are saying it's a rework of initiative, not a change from initiative to a completely different resource :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't assume it's gone it just looks different<br /> We made it wear a different hat and use smaller numbers lol</div> </div> </div> </div>So maybe now it's called momentum/advantage/lead or something like that, and maybe now it swings between 0 &amp; 20 instead of between -30 &amp; 70. That sort of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T00:48:04-07:00","id":1387947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1387907#post1387907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what the devs are saying it's a rework of initiative, not a change from initiative to a completely different resource :<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So maybe now it's called momentum/advantage/lead or something like that, and maybe now it swings between 0 &amp; 20 instead of between -30 &amp; 70. That sort of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could call it Bravery <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:26:31-07:00","id":1387959,"title":"","content":"I think they have decoupled initiative you get from attacks from turn order. So it'll have a different name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:34:55-07:00","id":1387962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1387959#post1387959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they have decoupled initiative you get from attacks from turn order. So it'll have a different name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh so the moment you act isn't tied to your damage pool ? Not necessarily a bad choice. I'm curious to see to what extent Essence combat system can be used instead of the Exalted 3e core combat system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:44:43-07:00","id":1387966,"title":"","content":"That's just a guess. Could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:57:11-07:00","id":1388030,"title":"","content":"My ideal would be basically Initiative, affecting turn order and all, but with smaller numbers and smaller swings, and with the relative importance of Damage and Accuracy rebalanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T07:04:09-07:00","id":1388035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1388030#post1388030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ideal would be basically Initiative, affecting turn order and all, but with smaller numbers and smaller swings, and with the relative importance of Damage and Accuracy rebalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I still can't figure my head around is the fact that, except with specific Charms, there is 0 account for the defensive ability of the party receiving a Decisive blow on turn 1, except solely the ability to not get hit by the attack. I don't know if it's good or bad, but I really feel like it's sort of dissonant with everything else in the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T03:06:59-07:00","id":1389228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1388030#post1388030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ideal would be basically Initiative, affecting turn order and all, but with smaller numbers and smaller swings, and with the relative importance of Damage and Accuracy rebalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I should say, someone said &quot;I think they've decoupled turn order from initiative, and also reduced the numbers for Withering&quot; and Monica said &quot;you're half right, I'm not saying which half.&quot;<br /> <br /> So maybe it's that.<br /> <br /> I actually find very low numbers with Withering dull, but I guess big numbers can be very swingy. I'm fine with them reducing damage if they also reduce soak from armour/etc, so you don't get one PC with soak 2 and another with soak 15, and then they're both hit with a 13-damage dice attack, which is hugely different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T03:31:35-07:00","id":1389232,"title":"","content":"So in Essence attributes are being condensed. Monica said &quot;Dexterity is not a god stat. Or even a thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, we will not see Getimians' attributes in Essence. I assume this is because the attributes are so different.<br /> <br /> Neall said &quot;Monica has come up with a truly elegant way to represent Attribute Exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> So here's a couple of radical theories:<br /> A)There's only 3-5 attributes.*<br /> B)Attribute Exalted are radically different. But they are not ability exalts.**<br /> <br /> <br /> *(I'd suggest 3-6, but if there was 6 I think you'd still do Attribute Exalted the same way as usual, just reduced a bit. Ie Full Moons choose 2 favoured attributes, 1 of which must be Brawn or Agility. Jade Castes choose 2 favoured attributes, one of which must be Brawn or Charisma. Winter Caste choose 2 favoured attributes, 1 of which must be Manipulation or Cunning. Etc. And I don't really see the point of reducing attributes to 7 or 8.)<br /> <br /> **So my first thought was they were just all Ability exalts now. You know, Full Moons get Athletics, Brawl, Dodge, Resistance, Survival. But I don't think it is that, simply because I would not really describe that as truly elegant! There'd be a lot of debate over what abilities to give them.<br /> <br /> So, I think in some ways it's easy to do Attribute-based stuff. Excellencies are easy (you get less but they apply to attributes rather than abilities). Character gen is easy, giving them more dots of attributes and less abilities (not what 3rd ed did with Lunars, but what previous eds did). Their own unique charms are fine, because you just put them in attribute trees.<br /> The hard bit is buying Universal charms (and this would apply even if the attributes were the same). What stat do you need to buy that Survival charm that is about resisting environmental damage? Stamina. But then that other Survival charm for making friends with animals isn't Stamina. Keywords? Seems awkward.<br /> You could of course have every single charm have prerequisites like &quot;Resistance 3/Stamina 3&quot;. Then it's mostly just awkward in terms of book layout. (With a lot less charm trees, it's not really so awkward that half the Survival charms are Stamina and the other are Wits or whatever.)<br /> <br /> Here's something else: Does Essence have favoured charms at all? If not, how does it Dawnify your Dawn? Because if it instead gives you bonus abilities or charms at character gen, say, then it'd be easy to instead say &quot;Full Moons get +1 to their Physical Attribute&quot; or some such. Though that might apply better to Lunars than Alchemicals, Liminals, etc.<br /> <br /> Discuss!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-17-2020, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T04:23:11-07:00","id":1389242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389228#post1389228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually find very low numbers with Withering dull, but I guess big numbers can be very swingy. I'm fine with them reducing damage if they also reduce soak from armour/etc, so you don't get one PC with soak 2 and another with soak 15, and then they're both hit with a 13-damage dice attack, which is hugely different.</div> </div> </div> </div> If withering damage still affects Initiative, but the associated numbers are reduced, it obviously follows that the significance of those numbers would increase to match. What would even be the point of changing one thing and then not dealing with any of the knock-on effects?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T04:31:03-07:00","id":1389245,"title":"","content":"I really hope that they will have a finished draft for this when the KS goes live. This time around I want to see what I get before commiting big amounts of money to it. Although after all that has been said here, I'm sadly not sure that I'm the target audience for this kind of &quot;light&quot; Exalted version <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But I'll take a look if KS pledges get you a draft and you can unpledge if you don't like what you see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25439-mnemon-liranan","name":"Mnemon Liranan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T04:33:42-07:00","id":1389246,"title":"","content":"All the previous kickstarters have had a finished draft. Though I don't think they let you uncommit if you don't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T04:47:06-07:00","id":1389247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389246#post1389246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the previous kickstarters have had a finished draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they didn't. The Corebook didn't even have any serious snippets of the product.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389246#post1389246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I don't think they let you uncommit if you don't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's normally a KS thing. You can cancel your pledge until the last moment of the duration of the KS. So I don't think OPP can change that. So if they have a draft, I'll probably pledge to see if I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25439-mnemon-liranan","name":"Mnemon Liranan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T04:58:00-07:00","id":1389253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389232#post1389232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in Essence attributes are being condensed. Monica said &quot;Dexterity is not a god stat. Or even a thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, we will not see Getimians' attributes in Essence. I assume this is because the attributes are so different.<br /> <br /> Neall said &quot;Monica has come up with a truly elegant way to represent Attribute Exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> So here's a couple of radical theories:<br /> A)There's only 3-5 attributes.*<br /> B)Attribute Exalted are radically different. But they are not ability exalts.**<br /> <br /> <br /> *(I'd suggest 3-6, but if there was 6 I think you'd still do Attribute Exalted the same way as usual, just reduced a bit. Ie Full Moons choose 2 favoured attributes, 1 of which must be Brawn or Agility. Jade Castes choose 2 favoured attributes, one of which must be Brawn or Charisma. Winter Caste choose 2 favoured attributes, 1 of which must be Manipulation or Cunning. Etc. And I don't really see the point of reducing attributes to 7 or 8.)<br /> <br /> **So my first thought was they were just all Ability exalts now. You know, Full Moons get Athletics, Brawl, Dodge, Resistance, Survival. But I don't think it is that, simply because I would not really describe that as truly elegant! There'd be a lot of debate over what abilities to give them.<br /> <br /> So, I think in some ways it's easy to do Attribute-based stuff. Excellencies are easy (you get less but they apply to attributes rather than abilities). Character gen is easy, giving them more dots of attributes and less abilities (not what 3rd ed did with Lunars, but what previous eds did). Their own unique charms are fine, because you just put them in attribute trees.<br /> The hard bit is buying Universal charms (and this would apply even if the attributes were the same). What stat do you need to buy that Survival charm that is about resisting environmental damage? Stamina. But then that other Survival charm for making friends with animals isn't Stamina. Keywords? Seems awkward.<br /> You could of course have every single charm have prerequisites like &quot;Resistance 3/Stamina 3&quot;. Then it's mostly just awkward in terms of book layout. (With a lot less charm trees, it's not really so awkward that half the Survival charms are Stamina and the other are Wits or whatever.)<br /> <br /> Here's something else: Does Essence have favoured charms at all? If not, how does it Dawnify your Dawn? Because if it instead gives you bonus abilities or charms at character gen, say, then it'd be easy to instead say &quot;Full Moons get +1 to their Physical Attribute&quot; or some such. Though that might apply better to Lunars than Alchemicals, Liminals, etc.<br /> <br /> Discuss!</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's some crazy speculation based on definitely not enough data :<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes/Abilities wild speculation:</b><br /> -There are 5 Attributes, one for each of the 5 Solar Archetypes (so Dawniness, Zenithness, Twilightiness, Nightiness and Eclipseness, though obviously with better names)<br /> <br /> -Each Ability is tied to 1 and only 1 Attribute, so e.g. Melee is always associated with the Dawn's Attribute and Craft is always associated with the Twilight Attribtue. The reshuffling of Abilities in Essence helps with this by redefining or separating Abilities which would be ambiguous right now in Core.<br /> <br /> -Therefore, even though everyone is treated as Ability-based in Essence (per word of dev), it's clear which Attribute you'd need as an Attribute Exalt to buy Charms in a given Ability (for instance, if a Charm requires 2 dots of Melee, then you know an Attribute-based Exalt could buy it with 2 dots of &quot;Dawn&quot;). Hence the dev comment that Attribute Exalts can be turned on and off &quot;like a switch&quot; in Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal wild speculation:</b><br /> -Your &quot;Supernal&quot; is an Attribute you pick among the 5 Attributes. Your Supernal determines your &quot;archetype&quot; in the player group (so someone picks the warrior attribute, someone else picks the scholar attribute, etc.). That way everyone's role is clearly established from the start.<br /> <br /> -Some Castes and Aspects are only associated with 1 Archetype so people will always pick the same Supernal for them (e.g. almost all Dawn players will Supernal the Dawn Attribute since it's the obvious choice). Others Castes/Aspects are more Ambiguous, so e.g. a Changing Moon might want to Supernal their Zenith-Attribute, their Night-Attribute or their Eclipse-Attribute.<br /> <br /> -Even with all that speculation it's not obvious to me what the benefit of Supernal will be. We know Supernal in Essence will work differently from Supernal in Core, but beyond that it could be anything. Maybe it simply tells you which Abilities you favor for Charm costs?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T05:00:36-07:00","id":1389255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mnemon Liranan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389247#post1389247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they didn't. The Corebook didn't even have any serious snippets of the product..</div> </div> </div> </div>Early 3e was a mess, they changed up the dev team and have been doing better since. Every KS since then has had a manuscript preview.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:25:46-07:00","id":1389290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mnemon Liranan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389247#post1389247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they didn't. The Corebook didn't even have any serious snippets of the product.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I should have said the current developers (who took over after the Core and Miracles) have had a draft for each Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's normally a KS thing. You can cancel your pledge until the last moment of the duration of the KS. So I don't think OPP can change that. So if they have a draft, I'll probably pledge to see if I like it. </div> </div> </div>Ah, sure. In the previous kickstarters, they've released the draft a quarter at a time per week.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T10:45:50-07:00","id":1389358,"title":"","content":"Having a draft for Kickstarters now is, to the best of my knowledge, official Onyx Path policy, specifically because of the uproar surrounding the Ex3 core KS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T11:09:29-07:00","id":1389365,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they know that did not go down well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T11:54:02-07:00","id":1389388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389358#post1389358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a draft for Kickstarters now is, to the best of my knowledge, official Onyx Path policy, specifically because of the uproar surrounding the Ex3 core KS.</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been exceptions, such as Dark Eras 2, but I think that was at least partly because the KS involved deciding what would go in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:26:10-07:00","id":1389412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389255#post1389255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early 3e was a mess, they changed up the dev team and have been doing better since. Every KS since then has had a manuscript preview.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is less Exalted itself and more early OPP KS in general. <b>Mummy: the Curse</b> and I think a couple other books didn't either and had similar issues. A lot of also what delayed and made some things weird in the Exalted corebook were things like backer rewards (which they dind't know if they were even getting) being put in the corebook, rather than a companion like later KSes do.<br /> <br /> Like for some fun context,the Trinity Continuum and Scion 2e cores were supposed to also releas ein 2013, but didn't come out until a few years later. Likely the issues with Exalted kind of pathfound that issue, for better or worse I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:56:53-07:00","id":1389423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389412#post1389412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is less Exalted itself and more early OPP KS in general. <b>Mummy: the Curse</b> and I think a couple other books didn't either and had similar issues. A lot of also what delayed and made some things weird in the Exalted corebook were things like backer rewards (which they dind't know if they were even getting) being put in the corebook, rather than a companion like later KSes do.<br /> <br /> Like for some fun context,the Trinity Continuum and Scion 2e cores were supposed to also releas ein 2013, but didn't come out until a few years later. Likely the issues with Exalted kind of pathfound that issue, for better or worse I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>the main thing that delayed the Core book was the fact that it clearly wasn\u2019t really written yet despite what the old devs were saying at the time, and then both system redesigns and real life got in the way of getting it done. Now OPP always has full draft text to share in kickstarters. There are edits of course, and then there\u2019s formatting and art to do, but they have the work to show us so we know it\u2019s real and well underway, and you can even start using it at your table immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:59:14-07:00","id":1389424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389246#post1389246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the previous kickstarters have had a finished draft. Though I don't think they let you uncommit if you don't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>of course they do! OPP eagerly encourages people to make nominal backing to check the draft out and pull out if they don\u2019t like it. Even if they didn\u2019t want to do that, it\u2019s not like they could change how Kickstarter works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:34:40-07:00","id":1389441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389423#post1389423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the main thing that delayed the Core book was the fact that it clearly wasn\u2019t really written yet despite what the old devs were saying at the time, and then both system redesigns and real life got in the way of getting it done. Now OPP always has full draft text to share in kickstarters. There are edits of course, and then there\u2019s formatting and art to do, but they have the work to show us so we know it\u2019s real and well underway, and you can even start using it at your table immediately.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also spent like a year in layout/art. Thing had a whole cascade going on on things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T15:14:57-07:00","id":1389474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389232#post1389232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Essence have favoured charms at all? If not, how does it Dawnify your Dawn? Because if it instead gives you bonus abilities or charms at character gen, say, then it'd be easy to instead say &quot;Full Moons get +1 to their Physical Attribute&quot; or some such. Though that might apply better to Lunars than Alchemicals, Liminals, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why Essence would need to drop Caste/Favored Abilities, but if it did, Caste-specific anima powers could be enough to distinguish a Dawn from other Solars.<br /> <br /> Heck, right now in Third Edition, other Solars can't get anything like Dawn Caste anima powers without using artifacts or sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389253#post1389253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Attributes/Abilities wild speculation:</b><br /> -There are 5 Attributes, one for each of the 5 Solar Archetypes (so Dawniness, Zenithness, Twilightiness, Nightiness and Eclipseness, though obviously with better names)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what?<br /> <br /> Strength for Dawns, Stamina for Zeniths, Intelligence for Twilights, Perception or Wits for Nights, and Charisma for Eclipses?<br /> <br /> It would just be easier to have Strength, Intelligence, and Charisma, and have none of them associated with a Caste. Each Caste has their own uses for each Attribute, what with Dawns being generals, Zeniths being public figures, and Eclipses needing to figure out air-tight legal documents.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Therefore, even though everyone is treated as Ability-based in Essence (per word of dev), it's clear which Attribute you'd need as an Attribute Exalt to buy Charms in a given Ability (for instance, if a Charm requires 2 dots of Melee, then you know an Attribute-based Exalt could buy it with 2 dots of &quot;Dawn&quot;). Hence the dev comment that Attribute Exalts can be turned on and off &quot;like a switch&quot; in Essence. </div> </div> </div>If the relationship between Attributes and Abilities is so one-to-one, why even have Attributes at all?<br /> <br /> You could just assume that whatever muscle groups you use to swing your sword are developed as part of your Melee Ability, and that those muscle groups are generally not the ones you need for Athletics. Which is pretty much how reality works, anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Supernal wild speculation:</b><br /> -Your &quot;Supernal&quot; is an Attribute you pick among the 5 Attributes. </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure we're told that Supernals don't exist in Essence, and that the Solar Exalt Advantages more than cover the essential concept of &quot;Master of Abilities&quot; and &quot;First Among Equals&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T15:53:59-07:00","id":1389482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't remember Mummy the Curse really having that issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least for me, a good chunk of the kind of blow-back I felt towards the book was that we were told it would be really cool, were hyped on it, and we didn't really get to see it until the book itself came, and we found there was a lot of issues with the corebook. I think it, Wraith 20Ae, and Exalted 3e were kind of the causes themselves of a lot of the ways OPP has done future KS, including <b>Demon if I remember</b>beng the first one with a manuscrit review.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T21:40:25-07:00","id":1389562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that might be a you thing, and not a that kickstarter thing in this particular case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not speaking just on experience. There is a lot of stuff I have read over the eyars about the game being unclear, poorly explained on what you do, and a lot of feeling I saw of folks feeling they in effect got a product based on promsies it failed to deliver. <b>Mummy: the Curse</b> was the first product OPP did that was a new property, not a 20th Annviersary corebook (Werewolf) or a sourcebook for an existing line (V20). Exalted 3e was the next after that, and solicitation material implied that year both Scion 2e and Trinity Continuum 2e were slated for that year.<br /> <br /> This didn't happen, they spread out their KSes a bit, including not doing them for CofD Vmapire, Wereowlf, and Mage 2e. And the next new KS property, <b>Demon: the Descent</b>, <i>did</i>the manuscript. This was done on a couple sourcebooks beforehand (<i>Hunters Hunted II</i>, <i>Changing Breeds</i>), but this was the first time for a new corebook. Mummy didn't do it. Exlated didn't do it and suffered dearly for it. Scion and Trinity didn't KS that year because they were not able to likely meet that new standard (and didn't, both didn't KS until 2016 and 2017 respectively)<br /> <br /> There were other things too that Exalted learned from that ended up in future KSes. Like the use of Companions for additional KS stretch goals, rather than trying to fit htem in the core book. This probably wouldn't have helped Ex3 too much in specific, but it would help later books down th eline in splitting things up a bit between multiple projects.<br /> <br /> Like, not saying Exalted's KS was flawless, far from it. And I think a lack of open manuscript like other properites, probably due to being KS'd to early, did a lot to hurt it. But it is not the only troubled item OPP had. Wraith took 3 years as well (funded in January 2015, didn't get to backers until February 2018), and seems to ahve had a lot of the same issues with layout bottlenecks and staff isuess Exalted did. That we got a year-about turn-around on DBs and Lunars now, and similar with both Trinity and Scion in the last coupl eyears, kidn fo shows they have htier shit figured out compared to in 2013.<br /> <br /> But like, saying that Exalted 3e was th eonly one to have such issues and tha tonly the devs were the reaosns for all of those issues feels like a bit of an act of scapegoating I guess. Again, not to say they couldn' thave done a lot better. Just that I don't think it's as simple as two guys not doing the management thing well, just a part of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T22:54:55-07:00","id":1389573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389474#post1389474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what?<br /> <br /> Strength for Dawns, Stamina for Zeniths, Intelligence for Twilights, Perception or Wits for Nights, and Charisma for Eclipses?<br /> <br /> It would just be easier to have Strength, Intelligence, and Charisma, and have none of them associated with a Caste. Each Caste has their own uses for each Attribute, what with Dawns being generals, Zeniths being public figures, and Eclipses needing to figure out air-tight legal documents.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 5 would be Fighting, Magnetism, Scholarship, Stealth, Embassy. I like your idea of Strenght/Intel/Charisma, but I'd be surprised if they reduced the number of attributes this drastically.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389474#post1389474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the relationship between Attributes and Abilities is so one-to-one, why even have Attributes at all?<br /> <br /> You could just assume that whatever muscle groups you use to swing your sword are developed as part of your Melee Ability, and that those muscle groups are generally not the ones you need for Athletics. Which is pretty much how reality works, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. I was looking at how to make Attribute Exalts simple and toggleable like a switch and went from there, but it's true this might make Attributes and Abilities redundant with each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389474#post1389474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure we're told that Supernals don't exist in Essence, and that the Solar Exalt Advantages more than cover the essential concept of &quot;Master of Abilities&quot; and &quot;First Among Equals&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're told that Supernal does exist, but it's a different beast from what it is in Core :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Supernal&quot; isn't quite the same thing in Essence. It's there, but it's taking a slightly different form - because it's tied directly into your Anima powers.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Melee Supernals don't exist in Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:22:04-07:00","id":1389658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389253#post1389253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's some crazy speculation based on definitely not enough data :<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes/Abilities wild speculation:</b><br /> -There are 5 Attributes, one for each of the 5 Solar Archetypes (so Dawniness, Zenithness, Twilightiness, Nightiness and Eclipseness, though obviously with better names)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Too based around one of the 10 different splats... but I do like the wild speculation!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Each Ability is tied to 1 and only 1 Attribute, so e.g. Melee is always associated with the Dawn's Attribute and Craft is always associated with the Twilight Attribtue. The reshuffling of Abilities in Essence helps with this by redefining or separating Abilities which would be ambiguous right now in Core. </div> </div> </div>At this point, having Attributes at all is a waste of time. Storyteller has good and bad points, but IMO being able to have people make a Perception+Melee or Stamina+Performance or Charisma+Sail roll when appropriate, is a good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:26:18-07:00","id":1389659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389253#post1389253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Therefore, even though everyone is treated as Ability-based in Essence (per word of dev)<br /> ..<br /> Hence the dev comment that Attribute Exalts can be turned on and off &quot;like a switch&quot; in Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Links? The second is vaguely familiar. Are they from Discord?<br /> <br /> On Supernal... honestly, I think there's loads of ways you can get people to be extra-good at one ability, and make that the defining part of their character.<br /> <br /> It could range from the simple (you get precisely 1 Ability at 5 at character gen) to reduced cost to free starting charms in it to something similar to how it works in 3e.<br /> <br /> I think it's interesting that Supernal is not one of the two Solar Advantages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:34:01-07:00","id":1389662,"title":"","content":"Hmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm.............<br /> <br /> So there's this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Supernal&quot; isn't quite the same thing in Essence. It's there, but it's taking a slightly different form - because it's tied directly into your Anima powers.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Melee Supernals don't exist in Essence. </div> </div> </div>So the second of this I reckon is not that you can't take Melee as supernal per-se, but rather that there's no Melee skill. As they wanted to reduce the number of Abilities, I suspect there's now a Close Combat-type ability that covers Melee and Brawl. This makes it easier to throw in simplified Martial Arts: MA isn't a seperate ability in Essence, it's just charms that modify your combat ability for appropriate weapons. So combining Melee/Brawl makes it simpler to use Snake charms to enhance your fist or your seven-section staff or your hook sword, as they're all with the same ability.<br /> <br /> The first one, being tied directly into your anima powers... Now that's interesting. Any ideas? Maybe when you're at full power you get a bonus with your Supernal ability (Monica did seem keen on your Anima powering you up), or even a range of Caste abilities?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:35:30-07:00","id":1389663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389573#post1389573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 5 would be Fighting, Magnetism, Scholarship, Stealth, Embassy. I like your idea of Strenght/Intel/Charisma, but I'd be surprised if they reduced the number of attributes this drastically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think, if you're simplifying the game, then 3 attributes is an easy and simple way to do it. No need to wonder &quot;is this Charisma or Manipulation? Intelligence or Wits?&quot; Because if it's Body/Face/Mind it's pretty easy to decide.<br /> <br /> Not saying they will, just that it won't surprise me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:37:05-07:00","id":1389664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389662#post1389662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm.............<br /> <br /> So there's this.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the second of this I reckon is not that you can't take Melee as supernal per-se, but rather that there's no Melee skill. As they wanted to reduce the number of Abilities, I suspect there's now a Close Combat-type ability that covers Melee and Brawl. This makes it easier to throw in simplified Martial Arts: MA isn't a seperate ability in Essence, it's just charms that modify your combat ability for appropriate weapons. So combining Melee/Brawl makes it simpler to use Snake charms to enhance your fist or your seven-section staff or your hook sword, as they're all with the same ability.<br /> <br /> The first one, being tied directly into your anima powers... Now that's interesting. Any ideas? Maybe when you're at full power you get a bonus with your Supernal ability (Monica did seem keen on your Anima powering you up), or even a range of Caste abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah would make sense to have a unified anima power that adapts depending on your supernal. I'm not sure it's when your anima-banner related though, or they have an idea to make certain abilities work differently (stealth, larceny)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:37:37-07:00","id":1389665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389474#post1389474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why Essence would need to drop Caste/Favored Abilities, but if it did, Caste-specific anima powers could be enough to distinguish a Dawn from other Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, though I guess you might want to rethink them with that in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T09:15:30-07:00","id":1389678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389659#post1389659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Links? The second is vaguely familiar. Are they from Discord?<br /> <br /> On Supernal... honestly, I think there's loads of ways you can get people to be extra-good at one ability, and make that the defining part of their character.<br /> <br /> It could range from the simple (you get precisely 1 Ability at 5 at character gen) to reduced cost to free starting charms in it to something similar to how it works in 3e.<br /> <br /> I think it's interesting that Supernal is not one of the two Solar Advantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, all Discord. Here's some quotes :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monica came up with a truly elegant way of representing Attribute Exalts<br /> <br /> But one that is literally easy to flip on or off like a switch</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, it seems I misremembered one of the quotes - the devs didn't say that everyone was Ability based, but rather that being Attribute based doesn't mean much in Essence:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, [Getimians] are Attribute Exalts, but that doesn't mean much in Essence's paradigm</div> </div> </div> </div>Some more quotes on Supernal being related to your Caste powers :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Supernal&quot; isn't quite the same thing in Essence. It's there, but it's taking a slightly different form - because it's tied directly into your Anima powers.<br /> <br /> now before you lose your minds over this: we've designed all Castes to shape what they're supposed to be really good at and encourage you to play in that space.<br /> This is so newbies can go &quot;I wanna be a fighty guy!&quot; and then know to immediately go pick up a Dawn or a Full Moon, or a Dusk, etc etc etc</div> </div> </div> </div>About anima powers :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do break things down into the &quot;classic five&quot; archetypes, with the caveat that not all of them fit neatly<br /> <br /> You can still be Dex Full Moon if you want to, but the real thing there is that you tend to slam into your problems with a lot of fury and power</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Supernal and anima powers are being discussed mostly together I'm assuming all Exalts get a &quot;Supernal&quot;, whatever Supernal is in Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T09:42:26-07:00","id":1389682,"title":"","content":"Oh about Embassy being a thing (the bolding is in the original quote):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that Essence supports [political ambitions such as &quot;Topple the realm&quot;]: using <b>Embassy </b>to make that kind of politicking happen.<br /> Especially if you're the Eclipse or other diplomat type character :smirk:</div> </div> </div> </div>which, along with all the other quotes, is how I ended up with a theory that Embassy is an Attribute which you can Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T10:29:47-07:00","id":1389693,"title":"","content":"I do expect Embassy to be, well, something. But it could well be an Ability. Which can be supernal for Eclipses.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T10:33:06-07:00","id":1389695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389678#post1389678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Supernal and anima powers are being discussed mostly together I'm assuming all Exalts get a &quot;Supernal&quot;, whatever Supernal is in Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would explain why Supernal isn't a Solar Advantage, certainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T11:44:08-07:00","id":1389713,"title":"","content":"Infernal having Supernals would be funny, since those words mean literally the opposite things.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf Below / Inferior\u201d versus \u201cOf Above / Superior\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T12:08:15-07:00","id":1389720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389695#post1389695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would explain why Supernal isn't a Solar Advantage, certainly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it is isn't it? Supernal Ability is the name of their &quot;Free Excellencies&quot; Solar Exalted Advantage, along wiht First Among Equals. Or at least something to that name/effect.<br /> <br /> My guess why there's nto Supernal-like-in-3e is in part just becuase there are other ays to achieve things, and as I understand it, Charms and their relations to Abiliteis at all might not be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T13:06:29-07:00","id":1389736,"title":"","content":"Oh was it? Well that's that then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T13:19:24-07:00","id":1389738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389693#post1389693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do expect Embassy to be, well, something. But it could well be an Ability. Which can be supernal for Eclipses.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an Ability, I guess it could be the fusion of Bureaucracy &amp; Socialize, and maybe Linguistics too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T13:33:26-07:00","id":1389741,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and those are the sort of abilities I expect to be merged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T13:43:59-07:00","id":1389744,"title":"","content":"I tried merging the Abilities as an exercise to see what Essence Abilities might look like, here's what I got :<br /> <br /> <b>Athletics </b>- Athletics, Dodge, Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Embassy </b>- Bureaucracy, Linguistics, Socialize<br /> <br /> <b>Fighting </b>- Archery, Brawl, Martial Arts, Melee, Thrown<br /> <br /> <b>Focus </b>- Awareness, Investigation, Integrity<br /> <br /> <b>Magnetism </b>- Presence, Performance, War<br /> <br /> <b>Stealth </b>- Larceny, Stealth<br /> <br /> <b>Scholarship </b>- Craft, Lore, Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> <b>Travel </b>- Ride, Sail, Survival<br /> <br /> War and Integrity in particular I'm not certain about, but the rest seem to fit together well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T13:52:02-07:00","id":1389745,"title":"","content":"I expect they won't reduce them that much, maybe to 15. Maybe 10. I expect a number divisible by 5.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T17:06:04-07:00","id":1389788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389720#post1389720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it is isn't it? Supernal Ability is the name of their &quot;Free Excellencies&quot; Solar Exalted Advantage, along wiht First Among Equals. Or at least something to that name/effect.<br /> <br /> My guess why there's nto Supernal-like-in-3e is in part just becuase there are other ays to achieve things, and as I understand it, Charms and their relations to Abiliteis at all might not be the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the name of the Free Excellencies Master of [something]? Master of Ability? Or... Technically it's called &quot;Supremacy of Ability&quot; looking at the backscroll.<br /> <br /> Which sounds a bit similar to Supernal Ability but I dunno if I'd call them the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T17:10:34-07:00","id":1389790,"title":"","content":"Getting below 15 feels like you'd risk making things too abstract for something that's supposed to be a simplified version of 3e. I mean, my 15 would be:<br /> <br /> Athletics - Dodge merged in, maybe some Stealth added.<br /> Awareness - Some Investigation added<br /> Bureaucracy - Some Linguistics, and Lore added<br /> Craft - One ability, not many, some Lore added<br /> Integrity<br /> Larceny - Larceny, Stealth, and some Investigation<br /> Marksmanship - Archery and Thrown<br /> Medicine - Some Lore added<br /> Melee - Melee and Brawl<br /> Occult - Some Lore added, and Occult<br /> Presence - Presence and Performance<br /> Resistance - Some Survival added<br /> Socialize - Some Linguistics added<br /> Travel - Ride, Sail, some Survival added<br /> War - Some Lore added (I know, weird, but I like the idea of spreading out the &quot;establish facts&quot; out a bit and this would cover it for combat, also some influence from older DB Charms).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:51:16-07:00","id":1389920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389744#post1389744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Athletics </b>- Athletics, Dodge, Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Embassy </b>- Bureaucracy, Linguistics, Socialize<br /> <br /> <b>Fighting </b>- Archery, Brawl, Martial Arts, Melee, Thrown<br /> <br /> <b>Focus </b>- Awareness, Investigation, Integrity<br /> <br /> <b>Magnetism </b>- Presence, Performance, War<br /> <br /> <b>Stealth </b>- Larceny, Stealth<br /> <br /> <b>Scholarship </b>- Craft, Lore, Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> <b>Travel </b>- Ride, Sail, Survival<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dig your merging. This would totally be my Stats list in an Exalted PbtA hack (or something along those lines) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25439-mnemon-liranan","name":"Mnemon Liranan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T04:05:23-07:00","id":1389928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1389788#post1389788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't the name of the Free Excellencies Master of [something]? Master of Ability? Or... Technically it's called &quot;Supremacy of Ability&quot; looking at the backscroll.<br /> <br /> Which sounds a bit similar to Supernal Ability but I dunno if I'd call them the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they did say it'd be a bit different. I can see it. It's &quot;your Solar swordsman is just better than a Dragonblood swordsman&quot;, but rather than it being that he's got E4 charms and the Dragonblood has E2, it's that he's throwing down a free excellency. And of course he also has free excellencies for other things, but it's most obvious in the one he has at the highest rating, assuming of course that excellencies are somehow Ability-based (they may not be).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I really like the free excellency because it cuts down on book-keeping. Assuming, of course, that it's balanced. There is the oddity of &quot;why not just give them more stats&quot; but oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T04:28:20-07:00","id":1389934,"title":"","content":"So on &quot;turning attribute-exalted on and off like a switch&quot;, my assumption here is that basically the difference between Attribute and Ability exalted is really simple. So you have to change very little design.<br /> <br /> Ie your Attribute-based Exigent is no harder to design than an Ability-based Exalt.<br /> <br /> So I'm wondering... what if it's just that dice caps are Ability-based for some Exalts and Attribute-based for others, but maybe they have to pay more for excellencies or something.<br /> <br /> That would lead me to ask about universal charms though. And their prerequisites. Because obviously that's the complex bit.<br /> <br /> (Hmmm... do they even necessarily have prerequisites? I'd say 3e's prerequisites are generally not a good thing, because they're too high. For Solars anyway. They're fine for Lunars, but that's quite a different base. Still, would not having prerequisites be way too weird?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T09:04:23-07:00","id":1391199,"title":"","content":"Something that's going to be interesting to see.<br /> Abyssals and Infernals have this habit of recontextualising Solars, while the core tries to avoid framing the Solar Exalted as the good guys to the point where some consider them a little too vanilla. The introduction of concepts like Abyssal Redemption pulls them violently in that direction, even discussion of their corrupted Solar Castes starts walling off character concepts - it's going to be interesting to see what happens when all 3 are playable at the same time even if Abyssals and Infernals avoid <b>&quot;these are the worst people in the world!&quot;</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T11:26:42-07:00","id":1391219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1391199#post1391199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that's going to be interesting to see.<br /> Abyssals and Infernals have this habit of recontextualising Solars, while the core tries to avoid framing the Solar Exalted as the good guys to the point where some consider them a little too vanilla. The introduction of concepts like Abyssal Redemption pulls them violently in that direction, even discussion of their corrupted Solar Castes starts walling off character concepts - it's going to be interesting to see what happens when all 3 are playable at the same time even if Abyssals and Infernals avoid <b>&quot;these are the worst people in the world!&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Abyssal and Infernal Exaltations are altered Solar ones, and that is inherently negative also kind of plays a bit on folks having a bit of a naturalist bias. That is saying, they kind of tend to think the natural thing or something in its natural state is the &quot;way it shoudl be.&quot; That Abyssal and Infernal Exaltation aren't the Exaltations are &quot;god intended it&quot; creates a bit of that narrative, and I think it fed a bit into the way the Exaltations were presented in previous editoins.<br /> <br /> I will say in context of 3e, this is soemthing I'm also curious how it's gone at. Since I thinka big thingw tih DBs and Lunars to me, at least in 3e, is how little it talked about Solars to define themselves, and I owuld suspect that sve origins, that therse Exalts will do the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T20:30:45-07:00","id":1391410,"title":"","content":"I would be fine with Abyssals losing the &quot;I am cursed to cause suffering and death by my mere presence, even when I try to fight it&quot;, and thus losing the single largest motivating factor for transforming into a Solar Exalt.<br /> <br /> But I want to keep the potential for Abyssals to become Solars and Solars to become Abyssals.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be anything more than a possibility one could achieve with a sorcerous working or an artifact/manse or the blessing of the Unconquered Sun (or the curse of the Neverborn).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T23:58:40-07:00","id":1391432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1391219#post1391219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Abyssal and Infernal Exaltations are altered Solar ones, and that is inherently negative also kind of plays a bit on folks having a bit of a naturalist bias. That is saying, they kind of tend to think the natural thing or something in its natural state is the &quot;way it shoudl be.&quot; That Abyssal and Infernal Exaltation aren't the Exaltations are &quot;god intended it&quot; creates a bit of that narrative, and I think it fed a bit into the way the Exaltations were presented in previous editoins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the whole implimentation of mirror charms too, the comparison between You Can Be More vs. Broken Heart Triumph was very leading for what Solar Exalted were meant to be in a way that no charm in the 2e core was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T17:09:06-07:00","id":1394185,"title":"","content":"Essence and Crucible are the only Exalted products I'm interested in right now. That's because both of them are going to give us actual information about all those things we were promised seven or eight years ago.<br /> <br /> Do we have anything new about Essence? I never understand the Monday meeting phases. Is it going faster or slower than expected?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T17:23:38-07:00","id":1394190,"title":"","content":"Well, they started in January and the first draft is done, then they moved on to playtesting, I'm not sure if that's finished or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T17:24:42-07:00","id":1394191,"title":"","content":"Sounds like decent progress to me, but I don't know what to compare it to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T18:05:39-07:00","id":1394197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1394191#post1394191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like decent progress to me, but I don't know what to compare it to.</div> </div> </div> </div>The turn around based on Lunars which didn't I think start until after the DB KS ended is something like 20-24 months for turn-around. Late 2e could get books done in 10 months, but htat's wiht 1) B&amp;W art 2) Still more layout resoruces than now and 3) Less quality contorl. SO take what you will there I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T18:11:27-07:00","id":1394198,"title":"","content":"Also writing a splatbook and writing a whole system are a bit different. Although with Essence being simplified it's probably going to be faster to get through, that doesn't necessarily make it super fast.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't imagine they'd spend more than a few months in playtesting, unless there's something that they just can't get to feel right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T01:23:13-07:00","id":1394522,"title":"","content":"Looks like this week\u2019s podcast is about Exalted in general and Essence in particular: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/episode-107-knights-of-the-exalted-developer-roundtable/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/episode-107-k...er-roundtable/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T10:40:31-07:00","id":1394584,"title":"","content":"Oh, this should be interesti-<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1:37:45 </div> </div> </div> Never mind.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm personally wondering on how Eclipse Charmshare might work in <i>Essence</i>. It's not really useful to speculate, because we don't know what PC <i>or</i> NPC Charms might look like, but I have to assume that they're not <i>too</i> different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T10:49:07-07:00","id":1394585,"title":"","content":"I think it'll probably be sort of the same. But if NPC charms work quite differently from PC charms, you might need a &quot;PC version&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T10:57:24-07:00","id":1394588,"title":"","content":"The interview itself is mostly an hour, all the rest comes from a bunch of tangents","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T13:32:08-07:00","id":1394617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1394584#post1394584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, this should be interesti-<br /> Never mind.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm personally wondering on how Eclipse Charmshare might work in <i>Essence</i>. It's not really useful to speculate, because we don't know what PC <i>or</i> NPC Charms might look like, but I have to assume that they're not <i>too</i> different.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main thing we know for sure is that like in 3e, you can't learn other Exalt Charms via it, nor in case of Essence, Exalt-specific Charm Modes for Universals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:36:25-07:00","id":1394808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1394617#post1394617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main thing we know for sure is that like in 3e, you can't learn other Exalt Charms via it, nor in case of Essence, Exalt-specific Charm Modes for Universals.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense that non-Exalted would have their own Modes for universal Charms and their own unique Charms, and that Eclipses would be able to learn some of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:42:45-07:00","id":1394811,"title":"","content":"I mean the podcast mentions that the Universal Charms are designed in such a way that they're assuming the Baseline of Charms in Essence is &quot;Exalt, with certain Modes being better&quot; as opposed to &quot;Assume the baseline is Solar, adjust lower for some of them&quot;.<br /> <br /> But yes, I think that Universal Charms for PCs are going to assume that the ones who take them are Exalts. Eclipse Charmshare, assuming it's still a thing, will probably be better suited for more niche things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T04:17:12-07:00","id":1395988,"title":"","content":"So tonight at 9pm EST Monica is streaming a game of Essence. <b>Exalted Essence </b><br /> 9:00 PM<br /> The premiere play-test of Exalted Essence. A fresh and streamlined version of Exalted Third Edition. Find out more about this exciting corebook in the last episode of the Onyx Pathcast.<br /> GM: Monica Speca<br /> Players: Neall Raemonn Price, Danielle Lauzon, Dixie Cochran, and Rich Thomas<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/TheOnyxPath\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/TheOnyxPath\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/TheOnyxPath\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/user/TheOnyxPath </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For those of you less excited by Essence and more by the wider available splat types, it looks like there will be some newer ones (well, Neall's playing an old one that doesn't have 3rd ed rules, so I guess like a Sidereal or Abyssal, and I think someone else is playing a newer one?).<br /> <br /> Unfortuntately, in her glorious majesty's time, 9pm EST is like 3am, so I can't watch live, but I think you can watch them afterwards as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-12-2020, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T14:49:18-07:00","id":1396075,"title":"","content":"The game will include one Sidereal, one Abyssal (a Moonshadow), one Solar and one Lunar PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-12-2020, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T18:20:14-07:00","id":1396089,"title":"","content":"Actual Play is now live","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","