uote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396140#post1396140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... anyone catch what excellencies actually <i>do</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubles your ability dice, I <i>think </i>it was commited motes rather than spent, but don't quote me on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T03:52:55-07:00","id":1396148,"title":"","content":"Sure.<br /> <br /> Considering how massively different those 3 Attributes are (more styles or approaches than strength, intelligence, etc are), I wonder if Lunars, etc, are based more on Abilities like Physique (hence the charm using that instead of force) than Attriutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T07:32:47-07:00","id":1396164,"title":"","content":"I think the dice is spent, otherwise that cheapens the Solar Advantage<br /> <br /> As for the other Exalted Game, apparently Neall hadn't decided what he was gonna run, whether normal Exalted or Essence and decided to do Essence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T08:10:18-07:00","id":1396174,"title":"","content":"Sounds like I really missed out. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T08:54:51-07:00","id":1396178,"title":"","content":"The Vod is up on Youtube if you wish to see. So its not like you missed it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T08:58:59-07:00","id":1396179,"title":"","content":"I can see the Storypath influence in the way threshold successes appear to be a resource you can spend for extra effects. Stunting, meanwhile, bares a blatant DnD 5e influence (not a bad thing, mind).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396148#post1396148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how massively different those 3 Attributes are (more styles or approaches than strength, intelligence, etc are)</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems like a further simplification of CofD/Storypath's Power/Finesse/Resistance, dropping the Mental/Physical/Social axis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-13-2020, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T10:10:13-07:00","id":1396187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396164#post1396164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the dice is spent, otherwise that cheapens the Solar Advantage</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Dixie mentioned she spent the Mote on her Stealth Excellency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the other Exalted Game, apparently Neall hadn't decided what he was gonna run, whether normal Exalted or Essence and decided to do Essence </div> </div> </div>I think it was originally scheduled to be Ex3, but at the tail end of the Essence demo he said he decided it'd be more fun to do another Essence game. And that Minton would be there. And then teased that someone may or may not be playing one of the New Exalt Types.<br /> <br /> Tease.<br /> <br /> And for people who missed the live event: You can watch it as a VoD. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/9iR2hvXoapQ\" target=\"_blank\">Relinking</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T13:03:13-07:00","id":1396204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396179#post1396179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stunting, meanwhile, bares a blatant DnD 5e influence (not a bad thing, mind).</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Maybe I missed something there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T13:34:18-07:00","id":1396205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396204#post1396204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? Maybe I missed something there.</div> </div> </div> </div> <b>Stunt (Exalted Essence):</b> a special resource you get for doing something cool, used to modify your roll, which you can save for later and potentially transfer to another player.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspiration (Dungeons and Dragons Fifth Edition):</b> a special resource you get for doing something cool, used to modify your roll, which you can save for later and potentially transfer to another player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T14:00:59-07:00","id":1396208,"title":"","content":"This doesn't actually seem any more simple than 3e. Just weird, different flavors of complexity.<br /> <br /> Dang, I was really hyped for a simpler, more narrative focused and easier-to-play version of Exalted. Essence is feeling more and more like somebody's Exalted heartbreaker, and less like what I had hoped for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T14:23:28-07:00","id":1396210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396208#post1396208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dang, I was really hyped for a simpler, more narrative focused and easier-to-play version of Exalted. Essence is feeling more and more like somebody's Exalted heartbreaker, and less like what I had hoped for.</div> </div> </div> </div>What had you hoped for? Sorry if you already said recently and I'm making you repeat yourself, but I glanced back and well... it's a big thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T14:28:15-07:00","id":1396213,"title":"","content":"I think it is simpler, apparently the charms are much shorter and so on, but I don't think it's a<i> lot</i> simpler.<br /> <br /> It does look fairly different (not inherently a bad or good thing), and so even if it is simpler, having a bunch of new things makes it seem more complex. It may be that for experienced Ex3 players, it's a bunch of changes, while for new players it seems much simpler than Ex3 standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-13-2020, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T15:22:58-07:00","id":1396218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396208#post1396208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't actually seem any more simple than 3e. Just weird, different flavors of complexity.<br /> <br /> Dang, I was really hyped for a simpler, more narrative focused and easier-to-play version of Exalted. Essence is feeling more and more like somebody's Exalted heartbreaker, and less like what I had hoped for.</div> </div> </div> </div>One time expenditures on excellencies, attacks separated from the initiative, turns are team-based, animas have <b>much </b>simpler scales(none/building/full), motes are scaled down into the single digits, charms/turn scaled way down, tiered foes and the universal charm set. I dunno this looks much more streamlined to me. Considering we're on the outside looking in and that was a WiP test game I'd say it was pretty comprehensible.<br /> <br /> I will say it has some of storypath's unintuitiveness, but that's more due to newer mechanical philosophies than slow mechanics, it's pretty easy to catch onto. Currently, my only gripe is that your mote pool won't be high enough to reach bonfire outside combat, and might be bit small for games/sessions with less combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 06-14-2020, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:28:54-07:00","id":1396254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396210#post1396210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What had you hoped for? Sorry if you already said recently and I'm making you repeat yourself, but I glanced back and well... it's a big thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>My hope with Exalted: Essence was for a game that removes a lot of the game's tedious math and fiddly bits (and some of its D&amp;D heritage) in favor of a streamlined, narrative-focused experience. I was expecting Charm design to move away from math-adjustments and +dice or +successes and towards unique special powers and capabilities. I hoped that Essence would rework Abilities to function along a broader set of narrative permissions, but they seem to be largely truncated into a smaller list. I guess I just expected Essence to be a larger move away from the complexity of 3e, but it's mostly just a lateral move to a different set of complex mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One time expenditures on excellencies, attacks separated from the initiative, turns are team-based, animas have <b>much </b>simpler scales(none/building/full), motes are scaled down into the single digits, charms/turn scaled way down, tiered foes and the universal charm set. I dunno this looks much more streamlined to me. Considering we're on the outside looking in and that was a WiP test game I'd say it was pretty comprehensible.<br /> <br /> I will say it has some of storypath's unintuitiveness that's more do to newer mechanical philosophies than slow mechanics, it's pretty easy to catch onto. Currently, my only gripe is that your mote pool won't be high enough to reach bonfire outside combat, and might be bit small for games/sessions with less combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking off attacks from initiative means more numbers to keep track of in combat. Anima has become a 0-10 scale as opposed to dim/glowing/burning/iconic. Charms have regained 2e's 'one per action' limitation in the form of '1 per attack step.' Some of these changes, like tiered foes and universal charms, are something of an improvement. Essence has also added a weird 7-part Virtue system which seems entirely superfluous, since it's keeping Intimacies as well. Also, in terms of unneccesary complexity, Essence has removed battlegroups and replaced them with individual mooks which must be defeated separately.<br /> <br /> None of these changes seem to make combat any quicker to resolve. We've still got all the dice, all the fiddly Charms, and as far as I can tell all the numbers of Exalted 3e. Withering, Decisive, soak, hardness, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:16:13-07:00","id":1396275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396254#post1396254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My hope with Exalted: Essence was for a game that removes a lot of the game's tedious math and fiddly bits (and some of its D&amp;D heritage) in favor of a streamlined, narrative-focused experience. I was expecting Charm design to move away from math-adjustments and +dice or +successes and towards unique special powers and capabilities. I hoped that Essence would rework Abilities to function along a broader set of narrative permissions, but they seem to be largely truncated into a smaller list. I guess I just expected Essence to be a larger move away from the complexity of 3e, but it's mostly just a lateral move to a different set of complex mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Breaking off attacks from initiative means more numbers to keep track of in combat. Anima has become a 0-10 scale as opposed to dim/glowing/burning/iconic. Charms have regained 2e's 'one per action' limitation in the form of '1 per attack step.' Some of these changes, like tiered foes and universal charms, are something of an improvement. Essence has also added a weird 7-part Virtue system which seems entirely superfluous, since it's keeping Intimacies as well. Also, in terms of unneccesary complexity, Essence has removed battlegroups and replaced them with individual mooks which must be defeated separately.<br /> <br /> None of these changes seem to make combat any quicker to resolve. We've still got all the dice, all the fiddly Charms, and as far as I can tell all the numbers of Exalted 3e. Withering, Decisive, soak, hardness, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how Initiative being decoupled from attacks would mean more numbers to keep track of, since outside of the first roll, its basically you &gt; them. That's it. You are keeping track of power but unlike 3e Initiative, power caps out as 10, so that's definitely more easier to get a hang on and because it's not trading off between opponents as in the normal game, it basically just goes up until you decide to attack. An opponent attacking you won't effect it unless they have a power that does that. And for Charms, I honestly don't see the problem with that one? It basically there to limit Charm combos which in 3e can get very out of hand. This allows players to not remember all the combinations of charms they can use and instead focus on some efficient and solid single ones <br /> <br /> There has been no indication that Battle Groups are gone, that hasnt been mentioned whatsoever. Honestly from what I heard from Neall they are very much still a part of the game.<br /> <br /> Anima is simpler because it is just every spent mote, instead of 5+ and thus trying to figure out costs to not to go over. It is just at you spent anything? It goes up. Now I do agree I'm not totally with it going and maxing at a number as high as 10 but that I'm sure is in the process of more testing since that very much influences how quickly you get your Iconic power.<br /> <br /> And regarding Virtues, hm it does seem superfluous at first glance but a reminder that a character would only have two of them, with the Major pretty much in the place of a Limit Trigger. Will have to see more of the systems that relate to them or their purposes.<br /> <br /> Edit: and as for quicker to resolve combat, well that was one of the first things we saw. Down and Dirty Rules. Single at set difficulty, boom you win. Not all fights need to spend hours on. Though even outside of that, looking at how quickly they were able to defeat the Nemissary and his minions, I'd say that combat was resolved quite quickly. But well will have to see how it handles against one of the talked about &quot;boss&quot; antags","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 06-13-2020, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T02:45:34-07:00","id":1396337,"title":"","content":"One charm per step only does make things simpler in reality, because often stuff gets slowed down a lot by the complexity of throwing 4 charms together.<br /> And overall, I do think it's simpler in a lot of ways, if not massively so. There does seem to be some new stuff that they feel is useful to Exalted, but isn't actually about simplifying it per-se.<br /> <br /> But. I also still don't see the point of virtues, seems like added complexity.<br /> And: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My hope with Exalted: Essence was for a game that removes a lot of the game's tedious math and fiddly bits in favor of a streamlined, narrative-focused experience. I was expecting Charm design to move away from math-adjustments and +dice or +successes and towards unique special powers and capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is a bit streamlined. But I don't think it's moved to a simplified, narrative game like FATE or something. Personally that's not quite what I want (except maybe what you said about charms, but not overall), but if that is what you want, no, it doesn't seem like that's what they're trying to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T05:09:45-07:00","id":1396357,"title":"","content":"I'm not feeling any &quot;lite-ning&quot; from what I saw on the play test, just changes. I am reserving judgment until I see the finished book, but sadly my hype is completely under control at this moment.<br /> <br /> I am not so fond of what seemed like Power being the replacement resource for Initiative and adding Stunts as another resource. They mentioned a Power Bar and Stunt Bar at some point. There are enough resources to keep track of to begin with.<br /> <br /> On the positive side, I was extremely happy not to see dice tricks (such as 1s doing this, and 6s doing that, which I loathe with the hate of ten thousand suns), so that's a major plus in my book. Of course, it might just be that none were used for this test. Again, reserving judgment.<br /> <br /> Happy to have the opportunity to see a play test. Time will tell about the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","user":"Aleks","date":". 06-14-2020, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T06:19:53-07:00","id":1396366,"title":"","content":"I believe there is another session of Essence, run by Neall, at 11EST?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T08:12:16-07:00","id":1396387,"title":"","content":"It's about to start:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2uBDR07CiG4&amp;feature=youtu.be\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2uBDR07CiG4&amp;feature=youtu.be\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2uBDR07CiG4&amp;feature=youtu.be\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2uBDR07CiG4&amp;feature=youtu.be </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T08:15:43-07:00","id":1396389,"title":"","content":"Exalted: Essence is to Exalted as Fate Accelerated is to Fate. Same system, just streamlined and made more accessible wherever we can. The entire Ex:Ess book will, I\u2019m guessing, be smaller than the Ex3 Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T10:32:20-07:00","id":1396428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396357#post1396357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not so fond of what seemed like Power being the replacement resource for Initiative and adding Stunts as another resource. They mentioned a Power Bar and Stunt Bar at some point. There are enough resources to keep track of to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody mentioned a Stunt BAR, IIRC. You get dice from Stunting that can be banked or spent.<br /> <br /> And the only mention I heard in the first session of a Power <b>BAR</b> was likening your Power that you build with Withering attacks to a Power Bar from a fighting game, in that you build it up.<br /> <br /> So yeah, instead of building Initiative and having that coupled to when you attack, you just go in Whatever Order (no need to keep track of who goes when with it fluctuating with each slap) you just have to keep a measure of how much Power you have and whether that means you can launch a Decisive Attack. And it may cap at 10. So yes, it IS replacing Initiative as a Thing To Keep Track Of, but instead of &quot;I need to keep track of this for my Decisive Damage Pool and when I react and oh right I gained another five from Crashing my opponent-&quot; it's just &quot;I gain this, I can launch a Decisive on my next turn&quot;. It's a Thing that you keep track of, yes, but you don't have to keep track of <i>as much</i> with it.<br /> <br /> Edit: And the second live game has just ended, I've updated my notes to the best of my ability on the first watch. Not a lot of new BASE mechanics revealed (though I got a few new Abilities on the List) but I got more Charms and Advantages","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-14-2020, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T11:10:22-07:00","id":1396434,"title":"","content":"I, for one, am incredibly excited by what I've seen in the two playtests. Mostly because it feels so much more elegant. And that was what I was looking for out of Essence- a more elegant Exalted system that facilitated actual play but still felt like Exalted. And it certainly looks like they've accomplished that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11951-taleswapper","name":"taleswapper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:30:24-07:00","id":1396445,"title":"","content":"Honestly, from playtests by people fairly familiar with the system, I can't really tell.<br /> <br /> So, abilities seem to be:<ul><li><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Awareness</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Close Combat</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craft</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Embassy</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Navigate</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Performance</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physique</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Presence</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ranged Combat</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sagacity</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stealth</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">War<br /> <br /> My guess is Physique covers Athletics/Resistance and Strength/Stamina kind of stuff (where not part of Force and Fortitude), Navigate is Ride/Sail/Survival, Sagacity is Lore/Occult/Intelligence, Embassy is probably all the social stuff. Craft of course is Craft X, Craft Y, Craft Z, etc, etc.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:56:57-07:00","id":1396452,"title":"","content":"But if Embassy is all the social stuff, what is Presence, and what is Performance?<br /> I can certainly imagine the distinctions, but then why fold so many different things into Physique?<br /> Probably need to wait and read the actual book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:02:06-07:00","id":1396455,"title":"","content":"Hmm, good point, I was reading too quickly.<br /> <br /> Maybe Embassy is everything social not covered by those, ie Socialise+Linguistics+Bureaucracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:20:13-07:00","id":1396466,"title":"","content":"From the names alone, here's how I'd probably do them.<br /> <br /> Presence is the direct short-term stuff, Embassy involves longer negotiations and planning.<br /> <br /> If you're talking to someone who works with the Guild and you're haggling to cut a deal, which may involve doing favors or something, that'd be Presence because the aim itself is short-term (get a good bargain on the goods)<br /> <br /> If you're talking to someone who works with the Guild and you're in negotiations for giving them a cut of the profits if they sell the goods you can secure them for the next year and a day, that'd probably be Embassy because you're working on long-term agreements and deals.<br /> <br /> Time will tell whether Grand Speeches will be Presence or Performance. I can see the logic for moving the Motivation Through Speech into Presence while Dancing, Painting, and Acting go into Performance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-14-2020, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T14:17:01-07:00","id":1396490,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised there's a Stealth ability instead of a Storypath-style Subterfuge, since that's where I'd expect all of the Larceny stuff to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T14:21:37-07:00","id":1396492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396490#post1396490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised there's a Stealth ability instead of a Storypath-style Subterfuge, since that's where I'd expect all of the Larceny stuff to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, that's a good observation. Maybe it's something that will change during playtesting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:05:23-07:00","id":1396539,"title":"","content":"Maybe disguise, pickpocketing and lockpicking... are just in Stealth.<br /> <br /> What else did we get from Neall's game, mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T19:27:14-07:00","id":1396586,"title":"","content":"Some Charms from Getimians, Liminals, some universal ones, some splat/anima Advantages. Not a whole lot or anything incredibly exciting I feel, the sessions are a bit too narrative and short to actually see much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T19:45:38-07:00","id":1396589,"title":"","content":"Most of what I got were a lot more specific than the stuff from Monica's game. Like how apparently the Moonsilver Alchemical was able to just sneak past Extras without a need for a check. I believe this is a Moonsilver thing. Saw some classic Tricks, like Optical Shroud was mentioned, and there was the Charm to make them look like a normal flesh-person instead of a shiny miracle being of clay and silver.<br /> <br /> I think we saw some of the Blood Aspect Liminal Powers. When their anima hits Active (2-9 Motes Committed or Spent) they can add their Essence in Automatic Successes on Embassy, Performance, and Presence rolls to inspire Lust, Greed, or Ambition. And when they go Iconic, they and all allies do extra damage. Maybe it was to Battlegroups or Extras, I'll need to watch it again. The Liminal also seemed to have a Charm that could be paid with Health Levels or Motes, which did levels of damage to Battlegroups, I think it was called &quot;Towering Corporeal Pillar&quot;?<br /> <br /> Minton played the Getimian, and there were a few things here and there. Apparently the Getimians still have two kinds of Essence, called <i>Still</i> and <i>Flowing</i>. I don't think I saw any of the Getimian Advantages, Exalt or Caste... There was a Charm used called, hold on, Sleeper-Guiding Whisper, I think? The Charm didn't seem to work and I didn't quite catch the effect.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1D5ejH585oYLEEtGUTzT0kO9R4u3ZbVCJ01jVDzEZcG8/\" target=\"_blank\">Relinking my frantic notes so they don't get lost</a>. They're not split by game, at best they're split by &quot;Charms&quot; &quot;Advantages&quot; and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T21:12:37-07:00","id":1396603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396589#post1396589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minton played the Getimian, and there were a few things here and there. Apparently the Getimians still have two kinds of Essence, called <i>Still</i> and <i>Flowing</i>. I don't think I saw any of the Getimian Advantages, Exalt or Caste... There was a Charm used called, hold on, Sleeper-Guiding Whisper, I think? The Charm didn't seem to work and I didn't quite catch the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Getimian Charm was to make the target forget the conversation the next time they sleep, BUT...<br /> <br /> There was some complexity where the Charm has both a Still and a Flowing Mode, and the Getimian needed to use Charm in Still Mode (whatever it does) before they were allowed to use the Charm in Flowing Mode (the Flowing Mode apparently being what makes a target forget a conversation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T22:09:23-07:00","id":1396612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396603#post1396603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Getimian Charm was to make the target forget the conversation the next time they sleep, BUT...<br /> <br /> There was some complexity where the Charm has both a Still and a Flowing Mode, and the Getimian needed to use Charm in Still Mode (whatever it does) before they were allowed to use the Charm in Flowing Mode (the Flowing Mode apparently being what makes a target forget a conversation).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thanks a million, I'll add that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T05:36:54-07:00","id":1396654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396539#post1396539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe disguise, pickpocketing and lockpicking... are just in Stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, <i>obviously.</i> It's just an odd name for it, akin to naming the Archery-Thrown ability &quot;Archery&quot; instead of &quot;Ranged Combat.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Power replaces Initiative pools from Ex3, starts at 0 at combat start<br /> - Build Power is an option to build withering damage power, always difficluty 3<br /> - Withering attacks build Power for every threshold success, plus weapon Accuracy successes<br /> - To make a decisive attack, the character must spend Power to overcome a target's Hardness. Damage = threshold successes and additional spent Power rolled + weapon Damage successes </div> </div> </div> So, if I understand this correctly, the Damage value of a weapon is basically <b>decisive</b> Accuracy, and the Build Power action exists for the low-Accuracy weapons (such as, presumably, grand daiklaves).<br /> <br /> I... think I like that? It sounds slightly better than EX3's Accuracy/Damage disparity, at least, assuming the Build Power option does what I think it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T05:58:34-07:00","id":1396656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396603#post1396603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Getimian Charm was to make the target forget the conversation the next time they sleep, BUT...<br /> <br /> There was some complexity where the Charm has both a Still and a Flowing Mode, and the Getimian needed to use Charm in Still Mode (whatever it does) before they were allowed to use the Charm in Flowing Mode (the Flowing Mode apparently being what makes a target forget a conversation).</div> </div> </div> </div>That was Sleeper-Guiding Whisper. It did, in fact, allow Eric to wipe the person's memory of the encounter; I was slightly mistaken in reading the Charm. It essentially allows you to instill shadow Intimacies in a target that don't normally affect their behavior, build them over time, and then the other variant of the Charm gives you a bonus to activate the shadow Intimacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T06:05:07-07:00","id":1396660,"title":"","content":"For those looking for a more narrative variant, we've always been pretty clear that this is primarily a streamlined version of Ex3 akin to Fate Accelerated to Fate Core. It plays similarly, though if you look under the hood there's definitely some different stuff in there, and it's meant to be a simpler and more narrative expression - that doesn't mean we're discarding the trad heritage in favor of pure story-style mechanics. However, we didn't feature a lot of the heavy story* inspired stuff - the dramatic editing and the Great Curse mechanics, for one, and the Virtues were streamlined a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T13:45:10-07:00","id":1396720,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/652577291318198316/721772434000314448/unknown.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> That's the ability spread. Some good choices there. Some I'm not so sure of. But I'm not 100% sure what's merged into what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-15-2020, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T15:51:27-07:00","id":1396741,"title":"","content":"If I had to take a guess (I don't, but I want to)...<br /> <br /> <b>Awareness:</b> Seems self-explanatory, but it wouldn't be too strange for it to also cover Investigation.<br /> <b>Close Combat:</b> Let's not waste time here.<br /> <b>Craft:</b> It's Craft.<br /> <b>Embassy:</b> Bureacracy-Socialize-Linguistics, no doubt. <i>The</i> Eclipse Ability.<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> It's Integrity. They could potentially put some of the more holy man-esque Resistance and Survival Charms here, like Hardship-Surviving Mendicant Spirit or Untiring Earth Meditation.<br /> <b>Navigate:</b> Sail and Survival, possibly with a side of Ride.<br /> <b>Performance: </b>Performance is Performance.<br /> <b>Physique:</b> Athletics, likely Resistance, possibly Dodge.<br /> <b>Presence:</b> Well.<br /> <b>Ranged Combat: </b>It's Archery and it's Thrown. Hopefully Elemental Bolt Attack goes here instead of in...<br /> <b>Sagacity: </b>If Embassy is about being an Eclipse (and it is), this is about being a Twilight-No Moon. It's Lore, it's Occult, it's probably Medicine, and if Investigation isn't folded into Awareness, it's folded into Sagacity.<br /> <b>Stealth:</b> Sneaky shit; Stealth and Larceny, maybe with the more Guile-focused Socialize effects alongside them.<br /> <b>War:</b> Huh! What is it good for?<br /> <br /> What stands out to me is the lack of a clear Ability for dealing with animals/familiars, which is odd given how big a deal those are in EX3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-16-2020, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T17:19:36-07:00","id":1396759,"title":"","content":"Given the amount of familiars they had in the playtest, I'm sure they have mechanics for it. But sadly we didn't get much chances of them showing that bit off","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T22:36:49-07:00","id":1396821,"title":"","content":"....Guys, do you think you could rename the attributes? Having three attributes that abbreviate to F, F, and F seems like it could get pretty confusing quickly. And, in this case, even going to two letters doesn\u2019t work, since it goes Fo, Fi, Fo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T23:38:27-07:00","id":1396828,"title":"","content":"I'd probably put Animal Training into Presence (getting it trained) or Sagacity (for exotic familiar)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396821#post1396821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....Guys, do you think you could rename the attributes? Having three attributes that abbreviate to F, F, and F seems like it could get pretty confusing quickly. And, in this case, even going to two letters doesn\u2019t work, since it goes Fo, Fi, Fo.</div> </div> </div> </div>The names are relatively short enough that I probably won't need to shorten them on a character sheet. And it's not like &quot;Force&quot;, &quot;Finesse&quot;, or &quot;Fortitude&quot; are difficult to say or mix up when you know the names.<br /> <br /> If you need to abbreviate them, well, you could go &quot;Force&quot; (it's a one-syllable word with five letters, it probably doesn't need to be abbreviate them), &quot;Fin&quot; and &quot;Fort&quot;<br /> <br /> Plus, alliteration. :P<br /> <br /> Edit: I just realized that if someone has, say, Dyslexia or some kind of trouble reading then that could possibly be a problem and that was an oversight. In that case maybe they can be changed in some groups to &quot;Power&quot;, &quot;Finesse&quot;, and &quot;Resilience&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-16-2020, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T00:03:17-07:00","id":1396829,"title":"","content":"I think I'd prefer Physical, Social and Mental to Force, Finesse and Fortitude. While Manipulation might overlap with some bits of Wits, I dont think Dex overlaps all that well with Manipulation. Likewise Strength =/= Charisma =/= Intelligence. I guess it puts more emphasis on Abilities, but I struggle to see why a high Force bruiser type should also be better at Charisma, just because he's also Strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T02:43:15-07:00","id":1396838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396829#post1396829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd prefer Physical, Social and Mental to Force, Finesse and Fortitude. While Manipulation might overlap with some bits of Wits, I dont think Dex overlaps all that well with Manipulation. Likewise Strength =/= Charisma =/= Intelligence. I guess it puts more emphasis on Abilities, but I struggle to see why a high Force bruiser type should also be better at Charisma, just because he's also Strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I had this reaction myself, but after discussing it with a friend I changed my mind.<br /> <br /> He pointed out that, essentially, one makes boring characters and the other makes interesting characters.<br /> <br /> Consider 3 roleplaying archetypes you'd get in a standard fantasy combat game.<br /> Leader McFighter is a really strong rugged guy with a big sword who leads from the front, shouts orders, etc.<br /> Stabby the Roguish Rascal is fast, cunning and tricksome. She wears light armour and dodges attacks. Probably steals stuff a lot.<br /> Tank Tankersdottir is extremely tough, extremely brave, and extremely stubborn. Probably drinks like a fish too.<br /> <br /> With Phys/Soc/Mental they all have Physical 5, and Soc and Men 2 or 3. Then they all have Close Combat 5. Also the second two both have high ratings in Physique, and the first two have high ratings in Presence... though the first probably has high Physique anyway as he's a combat character. So they end up as very samey.<br /> <br /> With this system Leader McFighter has Force 5, Stabby the Roguish Rascal has Finesse 5, and Tank Tankersdottir has Fortitude 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have 6 Lunar characters in my game, so currently they've picked phys/soc/men as their primary. But if we take the two social characters:<br /> Amira is a beautiful woman loved by all, with men, women and cute animals flocking around her, and also she's a competent archer.<br /> Jin is a cunning rogue who steals hearts and cash, and sometimes stabs people with a rapier.<br /> <br /> Now, both are going to be Social 5 characters, tbh. Which is awkward, because they're supposed to be doing two very different approaches to social-fu. Amira walks into a party and everyone looks at her, and the Queen invites her to sit at the top table. Jin spent weeks spying on a dragon of Realm troops and their officers from inside their camp, and they still think he was a poor stupid local seduced by one of the Yamabushi to be her summer fling.<br /> <br /> <br /> Admittedly, it's still not perfect. I am not really sure it would work so well for some other characters, tbh.<br /> As you said, why is the big bruiser actually quite smart in a straightforward way? I guess you represent it by Close Combat/Physique 5 and Sagacity 0. And one guy is playing a toad Lunar: tough, poisonous, a genius, and really annoying and rude so terrible at socialising. How does that work in this system?<br /> But that's the same with Phys/Soc/Mental. Going down to 3 attributes inevitably leads to a loss of granularity.<br /> <br /> But anyhow. I do look forward to a game where not 90% of combat characters have Dex 5, Melee 5 and a sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-16-2020, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T02:45:52-07:00","id":1396839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396828#post1396828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: I just realized that if someone has, say, Dyslexia or some kind of trouble reading then that could possibly be a problem and that was an oversight. In that case maybe they can be changed in some groups to &quot;Power&quot;, &quot;Finesse&quot;, and &quot;Resilience&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Power they've already used for a stat you use in combat. Essence's Initiative (in the sense of Withering, not in the sense of who goes first).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T02:57:47-07:00","id":1396841,"title":"","content":"So, on the abilities, I can't help feeling that some abilities are going to get rolled more than others (Sagacity vs War? Obviously depends on the game). Though obviously folding some things together makes it a bit better than standard 3rd ed. I was also hoping to no longer have to decide whether social rolls were Presence or Performance or Socialise/Embassy. If there was a Charisma stat I would mind less, but the lack of it I would think would make &quot;Social-fu stat&quot; more viable, like they've done with &quot;Mental-fu stat&quot; and &quot;Hit people stat&quot;.<br /> <br /> Investigation and tracking being folded into Awareness would be helpful for that (though tracking may of course be Navigate). I do frequently tell players &quot;Roll Perception+... I guess Awareness or Investigation or Survival maybe? Whichever.&quot; Not that this is a big problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmmmmmmmmm.... I wonder if directing a ship in naval combat is actually War and not Navigate. That'd make Dawn Admirals more viable... or it may not matter. I'm wondering about favoured abilities for Castes/Aspects. Do they have them? How many do they have? 13 is not an easy number to divide up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T10:47:42-07:00","id":1396900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396838#post1396838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you said, why is the big bruiser actually quite smart in a straightforward way? I guess you represent it by Close Combat/Physique 5 and Sagacity 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems worth noting the default Difficulty in Essence is 3.<br /> <br /> Force 5 + Physique 5 beats Diff 3 easily.<br /> Force 5 + Sagacity 0 does not.<br /> <br /> But this is the kind of thing playtesting is for. If they're going to stick to collapsing the Attributes to three, it can work, but the rest of the numbers need to add up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T11:50:37-07:00","id":1396908,"title":"","content":"I mean we don't even know how Chargen Dots are allocated in Essence. I personally am all behind the whole &quot;Attributes as Methodology/Approaches&quot; bus, because as Heavy Arms notes if you want to portray someone who's not too well-learned but is very good at Fight, that'd be denoted by a high Close Combat and a low Sagacity.<br /> <br /> We may not have seen enough, but instead of &quot;These are your Favored Abilities&quot; it may be that ExEss will just go &quot;As a Dawn, distribute X dots through Close Combat, Ranged Combat, or War, then spend Y dots among your other Abilities&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> I mean we don't even know what the XP costs will be. Or if Charms will even be grouped by Attribute or Ability. It may just be &quot;This is a Charm, Charms cost X experience, have fun&quot;<br /> <br /> (Also if I were forced to make a guess now, I'd think that your Attributes all start at 1 and you probably get like 6 dots to allocate among them, but that's just me guessing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-16-2020, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T11:59:35-07:00","id":1396910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396908#post1396908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We may not have seen enough, but instead of &quot;These are your Favored Abilities&quot; it may be that ExEss will just go &quot;As a Dawn, distribute X dots through Close Combat, Ranged Combat, or War, then spend Y dots among your other Abilities&quot; or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works, or something similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T19:15:13-07:00","id":1396988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396821#post1396821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....Guys, do you think you could rename the attributes? Having three attributes that abbreviate to F, F, and F seems like it could get pretty confusing quickly. And, in this case, even going to two letters doesn\u2019t work, since it goes Fo, Fi, Fo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fo, fi, fo, fum,<br /> <br /> I smell the blood of an Englishman!<br /> <br /> Be he live or be he dead,<br /> <br /> I'll slap a Thesaurus upside his head!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T19:17:41-07:00","id":1396991,"title":"","content":"I've begun keeping an eye out, and I'm interested where this is going so far. It's not perfectly exactly what I was hoping for, but I don't think I was ever going to get perfectly exactly what I was hoping for, and what I'm hearing sounds pretty reasonable so far.<br /> <br /> I don't have a whole lot to weigh in on, but the one thing that did catch my eye is that Solar Advantage: 0m Excellencies? Is that as powerful as it's scanning to me, or am I missing some important details limiting it from just firing off on every Ability roll, like a cooldown, a contribution to the anima, or an increased opportunity cost for Charm activation? Exalted Advantages should definitely have some wow kick to them (the Devil-Body, Liminal recovery from dismemberment), but the Solar Advantage at first glance is striking me as an outlier even among those. There is, however, almost certainly something I'm missing that distinguishes it from that blindly imagined first glance.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(Apologies, incidentally, to folks who replied to my original post very early in this thread and didn't get a response. The Exalted forum can be a very busy one, and at the early point the discussion was back then, I neither felt able to commit to keeping up with the conversation, nor like the thread would benefit from turning into an interrogation of my personal bugaboos in the absence of early spoilers. My original post was pretty brusquely put in the heat of the announcement's surprise.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T19:24:31-07:00","id":1396992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396991#post1396991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a whole lot to weigh in on, but the one thing that did catch my eye is that Solar Advantage: 0m Excellencies? Is that as powerful as it's scanning to me, or am I missing some important details limiting it from just firing off on every Ability roll, like a cooldown, a contribution to the anima, or an increased opportunity cost for Charm activation? Exalted Advantages should definitely have some wow kick to them (the Devil-Body, Liminal recovery from dismemberment), but the Solar Advantage at first glance is striking me as an outlier even among those. There is, however, almost certainly something I'm missing that distinguishes it from that blindly imagined first glance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I heard that in combat, you can only activate one Charm per step, and you gotta declare your Excellency in Step 1. So if you want to use ANOTHER Charm in that step, you can't stack your Excellency on top of it. So you won't be stacking your Excellency on top of <i>literally</i> everything.<br /> <br /> However I don't believe that this applies OUT of combat, so Solars will have their Excellencies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T19:44:06-07:00","id":1396995,"title":"","content":"Also I think excellencies are only one mote now, although the mote math has been redone so motes mean more, I think that dropping from 1 to 0 might not be as crazy a savings as it would be in Ex3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T20:26:26-07:00","id":1397001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1396992#post1396992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I heard that in combat, you can only activate one Charm per step, and you gotta declare your Excellency in Step 1. So if you want to use ANOTHER Charm in that step, you can't stack your Excellency on top of it. So you won't be stacking your Excellency on top of <i>literally</i> everything.<br /> <br /> However I don't believe that this applies OUT of combat, so Solars will have their Excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wasn't thinking in terms of combat tactics so much as just the extravagance of being able to commit freely to excellence in all your invested Abilities without any restraint except the attention it gets. The shift from 1m to 0m is a bigger shift than from 2m to 1m, especially when mote pools are greatly reduced in Essence.<br /> <br /> Then again, I also don't know how mote economy and regeneration works yet. For all I know it might not even be tracked outside combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T22:06:27-07:00","id":1397010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1397001#post1397001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I wasn't thinking in terms of combat tactics so much as just the extravagance of being able to commit freely to excellence in all your invested Abilities without any restraint except the attention it gets. The shift from 1m to 0m is a bigger shift than from 2m to 1m, especially when mote pools are greatly reduced in Essence.<br /> <br /> Then again, I also don't know how mote economy and regeneration works yet. For all I know it might not even be tracked outside combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the discord: Excellencies double ability scores, exalted have pools of 5m at essence 1, and I believe the cap was stated to be 15 at essence five (+2 at 2/4, +3 at 3/5), at essence 1 we saw a 1m/round regeneration in combat, and it was mentioned to have a (X)m/hour regen with full regen on rest. However all of this is subject to change with testing and feedback so any of this might be altered by second draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 06-17-2020, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T03:46:23-07:00","id":1397045,"title":"","content":"I tried watching the playtests, but the format (and the <i>length</i>) just isn't for me. I'll have to stick to Kyman and whoever's notes, I guess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T03:55:28-07:00","id":1397047,"title":"","content":"An interesting point; apparently, as Excellencies are applied in Step 1, they don't apply to defence (Step 2). So you need to buy Defensive charms for that, you can't boost your defence with the excellency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T08:09:40-07:00","id":1397092,"title":"","content":"Makes sense to me, we no longer have dodge as an ability and thus doesn't seem to be a difference between parry and evasion. I think anyway. Could be wrong","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T13:37:46-07:00","id":1397142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1397092#post1397092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense to me, we no longer have dodge as an ability and thus doesn't seem to be a difference between parry and evasion. I think anyway. Could be wrong</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, there <i>isn't</i> a Dodge Ability.<br /> <br /> I guess defending yourself from close range attacks is done with Close Combat, and defending yourself from ranged attacks is done with Ranged Combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T13:59:40-07:00","id":1397145,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I think it'd make more sense to defend yourself against Ranged attacks using Awareness, tbh.<br /> <br /> Dodging could be represented by Physique I guess. I would personally use Awareness though. Can't dodge if you don't know you're being attacked. Also, Awareness in ExEss doesn't have its prime combat use ie Initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T20:39:28-07:00","id":1397216,"title":"","content":"I mean we don't know HOW defense is calculated in ExEss. It might be like... Averaging Resilience and some Ability? Awareness? I doubt that there'll be multiple Defenses, as the playtest with more combat didn't seem to use different defenses when the target was being grappled versus when it was being sniped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T23:14:49-07:00","id":1397245,"title":"","content":"Seems interesting for the moment. Do you think most Charms are portable from Ex 3 Core to ExEss ? I like all the &quot;fluffy&quot; Charms in Ex 3 Core (Solars detect lie in Investigation, DB know when they are followed in Larceny I think, etc ...). Not talking about dice tricks Charms and other obviously incompatible Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T23:41:04-07:00","id":1397247,"title":"","content":"Hm, if Charms are simpler in ExEss then it'll probably be easy enough to patch in some basic Charms to fill any gaps that the ExEss charms don't fill.<br /> <br /> Like, say, making a Charm for Solars that combines Truth-Discerning Technique and maybe mixing in... Shit, what's that Investigation Solar Charm that goes Ding when there's stuff? As a GM that was the most useful charm my PCs got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T00:10:33-07:00","id":1397249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1397247#post1397247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, if Charms are simpler in ExEss then it'll probably be easy enough to patch in some basic Charms to fill any gaps that the ExEss charms don't fill.<br /> <br /> Like, say, making a Charm for Solars that combines Truth-Discerning Technique and maybe mixing in... Shit, what's that Investigation Solar Charm that goes Ding when there's stuff? As a GM that was the most useful charm my PCs got.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd combine them in one single Charms ? Are ExEss Charms very broad so you would combine different effects into one Charm ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T03:52:16-07:00","id":1397259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1397216#post1397216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean we don't know HOW defense is calculated in ExEss. It might be like... Averaging Resilience and some Ability? Awareness? I doubt that there'll be multiple Defenses, as the playtest with more combat didn't seem to use different defenses when the target was being grappled versus when it was being sniped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did anyone catch whether attacks still involved seperate attack and damage rolls? Weapons seem to have an accuracy and damage, but that may not all be rolled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T05:04:59-07:00","id":1397270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1397249#post1397249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd combine them in one single Charms ? Are ExEss Charms very broad so you would combine different effects into one Charm ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That they are. Charm Trees in Essence will be 3 charms deep at most. They are very much taking the core of many charms into a single one. This becomes even more apparent when you take Modes in account. I don't think it's very much combining charms with different effects but you know how in Ex3 you have long charm trees to effects a single action, making what you do with better and better as you buy more charms. Yeah because of the shrinkage those are the ones that will be compiled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T07:36:27-07:00","id":1397289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1397259#post1397259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did anyone catch whether attacks still involved seperate attack and damage rolls? Weapons seem to have an accuracy and damage, but that may not all be rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there's only an attack roll. Damage is calculated via threshold successes plus other things iirc. And then just auto-applied, not rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T09:33:16-07:00","id":1397312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1397145#post1397145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I think it'd make more sense to defend yourself against Ranged attacks using Awareness, tbh.<br /> <br /> Dodging could be represented by Physique I guess. I would personally use Awareness though. Can't dodge if you don't know you're being attacked. Also, Awareness in ExEss doesn't have its prime combat use ie Initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anticipating where and how a weapon will strike you is safer than seeing it : if you see it, well that's probably the last thing you will ever see.<br /> Anticipating where and how a weapon will strike is dependent on your understanding of the weapon. An Archer is the best equipped to guess where an arrow will land (factoring in the ballistic curve, the wind etc ...) and whether stepping aside will not actually place himself in the path of the arrow. And someone without any notion of what a Boomerang is will probably watch it right until the moment he eats it. <br /> It even more true for melee weapons. As a Kendo practioner, I can defend a shinai strike with a barely visible move, but against a Naginata, I am toast. And not just because of the reach, it would probably be the same against nunchuks but there I have no experience.<br /> Sorry if I appear too assertive but I just cannot I understand the concept of Dodge as an ability ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24379-hoardandsue","name":"HoardAndSue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T10:28:43-07:00","id":1397323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1397259#post1397259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did anyone catch whether attacks still involved seperate attack and damage rolls? Weapons seem to have an accuracy and damage, but that may not all be rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Withering attacks seem to only build Power based on threshold successes. Decisives seem to ahve bifurcated rolls still, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T14:29:03-07:00","id":1400397,"title":"","content":"The Brawl, Martial Arts, and Melee Abilities do not exist as such, along with Archery and Thrown. There's just Close Combat and Ranged Combat.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, all Exalted share a common body of Charms, with few splat-unique/exclusive Charms, and Charm trees are meant to be short.<br /> <br /> So, there is no Solar Brawl Tree or Solar Melee Tree, as such.<br /> <br /> Instead, there are likely Close Combat Charms exclusively for fighting with any weapon, Charms for fighting without any weapons, and Charms which can be used with or without weapons.<br /> <br /> Charms evoking Martial Arts Styles would generally be of the third category, but since there might be no real distinction between Melee and Martial Arts anymore, there might be weapon-dependent sets of Charms.<br /> <br /> Like, a universal set of Ranged Combat Charms for firewands and flamepieces could ignore the old divisions between Solar/Terrestrial Archery and Righteous Devil Style.<br /> <br /> A universal set of bareknuckle punching Charms could ignore the old divisions between Solar Brawl and any theoretical Boxing Style.<br /> <br /> Advanced grappling styles like Mantis might even grow out of basic, universal grappling Charms.<br /> <br /> I might not need to design an entire 12-Charm Martial Arts Style around two-handed hammers if I could instead get away with a three-deep set of Close Combat Charms that work exclusively with two-handed hammers and axes, and which does nothing but evoke the &quot;spin to win&quot; concept I've chased off-and-on for years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T23:15:20-07:00","id":1405248,"title":"","content":"Essence is on to the second draft stage now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T13:43:23-07:00","id":1405662,"title":"","content":"Since all Exalted are going to share the same basic Close Combat Charms for punching and grappling, might we see a second attempt at &quot;( ) Hero Style&quot;?<br /> <br /> A Style like Falcon Style Martial Arts would remain distinct from &quot;Brawl&quot; Charms because of armor-restrictions that &quot;Brawl&quot; Charms would not have, but &quot;Brawl&quot; Charms could gain their own Form Charm that (mostly) reject weaponry while allowing for the heaviest of armor.<br /> <br /> Such a Form Charm could be a Boxing Style Form, as Exalted Brawl Charms have traditionally evoked Western boxing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T14:56:57-07:00","id":1405671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1405662#post1405662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since all Exalted are going to share the same basic Close Combat Charms for punching and grappling, might we see a second attempt at &quot;( ) Hero Style&quot;?<br /> <br /> A Style like Falcon Style Martial Arts would remain distinct from &quot;Brawl&quot; Charms because of armor-restrictions that &quot;Brawl&quot; Charms would not have, but &quot;Brawl&quot; Charms could gain their own Form Charm that (mostly) reject weaponry while allowing for the heaviest of armor.<br /> <br /> Such a Form Charm could be a Boxing Style Form, as Exalted Brawl Charms have traditionally evoked Western boxing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalts will probably have unique Close Combat Charms. Whether those are shareable ala 2e Heor styles I'm pretty skeptical of. I kind of see things like Solars having Heaven Thunder Hammer, while DBs get the waterbending grappling, and those just being unique-to-that-splat takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T15:09:56-07:00","id":1405674,"title":"","content":"Is there something that spawned that thought? It doesn't seem like a very likely thing to me in absence of some comment from the team.<br /> <br /> Unarmed combat Charms will still have modes to capture different feels without Hero Styles. We're not going to need Hero Styles to let Solars punch/grapple Behemoths without penalty, Lunars get advantages from animal limbs, DBs to smack you with an elemental bonus, etc. There's already design space for that.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't feel like it fits any of Essence's stated goals to have the Hero Styles specifically for other Exalted to learn a different Exalted type's Hero Style. Either you're adding a possible ten Styles that are all extremely close in theme and mechanics, or you're adding one Style that's basically just a second set of universal unarmed Charms but you can buy other people's modes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T16:37:59-07:00","id":1405691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1405674#post1405674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there something that spawned that thought? It doesn't seem like a very likely thing to me in absence of some comment from the team.<br /> <br /> Unarmed combat Charms will still have modes to capture different feels without Hero Styles. We're not going to need Hero Styles to let Solars punch/grapple Behemoths without penalty, Lunars get advantages from animal limbs, DBs to smack you with an elemental bonus, etc. There's already design space for that.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't feel like it fits any of Essence's stated goals to have the Hero Styles specifically for other Exalted to learn a different Exalted type's Hero Style. Either you're adding a possible ten Styles that are all extremely close in theme and mechanics, or you're adding one Style that's basically just a second set of universal unarmed Charms but you can buy other people's modes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I woudl say it's almost antithetical to the idea of Hero styles. There's no cross-Exalt Charmshare has been soemthing we learned pretty early. ANd Hero Style Charms sort of are that, since rathr than an actual universla fihgting style it's &quot;I'm a Lunar wanting to fight like a Solar&quot; which feels just...against the gaols fo ahving Modes and still segragated non-universal Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T00:59:26-07:00","id":1405754,"title":"","content":"There was another Essence stream a few hours ago. I missed it, but I'll try to watch it after I get up and might be able to give some notes on things. Unless someone beats me to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T01:50:01-07:00","id":1405761,"title":"","content":"There were some new tidbits I gleaned here and there. The big one, IMO, would be Projects as a mechanic. Namely, it seems like things like Crafting, Sorcerous Workings, Investigations, and Travel are going to be handled by the same framework.<br /> <br /> The example used in the game was investigating a trapped party during a mystery murder, where the goal was to get some likely suspects, but with obstacles in the way: Specifically the obstacles of &quot;There's a lot of people here&quot; and &quot;Nobody feels like talking to you&quot;, both of which were difficulty 3 to overcome.<br /> <br /> There was some Social stuff as well, mentioning things such as influencing or instilling Intimacies as well as using threshold successes on influence rolls to persuade and dissuade targets","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T04:24:35-07:00","id":1405778,"title":"","content":"This makes me happy. Imo, one of the biggest problems of exalted has been a proliferation of too many subsystems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T08:11:27-07:00","id":1405792,"title":"","content":"I miscommunicated.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t mean that there would be multiple Hero Styles, or that other Exalted could learn the unique \u201cBrawl\u201d Charms of other Exalted.<br /> <br /> I was referring to how all (proper) Second Edition Hero Styles were essentially Boxing/Pankration with different flavors. So, the shared \u201cBrawl\u201d Charms would look very much like Solar Hero Style and Infernal Monster Style, with the different flavors being expressed through Modes and a few Charms unique to each Exalted Host.<br /> <br /> And if these Charms would continue to evoke Boxing, then perhaps they could have a Boxing Form Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T14:58:09-07:00","id":1405838,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that the only significant division between Brawl Charms and the Hero Styles was that the Hero Styles were MAs that could be learned like any other MA by other appropriate character. 1e and 3e still have Brawl Charms more oriented towards &quot;boxing/grappling&quot; without 2e's weird move to make the Hero Styles in response to collapsing Brawl and MA into one Ability.<br /> <br /> Giving everyone a unique Form Charm as part of their native close combat Charms could be a interesting departure from previous Charm designs; esp. as a space saving measure to collapse a bunch of Charms into a single package, but I don't think that alone really qualifies as bringing back the Hero Styles. It also seems a distinct waste to focus that limited space on making everyone have a &quot;boxing/grappling&quot; Form Charm, instead of using it to highlight each splats most iconic way of fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T08:34:24-07:00","id":1405949,"title":"","content":"The Brawl Charms could include an optional Boxing Form AND offer Host-specific \u201cHero\u201d Form Charms.<br /> <br /> The ideas are not mutually exclusive, and are distinct from each other. The Boxing Form would not work with grapples or kicks, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T11:09:32-07:00","id":1405969,"title":"","content":"This feels like a lot of speculation on something not even hinted at as bieng a goal in Essence, and which draws on a system thing that wasn't really ever liked. If they reallyw anted to do like, organized puglilist/boxer stuff, it probably will be presetned as a style in itself. &quot;Fighitng like a Solar&quot; is probablyw hat Clsoe Combat covers more in gneeral, which may or may not look like a Balrog, Sol Badguy, or Mitsurugi depending on how you skin them. Splat-specific combat Charms probably go for mor elike, the splat's aeshtetics rather than looking like boxing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T14:58:27-07:00","id":1406003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1405969#post1405969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels like a lot of speculation on something not even hinted at as bieng a goal in Essence, and which draws on a system thing that wasn't really ever liked. If they reallyw anted to do like, organized puglilist/boxer stuff, it probably will be presetned as a style in itself. &quot;Fighitng like a Solar&quot; is probablyw hat Clsoe Combat covers more in gneeral, which may or may not look like a Balrog, Sol Badguy, or Mitsurugi depending on how you skin them. Splat-specific combat Charms probably go for mor elike, the splat's aeshtetics rather than looking like boxing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about every splat having their own specific Boxing-type Form Charm.<br /> <br /> I am worried that we're never going to get a whole Boxing Style because too many Boxing tropes have always already been used in Brawl Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T17:06:04-07:00","id":1406017,"title":"","content":"Why do we need a boxing style? Esp. in Essence where the goal is to simplify and reduce things?<br /> <br /> Boxing is a sport/competition, it has been for thousands of years (and what kind of moves are or aren't allowed have changed repeatedly over that time). People don't train in boxing for self-defense (though some modern self defense classes might include boxing techniques as part of MMA) or a primary mode of fighting in a military or similar situation, they train in boxing to win boxing matches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T19:10:50-07:00","id":1406036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1406017#post1406017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do we need a boxing style? Esp. in Essence where the goal is to simplify and reduce things?<br /> <br /> Boxing is a sport/competition, it has been for thousands of years (and what kind of moves are or aren't allowed have changed repeatedly over that time). People don't train in boxing for self-defense (though some modern self defense classes might include boxing techniques as part of MMA) or a primary mode of fighting in a military or similar situation, they train in boxing to win boxing matches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Falcon Style is based on Luchadore wrestling, which is more of a sport than boxing in that Luchadore (and other professional wrestling) is largely a performance art.<br /> <br /> People don't train in Luchadore for self-defense.<br /> <br /> Your argument is invalid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T21:43:01-07:00","id":1406058,"title":"","content":"Given that Essence is trying to simplify things, I wager that if they do anything related to Brawl specifically it'll be like... There'll be one Punch Better Charm that may have some Modes for things like &quot;Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals gain bonus successes on top of it and knock the foe another range band away&quot;, and maybe a Grappling Charm that lets certain Exalts grab hold of things that are bigger than them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T04:12:14-07:00","id":1406085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1406036#post1406036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Falcon Style is based on Luchadore wrestling, which is more of a sport than boxing in that Luchadore (and other professional wrestling) is largely a performance art.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luchadore is part of the visual inspiration for Falcon Style, and is entertainment... but all of the Martial Arts Charms are that, because they're exaggerations and homages to various forms special effects based performance fighting rather than simply normal human real world martial arts taken to 11.<br /> <br /> More importantly, while you can use Falcon Style for a Luchadore if you want, it never forces that on you and is an entirely useful and fun MA for any Exalted that has access to flight (like a bird themed Lunar... as it's in the Lunar book and all). Instead it's fighting style based on the themes of an animal: in this case a bird of prey that swoops down on its prey for powerful strikes and grabs on with insane force. A concept that his heavily steeped in the martial arts entertainment that Exalted draws on for inspiration.<br /> <br /> If you've never watched a Luchadore, Falcon Style still makes complete sense. If you had to wear a mask when using Falcon Style, your counter point would have a lot more weight.<br /> <br /> I also might have missed it, but do we even know if Falcon Style is going to be in Essence? I somehow doubt Essence is going to have all the styles (unless it really cuts them down somehow), and Falcon style seems exactly the sort of cool style to stick in a supplement and not the core book that means it's not going to make the cut for Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your argument is invalid. </div> </div> </div>My argument isn't a long form dissertation and is thus open to nitpicks because I didn't think I'd have to waste the time to elaborate on all this.<br /> <br /> You also completely dodge the question to attack, &quot;my argument,&quot; which is annoyingly telling about where this is likely to go.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:03:56-07:00","id":1406088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1406036#post1406036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Falcon Style is based on Luchadore wrestling, which is more of a sport than boxing in that Luchadore (and other professional wrestling) is largely a performance art.<br /> <br /> People don't train in Luchadore for self-defense.<br /> <br /> Your argument is invalid.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is also a game about people punching gods. Dial it down, please.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T07:08:19-07:00","id":1406106,"title":"","content":"Yes, it is a game about punching gods, and there are legends and modern myths surrounding the art of Boxing.<br /> <br /> Why shouldn\u2019t there be a Martial Art for punching gods really fast in the kidneys and hard across the jaw?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T09:14:20-07:00","id":1406121,"title":"","content":"Sunder what the heck point are you even trying to make?<br /> <br /> Edit: A bit more words... In baseline Ex3, they have a Charmtree for &quot;Punching really hard&quot; for Solars and DBs<br /> <br /> It's called Brawl.<br /> <br /> For Lunars it's called Strength Charms.<br /> <br /> Given that in ExEss, the Ability that covers punching will be called Close Combat and the Attribute covering Punching Hard is called Force, those may not translate perfectly.<br /> <br /> I doubt there will be a Martial Arts Style, whether it echoes the Hero Styles or just covers &quot;Fuck any fancy stuff, I want to punch things&quot; (First Pulse Style, I think? Was that the thing in 2e?) if only because there are probably other Martial Arts that will likely be put in before a Hero Style.<br /> <br /> Again, as I posted a bit ago, I think it's more likely that there will be a couple of Charms for Punching Good and Grapple and Thrash, which may have some fun Modes on them.<br /> <br /> Like I'unno, maybe there'll be a DB Mode for a Grapple Charm that lets them do that &quot;Fling the target towards an ally for a combo attack&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 08-03-2020, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T12:31:21-07:00","id":1406133,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that outside of the MA styles that require you to use weapons to use them, pretty much all of them let you punch things fast and hard (at least as the system represents that).<br /> <br /> Punching someone in the kidneys or across the jaw is a 1-dot Stunt or just using a basic Excellency. Brawl Charms and MA Charms are about going way beyond that. Even for relatively straightforward styles for beating people up as hard as possible, like Tiger, you still end up with more than just punch better to have enough of a theme to work around to make it a MA worth getting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T14:39:54-07:00","id":1406151,"title":"","content":"Hey, hey.<br /> <br /> How many wrestling/grappling Styles do we already have, outside of Brawl?<br /> <br /> Mantis, Falcon... oh, and Bear is eventually coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T14:52:58-07:00","id":1406154,"title":"","content":"I think this conversation could benefit greatly from some &quot;I&quot; language.<br /> <br /> For instance: I enjoy the thematics of being a punchy-kicky (or just-punchy) type hero, and I feel like I can usually if not always accomplish that with Brawl-type effects. If I were to explore a Boxing MA, I would do research on boxing to learn more about its philosophies of footwork, defense, and offense, as well as looking at famous boxers in media and video games (e.g. Dudley from SF3) to see how they stand out from the other fighters. I might even consult with an actual boxer, as I did when writing up Ex3's capoeira equivalent.<br /> <br /> I actually wouldn't make any Hero style synonymous with boxing, though. Hero styles struck me as sort of &quot;natural&quot; fighting styles, with philosophies so informed by Exalted Essence that they couldn't map directly to a real-world fighting style. So I see why someone would want Boxing Charms distinct from Brawl Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T15:30:32-07:00","id":1406157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1406154#post1406154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this conversation could benefit greatly from some &quot;I&quot; language.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> I appreciate Brawl's potential to represent brawling; bare-handed combat techniques learned from street-fighting, or from desperate survival out in the wilderness when no weapons are available.<br /> <br /> I see Brawl as having an inherent strategy, but not to the degree of a Martial Arts Style as Exalted understands the concept. Brawl is more offensively-focused than Melee and suffers in terms of defense, but beyond that Brawl is formless and without a specific strategy compared to Martial Arts Styles.<br /> <br /> I think Brawl is meant to be more potentially adaptable and versatile than most Martial Arts Styles, but those qualities are counterbalanced by the need to explore the Brawl trees widely as well as deeply, whereas a Martial Arts Charms are narrower and more self-contained.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I were to explore a Boxing MA, I would question whether a single style could represent the three or four &quot;styles&quot; of boxing (Swarmer, Outboxer, Slugger, and possibly &quot;Punch-boxer&quot;) through the customary number of three post-form, pre-pinnacle branches. Or whether each of those three styles deserves its own Martial Art, perhaps with some Totem Animal to provide thematic reinforcement of each style's differences from the others.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boxing_styles_and_technique\" target=\"_blank\">According to Wikipedia</a>, the &quot;in-fighter / swarmer&quot; style is even called &quot;Bull Style&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Solars in Exalted: Essence might still have Ox-Stunning Blow, Knockout Blow, and the Solar Crosscounter punch Charm I don't recall at the moment. These might be Solar-unique, or available to everyone but with Solar Modes.<br /> <br /> If there is simply too much overlap between some Brawl punching Charms and the ideas of a Boxing Style, I would like to see a Boxing Form as an optional Brawl Charm.<br /> <br /> Depending on how many Brawl punching Charms there are, some of them might evoke the In-Fighter (Thunderclap Rush Attack, Hammer-on-Iron Technique) while others evoke the Outboxer (Wind-and-Stones Defense, Solar Crosscounter), and these might give rise to different Boxing Forms. (Ox-Stunning Blow and Burning Fist Burial might evoke the brutal slugger style.)<br /> <br /> But I would certainly want just a single Boxing Form, for simplicity's sake, if that worked better than having more than one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I actually wouldn't make any Hero style synonymous with boxing, though. </div> </div> </div>I didn't want to suggest such a thing.<br /> <br /> But the Hero Styles were the one time that Brawl trees were given Form Charms, and given how Brawl's striking Charms tend to draw on boxing tropes, Second Edition's Hero Styles became the closest we got to Exalted Boxing Style.<br /> <br /> So it seemed like an appropriate thing to bring up, even if I could have been much clearer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-03-2020, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T17:34:55-07:00","id":1406189,"title":"","content":"I can't help but feel as though the topic of Brawl vs Hero Styles may have gotten off-topic from Exalted Essence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T18:04:50-07:00","id":1406193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1406189#post1406189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel as though the topic of Brawl vs Hero Styles may have gotten off-topic from Exalted Essence</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though it was never intended to be about Hero Styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T12:31:08-07:00","id":1406315,"title":"","content":"Anyone watch the game Monica streamed on Friday? I looked at the Discord where people were discussing it, but I didn't really see any new information that had been revealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T13:06:50-07:00","id":1406319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1406315#post1406315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone watch the game Monica streamed on Friday? I looked at the Discord where people were discussing it, but I didn't really see any new information that had been revealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, there was mention of some Social Actions (Persuading, Dissuading, instilling Intimacies, Intimacies and your Virtue seem to influence the difficulty of social actions)<br /> <br /> There was also mention of Projects, which is a framework for complex multi-step goals like Crafting, Sorcerous Workings, Travel, and Investigations<br /> <br /> Like, the example during the Murder Mystery plot on Friday had this Project, after the murder was announced.<br /> <br /> Goal: Find a list of Suspects<br /> Obstacles:<ul><li>The guests are nervous and don't feel like talking (Difficulty 3)</li> <li>There's a lot of guests, it'll be tough to narrow them down (Difficulty 3)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T21:52:23-07:00","id":1406380,"title":"","content":"I wonder how this will handle the systems that are unique to each exalt--Sideral false identities, Lunar Shapeshifting or Alchemical built in charms. (Hey maybe we'll get colossi! Probably not, but one can dream...). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T22:51:19-07:00","id":1406385,"title":"","content":"The tentative name is Exalted Advantages. Each Exalt Splat gets two of them. Like, Sidereals get these:<ul><li>Arcane Fate: after leaving the scene people start to forget about the Sidereal, explaining their actions as the work of passing strangers as they forget all details of the Sidereal. For Exalts this may be contested by a Diff 5 Intergrity roll or if they have an Intimacy to the Sidereal. If so they always remember.</li> <li>Weaving Destiny: the Sidereal may weave a Destiny modeled after an archetype, profession, or social roll and give it to another character with a touch. When attempting a task which resonates with that archetype the target may transfer dice for automatic successes up to the Sidereals Essence. A destiny lasts for 5 years up to the Sidereals discretion. They may only be subject to one destiny at a time. A Sidereal may apply a Destiny to themselves and with it they lose access to Arcane Fate, allowing people to remember their fake destiny.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T05:20:16-07:00","id":1406614,"title":"","content":"Compacting the rules for Arcane Fate and Sidereal Astrology into two paragraphs is freaking <b>elegant</b>.<br /> <br /> It's one easy to digest and quick to reference package. Instead of... spread out over how many pages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T05:30:18-07:00","id":1406616,"title":"","content":"Just coming back to praise the idea of Exalted Essence, because I'm trying to assemble a group of player, and as I was explaining a bit of Exalted mechanics some player just said &quot;I think the system is too complex, I'd prefer we try another of the proposed game&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T06:08:57-07:00","id":1406620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1406614#post1406614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compacting the rules for Arcane Fate and Sidereal Astrology into two paragraphs is freaking <b>elegant</b>.<br /> <br /> It's one easy to digest and quick to reference package. Instead of... spread out over how many pages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though as there's no cost or limit it seems a bit OP. You can easily spam it on everyone you meet giving them a five year buff. But then, maybe that fits their role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T08:34:58-07:00","id":1406639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1406616#post1406616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just coming back to praise the idea of Exalted Essence, because I'm trying to assemble a group of player, and as I was explaining a bit of Exalted mechanics some player just said &quot;I think the system is too complex, I'd prefer we try another of the proposed game&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in a similar boat. One of my groups loved the world of Exalted but the game eventually stopped because Ex3 was too complex for them. So now I'm counting the days until we get the Essence manuscript so I can start a new game with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T13:46:52-07:00","id":1406667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1406620#post1406620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, though as there's no cost or limit it seems a bit OP. You can easily spam it on everyone you meet giving them a five year buff. But then, maybe that fits their role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the number of successes is gated by the Sidereal's Essence, that's probably not as busted as it could be. Converting dice into successes is powerful but I wager that it'll be more enhancement.<br /> <br /> Plus, why wouldn't a Sidereal want to just tag helpful friends and NPCs with a little help? :P Makes Astrology worth using rather than <i>not</i> worth using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T14:16:39-07:00","id":1406672,"title":"","content":"I think we might need to see more context around it, such as how specific a Destiny is. &quot;One of Creation's greatest warriors,&quot; can be put to more uses than, &quot;One of the greatest Marukan mounted archers.&quot; While the difference in how broadly they'd apply to combat is obvious, you also have things like if you're in the West, a warrior known all over Creation could intimidate away a small pirate band that doesn't want to get slaughtered, while they might not be able to even tell you that the Marukan forces prefer to fight on horseback let alone be scared on reputation alone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T11:19:29-07:00","id":1415091,"title":"","content":"\u200bI've been using someone's homebrew system for now since 3e is really unappealing to my players, so I'm very excited for Essence progress so far. Especially getting some Infernal and Alchemical goodness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T08:46:44-07:00","id":1416271,"title":"","content":"Huh, this thread is NOT about what I thought it was!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Apologies in advance, I've been out of the loop for awhile...but what exactly is this? This isn't going to be like Power Combat, is it, where each new book of the main line will now have to have two sets of traits for two systems? Or is this more like those rules-lite pamphlets they give out to get people interested in the game in the first place? Sooo confused...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T08:53:15-07:00","id":1416272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1416271#post1416271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, this thread is NOT about what I thought it was!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Apologies in advance, I've been out of the loop for awhile...but what exactly is this? This isn't going to be like Power Combat, is it, where each new book of the main line will now have to have two sets of traits for two systems? Or is this more like those rules-lite pamphlets they give out to get people interested in the game in the first place? Sooo confused...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. It\u2019s just a rules lite version of Exalted that\u2019s a one off for people who can\u2019t get into the main line because it\u2019s too mechanically finnicky. <br /> <br /> Moving forward no mainline exalted books will reference Essence or be made to work with it, except the fluff book. I imagine that it\u2019s possible to get another book expanding Essence but that\u2019s not the plan right now, and by the time that theoretical book comes out we\u2019ll probably be seeing fourth Edition getting pitched anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T09:01:11-07:00","id":1416274,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Ok, this will be interesting to see. Although I kinda wonder if its very existence is a tacit admission that the complexity of 3E may have gotten away from them...All I see on the site is that work will begin in 2020, but it looks like campaigns are already being run? I don't see it on DriveThru, is there an ETA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T09:54:29-07:00","id":1416286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1416274#post1416274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! Ok, this will be interesting to see. Although I kinda wonder if its very existence is a tacit admission that the complexity of 3E may have gotten away from them...All I see on the site is that work will begin in 2020, but it looks like campaigns are already being run? I don't see it on DriveThru, is there an ETA?</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s alpha build test games that the developers posted excerpts from.<br /> <br /> It might be a tacit admission of that, but then again I know people who genuinely think that DnD 5th edition is too complex and get turned off by it. I think Ex3 is a bit too complex, but not by too much and only in certain areas. I\u2019d be good with it being 80%-90% as finnicky, but some people can only handle it if it\u2019s like 20% as complicated. Essence might be for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T10:25:18-07:00","id":1416294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1416274#post1416274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! Ok, this will be interesting to see. Although I kinda wonder if its very existence is a tacit admission that the complexity of 3E may have gotten away from them...All I see on the site is that work will begin in 2020, but it looks like campaigns are already being run? I don't see it on DriveThru, is there an ETA?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a mix. The current devs operate in it ifine and one of the devs for Essence has noted not minding the complexity of Exalted. The three main heads (Monica, Neall, Dixie) on it are actually a good range of good-with-3e, tired-with-3e, and scared-away-by-3e as I gather from the interviews and podcasts on the topic. ANd the success of Lunars (the first all-by-current devs Minton and Vance) is sitll one of OPP's best Kickstaters since Dragon-Blooded last I checked, so there's still at least folks willing to play for it.<br /> <br /> But having another option on the other end of the system maximalism spectrum with some ptoentially genuinely fresh appraoch to the Exalted is pretty stand-out. And its stand-alone nature and promise to be so to me shows the confidence the mainline will do fine still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T10:57:16-07:00","id":1416303,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s also other things that make it newbie friendly like nearly completely flattening the power curve and giving all exalted the same treatment and content right out of the gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T11:05:48-07:00","id":1416307,"title":"","content":"Still a little unclear on what this will look like in action, tho...So it comes out, someone picks it up and likes it and wants to play more...But the only option for that are the supplements for the crazy complicated game they were intimidated by in the first place? Maybe I'm just too used to the business model of encouraging buyers to expand their collections, so I guess I'm just not seeing how it can be so completely self contained...It has all the same setting info as the Core?<br /> <br /> Say that one IS satisfied with 3E as is, is there any incentive to pick this up (beyond being a completist)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T11:55:28-07:00","id":1416318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1416307#post1416307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still a little unclear on what this will look like in action, tho...So it comes out, someone picks it up and likes it and wants to play more...But the only option for that are the supplements for the crazy complicated game they were intimidated by in the first place? Maybe I'm just too used to the business model of encouraging buyers to expand their collections, so I guess I'm just not seeing how it can be so completely self contained...It has all the same setting info as the Core?<br /> <br /> Say that one IS satisfied with 3E as is, is there any incentive to pick this up (beyond being a completist)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence is probably being designed to not need supplements. It has ten playable exalt types right form the start, so no splatbooks. Beyond that having a dozen supplements kind of kills the idea. \u201cHere\u2019s Exalted Essence, an easy, self contained rules-lite system, and here\u2019s the seven supplement books that you have to buy if you want to expand it with a huge intricate list of artifacts, marital arts, manse designing, new splats, expansions on old splats, and million new sorcery spells!\u201d If you\u2019re looking for a deeper and more complex experience just get ex3. <br /> <br /> If you like the main line picking it up will give you a preview of unreleased splats and maybe some ideas on houserule for the main game, but if you\u2019re a fan of Essence you probably won\u2019t pick up any mainline books for the crunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T14:20:36-07:00","id":1416339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1416307#post1416307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still a little unclear on what this will look like in action, tho...So it comes out, someone picks it up and likes it and wants to play more...But the only option for that are the supplements for the crazy complicated game they were intimidated by in the first place? Maybe I'm just too used to the business model of encouraging buyers to expand their collections, so I guess I'm just not seeing how it can be so completely self contained...It has all the same setting info as the Core?<br /> <br /> Say that one IS satisfied with 3E as is, is there any incentive to pick this up (beyond being a completist)?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> I think hit smost of the things there. A big thing to note is that the book itself will probablyb e pretty upfront on its relationship with the rest of the line. It is being designed to be well, minimal. If it does its job right, it won't <i>need</i> more systems since you'll be able to convert from the main game into it pretty easily. They even plan to provide an appendix to do that in tehre. And the same book will also point to the Exalted books which are needed to expand on. The nature of a rules-light system as they are trying to do it means that you just don't have like, a lot more to do mechancially if you get your bases covered well.<br /> <br /> Like, in talking about all ten canonical Exalted at once, it by its nature <i>can't</i> cover a shitload of setting important things that the big splas do. ANd as much as there is a lot of crunch in say, Lunars, I would fathom to ay that a lot of the book is still material relevant to Essence. The Introduction, first two chapters, the information on Lunar Exalted mechanics relevant to things like their Great Curse and Essence fever, the style of Charms hlep give ideas for things that might just not make it into ExEss for wordcount, the artifacts are all full of stuff to loot for such games, and the QCs are useful for anything also.<br /> <br /> And this is beyond books that well, aren't going to be as mechanical like <b>Crucible of Legends</b> or <b>Across the Eight Directions</b>, which are going to likely be pretty mechanics agnostic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T15:24:06-07:00","id":1416364,"title":"","content":"<i>Essence</i> shares the same setting of Third Edition, but it only has room for the same depth of setting information that's in the 3e core book \u2014 that is to say, it's pretty thoroughly abridged. If you want more setting information for <i>Essence</i>, you'll want to use the same 3e supplements that you'd use in concert with the 3e core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T15:25:34-07:00","id":1416366,"title":"","content":"As someone that's fine with the mechanical complexity of 3e (at least the level of it, not always the specific implementations of it), I have the following reasons for picking up Essence:<br /> <br /> 1) Just because I like high crunch doesn't mean I always want to play high crunch and having a lower crunch game in a familiar setting gives me more options to play based on my moods.<br /> <br /> 2) I play with different people with different tastes. Some people I play with have wanted Essence for 20 years. Some think that regular 3e is just fine. Having Essence and core 3e lets me play with both sets with mechanics the individual group enjoys.<br /> <br /> 3) Essence looks like it might have some solutions to issues I have with 3e's implementations that I might want to mine for house rule even if I don't keep Essence's relative simplicity. Also in general I like to tinker and appreciate good ideas for rules that I might apply elsewhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T16:59:43-07:00","id":1416381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1416307#post1416307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still a little unclear on what this will look like in action, tho...</div> </div> </div> </div>Boy howdy are <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9iR2hvXoapQ\" target=\"_blank\">you</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2uBDR07CiG4\" target=\"_blank\">in</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T-jcsS6XK8o\" target=\"_blank\">luck</a>!<br /> <br /> Yes I realize this is like nine hours to comb through, and that's a lot to assign. I've watched those, and there's a few things that make me like what I see. Short versions:<br /> <br /> <b>Things I Like The Look Of:</b><ul><li>It definitely looks simpler, but not so simplified that it doesn't look like it lacks some heft</li> <li>There's a few changes that seem to address some shortcomings in Ex3<ul><li>Different Craft system, with Craft being folded into a Projects system (previewed in the third link) alongside most complex actions such as traveling, Bureaucratic Projects, and Sorcerous Workings</li> <li>Instead of exchanging Initiative and having that determine who goes next, you build Power to launch Decisive Attacks, and this doesn't work by draining power from others, thus sidestepping the problem of &quot;We've fired off enough Decisive attacks that nobody has any more Initiative&quot; which I have seen.</li> </ul></li> <li>Stunts seem to be getting a revamp. Instead of ranking your Stunts, something is either a Stunt or it isn't. You get rewarded dice for Stunts, and you can spend them on one of your rolls or you can actually contribute them to a friend's die pool as an assist if they fail.</li> <li>The Exalt Advantages, which are little powers that different Exalt types share, look neat without being overwhelming. Each Exalt Type gets two Advantages the splat shares, and each Caste/Aspect gets three Advantages tied to your Anima. One that's available at all times, one that kicks in when your anima flares, and one that kicks in when your Anima goes Iconic.<ul><li>Example: Solars have two shared Advantages (Free Excellency, Win Ties), and Dawns, for instance, have a passive ability to just take out one Extra antagonist every round in combat (I hear that Dusks and Azimuths get similar abilities)</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b>Things I Don't Like the Look of/Am Unsure of:</b><ul><li>Hype as I am for this system... I admit there's some things I'm kind of resigned to rolling with. If you like the feeling of finding those Four Key Charms and firing them off all at once in a super Wombo Combo of cascading successes, Essence may not scratch that itch.</li> <li>I saw some people musing that with lower Mote costs, and what we've heard mentioned of the Anima Progression, it may be take some time for your Anima to get to Iconic. This chafes a little because as mentioned above, some of your abilities are tied to your Anima level. This may change in testing.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:01:02-07:00","id":1416414,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the info, guess I'll just wait and see as it gets closer to release. Have we been given any idea of the page count or price? And the chance to get a sneak peek at new Exalt types is a deal maker for me, esp as we probably can't expect to see them all for a few years yet...<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I see Crucible of Legends on the schedule, but no mention of what that's about? And am I the only one who's so nerdy that he's most stoked about the Essay collection??<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:36:44-07:00","id":1416425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1416414#post1416414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I see Crucible of Legends on the schedule, but no mention of what that's about? And am I the only one who's so nerdy that he's most stoked about the Essay collection??<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Storyteller Guide, including a guide on how Exalted is supposed to be run, official alternate rules and systems, and some other goodies. Every time I think about it I get Jeff Goldblum grabby hands.<br /> <br /> Gimme.<br /> <br /> Gimme now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T23:05:11-07:00","id":1416432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1416425#post1416425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the Storyteller Guide, including a guide on how Exalted is supposed to be run, official alternate rules and systems, and some other goodies. Every time I think about it I get Jeff Goldblum grabby hands.<br /> <br /> Gimme.<br /> <br /> Gimme now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All that, and <i>rules hacks</i>, too?!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <img src=\"https://giphy.com/gifs/ss15-lHBbcpFTS5c2Y\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://giphy.com/gifs/ss15-lHBbcpFTS5c2Y\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/lHBbcpFTS5c2Y/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T00:25:34-07:00","id":1416438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1416432#post1416432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that, and <i>rules hacks</i>, too?!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, ST info for every Exalted type, which'll give a bit more info on Getimians, Infernals and Alchemicals particularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T06:58:30-08:00","id":1425928,"title":"","content":"Any new spoilers for Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:53:12-08:00","id":1426009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1425928#post1425928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any new spoilers for Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah turns out they released the entire manuscript for open playtesting. Meant to mention it here but it totally slipped my mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More seriously, I haven't seen any new play feeds or anything so I haven't gotten any new tidbits","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T02:16:50-08:00","id":1426096,"title":"","content":"Uh, let's see here, stuff I saw on discord.<ul><li>Spells will have modes the same as charms, for sorcery and necromancy, with some spells being exclusive to one or the other.</li> <li>Eclipse oath sealing will no longer be limited to Iconic anima.</li> <li>There was a private playtest at metatopia that was apparently quite good.</li> <li>Death is one of several fates that can befall your character upon defeat, you the player may also choose from other fates, such as being abducted or temporarily losing access to one of your merits (such as your daiklave being destroyed and needing to be reforged Anduril style).</li> <li>Enemies will be designed in the vein of storypath with base stats of 3 dice pools (Great, Good, Everything Else), Qualities (passive abilities) and Flairs (activated abilities with cooldown), then have templates that buff them accordingly. Examples were buffing a Fighting Dude with templates such as Battlegroup and Exalt to make the Wyld Hunt. Another Example was Demon with second and third circle templates. I heard in the BonusXp podcast that one statblock is &quot;Militant God&quot;.</li> <li>Shaping Rituals are still around and will have different mechanics from each other.</li> <li>Righteous Devil will be an included Martial Art</li> <li>One or more Abilities (names or number) of the preview game have been changed</li> </ul><br /> Looking further back so this might have been mentioned before...<ul><li>Approaches/abilities will be assigned points with an array, however, a sidebar will remind you to just add the points together and redistribute them if you'd prefer not to use it.</li> <li>You'll start with either one free excellency or one free level of Ox-body in addition to normal charms</li> <li>Attribute Exalts (like Liminals and Lunars) will have an Excellency Mode that lets them double their approach instead of their ability</li> <li>Artifacts will have 1 base power + 1-3 evocations</li> <li>Establishing Facts and Dramatic Editing is still present, Sidereals interact with Dramatic Editing in some way or have charms that make you good at it.</li> </ul><br /> And as Essence is still in development stage it's worth noting that all of this is subject to change, and some older info (Such as eclipse Oath-Sealing) has already been overhauled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 11-29-2020, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T02:26:20-08:00","id":1428449,"title":"","content":"Essence is in Manuscript Approval now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T04:55:46-08:00","id":1428456,"title":"","content":"Already? This is super quick, which is very encouraging. Would this mean ExEss is the next KS...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T09:05:50-08:00","id":1428481,"title":"","content":"Apparently they've hired two new writers to boost stuff along, because they released very little in 2020 and so are keen to get lots of stuff out in 2021.<br /> <br /> I think Essence will be the next KS for Exalted, though obviously not the next KS from Onyx Path generally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-15-2020, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T09:26:40-08:00","id":1428486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1428481#post1428481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently they've hired two new writers to boost stuff along, because they released very little in 2020 and so are keen to get lots of stuff out in 2020.<br /> <br /> I think Essence will be the next KS for Exalted, though obviously not the next KS from Onyx Path generally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two new devs. One's been handling Exigents, the other's been doing Many-Faced Strangers and Across the Eight Directions, as well as assisting with Hundred Devils/Adversaries.<br /> <br /> (Also, that second 2020 should be 2021.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T12:10:49-08:00","id":1428499,"title":"","content":"You're right, cheers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}